in/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:338:    process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = \"1\";\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:343:        \"a required attestation must fail closed when no trusted gh exists\",\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:346:      assert.equal(readJournal(tmpPrefix), null, \"required attestation must fail before starting the journal\");\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:353:        \"required attestation must not leave upgrade staging or a journal\",\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:358:      if (savedAttestation === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:359:      else process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = savedAttestation;\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:363:  it(\"rejects required attestation when the trusted gh reports failure\", async () => {\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:376:    const savedAttestation = process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:377:    process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = \"1\";\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:381:        /Provenance attestation verification failed for .* or SHA256SUMS/,\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:382:        \"a trusted gh reporting failure must reject required attestation\",\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:385:      if (savedAttestation === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:386:      else process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = savedAttestation;\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:619:   const previousBase=process.env.NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL, previousAttest=process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:637:   process.env.NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=`http://127.0.0.1:${(server.address() as any).port}/releases`;process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=\"0\";\norigin/main:cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:658:    if(previousAttest===undefined)delete process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;else process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=previousAttest;\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:280:| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:322:| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:144:| Distribution and CI: `install.sh, harness.sh, Makefile, package.json` ×2, lockfiles, `scripts/*`, workflows, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `LICENSE`, `doctor.ts` | 20 | Full read + installer runs (6 scratch HOMEs + docker) + CI log | E_distribution | Lockfiles audited by tool, not by line |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:273:| REL-08 | S3 | RR | Installer | `install.sh:21-24` | RT | Opaque no-version failure | REQ-REL-105 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:275:| REL-10 | S3 | RR | Reinstall | `install.sh:48-49` | RT | Cannot repair | REQ-REL-105 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:276:| REL-11 | S4 | RR | Tag validation | `install.sh:26` | RT | Loose regex | REQ-REL-105 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:277:| REL-12 | S4 | RR | Installer UX | `install.sh:32-33` | RT | Noisy output | REQ-REL-105 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:17:| [DEC-09](#dec-09-release-provenance-mechanism) | Release provenance | GitHub artifact attestations | No |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:140:**Chosen:** GitHub artifact attestations (`actions/attest-build-provenance`). Users verify with `gh attestation verify`. SHA256SUMS is kept. There is no separate GPG or minisign key to manage.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:21:**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:293:3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:296:6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:76:| REQ-REL-001 | quickstart | Installer: non-root; SHA-256 verified; no shell-rc edits; refuses a foreign `nexus`; atomic symlink swap; failure leaves HOME untouched. | `install.sh` | RT (E §4); TEST installer-smoke | tested | N | — | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:78:| REQ-REL-003 | DEVELOPMENT.md; DEC-12 | Supported platform: Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22. Clear failure messages elsewhere. | `install.sh`, doctor, upgrade preflight | Runtime/workflow source candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9` passed PR #150 exact CI run `39866110578` (Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64`) and CodeQL `39866110533`; focused `node_floor.test.ts` passed 6/6 on Node 24. Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | partial | N | Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | ACC-PLAT | RR | SPEC-07 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:79:| REQ-REL-004 | quickstart | Upgrade and rollback by re-running the installer with a tag. Manual uninstall keeps user data. | `install.sh` | RT (alpha.1→2→1) | tested | N | Reinstall does not repair (REL-10) | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:190:| REQ-REL-105 | Audit | Installer: strict tag check, clear no-stable message, repair on reinstall, quiet output. | onboarding | `install.sh` | TEST (ACC-PKG-05; test:scripts/installer-smoke.sh) | tested | ACC-PKG-05 | RR | REL-08, REL-10, REL-11, REL-12 | SPEC-06 / PLAN-06 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:198:| REQ-REL-109 | TOP_TIER D4 | Provenance attestation; tag-pinned installer asset. | supply chain | `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-03; test:release.yml, install.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-03 | RR | REL-09 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:9:| install.sh | full read + RUNTIME (6 install runs, scratch HOMEs, + docker ubuntu:22.04) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:66:| REL-08 | S3 | installer, latest path | install.sh:21-24 | RUNTIME. Without NEXUS_VERSION: `curl: (22) ... 404` / `nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.` (only prereleases exist). The same message appears for API rate-limit (60/h unauthenticated) or network failure. There is no hint to set NEXUS_VERSION and no list of available prereleases. | The first-time \"omit version\" path fails opaquely until v1.0.0 exists, and later under rate limiting. | Tell the 404 apart from other errors. On 404 say \"no stable release yet; use NEXUS_VERSION=vX (latest prerelease: …)\". Fall back to the `releases/latest/download` redirect, which avoids the API. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:67:| REL-09 | S3 | integrity | install.sh:33-35; release.yml:44-48 | SOURCE. SHA256SUMS is fetched from the same release as the archive. There is no signature, cosign/sigstore, or GitHub build-provenance attestation, and the installer script itself is served from mutable `main`. | A compromise of the release or repo is not detectable. The checksum only protects against transport corruption. | v1: add `actions/attest-build-provenance` (verifiable with `gh attestation verify`), or minisign/cosign signatures. Offer an installer pinned to a tag URL. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:68:| REL-10 | S3 | installer, reinstall/repair | install.sh:48-49 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. When the version dir already exists, the verified archive is discarded and the existing tree is reused after checking only 3 executables + VERSION. A corrupted or partially edited install (e.g. deleted dist files) cannot be repaired by re-running the installer. Versions accumulate forever with no prune (two versions measured at 14M+15M). | Reinstall is not a repair path. Disk use grows. | Compare a manifest hash, or reinstall into a temp dir and swap. Add `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. Document or implement uninstall/prune (`nexus self uninstall`). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:69:| REL-11 | S4 | installer input validation | install.sh:26 | RUNTIME. `case v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*` accepts `v1.2.3/../../x`. That string flows into the URL and into `VERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"`, though the run failed at download. The input is user-controlled only. | Low. Path traversal is possible if combined with a malicious base URL. | Use a strict SemVer regex via `grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$'`. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:70:| REL-12 | S4 | installer UX | install.sh:32-33 | RUNTIME. `curl -fL` without `-s` prints two progress meters inside a `curl \\| sh` pipeline. The PATH hint prints the expanded absolute path. The failure message on Ubuntu 22.04 (distro node v12.22.9) is correct but gives no install pointer. | Cosmetic. | Use `-fsSL --show-error`. Link Node 20 install docs. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:88:env -i HOME=$S/h1 PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=$S bash -c 'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2 sh'\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:121:- **Installer is safe by default.** It installs as non-root under `$HOME/.local`, never edits shell rc files, and never overwrites a foreign `nexus` (install.sh:41-47; covered by installer-smoke.sh:48-51). Checksum failure leaves the existing install unchanged (installer-smoke.sh:43-46). The symlink swap is atomic (`ln` + `mv -f`). Failures leave HOME untouched (RUNTIME, h2/h3).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:153:| E-R6 | Release provenance: signed or attested assets, and the installer can verify them. | supply chain | RELEASE-REQUIRED | `gh attestation verify nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0.tar.gz -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` passes. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:174:- Installer runs with `env -i HOME=<scratch>/h{1,2,3,3b,4} PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=<scratch> bash -c 'curl -fsSL …/install.sh | [NEXUS_VERSION=…] sh'`, covering alpha.2, none, v9.9.9, no-v, traversal, and alpha.1→alpha.2→alpha.1.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:72:| REQ-REL-11 | D3/R11 | Versioned install, upgrade, rollback; LICENSE/SECURITY/CHANGELOG | TOP_TIER D3/D4 | install.sh + GitHub prereleases v0.1.0-alpha.1/.2 with SHA256SUMS; LICENSE present; **no SECURITY.md, no CHANGELOG, no rollback procedure, no signing/provenance** | N |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:132:| HIST-07 | S2 | Release/supply chain | scripts/generate_sbom.sh:32-94; .github/workflows/release.yml | SOURCE: SBOM from direct deps only; not part of release workflow; no signing/attestation; no SECURITY.md. REL-002/003/004 marked DEMONSTRATED; REL-004 patch obligation now live (public prereleases) | No vulnerability intake path; SBOM incomplete | Lockfile-derived SBOM in release, SECURITY.md, provenance |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:198:| REQ-REL-V1-02 | SECURITY.md + CHANGELOG + lockfile-derived validated SBOM + checksum signing/provenance in release workflow | REL-002..004 obligations now live | RELEASE-REQUIRED | release.yml produces SBOM validated by cyclonedx-cli; attestation present |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:254:Spot-checks: grep in cli/src/{plugins,mcp,agent,tools,security,tester,parser,worktree,client,index,sandbox}.ts, cli/src/core/{capabilities,egress,candidate}.ts, core/src/{file_ops,search}.rs, scripts/{security_gates,generate_sbom}.sh, install.sh, .github/workflows/*.yml\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:16:| trusted-broker-bundle/install.sh | targeted read (lines 1-60, plus grep for the verify, manifest and prior-install steps) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:82:| CON-005 | S2 (contest) | Broker install | trusted-broker-bundle/BUNDLE.sha256:11; trusted-object-manifest.json:113-121; install.sh:52-60,92 | RUNTIME: `sha256sum -c BUNDLE.sha256` gives `./broker/demo-transport.mjs: FAILED` (actual 0ad7c7da…, recorded 3238d2e9…). install.sh:92 runs `sha256sum --check` under `set -e`, so **the committed bundle cannot be installed**; it fails closed. The installer also *requires* a prior install at /opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker with a pinned prior manifest (:5-7,52-60). There is no fresh-install path. | The parameterized transport has never been reviewed or hashed into the trust root. The \"upgrade-only\" installer cannot bootstrap a clean host. | Re-hash after review. Add a fresh-install mode. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:132:- **The vendored Node trust root checks out (RUNTIME):** the pubring sha256 matches the README; `gpgv` gives \"Good signature\" from 5BE8A3F6…; the SHASUMS line for linux-x64 matches install.sh:11; the manifest sha matches install.sh:13. The installer fails closed on a checksum mismatch.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:166:| CON-R3 | Fresh-install path for the broker (no prior-manifest requirement); uid and HOME as build parameters; BUNDLE.sha256 and manifest regenerated after review | workflow | BLOCKER (contest) | `install.sh --fresh` on a clean VM, followed by `post-install-qualify.py`, passes. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:15:- `install.sh`\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:37:| 7 | Installer: strict tag regex; `-fsSL --show-error`; no-stable-release hint naming the latest prerelease; rate-limit message; `MANIFEST.sha256` repair on reinstall; `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. | `install.sh:21-49`; `package-linux.sh` (write manifest) | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:29:| 5 | Add provenance with `actions/attest-build-provenance` on the tarball and SHA256SUMS, and upload `install.sh` as a release asset. The installer optionally runs `gh attestation verify` when `gh` is available. | `release.yml:44-48`; `install.sh` | — |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:50:- **ACC-SUP-03.** Run `gh attestation verify` in a post-release verification job against the published asset.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:61:- The release assets are: tarball, SHA256SUMS, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt, the SBOM, install.sh, and the attestation.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:16:- `install.sh` (installer durable provenance recording)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:12:| C4 | `install.sh --fresh`: no prior manifest needed. The demo uid and HOME become build parameters of `build-launcher.sh`. Regenerate `BUNDLE.sha256` and `trusted-object-manifest.json` after review. | `trusted-broker-bundle/{install.sh,build-launcher.sh,BUNDLE.sha256,trusted-object-manifest.json}` | High |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:5:| Status | Ready. GitHub attestations for provenance (DEC-09); `cli/dist` untracked (DEC-10). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:20:| REL-09 | There is no signature or provenance attestation, and the installer is served from mutable `main`. | SOURCE |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:57:- **Provenance.** Add `permissions: id-token: write, attestations: write` to release.yml and a step `actions/attest-build-provenance@v1` with `subject-path` set to the tarball and SHA256SUMS. Docs: `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:66:| ACC-SUP-03 | `gh attestation verify` passes for the RC tarball. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:14:Nexus currently requires operators to re-run the external `install.sh` script via `curl -fsSL ... | sh` to upgrade or downgrade installed binaries. There is no CLI command (`nexus upgrade`) and no TUI slash command (`/upgrade`) to:\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:47:   - Establish publisher trust boundary and attestation recommendations in `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:95:  - If a trusted `gh` exists at `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh` and `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION != 0`, verifies\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:96:    GitHub build provenance attestation. `PATH`-resolved `gh` is not used; with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`, a\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:130:| ACC-UPG-14 | Publisher Authenticity Assessment | Evaluates trust boundary, SHA-256 baseline, and documents signing/attestation recommendations in `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md`. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:44:3. **REQ-CON-103.** The broker gets a fresh-install mode (`install.sh --fresh`). The demo uid and HOME become build parameters. `BUNDLE.sha256` and the trusted-object manifest are regenerated after review.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:62:- `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes on a clean VM.\norigin/main:scripts/package-linux.sh:215:# Publish install.sh as release asset (REQ-REL-109)\norigin/main:scripts/package-linux.sh:216:cp \"$ROOT/install.sh\" \"$OUT/install.sh\"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30443}},"started_at_ms":1792900908868,"completed_at_ms":1792900908869}}
