{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:02:07.000Z","ordinal":323297,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17136-12b9-7661-904c-f2b43120b5c8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-87c14733-4f67-4d73-ba8f-db2b5d547911","process_id":"94528","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:scripts/installer-smoke.sh | sed -n '1,240p'; git show origin/main:install.sh | sed -n '1,180p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md | sed -n '1,100p'; git status --porcelain=v1 | wc -l"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:scripts/installer-smoke.sh | sed -n '1,240p'; git show origin/main:install.sh | sed -n '1,180p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md | sed -n '1,100p'; git status --porcelain=v1 | wc -l"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\nINSTALLER=${1:?usage: installer-smoke.sh INSTALLER ARCHIVE}\nARCHIVE=${2:?usage: installer-smoke.sh INSTALLER ARCHIVE}\nTMP=$(mktemp -d)\nSERVER_PID=\ncleanup() { [ -z \"$SERVER_PID\" ] || kill \"$SERVER_PID\" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nNAME=$(basename \"$ARCHIVE\")\nVERSION=${NAME#nexus-linux-x86_64-}\nVERSION=${VERSION%.tar.gz}\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION\" \"$TMP/prefix/bin\"\ncp \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/$NAME\"\n(cd \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION\" && sha256sum \"$NAME\" > SHA256SUMS)\npython3 \"$(dirname \"$0\")/package-smoke-http.py\" \"$TMP/release\" > \"$TMP/http.log\" 2>&1 &\nSERVER_PID=$!\nfor _ in $(seq 1 50); do\n  PORT=$(sed -n 's/^PORT=//p' \"$TMP/http.log\" | head -n 1)\n  [ -n \"$PORT\" ] && break\n  sleep 0.1\ndone\n[ -n \"${PORT:-}\" ] || { cat \"$TMP/http.log\" >&2; echo \"HTTP fixture did not start\" >&2; exit 1; }\nrun_installer() {\n  NEXUS_VERSION=\"$VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" \\\n    sh \"$INSTALLER\"\n}\nrun_installer\n\"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\" --version | grep -F \"${VERSION#v}\" >/dev/null\nnode - \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/.provenance.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$TMP/prefix\" \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION\" \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\" \"$NAME\" \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/$NAME\" <<'NODE'\nconst assert = require(\"node:assert/strict\");\nconst crypto = require(\"node:crypto\");\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [recordPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archivePath] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(recordPath, \"utf8\"));\nassert.equal(record.formatVersion, 1);\nassert.equal(record.method, \"installer\");\nassert.equal(record.product, \"nexus-code\");\nassert.equal(record.version, version);\nassert.equal(record.prefix, prefix);\nassert.equal(record.installedPath, installedPath);\nassert.equal(record.binPath, binPath);\nassert.equal(record.managed, true);\nassert.equal(record.archive, archive);\nassert.match(record.archiveSha256, /^[a-f0-9]{64}$/);\nassert.equal(record.archiveSha256, crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(archivePath)).digest(\"hex\"));\nNODE\n# A same-version install is reused only when its recorded package digest matches the downloaded archive.\nnode - \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst file = process.argv[2];\nconst record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nrecord.archiveSha256 = \"0\".repeat(64);\nfs.writeFileSync(file, `${JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)}\\n`);\nNODE\nprintf 'stale-package-content\\n' > \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/stale.txt\"\nrun_installer\nif [ -e \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/stale.txt\" ]; then\n  echo \"installer reused a version directory with a different archive digest\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: bad tag v1.2.3/../x is rejected before network\nif NEXUS_VERSION=\"v1.2.3/../x\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/bad-tag.out\" 2>&1; then\n  echo \"bad tag unexpectedly accepted\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\ngrep -F \"version must be a release tag\" \"$TMP/bad-tag.out\" >/dev/null\n\n# ACC-UPG-07: unsupported compatibility metadata schemas fail before installation.\nSCHEMA_VERSION=\"$VERSION-unsupported-schema\"\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$SCHEMA_VERSION\" \"$TMP/schema-unpack\"\ntar -xzf \"$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/schema-unpack\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$SCHEMA_VERSION\" > \"$TMP/schema-unpack/nexus/VERSION\"\nnode - \"$TMP/schema-unpack/nexus\" \"$SCHEMA_VERSION\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst [root, tag] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst version = tag.replace(/^v/, \"\");\nconst pkgPath = path.join(root, \"lib/cli/package.json\");\nconst pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(pkgPath, \"utf8\"));\npkg.version = version;\nfs.writeFileSync(pkgPath, `${JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2)}\\n`);\nconst file = path.join(root, \"compatibility.json\");\nconst metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nmetadata.version = version;\nfor (const component of Object.keys(metadata.components)) metadata.components[component] = version;\nmetadata.platforms[\"linux-x86_64\"].archive = `nexus-linux-x86_64-${tag}.tar.gz`;\nmetadata.schemaVersion = 2;\nfs.writeFileSync(file, `${JSON.stringify(metadata, null, 2)}\\n`);\nNODE\n(cd \"$TMP/schema-unpack/nexus\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs sha256sum > MANIFEST.sha256)\nSCHEMA_ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$SCHEMA_VERSION.tar.gz\"\ntar -C \"$TMP/schema-unpack\" -czf \"$TMP/release/download/$SCHEMA_VERSION/$SCHEMA_ARCHIVE\" nexus\n(cd \"$TMP/release/download/$SCHEMA_VERSION\" && sha256sum \"$SCHEMA_ARCHIVE\" > SHA256SUMS)\nif NEXUS_VERSION=\"$SCHEMA_VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/unsupported-schema.out\" 2>&1; then\n  echo \"installer accepted unsupported compatibility metadata schema\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\ngrep -F \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched\" \"$TMP/unsupported-schema.out\" >/dev/null\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: deleting a dist file then reinstalling repairs it\nDELETED=\"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/lib/cli/dist/index.js\"\nif [ -f \"$DELETED\" ]; then\n  rm \"$DELETED\"\n  [ ! -f \"$DELETED\" ]\n  run_installer\n  [ -f \"$DELETED\" ] || { echo \"manifest repair failed to restore deleted file\" >&2; exit 1; }\nfi\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: NEXUS_FORCE=1 forces re-extraction even when intact\nprintf 'extraneous-file\\n' > \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/extra.txt\"\nNEXUS_FORCE=1 run_installer\n[ ! -f \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/extra.txt\" ] || { echo \"NEXUS_FORCE=1 failed to clean reinstall\" >&2; exit 1; }\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: no-version with only prereleases prints the latest-prerelease hint\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/api\"\nprintf '[{\"tag_name\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.2\",\"prerelease\":true}]\\n' > \"$TMP/release/api/rel\"\nif NEXUS_RELEASES_API=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/api/rel\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/no-stable.out\" 2>&1; then\n  echo \"installer unexpectedly succeeded when latest stable is 404\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\ngrep -F \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is v0.1.0-alpha.2 — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2\" \"$TMP/no-stable.out\" >/dev/null\n\n# Distinct from the version under test, whatever it is, so the upgrade path is always exercised.\nUPGRADE_VERSION=\"$VERSION-upgrade-smoke\"\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION\" \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\ntar -xzf \"$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" > \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus/VERSION\"\nnode - \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst [root, tag] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst version = tag.replace(/^v/, \"\");\nconst packagePath = path.join(root, \"lib/cli/package.json\");\nconst pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(packagePath, \"utf8\"));\npkg.version = version;\nfs.writeFileSync(packagePath, `${JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2)}\\n`);\nconst metadataPath = path.join(root, \"compatibility.json\");\nconst metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\"));\nmetadata.version = version;\nfor (const component of Object.keys(metadata.components)) metadata.components[component] = version;\nmetadata.platforms[\"linux-x86_64\"].archive = `nexus-linux-x86_64-${tag}.tar.gz`;\nfs.writeFileSync(metadataPath, `${JSON.stringify(metadata, null, 2)}\\n`);\nNODE\n(cd \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs sha256sum > MANIFEST.sha256)\nUPGRADE_ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$UPGRADE_VERSION.tar.gz\"\ntar -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\" -czf \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION/$UPGRADE_ARCHIVE\" nexus\n(cd \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION\" && sha256sum \"$UPGRADE_ARCHIVE\" > SHA256SUMS)\nNEXUS_VERSION=\"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\"\n[ \"$(readlink \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\")\" = \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$UPGRADE_VERSION/bin/nexus\" ]\nprintf 'preserve-me\\n' > \"$TMP/prefix/bin/other\"\ngrep -Fx preserve-me \"$TMP/prefix/bin/other\" >/dev/null\ncp \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/SHA256SUMS\" \"$TMP/good-sums\"\nprintf 'bad  %s\\n' \"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\" > \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/SHA256SUMS\"\nLINK_BEFORE=$(readlink \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\")\nif run_installer > \"$TMP/bad-checksum.out\" 2>&1; then echo \"checksum mismatch unexpectedly installed\" >&2; exit 1; fi\n[ \"$(readlink \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\")\" = \"$LINK_BEFORE\" ]\nmv \"$TMP/good-sums\" \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/SHA256SUMS\"\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/conflict/bin\"\nprintf 'unrelated file\\n' > \"$TMP/conflict/bin/nexus\"\nif NEXUS_VERSION=\"$VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/conflict\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/conflict.out\" 2>&1; then echo \"installer overwrote a non-Nexus path\" >&2; exit 1; fi\ngrep -Fx 'unrelated file' \"$TMP/conflict/bin/nexus\" >/dev/null\nprintf 'INSTALLER_SMOKE_PASS\\n'\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n    fail \"could not query GitHub releases API (HTTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"\n  trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM\nfi\n\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nNORMALIZED_VERSION=${VERSION#v}\nURL=\"$BASE/download/$VERSION\"\nTMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-install.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\ncleanup() { rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/SHA256SUMS\" -o \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" || fail \"could not download release checksums.\"\ngrep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\nARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n\nif [ \"${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}\" != \"0\" ] && command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  if gh attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n     gh attestation verify \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n  elif [ \"${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    fail \"provenance attestation verification failed for $ARCHIVE or SHA256SUMS.\"\n  fi\nfi\n\nVERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"\nBIN_DIR=\"$PREFIX/bin\"\nLINK=\"$BIN_DIR/nexus\"\nmkdir -p \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus\" \"$BIN_DIR\"\nif [ -e \"$LINK\" ] && [ ! -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  fail \"$LINK exists and is not a symlink; left it unchanged.\"\nfi\nif [ -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  OLD=$(readlink \"$LINK\")\n  case \"$OLD\" in \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/\"*) ;; *) fail \"$LINK points outside the Nexus installation; left it unchanged.\" ;; esac\nfi\n\nFORCE=${NEXUS_FORCE:-0}\nNEEDS_EXTRACT=1\nif [ -d \"$VERSION_DIR\" ] && [ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" ]; then\n  if [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && \\\n     [ \"$(cat \"$VERSION_DIR/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ]; then\n    if [ -f \"$VERSION_DIR/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n      if (cd \"$VERSION_DIR\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256 2>/dev/null); then\n        NEEDS_EXTRACT=0\n      fi\n      if [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"0\" ]; then\n        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, archiveSha256] = process.argv.slice(2);\ntry {\n  const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n  if (record.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) process.exit(1);\n} catch { process.exit(1); }\nNODE\n        then\n          NEEDS_EXTRACT=1\n        fi\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n\nif [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$TMP/unpack\"\n  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n  PACKAGE=\"$TMP/unpack/nexus\"\n  [ -x \"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\nconst record = {\n  formatVersion: 1,\n  method: \"installer\",\n  product: \"nexus-code\",\n  version,\n  ...(metadata?.revision ? { revision: metadata.revision } : {}),\n  ...(metadata?.builtAt ? { builtAt: metadata.builtAt } : {}),\n  prefix,\n  installedPath,\n  binPath,\n  managed: true,\n  archive,\n  archiveSha256,\n};\nfs.writeFileSync(output, `${JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)}\\n`, { mode: 0o644 });\nfs.chmodSync(output, 0o644);\nNODE\nNEXT=\"$BIN_DIR/.nexus-link.$$\"\nln -s \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" \"$NEXT\"\n# PLAN-07: Supply chain, compliance and release engineering\n\nThis plan implements [SPEC-07](../specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md). It belongs to milestone **M2**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-REL-107 to REQ-REL-114.\n- Decisions: DEC-09, DEC-10.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/generate_sbom.sh`, `scripts/security_gates.sh`, `scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`\n- `cli/test/security_gates.test.ts` (required by ACC-SUP-04; scanner behavior must remain fail-closed)\n- `.github/workflows/{ci,release}.yml`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`\n- `Makefile`\n- new `about.toml`, `about.hbs`, `deny.toml`, `rust-toolchain.toml`\n- `core/Cargo.toml` (`rust-version`)\n- `cli/package.json` (`engines`)\n- `.gitignore`, `cli/dist` (untrack)\n- new `SECURITY.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`\n- `docs/releases/`\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Code locations | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Add `rust-toolchain.toml` pinned to the current stable (1.95.0 at audit time), set `rust-version` in Cargo.toml, and add `\"engines\": {\"node\": \">=22\"}` (DEC-12). | root, `core/Cargo.toml`, `cli/package.json` | — |\n| 2 | Third-party notices: install cargo-about and the npm license checker in CI. Use `about.toml` with an allowlist (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3, ISC, Unicode-3.0, Zlib, MPL-2.0 only if reviewed). Have `package-linux.sh` write `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` and upload it as an asset. | `package-linux.sh:22`; `release.yml` | 1 |\n| 3 | `cargo deny check licenses advisories` in CI. Make `security_gates.sh` fail if `cargo-audit`/`cargo-deny` is missing, and delete `audit_rust_deps.py`. | `security_gates.sh:84-97`; `ci.yml`; `release.yml` | 1 |\n| 4 | Build the SBOM from lockfiles with cyclonedx-npm and cargo-cyclonedx, merge and validate, and attach it to the release. Replace `generate_sbom.sh` and update `make sbom`. | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh`; `Makefile`; `release.yml` | — |\n| 5 | Add provenance with `actions/attest-build-provenance` on the tarball and SHA256SUMS, and upload `install.sh` as a release asset. The installer optionally runs `gh attestation verify` when `gh` is available. | `release.yml:44-48`; `install.sh` | — |\n| 6 | Add a CI matrix for Node 22/24 (tests). Packaging, release and reproducibility builds use Node 22. Pin the cargo-audit version. | `ci.yml` | 1 |\n| 7 | Untrack `cli/dist`: `git rm -r --cached cli/dist`, add it to `.gitignore`, and check that the docs and `make build` cover it. Confirm `harness.sh` still errors helpfully when dist is missing. | `.gitignore`; `harness.sh`; docs | — |\n| 8 | Delete `.gitlab-ci.yml`. Remove tracked `*.pyc` and ignore them. Point `make verify-reproducibility` at `package-linux.sh` run twice with mktemp and cmp. | `.gitlab-ci.yml`; `experiments/context-validation-2026-10-04/harness/__pycache__`; `Makefile:36-45` | — |\n| 9 | Write `SECURITY.md` (private reporting via GitHub Security Advisories, supported versions, 7-day acknowledgement target) and `CHANGELOG.md` (back-filled from docs/releases). Set the release body from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (`body_path`), and fail if that file is missing. | root; `release.yml` | — |\n| 10 | Cross-runner reproducibility: a workflow_dispatch job builds on ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04 with the pinned toolchain and compares the outputs. Run it once for the RC. | new `.github/workflows/repro.yml` | 1 |\n\n## PR slices\n\n| PR | Tasks |\n|---|---|\n| PR-7a | 1, 6, 8 |\n| PR-7b | 2, 3 (notices and gates) |\n| PR-7c | 4, 5 (SBOM and provenance) |\n| PR-7d | 7 (dist untrack, isolated because the diff is large) |\n| PR-7e | 9, 10 |\n\n## Tests\n\n- **ACC-SUP-01.** Add `scripts/check_notices.mjs`. It takes `cargo metadata --locked --format-version 1` (filtered to the dependency closure of the `harness-core` and `nexus-tui` targets) plus `npm ls --omit=dev --all --json`, and checks that every listed package appears in the notices file.\n- **ACC-SUP-02.** Run `cyclonedx validate` in release.\n- **ACC-SUP-03.** Run `gh attestation verify` in a post-release verification job against the published asset.\n- **ACC-SUP-04.** Add a negative test to `security_gates.test.ts`: with `PATH` stripped of cargo-audit, the gate exits non-zero.\n- **ACC-SUP-05 to ACC-SUP-08.** These are observed in CI or the repo state.\n\n## Rollback\n\nWorkflow changes revert per PR. Untracking dist is reversible with `git add -f`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 pass for the RC.\n- The release assets are: tarball, SHA256SUMS, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt, the SBOM, install.sh, and the attestation.\n25\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":46716}},"started_at_ms":1792900926999,"completed_at_ms":1792900926999}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:02:08.054Z","ordinal":323298,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17139-1235-76c2-8fda-a37c984ea9f6","call_id":"call_4cfa4fe51beb418796b8dd0448fdeb01","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\nINSTALLER=${1:?usage: installer-smoke.sh INSTALLER ARCHIVE}\nARCHIVE=${2:?usage: installer-smoke.sh INSTALLER ARCHIVE}\nTMP=$(mktemp -d)\nSERVER_PID=\ncleanup() { [ -z \"$SERVER_PID\" ] || kill \"$SERVER_PID\" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nNAME=$(basename \"$ARCHIVE\")\nVERSION=${NAME#nexus-linux-x86_64-}\nVERSION=${VERSION%.tar.gz}\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION\" \"$TMP/prefix/bin\"\ncp \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/$NAME\"\n(cd \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION\" && sha256sum \"$NAME\" > SHA256SUMS)\npython3 \"$(dirname \"$0\")/package-smoke-http.py\" \"$TMP/release\" > \"$TMP/http.log\" 2>&1 &\nSERVER_PID=$!\nfor _ in $(seq 1 50); do\n  PORT=$(sed -n 's/^PORT=//p' \"$TMP/http.log\" | head -n 1)\n  [ -n \"$PORT\" ] && break\n  sleep 0.1\ndone\n[ -n \"${PORT:-}\" ] || { cat \"$TMP/http.log\" >&2; echo \"HTTP fixture did not start\" >&2; exit 1; }\nrun_installer() {\n  NEXUS_VERSION=\"$VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" \\\n    sh \"$INSTALLER\"\n}\nrun_installer\n\"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\" --version | grep -F \"${VERSION#v}\" >/dev/null\nnode - \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/.provenance.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$TMP/prefix\" \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION\" \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\" \"$NAME\" \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/$NAME\" <<'NODE'\nconst assert = require(\"node:assert/strict\");\nconst crypto = require(\"node:crypto\");\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [recordPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archivePath] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(recordPath, \"utf8\"));\nassert.equal(record.formatVersion, 1);\nassert.equal(record.method, \"installer\");\nassert.equal(record.product, \"nexus-code\");\nassert.equal(record.version, version);\nassert.equal(record.prefix, prefix);\nassert.equal(record.installedPath, installedPath);\nassert.equal(record.binPath, binPath);\nassert.equal(record.managed, true);\nassert.equal(record.archive, archive);\nassert.match(record.archiveSha256, /^[a-f0-9]{64}$/);\nassert.equal(record.archiveSha256, crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(archivePath)).digest(\"hex\"));\nNODE\n# A same-version install is reused only when its recorded package digest matches the downloaded archive.\nnode - \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst file = process.argv[2];\nconst record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nrecord.archiveSha256 = \"0\".repeat(64);\nfs.writeFileSync(file, `${JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)}\\n`);\nNODE\nprintf 'stale-package-content\\n' > \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/stale.txt\"\nrun_installer\nif [ -e \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/stale.txt\" ]; then\n  echo \"installer reused a version directory with a different archive digest\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: bad tag v1.2.3/../x is rejected before network\nif NEXUS_VERSION=\"v1.2.3/../x\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/bad-tag.out\" 2>&1; then\n  echo \"bad tag unexpectedly accepted\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\ngrep -F \"version must be a release tag\" \"$TMP/bad-tag.out\" >/dev/null\n\n# ACC-UPG-07: unsupported compatibility metadata schemas fail before installation.\nSCHEMA_VERSION=\"$VERSION-unsupported-schema\"\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$SCHEMA_VERSION\" \"$TMP/schema-unpack\"\ntar -xzf \"$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/schema-unpack\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$SCHEMA_VERSION\" > \"$TMP/schema-unpack/nexus/VERSION\"\nnode - \"$TMP/schema-unpack/nexus\" \"$SCHEMA_VERSION\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst [root, tag] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst version = tag.replace(/^v/, \"\");\nconst pkgPath = path.join(root, \"lib/cli/package.json\");\nconst pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(pkgPath, \"utf8\"));\npkg.version = version;\nfs.writeFileSync(pkgPath, `${JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2)}\\n`);\nconst file = path.join(root, \"compatibility.json\");\nconst metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nmetadata.version = version;\nfor (const component of Object.keys(metadata.components)) metadata.components[component] = version;\nmetadata.platforms[\"linux-x86_64\"].archive = `nexus-linux-x86_64-${tag}.tar.gz`;\nmetadata.schemaVersion = 2;\nfs.writeFileSync(file, `${JSON.stringify(metadata, null, 2)}\\n`);\nNODE\n(cd \"$TMP/schema-unpack/nexus\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs sha256sum > MANIFEST.sha256)\nSCHEMA_ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$SCHEMA_VERSION.tar.gz\"\ntar -C \"$TMP/schema-unpack\" -czf \"$TMP/release/download/$SCHEMA_VERSION/$SCHEMA_ARCHIVE\" nexus\n(cd \"$TMP/release/download/$SCHEMA_VERSION\" && sha256sum \"$SCHEMA_ARCHIVE\" > SHA256SUMS)\nif NEXUS_VERSION=\"$SCHEMA_VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/unsupported-schema.out\" 2>&1; then\n  echo \"installer accepted unsupported compatibility metadata schema\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\ngrep -F \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched\" \"$TMP/unsupported-schema.out\" >/dev/null\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: deleting a dist file then reinstalling repairs it\nDELETED=\"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/lib/cli/dist/index.js\"\nif [ -f \"$DELETED\" ]; then\n  rm \"$DELETED\"\n  [ ! -f \"$DELETED\" ]\n  run_installer\n  [ -f \"$DELETED\" ] || { echo \"manifest repair failed to restore deleted file\" >&2; exit 1; }\nfi\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: NEXUS_FORCE=1 forces re-extraction even when intact\nprintf 'extraneous-file\\n' > \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/extra.txt\"\nNEXUS_FORCE=1 run_installer\n[ ! -f \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$VERSION/extra.txt\" ] || { echo \"NEXUS_FORCE=1 failed to clean reinstall\" >&2; exit 1; }\n\n# ACC-PKG-05: no-version with only prereleases prints the latest-prerelease hint\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/api\"\nprintf '[{\"tag_name\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.2\",\"prerelease\":true}]\\n' > \"$TMP/release/api/rel\"\nif NEXUS_RELEASES_API=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/api/rel\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/no-stable.out\" 2>&1; then\n  echo \"installer unexpectedly succeeded when latest stable is 404\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\ngrep -F \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is v0.1.0-alpha.2 — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2\" \"$TMP/no-stable.out\" >/dev/null\n\n# Distinct from the version under test, whatever it is, so the upgrade path is always exercised.\nUPGRADE_VERSION=\"$VERSION-upgrade-smoke\"\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION\" \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\ntar -xzf \"$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" > \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus/VERSION\"\nnode - \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst [root, tag] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst version = tag.replace(/^v/, \"\");\nconst packagePath = path.join(root, \"lib/cli/package.json\");\nconst pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(packagePath, \"utf8\"));\npkg.version = version;\nfs.writeFileSync(packagePath, `${JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2)}\\n`);\nconst metadataPath = path.join(root, \"compatibility.json\");\nconst metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\"));\nmetadata.version = version;\nfor (const component of Object.keys(metadata.components)) metadata.components[component] = version;\nmetadata.platforms[\"linux-x86_64\"].archive = `nexus-linux-x86_64-${tag}.tar.gz`;\nfs.writeFileSync(metadataPath, `${JSON.stringify(metadata, null, 2)}\\n`);\nNODE\n(cd \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs sha256sum > MANIFEST.sha256)\nUPGRADE_ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$UPGRADE_VERSION.tar.gz\"\ntar -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\" -czf \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION/$UPGRADE_ARCHIVE\" nexus\n(cd \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION\" && sha256sum \"$UPGRADE_ARCHIVE\" > SHA256SUMS)\nNEXUS_VERSION=\"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/prefix\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\"\n[ \"$(readlink \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\")\" = \"$TMP/prefix/lib/nexus/$UPGRADE_VERSION/bin/nexus\" ]\nprintf 'preserve-me\\n' > \"$TMP/prefix/bin/other\"\ngrep -Fx preserve-me \"$TMP/prefix/bin/other\" >/dev/null\ncp \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/SHA256SUMS\" \"$TMP/good-sums\"\nprintf 'bad  %s\\n' \"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\" > \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/SHA256SUMS\"\nLINK_BEFORE=$(readlink \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\")\nif run_installer > \"$TMP/bad-checksum.out\" 2>&1; then echo \"checksum mismatch unexpectedly installed\" >&2; exit 1; fi\n[ \"$(readlink \"$TMP/prefix/bin/nexus\")\" = \"$LINK_BEFORE\" ]\nmv \"$TMP/good-sums\" \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/SHA256SUMS\"\nmkdir -p \"$TMP/conflict/bin\"\nprintf 'unrelated file\\n' > \"$TMP/conflict/bin/nexus\"\nif NEXUS_VERSION=\"$VERSION\" NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$TMP/conflict\" NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\" sh \"$INSTALLER\" > \"$TMP/conflict.out\" 2>&1; then echo \"installer overwrote a non-Nexus path\" >&2; exit 1; fi\ngrep -Fx 'unrelated file' \"$TMP/conflict/bin/nexus\" >/dev/null\nprintf 'INSTALLER_SMOKE_PASS\\n'\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n    fail \"could not query GitHub releases API (HTTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"\n  trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM\nfi\n\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nNORMALIZED_VERSION=${VERSION#v}\nURL=\"$BASE/download/$VERSION\"\nTMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-install.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\ncleanup() { rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/SHA256SUMS\" -o \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" || fail \"could not download release checksums.\"\ngrep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\nARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n\nif [ \"${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}\" != \"0\" ] && command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  if gh attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n     gh attestation verify \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n  elif [ \"${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    fail \"provenance attestation verification failed for $ARCHIVE or SHA256SUMS.\"\n  fi\nfi\n\nVERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"\nBIN_DIR=\"$PREFIX/bin\"\nLINK=\"$BIN_DIR/nexus\"\nmkdir -p \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus\" \"$BIN_DIR\"\nif [ -e \"$LINK\" ] && [ ! -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  fail \"$LINK exists and is not a symlink; left it unchanged.\"\nfi\nif [ -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  OLD=$(readlink \"$LINK\")\n  case \"$OLD\" in \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/\"*) ;; *) fail \"$LINK points outside the Nexus installation; left it unchanged.\" ;; esac\nfi\n\nFORCE=${NEXUS_FORCE:-0}\nNEEDS_EXTRACT=1\nif [ -d \"$VERSION_DIR\" ] && [ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" ]; then\n  if [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && \\\n     [ \"$(cat \"$VERSION_DIR/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ]; then\n    if [ -f \"$VERSION_DIR/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n      if (cd \"$VERSION_DIR\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256 2>/dev/null); then\n        NEEDS_EXTRACT=0\n      fi\n      if [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"0\" ]; then\n        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, archiveSha256] = process.argv.slice(2);\ntry {\n  const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n  if (record.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) process.exit(1);\n} catch { process.exit(1); }\nNODE\n        then\n          NEEDS_EXTRACT=1\n        fi\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n\nif [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$TMP/unpack\"\n  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n  PACKAGE=\"$TMP/unpack/nexus\"\n  [ -x \"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\nconst record = {\n  formatVersion: 1,\n  method: \"installer\",\n  product: \"nexus-code\",\n  version,\n  ...(metadata?.revision ? { revision: metadata.revision } : {}),\n  ...(metadata?.builtAt ? { builtAt: metadata.builtAt } : {}),\n  prefix,\n  installedPath,\n  binPath,\n  managed: true,\n  archive,\n  archiveSha256,\n};\nfs.writeFileSync(output, `${JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)}\\n`, { mode: 0o644 });\nfs.chmodSync(output, 0o644);\nNODE\nNEXT=\"$BIN_DIR/.nexus-link.$$\"\nln -s \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" \"$NEXT\"\n# PLAN-07: Supply chain, compliance and release engineering\n\nThis plan implements [SPEC-07](../specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md). It belongs to milestone **M2**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-REL-107 to REQ-REL-114.\n- Decisions: DEC-09, DEC-10.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/generate_sbom.sh`, `scripts/security_gates.sh`, `scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`\n- `cli/test/security_gates.test.ts` (required by ACC-SUP-04; scanner behavior must remain fail-closed)\n- `.github/workflows/{ci,release}.yml`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`\n- `Makefile`\n- new `about.toml`, `about.hbs`, `deny.toml`, `rust-toolchain.toml`\n- `core/Cargo.toml` (`rust-version`)\n- `cli/package.json` (`engines`)\n- `.gitignore`, `cli/dist` (untrack)\n- new `SECURITY.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`\n- `docs/releases/`\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Code locations | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Add `rust-toolchain.toml` pinned to the current stable (1.95.0 at audit time), set `rust-version` in Cargo.toml, and add `\"engines\": {\"node\": \">=22\"}` (DEC-12). | root, `core/Cargo.toml`, `cli/package.json` | — |\n| 2 | Third-party notices: install cargo-about and the npm license checker in CI. Use `about.toml` with an allowlist (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3, ISC, Unicode-3.0, Zlib, MPL-2.0 only if reviewed). Have `package-linux.sh` write `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` and upload it as an asset. | `package-linux.sh:22`; `release.yml` | 1 |\n| 3 | `cargo deny check licenses advisories` in CI. Make `security_gates.sh` fail if `cargo-audit`/`cargo-deny` is missing, and delete `audit_rust_deps.py`. | `security_gates.sh:84-97`; `ci.yml`; `release.yml` | 1 |\n| 4 | Build the SBOM from lockfiles with cyclonedx-npm and cargo-cyclonedx, merge and validate, and attach it to the release. Replace `generate_sbom.sh` and update `make sbom`. | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh`; `Makefile`; `release.yml` | — |\n| 5 | Add provenance with `actions/attest-build-provenance` on the tarball and SHA256SUMS, and upload `install.sh` as a release asset. The installer optionally runs `gh attestation verify` when `gh` is available. | `release.yml:44-48`; `install.sh` | — |\n| 6 | Add a CI matrix for Node 22/24 (tests). Packaging, release and reproducibility builds use Node 22. Pin the cargo-audit version. | `ci.yml` | 1 |\n| 7 | Untrack `cli/dist`: `git rm -r --cached cli/dist`, add it to `.gitignore`, and check that the docs and `make build` cover it. Confirm `harness.sh` still errors helpfully when dist is missing. | `.gitignore`; `harness.sh`; docs | — |\n| 8 | Delete `.gitlab-ci.yml`. Remove tracked `*.pyc` and ignore them. Point `make verify-reproducibility` at `package-linux.sh` run twice with mktemp and cmp. | `.gitlab-ci.yml`; `experiments/context-validation-2026-10-04/harness/__pycache__`; `Makefile:36-45` | — |\n| 9 | Write `SECURITY.md` (private reporting via GitHub Security Advisories, supported versions, 7-day acknowledgement target) and `CHANGELOG.md` (back-filled from docs/releases). Set the release body from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (`body_path`), and fail if that file is missing. | root; `release.yml` | — |\n| 10 | Cross-runner reproducibility: a workflow_dispatch job builds on ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04 with the pinned toolchain and compares the outputs. Run it once for the RC. | new `.github/workflows/repro.yml` | 1 |\n\n## PR slices\n\n| PR | Tasks |\n|---|---|\n| PR-7a | 1, 6, 8 |\n| PR-7b | 2, 3 (notices and gates) |\n| PR-7c | 4, 5 (SBOM and provenance) |\n| PR-7d | 7 (dist untrack, isolated because the diff is large) |\n| PR-7e | 9, 10 |\n\n## Tests\n\n- **ACC-SUP-01.** Add `scripts/check_notices.mjs`. It takes `cargo metadata --locked --format-version 1` (filtered to the dependency closure of the `harness-core` and `nexus-tui` targets) plus `npm ls --omit=dev --all --json`, and checks that every listed package appears in the notices file.\n- **ACC-SUP-02.** Run `cyclonedx validate` in release.\n- **ACC-SUP-03.** Run `gh attestation verify` in a post-release verification job against the published asset.\n- **ACC-SUP-04.** Add a negative test to `security_gates.test.ts`: with `PATH` stripped of cargo-audit, the gate exits non-zero.\n- **ACC-SUP-05 to ACC-SUP-08.** These are observed in CI or the repo state.\n\n## Rollback\n\nWorkflow changes revert per PR. Untracking dist is reversible with `git add -f`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 pass for the RC.\n- The release assets are: tarball, SHA256SUMS, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt, the SBOM, install.sh, and the attestation.\n25\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17136-12b9-7661-904c-f2b43120b5c8","create_time":1792900928.0538018}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
