{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:03:28.499Z","ordinal":323367,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1713a-4c73-7951-b15a-55a03ed5dc3e","call_id":"call_a5d0f647d95844f791fc8fee58b12a14","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The missing trusted-`gh` path is covered deterministically: the test injects an empty trusted-path list, places a success-returning shim in `PATH`, and confirms the shim is not executed and rejection happens before journal or staging creation. The separate test covers a trusted `gh` that fails attestation. The documented behavior change for `gh` outside the fixed system paths presents no additional blocker.\\n\\nBase: `19b30a4`  \\nHead: `94ad942bd492ee6586bf73a595bbb642f8f73757`  \\nDiff SHA-256: `f40941e0ead3aba1babb4dbc920e03ef5bc09d0fffd5b7825435636eea2b94e8`\\n\\nRead-only review; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact HEAD `f07b73bc4240346b4025d96f08a915143d1fd31d`, base `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca`.\\n\\nThe diff changes exactly the six previously reviewed files. It aligns with REQ-PER-105’s requirement that telemetry not be committable by default, and the linked and nested workspace paths fail closed when Git metadata cannot be resolved. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests.\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `55b0230bcdb125cecc263c83afbb83dc9bc54cab24ca557209a92f57d503de7a`\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17136-12b9-7661-904c-f2b43120b5c8","create_time":1792901008.4996161}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
