{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:06:10.818Z","ordinal":323489,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17136-12b9-7661-904c-f2b43120b5c8","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add80314d5481a0947887478b9b3b96","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Approval default:** review. Current `origin/main` already defaults to review and keeps folder trust separate from permission settings.\n\n**Installer fix:** In an isolated worktree based on `a3e1b65`, I changed the installer to fail before downloading when attestation is required but no trusted `gh` exists, and to invoke only `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh`. The new smoke fixture checks both the missing-tool failure and resistance to a successful fake `gh` earlier in `PATH`. An independent review accepted the change.\n\nShell syntax and `git diff --check` pass. **Behavioral tests have not run:** the existing `SUITE` claim is held by KimiCode, and its full test run is still active in another worktree. I’m keeping this slice uncommitted until that run reaches a safe handoff and the installer smoke test can run.\n\nCurrent main CI run `40160250252` remains in progress on `a3e1b65`; CodeQL run `40160250231` succeeded. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; no accepted RC or completed release is claimed."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792901169330,"completed_at_ms":1792901170818}}
