from the user's request.\n\n## My request:\nThis is what I meant to send that is still missing in Nexus.. on startup\n","turn_id":"01a16c58-2eac-7613-82d0-9755c16da08a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a16f94-56bb-76a1-90d9-32341d35c642","order":15556,"revision":"retained_01a16f94-56bb-76a1-90d9-325c8fb8f4db","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_253db302107c48d6b21342c828373634\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"Should folder trust affect tool approvals?\",\"answer\":\"No, separate trust from approvals; use permission settings\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n","turn_id":"01a16f93-d17f-7222-b62b-744f32aec213"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a16f9a-5e10-7910-a660-77abaa050652","order":15565,"revision":"retained_01a16f9a-5e10-7910-a660-77c46624541c","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_0f87c48f4f294a46868cb58142112d55\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"Default approval mode\",\"answer\":\"Default to review\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n","turn_id":"01a16f93-d17f-7222-b62b-744f32aec213"}],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a17164-b13c-7da1-a454-85a54de1f1a3","window_number":344}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:49:46.878Z","ordinal":324377,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/home/mike/nexus-code","text":"# Project Guidelines & Agent Instructions\n\n## Commands\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\n\n## Code Conventions\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\n\n## v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\n- The v1.0.0 plan is in `docs/v1.0.0/` (start at `docs/v1.0.0/README.md`). Implement one claimed PR slice at a time, within the safe change boundary in its plan.\n- When more than one agent may be working, follow `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`. In short:\n  - Claim the slice atomically under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n  - Use one worktree and branch per slice; never edit `~/nexus-code` directly.\n  - Isolate `HOME` for every test or probe run.\n  - Claim hot files before editing them.\n  - Take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run.\n  - Never use `pkill -f`.\n  - Check `git log` for foreign commits before every commit.\n  - Leave push, tag and publish to the owner.\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"base_instructions":"cbcd6e6ca31b3667c3a6fb7fd063b0fec26e3174","collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6-luna","instructions":"afcdf1ff905fb4e61ff4d6d89af089dbda3d5e4e"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-10-25","timezone":"Etc/UTC","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/home/mike/nexus-code</root><root>/home/mike/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/18/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></f