{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:50:25.851Z","ordinal":324435,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1715b-2cc0-7ec0-b38e-9954515e542c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add8a91183481a09355e0ecccc18e49","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The correction is sound: the smoke script’s test-only opt-out was leaking into the strict negative case. The follow-up commit removes that variable for that invocation, restoring the installer’s default fail-closed mode while keeping the PATH shim test. Independent source review accepted it. I’m updating PR #211 to this exact candidate so CI reruns against the fix."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792903825121,"completed_at_ms":1792903825851}}
