{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:50:48.434Z","ordinal":324460,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17165-a1f2-7112-a0fc-8bbe5bad3baf","call_id":"call_d338821903aa4c0f89efd114c1ddd7c1","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** `env -u NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION` removes the smoke script’s exported opt-out for the missing-`gh` case, so the installer uses its default required mode. The `PATH` shim remains present to verify it is ignored. Other fixture calls set their intended attestation mode explicitly.\\n\\nRead-only review; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact HEAD `f07b73bc4240346b4025d96f08a915143d1fd31d`, base `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca`.\\n\\nThe diff changes exactly the six previously reviewed files. It aligns with REQ-PER-105’s requirement that telemetry not be committable by default, and the linked and nested workspace paths fail closed when Git metadata cannot be resolved. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests.\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `55b0230bcdb125cecc263c83afbb83dc9bc54cab24ca557209a92f57d503de7a`\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1715b-2cc0-7ec0-b38e-9954515e542c","create_time":1792903848.4344761}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
