{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:51:53.294Z","ordinal":324512,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17166-29c6-7782-8ecb-9326d4f90716","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-03cec6e4-79c3-414b-91ef-ff37e50d065d","process_id":"92492","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'trust this folder|folder trust|trusted folder|workspace trust|trust.*approval|approval mode|permission mode' cli/src cli/test docs | head -100; gh pr list --state open --limit 30 --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName,headRefOid,updatedAt,url"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan-07-installer-attestation-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'trust this folder|folder trust|trusted folder|workspace trust|trust.*approval|approval mode|permission mode' cli/src cli/test docs | head -100; gh pr list --state open --limit 30 --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName,headRefOid,updatedAt,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"cli/src/sidecar.ts:1060:    .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:498:| **EXT-003** | In accordance with Operator Decision 2, interactive confirmation MUST NOT be mandated as the universal extension trust mechanism. Valid extension authorization policies MUST include: preconfigured user configuration, explicit allowlists, operator trust prompts, bounded isolation, and deliberately broad trust. | A developer who preconfigures trust for a repository plugin in `~/.config/nexus/config.json` MUST NOT be interrupted by interactive approval prompts. |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:97:| EXT-003 | 15: MCP, Plugin & Extension | In accordance with Operator Decision 2, interactive confirmation MUST NOT be mandated as the universal extension trust mechanism. Valid extension authorization policies MUST include: preconfigured user configuration, explicit allowlists, operator trust prompts, bounded isolation, and deliberately broad trust. | A developer who preconfigures trust for a repository plugin in `~/.config/nexus/config.json` MUST NOT be interrupted by interactive approval prompts. | Phase 2 §19 | `cli/src/plugins.ts, cli/src/mcp.ts`; cli/test/harness.test.ts | SATISFIED_BY_INTEGRATED_SYSTEM | None | Satisfied |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:5:This release delivers the complete Nexus Code client architecture with comprehensive boundary hardening, process ownership, workspace trust enforcement, and egress protection.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:55:### Workspace Trust: Skills & Knowledge (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114)\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:56:- Workspace trust now gates workspace skill directories (`skills/`, `.nexus/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`) and workspace knowledge (`.nexus/knowledge.json`).\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:78:### Approval Mode Independent of Folder Trust (amended DEC-01)\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:79:- **Problem addressed (SEC-01):** Folder trust and tool authority were coupled, making workspace trust silently change the approval posture.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:80:- **New behavior:** Tool permission mode is independent of workspace trust and defaults to `review` in every folder. `--mode auto` selects autonomous writes and command execution while keeping first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass all approval prompts, including egress.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:82:- **Trusting your own repository:** Run `nexus trust .` (or `nexus trust <path>`) to load project instructions and workspace integrations. Trust does not change tool permission mode.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:84:  - `--approve` / `--mode review`: Enforces review posture regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:119:- In review mode, the first verifier execution is gated by an approval prompt displaying the exact command and the resolved test script body (extracted from `package.json` `scripts.test`, Makefile recipes, or `Cargo.toml`). Folder trust does not authorize verifier execution.\ncli/src/config.ts:253:    // Folder trust controls project instructions and integrations, not tool authority.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:261:- **Minimum Requirements-Level Correction:** Reframe `SUBP-002` and `CRED-002` to clarify that scrubbing ambient host credentials is the mandatory default for untrusted or bounded domains, but that execution domain policy MAY explicitly authorize subprocesses to inherit or access designated environment credentials without requiring per-invocation micro-approvals.\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:60:3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress. Folder trust only controls project instructions and workspace integrations. Input safety is strictly enforced across surfaces (REQ-SEC-103): lone Enter defaults to No, a 400ms grace period discards typed-ahead input, and approve-all requires explicit confirmation (`all` in REPL, confirmation Enter in TUI). *Limit:* in explicit `auto` posture, commands and file writes execute autonomously regardless of folder trust.\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:61:4. **Workspace trust.** Trust is managed via `nexus trust` and stored in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json`; interactive startup asks for trust before loading project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`). In untrusted workspaces, project instructions, workspace MCP configs, plugins, skills, and `.nexus/knowledge.json` are not loaded (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114). The operator may continue without trust under the existing permission mode or exit. *Limit:* configuration in the operator's home directory (`~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/`) is always trusted.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:20:- On each interactive launch from an untrusted folder, Nexus asks whether to trust the folder, continue without trust, or exit. Trust loads project instructions when present and enables trusted workspace integrations. Folder trust is separate from tool permissions: an explicit mode controls approvals, and an unset mode defaults to `review` in every folder. Non-interactive launches do not prompt and do not load project instructions unless the folder is already trusted.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:22:### Execution Postures & Approval Modes\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:24:Nexus Code resolves tool approval posture from permission settings, independently of workspace trust (amended DEC-01):\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:25:- **Default:** `review` posture, requiring human confirmation before executing shell commands, file modifications, network requests, or verifier test runs, regardless of folder trust.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:26:- **Auto:** Select with `--mode auto`. Writes and commands run without approval; network egress still asks on first use of each origin. This is independent of folder trust.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:31:- **Review mode (human-in-the-loop):** Run `nexus --approve` (or `nexus --mode review`) to require explicit approval for all actions regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:367:- **Workspace Trust & Context Provenance (REQ-SEC-113, CTX-001)**: An opened workspace is data until explicitly trusted by the operator. Workspace trust covers:\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:390:- **Verifier Execution Gating (REQ-SEC-119)**: Automated test runs and verifiers (`run_tests`, `/test`, completion oracle) are classified as `exec` capabilities subject to the configured approval mode. In review mode, the first verifier execution prompts for approval, displaying the exact test command and resolved script body from `package.json`, `Makefile`, or `Cargo.toml`; folder trust alone does not authorize it.\ncli/src/core/capabilities.ts:12: * `egress`; `context_inject` is gated by workspace trust instead; `read_workspace`, `delegate` (the child's own calls are\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:161:  test(\"exec approval follows permission mode regardless of workspace trust\", () => {\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:164:    // Auto mode follows the operator's permission setting in both trusted and untrusted folders.\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:182:  test(\"workspace trust does not change context-injection approval; untrusted sources remain gated\", () => {\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:5: * - Explicit auto mode runs without asking regardless of workspace trust.\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:46:  test(\"folder trust alone keeps an unset permission mode in review\", () => {\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:85:  test(\"trusted and untrusted repos in review mode prompt for verifier and script body, write sentinel only after approval, and cache session decision\", async () => {\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:226:      assert.equal(promptLog.length, 0, \"explicit auto mode should not depend on workspace trust\");\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:9:| [DEC-01](#dec-01-default-execution-posture) | Default execution posture | Review by default; permission mode is independent of folder trust | No (resolved) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:40:**Rationale.** Folder trust protects project instructions and workspace integrations from being loaded before the operator approves those sources. Tool authority is governed by the operator's permission settings and must not change when a folder is trusted. A configured `auto` mode remains the operator's choice; when no permission mode is configured, Nexus defaults to `review`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:42:**Amendment (2026-10-24, operator direction).** This supersedes the original trust-derived mode and approval behavior. Trust affects project instruction and integration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\ncli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py:58:            session.wait_text(\"Trust this folder?\", timeout=20)\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:118:- **Workspace trust before executing project configuration** (Claude Code and Codex document trust prompts for\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:259:| B2 | **Workspace trust**: never import workspace plugins or start workspace MCP servers until the operator trusts that workspace (per-path trust record); `--read-only` disables both; MCP children get an environment allowlist | T-03 | clone a repo containing `plugins/x.mjs` and `.mcp.json` that touch a sentinel → no sentinel without explicit trust, in every mode |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:296:| 1 | B1 execution authority + B2 workspace trust (+ R4 listing confinement, T13 dry-run) | 0 | capability × mode × context matrix complete and enforced; adversarial suite blocked; no regression in existing suites |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:5:| Status | Updated by [DEC-01](../DECISIONS.md#dec-01-default-execution-posture): permission mode is independent of folder trust; unset mode defaults to review. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:14:The observations in this section describe the original audit baseline and are not assertions about the amended DEC-01 behavior. In particular, the reported trust-derived `auto` default was the defect identified by SEC-01; DEC-01 was amended on 2026-10-24 to make permission mode independent of folder trust and default to `review`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:63:8. **REQ-SEC-119.** Verifier executions that Nexus initiates itself (change baseline, completion oracle, independence copy, `run_tests`, `/test`) are `exec`-class actions. They are subject to the same permission mode as `run_command`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:65:   - An explicitly configured auto posture runs without asking regardless of workspace trust; folder trust controls project instructions and integrations only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:98:| `exec` | run_command, run_tests, LSP server spawn, plugin and MCP tool calls | refused, except the confined read-only allowlist | ask | allowed under explicit auto mode regardless of folder trust |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:101:| `context_inject` | activate_skill, manage_knowledge write | refused (write) | ask when the source is untrusted (see SPEC-03) | ask only when the source is untrusted; folder trust does not decide |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:107:In `cli/src/agent.ts:3945-3947`, replace `onConfirm && isMutating` with `policy.requiresDecision(cap.effect, context)`. `context` contains the permission mode, source trust, sandbox state and per-origin egress memory. Workspace trust is reported separately and never selects authority.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:142:- Persisted sessions do **not** persist an approval mode. Resume uses the current launch posture. This avoids resurrecting authority, per PERS-004.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:146:- Unset approval mode defaults to review regardless of folder trust. Release notes and startup messaging must distinguish permission mode from folder trust. Use `--mode auto` for automatic writes and commands with per-origin egress approval; use `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` or `--yes` for full access.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:183:- **DEC-01** is resolved as amended: review by default; explicit permission mode controls approvals independently of folder trust. Nothing in this spec is blocked by the decision.\ncli/test/config.test.ts:10:  test(\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\", () => {\ncli/test/startup_unreachable_e2e.test.ts:65:prompted = read_until(\"Trust this folder?\", 10.0)\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:65:    assert.match(rendered, /Trust this folder\\?/);\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:73:    assert.match(rendered, /Folder trust doesn't change approvals/);\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:112:test(\"trust choice persists workspace trust and returns trusted\", async () => {\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:254:test(\"AutonomousAgent omits project rules until workspace trust is explicit\", () => {\ncli/src/core/approval_policy.ts:11:  /** Workspace trust is reported separately; it never selects or widens tool authority. */\ncli/src/core/approval_policy.ts:23:   * Permission mode controls tool approvals independently of workspace trust:\ncli/src/core/approval_policy.ts:26:   * - Untrusted context sources remain distinguishable from workspace trust.\ncli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:190:    assert.equal(result.approvalPrompt, mode !== \"auto\", \"approval mode is independent of folder trust\");\ncli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:201:ptyTest(\"ACC-SAFE-01: launcher permission mode is independent of folder trust\", { timeout: 900_000 }, async () => {\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY `test:cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts::\"ACC-SAFE-01: launcher permission mode is independent of folder trust\"`; evidence `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md` | tested | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:122:| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts`; `workspace_commands.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"trusted and untrusted repos in review mode prompt for verifier and script body, write sentinel only after approval, and cache session decision\"`; `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"denied verifier does not execute verifier and sentinel is not written\"`; `test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"run_tests keeps repository test side effects inside worktree authority and honors read-only, dry-run, and required sandbox\"`; PTY `test:cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts::\"ACC-SAFE-09/10: /test approval, trust independence, sandbox and cancellation\"`; evidence `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md` | tested | ACC-SAFE-09, ACC-SAFE-10 | **B** | VER-01, VER-14 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:37:- **Trust boundary.** Verifier commands run repository-defined code: Makefile recipes, package.json scripts, build.rs, conftest.py. They run through `bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\")` directly, so the dispatch approval gate (agent.ts:3947) never sees them. The sandbox applies only if `--sandbox`/read-only is set (tools.ts:755). No workspace-trust check applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:52:| VER-01 | S2 | Any session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:134:| R-VER-1 | Repo-defined verifier commands (discovered) run only in a trusted workspace or after one approval that shows the command and script body. They run sandboxed when a sandbox is available. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted temp repo with `\"test\":\"touch /tmp/pwn\"` plus an edit request: no file created without a prompt, in both default and --approve modes. |\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:40:describe(\"workspace trust\", () => {\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:211:   * Gated by workspace trust: returns empty string if workspace is untrusted (REQ-SEC-113).\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:238:   * Gated by workspace trust and read-only mode.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:68:- Remediation: load workspace-scoped plugins/MCP only after an explicit, persisted per-workspace trust decision (hash of the config/plugin\ncli/src/startup_trust.ts:106:      `Run 'nexus trust .' to load them. Tool approvals follow your permission settings.\\n`,\ncli/src/startup_trust.ts:132:        \"Trust this folder?\",\ncli/src/startup_trust.ts:142:        \"Folder trust doesn't change approvals.\",\ncli/src/index.ts:288:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:353:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:385:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:33: * In --read-only mode, workspace trust never authorizes executing project plugins/MCP.\ncli/src/skills.ts:64:    // Project workspace locations (gated by workspace trust)\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:16:| **1. Objective completion** | `/plan` toggles plan mode; `/goal` sets a persistent objective whose text \"becomes both the first prompt and the completion criteria\"; docs tell users to include verification (tests/measurements) in the goal; goal keeps the existing sandbox/approval policy and pauses for decisions [CX-LONG][CX-SLASH]. `/review` reviews uncommitted changes or vs a base branch [CX-SLASH]. | `plan` permission mode blocks edits until the user approves a plan (`ExitPlanMode` needs approval) [CC-PERM][CC-TOOLS]; task list tools `TaskCreate/TaskList/TaskUpdate` (TodoWrite legacy) [CC-TOOLS]; goals carry over on resume [CC-SESS]; Stop/SubagentStop `prompt` hooks judge whether to stop (2.1.294 fix to reduce early stops) [CC-CHG]. | Plan agent (edits and bash default to `ask`) vs Build agent, toggled with Tab [OC-INTRO][OC-AGENTS]. No todo tool on the tools page [OC-TOOLS]. | `GOOSE_MAX_TURNS` (default 1000) caps consecutive actions, then asks to continue [GS-CTX]. Recipes/subrecipes for repeatable tasks [GS-HOME]. | `--test-cmd` + `--auto-test` run tests after each edit; lint runs by default; on non-zero exit aider \"will try and fix any errors\" [AI-LINT]. Architect mode = planner model + editor model [AI-EDIT]. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:19:| **4. Operator control / trust** | Sandbox modes `read-only` / `workspace-write` / `danger-full-access`; macOS Seatbelt, Linux bubblewrap (PATH or bundled helper needing unprivileged userns), WSL2 Linux sandbox, native Windows sandbox; `writable_roots`; `sandbox_workspace_write.network_access`; approvals `on-request`/`never`/granular (`untrusted` retired, `on-failure` deprecated); `approvals_reviewer = auto_review` delegates eligible prompts to a reviewer agent without widening the sandbox [CX-SBX][CX-CFG]. `shell_environment_policy` (inherit all/core/none; KEY/SECRET/TOKEN name exclusion when `ignore_default_excludes=false`); project-local config cannot set provider/notify/otel; command + MCP-tool hooks [CX-CFG]. | Modes default(Manual)/acceptEdits/plan/auto(classifier)/dontAsk/bypassPermissions; auto is the starting mode since v2.1.283; deny rules apply in every mode; critical-path `rm` and protected paths never auto-approved; `blockReadsOutsideWorkingDirectories` [CC-PERM]. Bash sandbox: Seatbelt (macOS), bubblewrap+socat+seccomp (Linux/WSL2), network through local proxy with domain allowlist, built on open-source `@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime`; file tools, MCP and hooks run outside it; native Windows unsandboxed; unsandboxed retry needs approval [CC-SBX]. Hooks incl. `onFailure:\"block\"` (2.1.295) [CC-CHG]; managed settings, `allowedProviders` pin [CC-GW]. | Per-tool `allow/ask/deny` with glob patterns, last match wins; `external_directory` and `doom_loop` (3 identical calls) default `ask`; `*.env` reads denied by default; `--auto` keeps explicit denies [OC-PERM]. No OS sandbox documented [OC-PERM]. | Modes auto (default per docs) / approve / smart_approve (risk-based) / chat; per-tool Always/Ask/Never in approve & smart modes; first-run mode prompt (v1.54.0); adversary-mode reviewer; prompt-injection detection mentioned [GS-PERM][GS-REL][GS-HOME]. OS sandbox not verified. | No approval/sandbox model documented on pages read; safety relies on git commits + `/undo` [AI-GIT]. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:107:| CC-PERM | https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permission-modes.md | Choose a permission mode |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:131:| GS-PERM | https://goose-docs.ai/docs/guides/goose-permissions (via official-domain search result; direct fetch returned empty) | goose Permission Modes |\ncli/src/repl.ts:1676:            // Verifier gating follows the permission mode; trust only controls workspace integrations.\ncli/src/types.ts:61:  approvalMode?: \"auto\" | \"review\" | \"read-only\"; // Permission posture: auto, review, or read-only (DEC-01, independent of folder trust)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:112:| AGT-R8 | No implicit standing rules from prompts; no workspace writes in read-only mode; workspace-supplied knowledge gated by workspace trust. | safety (AGT-10) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Read-only run leaves no `.nexus/`; prompt \"never run tests\" does not appear in next session's system prompt. |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:23:**Acceptance evidence:** negative tests proving untrusted workspace configuration cannot silently redirect context; positive tests for explicit operator approval; end-to-end audit/receipt naming destination/provider/model and data class; enforceable spend/request limits.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:136:| R-SEC-5 | Workspace skills are subject to workspace trust. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted fixture repo with `skills/x/SKILL.md` does not appear in the system prompt or `/skills` without trust. |\ncli/src/agent.ts:1275:    // Workspace trust controls project instructions and integrations; permission settings alone select approval posture.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:3:**DEC-01 amendment (2026-10-24):** This plan's original trust-derived default is superseded. Folder trust controls project-instruction and workspace-integration loading only. Tool approval posture follows the operator's permission settings; an unset mode defaults to `review` in both trusted and untrusted workspaces.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:41:| 2 | Add `ApprovalPolicy`: `requiresDecision(effect, {mode, trusted, sandbox, egressOrigins})`. Test the full matrix and verify that folder trust does not change decisions for a fixed mode. | new `cli/src/core/approval_policy.ts` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:43:| 4 | Replace the `autoApprove` booleans with `HarnessConfig.approvalMode`. Explicit flags and permission settings select the mode; if none is configured, default to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` retains per-origin egress approval; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access. | `config.ts:107`, `types.ts`, `index.ts:93,115`, `repl.ts:69,281,644-648`, `sidecar.ts:53,66,478,638,935` | 3 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:44:| 5 | Route verifier executions through the policy as `exec`. In review mode, when no prior approval exists, emit the approval with `kind: \"verifier\"`, the command, and the resolved script body (read `package.json` `scripts.test`, the Makefile `test:` recipe, `Cargo.toml`/`pytest.ini` presence). Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, not folder trust. Cache the approval per (workspace, command, script digest) for the session. | `agent.ts:1602-1630,3432-3436,4034`; `tester.ts:113-136` (add `describeVerifier()`); `approval_review.ts` (new kind) | 3 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:39:  - workspace trust;\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:140:| Tools, security, persistence: `tools, safe_fs, sandbox, security, session, session_export, checkpoint, flight, evidence, git, worktree, mcp, plugins, skills, browser, lsp, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, workspace_trust`, `core/{authority, resources, durable_file, persistence_protection, capabilities, workspace_path, independent_check, tool_groups}` | 28 | Full read for security-critical files. Grep or skim for session_export, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, resources, browser, lsp, mcp transports. | C_tools_security_persistence; this file (workspace_trust, workspace_path, tool_groups, independent_check, approval_review, read by lead) | MCP remote transports, browser.ts and lsp.ts got only a skim review: **qualification gap** |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:15:- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-01' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. The test launches the actual `nexus` TUI and `nexus repl` in trusted and untrusted workspaces with explicit `review`, explicit `auto`, and unset mode. It verifies that unset mode prompts in both trust states, auto mode executes, review mode denies without approval, and project instructions load only after trust.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/post-integration-verification-d2c4.md:14:- REQ-AGT-010 coverage: the focused suite exercised ACC-TRUST-04 and adjacent workspace trust behavior. This does not establish provenance for every injected-context source.\n[{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"v1/plan-07-installer-attestation-fix\",\"headRefOid\":\"8faf36aa43e9f74b823e68233f37180e68ff5cdb\",\"number\":211,\"title\":\"Fix installer attestation fail-closed behavior\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T04:51:09Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/211\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed-current-main-20261025\",\"headRefOid\":\"f6f2c152975d158557513db2d9d29141f5c8a60a\",\"number\":207,\"title\":\"fix(git): safely exclude Nexus workspace state\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:51:29Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/207\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed\",\"headRefOid\":\"81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20\",\"number\":200,\"title\":\"fix(git): avoid duplicate ineffective exclusion rules\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:56:13Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"v1/docs-post-v1-roadmap\",\"headRefOid\":\"eb834816db0d37c2df5e34005f46367516f33783\",\"number\":131,\"title\":\"docs(post-v1): add post-v1.0.0 documentation, roadmap (v1.1-v1.3), GBNF tool calling, and Composio integration\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T20:36:31Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownyc