50:08Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/104\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/REDACTED\",\"headRefOid\":\"25b39142f444a2586f4bf6be1c8c0e04036df863\",\"number\":103,\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/attest-build-provenance from 92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc to ef244123eb79f2f7a7e75d99086184180e6d0018\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:06:47Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/103\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":252752865}},"started_at_ms":1792903912038,"completed_at_ms":1792903913292}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:51:54.363Z","ordinal":324513,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17166-a37b-72c2-90c2-f3048041a3b2","call_id":"call_fbc4442a737a4aca8393d920f665fb2a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 9669)\nTotal output lines: 99\n\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:1060:    .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:498:| **EXT-003** | In accordance with Operator Decision 2, interactive confirmation MUST NOT be mandated as the universal extension trust mechanism. Valid extension authorization policies MUST include: preconfigured user configuration, explicit allowlists, operator trust prompts, bounded isolation, and deliberately broad trust. | A developer who preconfigures trust for a repository plugin in `~/.config/nexus/config.json` MUST NOT be interrupted by interactive approval prompts. |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:97:| EXT-003 | 15: MCP, Plugin & Extension | In accordance with Operator Decision 2, interactive confirmation MUST NOT be mandated as the universal extension trust mechanism. Valid extension authorization policies MUST include: preconfigured user configuration, explicit allowlists, operator trust prompts, bounded isolation, and deliberately broad trust. | A developer who preconfigures trust for a repository plugin in `~/.config/nexus/config.json` MUST NOT be interrupted by interactive approval prompts. | Phase 2 §19 | `cli/src/plugins.ts, cli/src/mcp.ts`; cli/test/harness.test.ts | SATISFIED_BY_INTEGRATED_SYSTEM | None | Satisfied |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:5:This release delivers the complete Nexus Code client architecture with comprehensive boundary hardening, process ownership, workspace trust enforcement, and egress protection.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:55:### Workspace Trust: Skills & Knowledge (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114)\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:56:- Workspace trust now gates workspace skill directories (`skills/`, `.nexus/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`) and workspace knowledge (`.nexus/knowledge.json`).\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:78:### Approval Mode Independent of Folder Trust (amended DEC-01)\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:79:- **Problem addressed (SEC-01):** Folder trust and tool authority were coupled, making workspace trust silently change the approval posture.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:80:- **New behavior:** Tool permission mode is independent of workspace trust and defaults to `review` in every folder. `--mode auto` selects autonomous writes and command execution while keeping first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass all approval prompts, including egress.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:82:- **Trusting your own repository:** Run `nexus trust .` (or `nexus trust <path>`) to load project instructions and workspace integrations. Trust does not change tool permission mode.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:84:  - `--approve` / `--mode review`: Enforces review posture regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:119:- In review mode, the first verifier execution is gated by an approval prompt displaying the exact command and the resolved test script body (extracted from `package.json` `scripts.test`, Makefile recipes, or `Cargo.toml`). Folder trust does not authorize verifier execution.\ncli/src/config.ts:253:    // Folder trust controls project instructions and integrations, not tool authority.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:261:- **Minimum Requirements-Level Correction:** Reframe `SUBP-002` and `CRED-002` to clarify that scrubbing ambient host credentials is the mandatory default for untrusted or bounded domains, but that execution domain policy MAY explicitly authorize subprocesses to inherit or access designated environment credentials without requiring per-invocation micro-approvals.\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:60:3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress. Folder trust only controls project instructions and workspace integrations. Input safety is strictly enforced across surfaces (REQ-SEC-103): lone Enter defaults to No, a 400ms grace period discards typed-ahead input, and approve-all requires explicit confirmation (`all` in REPL, confirmation Enter in TUI). *Limit:* in explicit `auto` posture, commands and file writes execute autonomously regardless of folder trust.\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:61:4. **Workspace trust.** Trust is managed via `nexus trust` and stored in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json`; interactive startup asks for trust before loading project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`). In untrusted workspaces, project instructions, workspace MCP configs, plugins, skills, and `.nexus/knowledge.json` are not loaded (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114). The operator may continue without trust under the existing permission mode or exit. *Limit:* configuration in the operator's home directory (`~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/`) is always trusted.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:20:- On each interactive launch from an untrusted folder, Nexus asks whether to trust the folder, continue without trust, or exit. Trust loads project instructions when present and enables trusted workspace integrations. Folder trust is separate from tool permissions: an explicit mode controls approvals, and an unset mode defaults to `review` in every folder. Non-interactive launches do not prompt and do not load project instructions unless the folder is already trusted.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:22:### Execution Postures & Approval Modes\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:24:Nexus Code resolves tool approval posture from permission settings, independently of workspace trust (amended DEC-01):\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:25:- **Default:** `review` posture, requiring human confirmation before executing shell commands, file modifications, network requests, or verifier test runs, regardless of folder trust.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:26:- **Auto:** Select with `--mode auto`. Writes and commands run without approval; network egress still asks on first use of each origin. This is independent of folder trust.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:31:- **Review mode (human-in-the-loop):** Run `nexus --approve` (or `nexus --mode review`) to require explicit approval for all actions regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:367:- **Workspace Trust & Context Provenance (REQ-SEC-113, CTX-001)**: An opened workspace is data until explicitly trusted by the operator. Workspace trust covers:\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:390:- **Verifier Execution Gating (REQ-SEC-119)**: Automated test runs and verifiers (`run_tests`, `/test`, completion oracle) are classified as `exec` capabilities subject to the configured approval mode. In review mode, the first verifier execution prompts for approval, displaying the exact test command and resolved script body from `package.json`, `Makefile`, or `Cargo.toml`; folder trust alone does not authorize it.\ncli/src/core/capabilities.ts:12: * `egress`; `context_inject` is gated by workspace trust instead; `read_workspace`, `delegate` (the child's own calls are\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:161:  test(\"exec approval follows permission mode regardless of workspace trust\", () => {\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:164:    // Auto mode follows the operator's permission setting in both trusted and untrusted folders.\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:182:  test(\"workspace trust does not change context-injection approval; untrusted sources remain gated\", () => {\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:5: * - Explicit au