md:99:- **Terminal evidence** comes from `pyte` emulation plus the repository's PTY suites. Real emulators (kitty keyboard protocol, tmux, VS Code) were not exercised.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_tui_2026-10-11.cast:1:{\"version\": 2, \"width\": 120, \"height\": 40, \"timestamp\": 1791745172, \"title\": \"Nexus TUI maturity fixes (PTY e2e)\", \"env\": {\"TERM\": \"xterm-256color\"}}\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:13:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:119:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:140:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:155:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:274:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:19:Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:23:| xterm | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:24:| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:25:| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:27:| GNOME Terminal | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:49:| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:50:| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:51:| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:52:| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:5