{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:56:58.660Z","ordinal":324767,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17166-29c6-7782-8ecb-9326d4f90716","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5423918b-7004-4c71-ae17-622392f0b755","process_id":"67720","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'attestation|verify.*provenance|NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION|trusted GitHub CLI|install\\.sh' README.md docs cli README* | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan-07-installer-attestation-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'attestation|verify.*provenance|NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION|trusted GitHub CLI|install\\.sh' README.md docs cli README* | head -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"README.md:17:curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\nREADME.md:17:curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:120:  attestationVerified?: boolean;\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:517:    // Check if prereleases exist (matching install.sh behavior)\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:581:      \"Nexus is running from a source development checkout. Use `git pull && make build` to update, or install the packaged release via `install.sh`.\"\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:917:  const verifyAttestation = process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION ?? \"auto\";\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:920:  if (verifyAttestation === \"1\" && !trustedGh) {\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:922:      \"Provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\",\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1069:    // Optional attestation check via a trusted gh if present. Do not resolve it from PATH: a shim that exits 0\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1070:    // must not be able to claim a verified attestation, and a missing gh must fail closed when verification is required.\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1071:    let attestationVerified: boolean | undefined;\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1072:    if (verifyAttestation !== \"0\") {\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1074:        options?.onProgress?.(\"verifying_attestation\", \"Checking build provenance attestation...\");\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1075:        const attestCheck = spawnSync(trustedGh, [\"attestation\", \"verify\", localArchive, \"-R\", CANONICAL_REPO]);\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1076:        const indexAttestCheck = spawnSync(trustedGh, [\"attestation\", \"verify\", localSums, \"-R\", CANONICAL_REPO]);\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1078:          attestationVerified = true;\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1079:        } else if (verifyAttestation === \"1\") {\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1080:          throw new Error(`Provenance attestation verification failed for ${archiveName} or SHA256SUMS.`);\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1082:      } else if (verifyAttestation === \"1\") {\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1084:          \"Provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\",\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1123:    // The in-archive copy is authenticated by the archive checksum/attestation.\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1268:      attestationVerified,\ncli/test/node_floor.test.ts:27:    return spawnSync(\"/bin/sh\", [path.join(root, \"install.sh\")], {\ncli/test/node_floor.test.ts:78:  assert.match(read(\"install.sh\"), new RegExp(`\"\\\\$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge ${FLOOR} \\\\]`));\ncli/test/repro_identity.test.ts:44:      ...(overrides.missingAsset ? {} : { \"install.sh\": \"i\" }),\ncli/test/repro_identity.test.ts:132:    for (const name of [\"nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.1.tar.gz\", \"compatibility.json\", \"SHA256SUMS\", \"THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\", \"sbom.cdx.json\", \"install.sh\"]) {\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:303:    // 9. Verify durable provenance recorded in new version directory\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:317:  it(\"refuses an upgrade that requires attestation when gh is unavailable\", async () => {\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:329:    const savedAttestation = process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:330:    // A PATH shim that claims success must not satisfy *required* attestation, and an empty trusted-path list must\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:338:    process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = \"1\";\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:342:        /no trusted GitHub CLI was found at \\/usr\\/bin\\/gh/,\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:343:        \"a required attestation must fail closed when no trusted gh exists\",\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:346:      assert.equal(readJournal(tmpPrefix), null, \"required attestation must fail before starting the journal\");\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:353:        \"required attestation must not leave upgrade staging or a journal\",\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:358:      if (savedAttestation === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:359:      else process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = savedAttestation;\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:363:  it(\"rejects required attestation when the trusted gh reports failure\", async () => {\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:376:    const savedAttestation = process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:377:    process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = \"1\";\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:381:        /Provenance attestation verification failed for .* or SHA256SUMS/,\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:382:        \"a trusted gh reporting failure must reject required attestation\",\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:385:      if (savedAttestation === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\ncli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts:386:      else process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION = savedAttestation;\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:144:| Distribution and CI: `install.sh, harness.sh, Makefile, package.json` ×2, lockfiles, `scripts/*`, workflows, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `LICENSE`, `doctor.ts` | 20 | Full read + installer runs (6 scratch HOMEs + docker) + CI log | E_distribution | Lockfiles audited by tool, not by line |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:273:| REL-08 | S3 | RR | Installer | `install.sh:21-24` | RT | Opaque no-version failure | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:275:| REL-10 | S3 | RR | Reinstall | `install.sh:48-49` | RT | Cannot repair | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:276:| REL-11 | S4 | RR | Tag validation | `install.sh:26` | RT | Loose regex | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:277:| REL-12 | S4 | RR | Installer UX | `install.sh:32-33` | RT | Noisy output | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:280:| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:322:| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:12:| C4 | `install.sh --fresh`: no prior manifest needed. The demo uid and HOME become build parameters of `build-launcher.sh`. Regenerate `BUNDLE.sha256` and `trusted-object-manifest.json` after review. | `trusted-broker-bundle/{install.sh,build-launcher.sh,BUNDLE.sha256,trusted-object-manifest.json}` | High |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:16:- `install.sh` (installer durable provenance recording)\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:14:| Default workflow token | `read`; workflows request extra permissions themselves (`release.yml`: `contents`, `id-token`, `attestations` write) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:15:- `install.sh`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:37:| 7 | Installer: strict tag regex; `-fsSL --show-error`; no-stable-release hint naming the latest prerelease; rate-limit message; `MANIFEST.sha256` repair on reinstall; `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. | `install.sh:21-49`; `package-linux.sh` (write manifest) | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:29:| 5 | Add provenance with `actions/attest-build-provenance` on the tarball and SHA256SUMS, and upload `install.sh` as a release asset. The installer optionally runs `gh attestation verify` when `gh` is available. | `release.yml:44-48`; `install.sh` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:50:- **ACC-SUP-03.** Run `gh attestation verify` in a post-release verification job against the published asset.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:61:- The release assets are: tarball, SHA256SUMS, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt, the SBOM, install.sh, and the attestation.\ncli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:619:   const previousBase=process.env.NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL, previousAttest=process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;\ncli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:637:   process.env.NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL=`http://127.0.0.1:${(server.address() as any).port}/releases`;process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=\"0\";\ncli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:658:    if(previousAttest===undefined)delete process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION;else process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=previousAttest;\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:30:Packaging builds the Rust binaries inside the approved, digest-pinned builder image (`APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE` in the `Makefile`) and requires Docker. Unless `NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1` is set, `scripts/package-linux.sh` exits with status 2 if `NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE` is unset; it always exits with status 2 if the variable names any other image. `make verify-reproducibility` builds the package twice with that image and compares the archive, `SHA256SUMS`, notices, SBOM and `install.sh` byte for byte. For a local, non-release build only, setting `NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1` with `NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE` unset builds with the host Rust toolchain instead; if the image variable is set, packaging still uses the container and still rejects any non-approved image. A host-built package is not a release candidate.\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:38:- `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh`\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:17:| [DEC-09](#dec-09-release-provenance-mechanism) | Release provenance | GitHub artifact attestations | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:140:**Chosen:** GitHub artifact attestations (`actions/attest-build-provenance`). Users verify with `gh attestation verify`. SHA256SUMS is kept. There is no separate GPG or minisign key to manage.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/own.md:43:- Observed: `package.json` declares `\"license\": \"MIT\"` but there is no LICENSE file; no SECURITY.md or vulnerability-reporting process; no CHANGELOG. `make verify-reproducibility` (Makefile:36-45) only rebuilds the TypeScript CLI twice (Rust artefacts not checked; fixed /tmp paths). Security gates run npm audit and cargo audit and a pattern secret scan (`scripts/security_gates.sh:26-127`); `scripts/generate_sbom.sh` writes a CycloneDX-style SBOM to `dist/` but nothing signs artefacts or records provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:76:| REQ-REL-001 | quickstart | Installer: non-root; SHA-256 verified; no shell-rc edits; refuses a foreign `nexus`; atomic symlink swap; failure leaves HOME untouched. | `install.sh` | RT (E §4); TEST installer-smoke | tested | N | — | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:78:| REQ-REL-003 | DEVELOPMENT.md; DEC-12 | Supported platform: Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22. Clear failure messages elsewhere. | `install.sh`, doctor, upgrade preflight | Runtime/workflow source candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9` passed PR #150 exact CI run `39866110578` (Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64`) and CodeQL `39866110533`; focused `node_floor.test.ts` passed 6/6 on Node 24. Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | partial | N | Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | ACC-PLAT | RR | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:79:| REQ-REL-004 | quickstart | Upgrade and rollback by re-running the installer with a tag. Manual uninstall keeps user data. | `install.sh` | RT (alpha.1→2→1) | tested | N | Reinstall does not repair (REL-10) | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:190:| REQ-REL-105 | Audit | Installer: strict tag check, clear no-stable message, repair on reinstall, quiet output. | onboarding | `install.sh` | TEST (ACC-PKG-05; test:scripts/installer-smoke.sh) | tested | ACC-PKG-05 | RR | REL-08, REL-10, REL-11, REL-12 | SPEC-06 / PLAN-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:198:| REQ-REL-109 | TOP_TIER D4 | Provenance attestation; tag-pinned installer asset. | supply chain | `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-03; test:release.yml, install.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-03 | RR | REL-09 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:21:**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:293:3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:296:6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:44:3. **REQ-CON-103.** The broker gets a fresh-install mode (`install.sh --fresh`). The demo uid and HOME become build parameters. `BUNDLE.sha256` and the trusted-object manifest are regenerated after review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:62:- `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes on a clean VM.\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:83:## 4. Publisher Authenticity: Current Baseline vs. Cryptographic Attestation (ACC-UPG-14)\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:93:1. **GitHub Artifact Attestations (Sigstore / Cosign)**:\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:94:   - Use GitHub's native artifact attestation action during release builds:\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:100:   - This produces an immutable, cryptographic in-toto attestation signed via Sigstore's Fulcio certificate authority and recorded in the Rekor transparency log, binding the binary to the repository, workflow, and commit SHA.\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:101:   - The updater can verify this provenance using `gh attestation verify` (automated hook already provided in `cli/src/upgrade.ts`) or an embedded pure-JS Sigstore bundle verifier.\ndocs/cloudflare/CONTEST_CREDENTIAL_LIFECYCLE_PREQUALIFICATION_2026-10-02.md:86:| Shell syntax | `install.sh` and `rollback.sh` passed `bash -n` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:14:Nexus currently requires operators to re-run the external `install.sh` script via `curl -fsSL ... | sh` to upgrade or downgrade installed binaries. There is no CLI command (`nexus upgrade`) and no TUI slash command (`/upgrade`) to:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:47:   - Establish publisher trust boundary and attestation recommendations in `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:95:  - If a trusted `gh` exists at `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh` and `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION != 0`, verifies\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:96:    GitHub build provenance attestation. `PATH`-resolved `gh` is not used; with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`, a\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:130:| ACC-UPG-14 | Publisher Authenticity Assessment | Evaluates trust boundary, SHA-256 baseline, and documents signing/attestation recommendations in `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:5:| Status | Ready. GitHub attestations for provenance (DEC-09); `cli/dist` untracked (DEC-10). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:20:| REL-09 | There is no signature or provenance attestation, and the installer is served from mutable `main`. | SOURCE |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:57:- **Provenance.** Add `permissions: id-token: write, attestations: write` to release.yml and a step `actions/attest-build-provenance@v1` with `subject-path` set to the tarball and SHA256SUMS. Docs: `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:66:| ACC-SUP-03 | `gh attestation verify` passes for the RC tarball. |\nd