{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:58:51.271Z","ordinal":324863,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17166-29c6-7782-8ecb-9326d4f90716","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add8c88258881a09ba713f5e2f95eda","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Your “Default to review” choice matches current `main`: folder trust and tool approvals are separate. RC4 still defaults trusted workspaces to `auto`, so it does not include that newer behavior; the current source does.\n\n**Release progress**\n\n- PR #211 is at `8faf36aa43e9f74b823e68233f37180e68ff5cdb`. Its correction was independently reviewed as accepted, and CodeQL passed. Exact-head CI is still running its Node 22 and Node 24 CLI suites. The earlier candidate’s Linux failure was caused by a test fixture leaking an opt-out setting into the strict check.\n- Main CI on `a3e1b65a36b4c64f44e5def6500214d1b256d4be` had a runner communication failure during Node 22 testing. The automatic retry is now running the CLI suite; Node 24 and CodeQL passed. The failed attempt provides no product-test conclusion.\n- I did not run local tests because the full-suite claim is held by a live test process.\n\n**Terminal setup**\n\nI reached `10.0.8.3` and verified an active Ubuntu 26.04.1 GNOME desktop with xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code installed. This prepares the environment, but the human matrix remains **0/15**: it must use the selected installed RC and include operator observations and screenshots.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC4 is still the latest prerelease; held-out custody is unanswered, and no held-out qualification or stable release is established. I’ll proceed when the exact-head checks finish.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":810,"note":"release gate and acceptance boundary"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1792904328177,"completed_at_ms":1792904331271}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:58:51.276Z","ordinal":324864,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add8c88258881a09ba713f5e2f95eda","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Your “Default to review” choice matches current `main`: folder trust and tool approvals are separate. RC4 still defaults trusted workspaces to `auto`, so it does not include that newer behavior; the current source does.\n\n**Release progress**\n\n- PR #211 is at `8faf36aa43e9f74b823e68233f37180e68ff5cdb`. Its correction was independently reviewed as accepted, and CodeQL passed. Exact-head CI is still running its Node 22 and Node 24 CLI suites. The earlier candidate’s Linux failure was caused by a test fixture leaking an opt-out setting into the strict check.\n- Main CI on `a3e1b65a36b4c64f44e5def6500214d1b256d4be` had a runner communication failure during Node 22 testing. The automatic retry is now running the CLI suite; Node 24 and CodeQL passed. The failed attempt provides no product-test conclusion.\n- I did not run local tests because the full-suite claim is held by a live test process.\n\n**Terminal setup**\n\nI reached `10.0.8.3` and verified an active Ubuntu 26.04.1 GNOME desktop with xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code installed. This prepares the environment, but the human matrix remains **0/15**: it must use the selected installed RC and include operator observations and screenshots.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC4 is still the latest prerelease; held-out custody is unanswered, and no held-out qualification or stable release is established. I’ll proceed when the exact-head checks finish.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:777-810|note=[release gate and acceptance boundary]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_