{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:59:29.960Z","ordinal":324884,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1716d-4ef9-7030-a040-e096bc518776","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a23d3495-c521-4237-a43f-0ab0bc745005","process_id":"27702","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 2 --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,latest:(.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:600])})}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan-07-installer-attestation-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 2 --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,latest:(.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:600])})}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"latest\":{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"T4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an execution denominator.\\n\\nThis resolves the planning-text discrepancy only. T4 qualification has not run \",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"},\"number\":2,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 11: complete preregistered M5 qualification runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":512055623}},"started_at_ms":1792904368447,"completed_at_ms":1792904369960}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:59:30.072Z","ordinal":324885,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1716d-4ef9-7030-a040-e096bc518776","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4235a673-c3cc-4318-b9a4-ba3a6506b64e","process_id":"23723","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 3 --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,latest:(.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:600])})}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan-07-installer-attestation-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 3 --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,latest:(.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:600])})}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"latest\":{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Terminal environment preflight (setup only; no qualification cells run)\\n\\nThe connected Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME desktop is reachable and has an active local GNOME/Wayland session. All required terminal applications are installed: xterm XTerm(407), kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1. The `nexus` command is not installed on that host yet.\\n\\nThe matrix remains 0/15. Each cell still requires the real interactive checks in ACCEPTANCE.md §5.3 and two screenshots (approval panel and post-exit terminal state). Current public RC4 is not the current source head: its commit i\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:55:35Z\"},\"number\":3,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 12: complete the real-terminal acceptance matrix\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:55:35Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":564341178}},"started_at_ms":1792904368508,"completed_at_ms":1792904370072}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:59:30.089Z","ordinal":324886,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1716d-4ef9-7030-a040-e096bc518776","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-56841dfb-fa32-40b6-884f-62c81e8e2bb3","process_id":"52779","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 5 --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,latest:(.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:600])})}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan-07-installer-attestation-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 5 --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,latest:(.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:600])})}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"latest\":{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code): the workflow is integrated. `.github/workflows/repro.yml` plus `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20) build on ubuntu-22.04 and 24.04 with fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity. It has **not** run on an RC because no RC tag exists yet. REQ-REL-114 is still `RR`, correctly. Next action: once the RC is tagged, the release publisher (codex-api-root) runs repro.yml on the exact RC and attaches the run ID and artifact hashes here.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\"},\"number\":5,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-07 PR-7e: prove cross-runner release reproducibility\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":536322390}},"started_at_ms":1792904368552,"completed_at_ms":1792904370089}}
