{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:01:01.425Z","ordinal":324961,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1716e-fc71-7980-a507-c83be88749e4","call_id":"call_2b626d0f30584d8dba3aa4667f600c30","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Releases · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/releases)\nciteturn65search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; `gh release download`, `gh run download`, `gh repo read-file --output`, and `gh attestation download` could write remote content to an unintended local file when the destination contained symbolic links. ... `gh attestation verify` matched the `--signer-workflow` value against only the start of the signing certificate's identity, so an attestation signed by a different workflow in the pinned repository could pass verification when its path began with the pinned value. ... Users on Windows or macOS, and users who installed `gh` through Homebrew, GitHub Releases, another package manager, or from source, are not affected. ...   * Bump github.com/cli/go-gh/v2 to v2.16.1 by @niik in #14461\n\n13.4 MB 2026-10-23T20:24:05Z\n\n  * GitHub CLI 2.103.2 linux amd64 deb\n\nsha256:30463d8e1fdce73f178f76b0082b7ab0657b0740b87274890e831def647ca979\n\n14.4 MB 2026-10-23T20:24:05Z\n\n  * GitHub CLI 2.103.2 linux amd64 RPM\n\nsha256:fdcb809819ef9d097d23fa41e62cbb0f6c224f75c1b9dc8add822105f24dd774\n\n14.9 MB 2026-10-23T20:24:06Z\n\n  * GitHub CLI 2.103.2 linux amd64\n\nsha256:62ccf747115ddc61237efffdde66a3c8f70ba249433dc64f70801089b59c59c8\n\n14.3 MB 2026-10-23T20:24:06Z\n\n  * GitHub CLI 2.103.2 linux arm64 deb\n\nsha256:41290f26363155b0bef44a751d011994771f537e1f8c4253d1f53b5cf3b8641e\n\n13.1 MB 2026-10-23T20:24:07Z\n\n  * GitHub CLI 2.103.2 linux arm64 RPM\n\nsha256:61dd1b37309fe38c34450d85cdb6970a2fde34ed6b594023ede1e74f7f9c0c48\n\n13.5 MB 2026-10-23T20:24:07Z\n\n  * GitHub CLI 2.103.2 linux arm64\n\nsha256:4c3e99a50bd8b181a3fe9d69b25dd978bac768148d88f01507c6b4d1ef61a443\n\n13 MB 2026-10-23T20:24:07Z\n\n  * Source code (zip)\n\n2026-10-23T20:08:01Z\n\n  * Source code (tar.gz)\n\n2026-10-23T20:08:01Z\n\n  * Release attestation (json)\n\n2026-10-23T20:08:01Z\n\n## No results found\n\nView all tags\n\nImage: @github-actions github-actions released this 30 Sep 02:40\n\nImmutable release. Only release title and notes can be modified.\n\nv2.102.0\n\n`fc4b137`\n\nThis commit was created on GitHub.com and signed with GitHub’s verified signature.\n\nGPG key ID: B5690EEEBB952194\n\nVerified\n\nLearn about vigilant mode.\n\n## Security\n\nFour security vulnerabilities have been identified, and fixed, in this release. Users are advised to update gh to version `v2.102.0` as soon as possible.\n\n`gh release download`, `gh run download`, `gh repo read-file --output`, and `gh attestation download` could write remote content to an unintended local file when the destination contained symbolic links.\n\nSee GHSA-39wj-f2f4-978v for more information.\n\n`gh attestation verify` compared the `--source-ref` value case-insensitively, so an attestation built from a branch whose name differs only in case could satisfy a policy that named a different branch.\n\nSee GHSA-4mq3-hpgx-9cx8 for more information.\n\nInteractive `gh skill search` passed repository paths from search results to `gh skill install` without an option separator, so a search result could inject installer options and change where skill files were written.\n\nSee GHSA-qcwj-mr2r-2cx7 for more information.\n\n`gh attestation verify` matched the `--signer-workflow` value against only the start of the signing certificate's identity, so an attestation signed by a different workflow in the pinned repository could pass verification when its path began with the pinned value.\n\nSee GHSA-wjmr-j3rp-mh2g for more information.\n\n## What's Changed\n\n### 🐛 Fixes\n\n  * Allow `ghu_` tokens for supported actors to attach files by @BagToad in #14516\n  * Allow repo set-default --unset without an argument by @williammartin in #14540\n\n### 📚 Docs & Chores\n\n  * Prioritize HackerOne for vulnerability reports by @BagToad in #14497\n  * chore(deps): bump the codeql-actions group with 3 updates by @dependabot in #14543\n\nFull Changelog: `v2.101.0...v2.102.0`\n\n## Security\n\nFour security vulnerabilities have been identified, and fixed, in this release. Users are advised to update gh to version `v2.102.0` as soon as possible.\n\n`gh release download`, `gh run download`, `gh repo read-file --output`, and `gh attestation download` could write remote content to an unintended local file when the destination contained symbolic links.\n\nSee GHSA-39wj-f2f4-978v for more information.\n\n`gh attestation verify` compared the `--source-ref` value case-insensitively, so an attestation built from a branch whose name differs only in case could satisfy a policy that named a different branch.\n\nSee GHSA-4mq3-hpgx-9cx8 for more information.\n\nInteractive `gh skill search` passed repository paths from search results to `gh skill install` without an option separator, so a search result could inject installer options and change where skill files were written.\n\nSee GHSA-qcwj-mr2r-2cx7 for more information.\n\n`gh attestation verify` matched the `--signer-workflow` value against only the start of the signing certificate's identity, so an attestation signed by a different workflow in the pinned repository could pass verification when its path began with the pinned value.\n\nSee GHSA-wjmr-j3rp-mh2g for more information.\n\n## What's Changed\n\n### 🐛 Fixes\n\n  * Allow `ghu_` tokens for supported actors to attach files by @BagToad in #14516\n  * Allow repo set-default --unset without an argument by @williammartin in #14540\n\n### 📚 Docs & Chores\n\n  * Prioritize HackerOne for vulnerability reports by @BagToad in #14497\n  * Clarify reviewer-facing PR guidance by @williammartin in #14509\n  * Add a skill for chaptered CLI recordings by @BagToad in #14475\n  * Improve CLI recording rendering by @williammartin in #14507\n  * Mention gh CLI in the README intro by @BagToad in #14517\n  * Document search operator support in `gh search` help by @waldyrious in #14519\n  * Remove host versions from `gh project item-list` help by @BagToad in #14553\n\n### Image: :dependabot: Dependencies\n\n  * chore(deps): bump the codeql-actions group with 3 updates by @dependabot in #14486\n  * chore(deps): bump nodeselector/setup-apple-codesign from 0.0.2 to 0.0.3 by @dependabot in #14487\n  * chore(deps): bump charm.land/bubbletea/v2 from 2.0.9 to 2.0.10 by @dependabot in #14541\n  * chore(deps): bump github.com/klauspost/compress from 1.20.0 to 1.20.1 by @dependabot in #14542\n  * chore(deps): bump the codeql-actions group with 3 updates by @dependabot in #14543\n\nFull Changelog: `v2.101.0...v2.102.0`\n\n## GitHub CLI 2.97.0\n\nGitHub CLI 2.97.0\n\nCompare\n\n# Choose a tag to compare\n\n## Sorry, something went wrong.\n\nFilter\n\nLoading [Input]\n\n## Sorry, something went wrong.\n\n### Uh oh!\n\nThere was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\n\n## No results found\n\nView all tags\n\nImage: @github-actions github-actions released this 31 Jul 02:04\n\nImmutable release. Only release title and notes can be modified.\n\nv2.97.0\n\n`55dbb4d`\n\nThis commit was created on GitHub.com and signed with GitHub’s verified signature.\n\nGPG key ID: B5690EEEBB952194\n\nVerified\n\nLearn about vigilant mode.\n\n## Security\n\nFour security vulnerabilities have been identified, and fixed, in this release. Users are advised to update gh to version `v2.97.0` as soon as possible.\n\nSeveral commands (including `gh gist view`, `gh api`, `gh pr diff`, `gh release download --output -`, `gh codespace logs`, `gh skills preview`, and `gh agent-task view`/`create`) printed externally controlled content without neutralizing terminal escape sequences, allowing escape sequence injection into a user's terminal.\n\nSee GHSA-3m3g-3wcr-px46 for more information.\n\nSome request URLs were built without escaping their variable path components, so a value containing URL path metacharacters could alter the request path and cause `gh` to address a different resource than intended.\n\nSee GHSA-4fjg-2h4q-fwg3 for more information.\n\n`gh auth status` (without `--show-token`) could print a portion of the authentication token in plaintext for token types whose format contains an underscore after the prefix, such as `github_pat_*`, `ghs_*`, and `ghu_*`.\n\nSee GHSA-cg6r-mpgc-h9mm for more information.\n\n`gh attestation verify` built the certificate matcher from `--signer-repo` and `--signer-workflow` without escaping regex metacharacters, so a lookalike repository or workflow name could satisfy a matcher intended for a trusted signer and bypass attestation verification.\n\nSee GHSA-mm27-mwq9-fr5g for more information.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - cli/cli: GitHub’s official command line tool · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli)\nciteturn65search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Since version 2.50.0, `gh` has been producing Build Provenance Attestation, enabling a cryptographically verifiable paper-trail back to the origin GitHub repository, git revision, and build instructions used. ...     $ gh at verify -R cli/cli gh_2.62.0_macOS_arm64.zip ...     cli/cli  https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1  .github/workflows/deployment.yml@refs/heads/trunk ... To perform this, download the attestation for the downloaded release and use cosign to verify the authenticity of the downloaded release:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub CLI | Take GitHub to the command line (https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_attestation)\nciteturn65search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;   * gh attestation verify\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub CLI | Take GitHub to the command line (https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_attestation_verify)\nciteturn65search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Given the `--format=json` flag, upon successful verification this command will output a JSON array containing one entry per verified attestation. ...     $ gh attestation verify example.bin --repo github/example ...     $ gh attestation verify example.bin --owner github\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub CLI | Take GitHub to the command line (https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_release_verify)\nciteturn65search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Verify that a GitHub Release is accompanied by a valid cryptographically signed attestation. ...     gh release verify v1.2.3\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSecurity Advisories · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/security/advisories)\nciteturn65search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week;   * `gh attestation verify` compares `--source-ref` case-insensitively ...   * GitHub CLI filesystem operations can write outside intended destinations through symlinksGHSA-39wj-f2f4-978v published Sep 30, 2026 by BagToad ... GHSA-3m3g-3wcr-px46 published Jul 31, 2026 by BagToad\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub CLI | Take GitHub to the command line (https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_help_reference)\nciteturn65search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;     -o, --owner string            GitHub organization to scope attestation lookup by ...         --bundle-from-oci              When verifying an OCI image, fetch the attestation bundle from the OCI registry instead of from GitHub ... ### `gh release verify-asset [<tag>] <file-path> [flags]`\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAttestations · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/attestations)\nciteturn65search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago;   * #### gh_2.101.0_linux_386.deb and 20 others ... https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1 · ... Download attestation #21158102\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n`gh attestation verify` compares `--source-ref` case-insensitively · Advisory · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/security/advisories/GHSA-4mq3-hpgx-9cx8)\nciteturn65search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; Crawled: last week; github.com/cli/cli/v2 (Go) ... GitHub CLI's `gh attestation verify` compared the `--source-ref` value against the signing certificate's source ref without regard to case.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n`gh attestation verify` treats `--signer-workflow` as a prefix · Advisory · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/security/advisories/GHSA-wjmr-j3rp-mh2g)\nciteturn65search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; Crawled: last week; github.com/cli/cli/v2 (Go) ... GitHub CLI's `gh attestation verify` matched the `--signer-workflow` value against the start of the signing certificate's Subject Alternative Name (SAN) instead of the complete workflow identity.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAttestation verification bypass via unescaped regex metacharacters in SAN matching · Advisory · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/security/advisories/GHSA-mm27-mwq9-fr5g)\nciteturn65search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; github.com/cli/cli/v2 (Go) ... A security vulnerability has been identified in GitHub CLI that could allow attestation verification bypass when using `gh attestation verify` with `--signer-repo` or `--signer-workflow` flags.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncli/pkg/cmd/release/verify/verify.go at trunk · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/pkg/cmd/release/verify/verify.go)\nciteturn65search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; `), Example: heredoc.Doc(` # Verify the latest release gh release verify # Verify a specific release by tag gh release verify v1.2.3 # Verify a specific release by tag and output the attestation in JSON format gh release verify v1.2.3 --format json `), RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error { if len(args) > 0 { opts.TagName = args[0] } baseRepo, err := f.BaseRepo() if err ! ... \"github.com/cli/cli/v2/pkg/cmd/attestation/verification\"\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub Agentic Workflows (https://github.github.com/gh-aw/slides/20260224-github-agentic-workflows.pdf)\nciteturn65search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; GitHub CLI (gh) v2.0.0+\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub Agentic Workflows (https://github.github.com/gh-aw/slides/github-agentic-workflows.pdf)\nciteturn65search13 [wordlim: 200] - GitHub CLI (gh) v2.0.0+\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1716d-4ef9-7030-a040-e096bc518776","create_time":1792904461.4257133}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
