ps://github.com/cli/cli/releases are considered official binaries. ... ### Debian, Ubuntu Linux, Raspberry Pi OS (apt) ... && echo \"deb [arch","title":"github-cli/docs/install_linux.md at trunk · tep/github-cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/tep/github-cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_linux.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn66search4","snippet":"A git commit is created in the `cli.github.com` site repository containing the contents of the CLI Manual uploaded by the `linux` job. ... The `cli.github.com`","title":"cli/docs/release-process-deep-dive.md at trunk · cli/cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/docs/release-process-deep-dive.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn66search5","snippet":"* GitHub CLI 2.103.2 linux 386 deb ... GitHub CLI's APT and RPM repositories, along with individual RPM packages, are now signed only with the","title":"Releases · cli/cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/releases"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn66search6","snippet":"# install_linux.md ... Packages downloaded from https://cli.github.com or from https://github.com/cli/cli/releases are considered official binaries. ... && echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture)","title":"github-cli/docs/install_linux.md at trunk · vitaly-z/github-cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/vitaly-z/github-cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_linux.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn66search7","snippet":"sudo add-apt-repository ppa:gh/cli ... * I find the installation commands for https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/v2.93.0/docs/install_linux.md#debian to be too verbose.","title":"Add installation via PPA · Issue #14256 · cli/cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/14256"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn66search8","snippet":"winget install --id GitHub.cli --source winget ... It works on Linux, OS X and Windows, and was created for Python programs but can package and","title":"cli/docs/install_windows.md at trunk · cli/cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_windows.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn66search9","snippet":"Clone this repository $ git clone https://github.com/cli/cli.git gh-cli ... Build and install ... > go run script\\build.go clean bin\\gh GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm GOARM=7 CGO_ENABLED=0","title":"cli/docs/install_source.md at trunk · cli/cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_source.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"cli.github.com","ref_id":"turn66search10","snippet":"* * Linux — apt (Debian, Ubuntu) ... GitHub’s official command line tool ... View this repository on GitHub: https://github.com/cli/cli ... View installation instructions →","title":"GitHub CLI | Take GitHub to the command line","url":"https://cli.github.com/?ref=xingzhi.dev"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn66search11","snippet":"Linux users who installed `gh` from the official APT or RPM repositories before April 8, 2026, and have not refreshed their keyring, may now see","title":"Releases · cli/cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/releases?ref=explainx"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"training.github.com","ref_id":"turn66search12","snippet":"## Install ... Git distributions for Linux and POSIX systems are available on the official Git SCM web site. ... <tr><td>$ git clone [url]</td><td>Clone (download)","title":"GitCheatSheet_issue#2366_102019-V5","url":"https://training.github.com/downloads/github-git-cheat-sheet.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"resources.github.com","ref_id":"turn66search13","snippet":"Git is the open source distributed version control system that facilitates GitHub activities on your laptop or ... INSTALL GIT ... Git distributions for Linux","title":"V 1.1.1\nGIT CHEAT SHEET\nGit is the open source dis","url":"https://resources.github.com/downloads/github-git-cheat-sheet.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.github.com","ref_id":"turn66search14","snippet":"GitHub Repository - A repository where you have write access ... Operating System: Linux, macOS, or Windows with WSL ... Install the GitHub Agentic Workflows","title":"GitHub Agentic Workflows","url":"https://github.github.com/gh-aw/slides/20260224-github-agentic-workflows.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.github.com","ref_id":"turn66search15","snippet":"- GitHub Repository - A repository where you have write access ... - Operating System: Linux, macOS, or Windows with WSL ... Install the GitHub","title":"GitHub Agentic Workflows","url":"https://github.github.com/gh-aw/slides/github-agentic-workflows.pdf"}]},"started_at_ms":1792904468468,"completed_at_ms":1792904469565}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:01:11.547Z","ordinal":324970,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1716f-23fa-7d81-bf53-1aed5590e665","call_id":"call_8fc1c9966b214f5cb639efea1588ccbb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"cli/docs/install_linux.md at trunk · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_linux.md)\nciteturn66search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # install_linux.md ...     \t&& echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg] https://cli.github.com/packages stable main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/github-cli.list > /dev/null \\ ... The GitHub CLI package is supported by the Alpine Linux community with updates powered by alpine/aports. ... As of November 2025, GitHub CLI maintainers strongly recommend official Debian packages especially as the community-distributed `2.45.x` / `2.46.x` version is broken due to deprecated GitHub APIs.\n\n# install_linux.md\n\n487 lines (323 loc) · 14.4 KB\n\nRaw\n\nCopy raw file\n\nDownload raw file\n\nOutline\n\nEdit and raw actions\n\n# Installing gh on Linux and BSD\n\n## Recommended (Official)\n\nImportant\n\nOur Linux packages and repository metadata are signed with the following PGP key fingerprints:\n\n  * `2C6106201985B60E6C7AC87323F3D4EA75716059`\n  * `7F38BBB59D064DBCB3D84D725612B36462313325`\n\nYou may be prompted to confirm the import of these keys during installation.\n\nExpand for SHA256/SHA512/MD5 checksums of our official keyring files.\n\nFor security reasons, it is strongly recommended to only rely on SHA256/SHA512 checksums. MD5 checksums below are only for legacy systems where SHA256/SHA512 tooling is not available.\n\n  * `https://cli.github.com/packages/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg` (Binary):\n    \n    `SHA256: 6084d5d7bd8e288441e0e94fc6275570895da18e6751f70f057485dc2d1a811b\n    SHA512: ce6b9466dbd2a90b3227e177aa9b8187bd2405b1c29f91d78de83b9699dbbe2af35efd733bf53da622e7a38c59a7bc55539d63a3deae3c9ff9c2bff8af626434\n    MD5:    23748c0965069fb1edae1b83c17890e1\n    `\n\n  * `https://cli.github.com/packages/githubcli-archive-keyring.asc` (ASCII-armored):\n    \n    `SHA256: cec6e9ed82d3949ca5f4428cc968b41ef5e7416cb3653cdfc2a421977663bbfd\n    SHA512: 2ca9487d88a508a1c87f06b46ba336b11cc5f20bd83915b4c2acde49d2cffbbce76af1641bf8494c29a765f96bc1fd694ebde2954b28b80dcc76376b6f1b766d\n    MD5:    97100400ef48007b69e42be348cc6582\n    `\n\n### Debian\n\nDebian packages are hosted on the GitHub CLI marketing site for various operating systems including:\n\n  * Debian\n  * Raspberry Pi\n  * Ubuntu Linux\n\nThese packages are supported by the GitHub CLI maintainers with updates powered by GitHub CLI deployment workflow.\n\nTo install:\n    \n    (type -p wget >/dev/null || (sudo apt update && sudo apt install wget -y)) \\\n    \t&& sudo mkdir -p -m 755 /etc/apt/keyrings \\\n    \t&& out=$(mktemp) && wget -nv -O$out https://cli.github.com/packages/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg \\\n    \t&& cat $out | sudo tee /etc/apt/keyrings/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg > /dev/null \\\n    \t&& sudo chmod go+r /etc/apt/keyrings/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg \\\n    \t&& sudo mkdir -p -m 755 /etc/apt/sources.list.d \\\n    \t&& echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg] https://cli.github.com/packages stable main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/github-cli.list > /dev/null \\\n    \t&& sudo apt update \\\n    \t&& sudo apt install gh -y\n\nTo upgrade:\n    \n    sudo apt update\n    sudo apt install gh\n\nTip\n\nTo verify PGP keys before installing `gh`, you can run this and match the listed fingerprints with those at the top of this document:\n    \n    curl -fsSL -o - https://cli.github.com/packages/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg | gpg --show-keys\n\n### RPM\n\nRPM packages are hosted on the GitHub CLI marketing site for various operating systems including:\n\n  * Amazon Linux 2\n  * CentOS\n## Community (Unofficial)\n\nImportant\n\nThe GitHub CLI team does not maintain the following packages or repositories. We are unable to provide support for these installation methods or any guarantees of stability, security, or availability for these installation methods.\n\n### Alpine Linux\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is supported by the Alpine Linux community with updates powered by alpine/aports.\n\nTo install stable release:\n    \n    apk add github-cli\n\nTo install edge release:\n    \n    echo \"@community http://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/edge/community\" >> /etc/apk/repositories\n    apk add github-cli@community\n\n### Android\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is supported by the Termux community with updates powered by termux/termux-packages.\n\nTo install and upgrade:\n    \n    pkg install gh\n\n### Arch Linux\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is supported by the Arch Linux community with updates powered by Arch Linux packaging.\n\nNote\n\nAs of November 2025, GitHub CLI maintainers strongly recommend official Debian packages especially as the community-distributed `2.45.x` / `2.46.x` version is broken due to deprecated GitHub APIs.\n\n### Fedora Community\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is supported by the Fedora community with updates powered by Fedora Project.\n\nTo install:\n    \n    sudo dnf install gh\n\nTo upgrade:\n    \n    sudo dnf update gh\n\n### Flox\n\nFlox is a virtual environment and package manager all in one. With Flox you create environments that layer and replace dependencies just where it matters, making them portable across the full software lifecycle.\n\nFlox relies upon the GitHub CLI package supported by the NixOS community\n\nTo install:\n    \n    flox install gh\n\nTo upgrade:\n    \n    flox upgrade toplevel\n\n### FreeBSD\n\nThe GitHub CLI port is supported by the FreeBSD community with updates powered by FreeBSD ports.\n    sudo zypper update gh\n\n### Solus Linux\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is supported by the Solus Linux community with updates powered by getsolus/packages.\n\nTo install:\n    \n    sudo eopkg install github-cli\n\n### Spack\n\nSpack is a flexible package manager supporting multiple versions, configurations, platforms, and compilers for supercomputers, Linux, and macOS.\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is supported by the Spack community with updates powered by spack/spack-packages.\n\nTo install:\n    \n    spack install gh\n\nTo upgrade:\n    \n    spack uninstall gh && spack install gh\n\n### Ubuntu Community\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is synced from upstream Debian Community package.\n\nNote\n\nAs of November 2025, GitHub CLI maintainers strongly recommend official Debian packages especially as the community-distributed `2.45.x` / `2.46.x` version is broken due to deprecated GitHub APIs.\n\n### Void Linux\n\nThe GitHub CLI package: is supported by the Void Linux community with updates powered by void-linux/void-packages.\n\nTo install:\n    \n    sudo xbps-install github-cli\n\n### Webi\n\nWebi is a tool that aims to effortlessly install developer tools with easy-to-remember URLs from official builds quickly, without sudo or Admin, without a package manager, and without changing system file permissions.\n\nThe GitHub CLI package is supported by the Webi community with updates powered by webinstall/webi-installers.\n\nTo install:\n    \n    curl -sS https://webi.sh/gh | sh\n\nTo upgrade:\n    \n    webi gh@stable\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncli/docs/install_linux.md at trunk · cli/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_linux.md?plain=1)\nciteturn66search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; > Our Linux packages and repository metadata are signed with the following PGP key fingerprints: ... && echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/githubcli-archive-keyring.gpg] https://cli.github.com/packages stable main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/github-cli.list > /dev/null \\ ... The [GitHub CLI package](https://pkgsrc.se/net/gh) is supported by the NetBSD community with updates powered by [NetBSD/pkgsrc](https://github.com/NetBSD/pkgsrc/tree/trunk/net/gh). ... The GitHub CLI package is supported by the Solus Linux community with updates powered by [getsolus/packages](https://github.com/getsolus/packages/blob/main/packages/g/github-cli/). ... [Webi](https://webinstall.dev/) is a tool that aims to effortlessly install developer tools with easy-to-remember URLs from official builds quickly, without sudo or Admin, without a package manager, and without changing system file permissions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - cli/cli: GitHub’s official command line tool · GitHub (https://github.com/cli/cli)\nciteturn66search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; AGENTS.md  | AGENTS.md  |    | ... GitHub CLI's PGP signing key rotation for Linux package repositories is effective September 5, 2026; users experiencing package installation or update problems can find solutions in the public announcement. ... If a specific version is needed, your GitHub Actions workflow will need to install it based on the macOS, Linux & Unix, or Windows instructions above. ... Since version 2.50.0, `gh` has been producing Build Provenance Attestation, enabling a cryptographically verifiable paper-trail back to the origin GitHub repository, git revision, and build instructions used. ...           --certificate-identity=\"https://github.com/cli/cli/.github/workflows/deployment.yml@refs/heads/trunk\" \\ ... For many years, hub was the unofficial GitHub CLI tool. `gh` is a new project that helps us explore what an official GitHub CLI tool can look like with a fundamentally different design.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ngithub-cli/docs/install_linux.md at trunk · tep/github-cli · GitH