XUS_APPROVAL_MODE)?.trim().toLowerCase();\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:236:  let approvalMode: ApprovalMode;\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:240:    approvalMode = \"read-only\";\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:242:    approvalMode = \"auto\";\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:245:    approvalMode = \"review\";\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:247:    approvalMode = modeOption as ApprovalMode;\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:248:    if (approvalMode === \"auto\" && options.yes) fullAccess = true;\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:250:    approvalMode = envMode as ApprovalMode;\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:251:    if (approvalMode === \"auto\") fullAccess = true;\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:255:    approvalMode = fullAccess ? \"auto\" : \"review\";\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:312:    approvalMode,\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:227:  const repl = new InteractiveRepl(app, config.approvalMode, resumeId);\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:172:- Client work that touched `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` (PLAN-01 task 8, `--yes`) was deferred while judging was open. That deferral has ended; update the demo alongside the client where needed. The runner may continue to pass `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` when required by the current CLI contract.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:140:- `HarnessConfig.approvalMode: \"auto\" | \"review\" | \"read-only\"`. This replaces the boolean `autoApprove` flags in the REPL and sidecar. `--mode auto` selects auto with per-origin egress approval; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass egress approval too. `--approve` selects review and `--read-only` selects read-only.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:146:- Unset approval mode defaults to review regardless of folder trust. Release notes and startup messaging must distinguish permission mode from folder trust. Use `--mode auto` for automatic writes and commands with per-origin egress approval; use `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` or `--yes` for full access.\n| [DEC-14](#dec-14-free-text-on-the-command-line) | Free text on the command line | Explicit `nexus run` required | No |\n| [DEC-15](#dec-15-knowledge-auto-extraction) | Knowledge auto-extraction | Off by default, opt-in | No |\n| [DEC-16](#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment) | Standalone qualification with no direct worker access | Stripping proxy over the gateway for live runs, plus server-kind conformance fixtures | No |\n| [DEC-17](#dec-17-token-estimator-floor-versus-the-calibration-band) | Token-estimator floor vs the ACC-VER-07 calibration band | The REQ-AGT-118 ≥ 1 token/char floor takes precedence for merging scripts; the resulting over-estimate is an accepted, bounded bias | No |\n\n---\n\n## DEC-01: Default execution posture\n\n**Question.** What protects the user by default from model-initiated command execution and network egress? See SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05 and TUI-07.\n\n| Option | Description | Tradeoffs |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Review by default: write, exec and egress ask | Safest. More prompts. Changes existing users' habits. |\n| B | Auto with an enforced sandbox by default | Few prompts. bwrap is unavailable on some hosts (WSL, rootless containers), and the Docker fallback is unpinned and networked. Egress is unsolved. |\n| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\n| D | Keep auto | Contradicts REQ-SEC-101; rejected. |\n\n**Rationale.** Folder trust protects project instructions and workspace integrations from being loaded before the operator approves those sources. Tool authority is governed by the operator's permission settings and must not change when a folder is trusted. A configured `auto` mode remains the operator's choice; when no permission mode is configured, Nexus defaults to `review`.\n\n**Amendment (2026-10-24, operator direction).** This supersedes the original trust-derived mode and approval behavior. Trust affects project instruction and integration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\n\n**Further rules:**\n- Headless `nexus run` with no TTY: decision-required calls are DENIED with a typed reason unless `--yes` is given.\n- The eval and demo runners pass `--yes` explicitly.\n\n**Affected requirements:** REQ-SEC-101, 102 and 119; REQ-TUI-102; SPEC-01; PLAN-01; ACC-SAFE-01.\n\n## DEC-02: Role of the REPL\n\n**Options.** (A) Remove the REPL. **(B, chosen)** The REPL is a supported secondary surface: used for non-TTY input, scripting and fallback, with its approvals fixed to the TUI's standard. (C) The REPL stays the default.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":54192}},"started_at_ms":1792906048400,"completed_at_ms":1792906048401}}
