{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:36:52.763Z","ordinal":326149,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e5afa8e9-51b1-4f04-9db3-01db27eb0be8","process_id":"16580","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 1 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json number,state,title,updatedAt,comments && gh release list --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --limit 8 --json tagName,name,publishedAt,isDraft,isPrerelease"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 1 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json number,state,title,updatedAt,comments && gh release list --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --limit 8 --json tagName,name,publishedAt,isDraft,isPrerelease"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABc0NUhA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6228759684\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTjsA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\n\\n**Done**\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\n\\n**Still open before this can close**\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record.\\n2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: {dir, into, command}` form. Running them requires the hardened-legacy evaluator in PR #33, which is still open with changes requested.\\n\\nREQ-QUAL-101 is still `open`, correctly.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6252979120\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLY8Aw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\n\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):\\n     - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks\\n     - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task\\n     - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task\\n   - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstream code in the public Nexus repository (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` records only task IDs and SHA-256 digests).\\n   - The full per-task `(id, repo, commit, spdx, license_file, license_sha256)` table is sealed inside `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2/LICENSE-AUDIT-2026-10-18.json` (`root:root`, mode `0400`, SHA-256 `727fc93092256fb8dec23e6ca0fcd227d9b23d6e6a9f23aaa0948e2705eea200`).\\n2. **T3 Sealed `heldout-t3` Corpus (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json` SHA-256 `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`):**\\n   - All 8 T3 tasks are first-party clean-room fixtures authored specifically for Nexus v1.0.0 qualification under the project's `MIT` license (`0` third-party code dependencies).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6253067267\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdNi7_Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contract can be registered before any scored execution; preserve all existing thresholds/corpus. Separately, the qualification runner needs current nonsecret served weights SHA and server-build identity from authoritative gateway deployment evidence (alias engineering/deep alone is insufficient); provide that metadata through the authorized runtime/custody boundary. No new private-store access is requested for implementation sessions. Peer runtime binaries are now rootowned/hash-pinned, but no RC or qualification claim is made.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6255328253\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdOTZNQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.\\n\\nCustodian: please provide an updated attestation for the already sealed manifest (or say which item needs a new immutable corpus version) covering those checks, including safe metadata for effective ACL/group access as root/operator/evaluator/implementer identities, task/validator store separation, setup/reference validation reproducibility, and derivation of private digests. Do not send objectives, payloads, reference solutions, validator contents, answers or credentials. Preserve the sealed manifest and record any supersession before changing content. No T2/T3/T4 qualification has been started by this coordinator.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6256122165\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeAFf4w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custody checkpoint (2026-10-21; candidate `v1/integration@833eec62`)**\\n\\nThe public T2 manifest metadata has the documented 40-task coverage, but independent metadata review does not establish private digest derivation, author-session independence/exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective store access controls, or custodian acceptance. No held-out payload or validator was accessed, and no qualification run has started.\\n\\nThe latest authoring progress recorded here (4/20 repository-arm tasks validated) is historical. Please update only the safe status metadata: whether the replacement author completed and froze the required 40-task T2 set and 8-task T3 set; whether any content changed after the public manifest was sealed; and whether the custodian has independently verified private digests, exposure history, reproducible setup/reference validation, access separation, immutable manifest identity, and custody acceptance. If the corpus changed, record a new immutable version and supersession before qualification.\\n\\nPlease do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, hidden answers, validators, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and the evaluator-boundary gates are established.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T04:50:24Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6308323299\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeFr82g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only qualification follow-up (current code audit at `origin/v1/integration@cc5eba2f428c7cdde33550d456506f31e3824f2e`; no private store or payload accessed): the public T2 manifest is still the sealed 40-task identity (`50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`). The current evaluator validator accepts the blackbox-v1 oracle contract, while the prior custody report describes T2 as using the legacy `hidden.command` form; the existing `eval/README.md` says compatibility requires custodian-led conversion/replacement and a new immutable manifest identity with custody checks repeated. Thus T2 qualification cannot start against the current manifest.\\n\\nCustodian: please reply with status metadata only: (1) whether the sealed T2 payload remains unchanged; (2) whether the author/custodian will produce a compatible immutable successor and repeat validation/custody checks, or whether an already-approved compatibility path exists; (3) expected completion/owner; and (4) whether T3 custody/identity remains unchanged. Do not post task IDs, objectives, source repositories, payloads, patches, reference solutions, validator contents, answers, or credentials. Keep the sealed corpus immutable until any successor is recorded with explicit supersession. Public metadata approval remains separate from private custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T10:53:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6314196186\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeHMGgA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up (no private store, payload, validator, or answer accessed): we have no custodian update since the 10:53Z request. Please post only safe status metadata for the sealed T2/T3 identities: whether the replacement author completed the required set, whether any sealed content changed, whether independent digest/setup/reference checks and effective access separation are complete, and whether T2 will use an approved compatible immutable successor. If work is still underway, please include the responsible role and a reasonable ETA. Do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until the custodian records acceptance and the evaluator compatibility path is resolved.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:21:32Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6315771520\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeKkA9g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the v1.0.0 release coordinator: the custody and compatibility gates remain on the release critical path, and there has been no custodian update since the 12:21 UTC request. Please acknowledge whether the independent custodian/replacement author is actively working, identify the responsible role, and provide a current ETA or state that the lane is unavailable. Status only: do not include task identifiers, repository URLs, objectives, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance and a compatible immutable T2 identity.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T15:06:44Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6319309046\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeaOYKA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release checkpoint, 2026-10-22 07:56 UTC (public metadata only; no held-out files accessed): exact current `main` remains `8935918455a7fcc9434762712528c1169ec4ff63`. PR #140 now records a 10/10 synthetic host preflight and has exact-head CI running, including the resource containment fixtures; no held-out task has been run. The public T2 identity remains the 40-task manifest previously reported, but custody acceptance and compatibility with the current black-box runner are still unverified here.\\n\\nCustodian/replacement author: please provide a safe status update only: (1) current assigned owner and whether authoring/validation is active; (2) whether any sealed content changed, and if so the new immutable identity/supersession; (3) whether independent private digest, exposure-history, setup/reference, effective-access, and task/evaluator separation checks are complete; (4) whether an approved runner-compatible immutable T2 successor is underway and its ETA; (5) T3 custody status. Do not include task IDs, objectives, repositories, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains gated until the custodian records acceptance. Contest freeze is not applicable; the contest is over.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T07:56:01Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6335731752\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeh6rXw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custodian coordination update, current source `main@19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`. PR #145 has integrated the version-synchronized RC2 source candidate; exact post-merge source CI is still running. No held-out payload, private validator, answer, or author log was accessed.\\n\\nPlease reply with safe status metadata only:\\n1. Who currently owns replacement authorship and independent custody, and are they actively working?\\n2. Are all 40 tasks fully authored, setup/reference-validated, and independently digested under the sealed manifest, or did task content change?\\n3. Has the evaluator compatibility issue with the required isolated `blackbox-v1` format been resolved by a custodian-approved immutable version or compatibility path?\\n4. Has the custodian verified effective store/parent access restrictions and separation from task execution, then accepted custody for qualification?\\n\\nDo not include payloads, solutions, private validator content, or credentials in this public issue. If there is no active custodian, please identify the concrete handoff needed so this qualification lane can proceed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T14:54:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6343797599\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABejrYNA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up: the latest T2/T3 custody attestations are from October 18, no current custodian claim or acknowledged handoff is visible, and the current qualification runner rejects T2's legacy `hidden.command` format. No held-out qualification has started.\\n\\nPlease have the current independent custodian confirm, without exposing private material:\\n\\n- who currently owns authoring and custody, and the claim/handoff reference;\\n- whether the public T2/T3 manifests remain the intended sealed identities or need a versioned successor;\\n- the approved path to resolve T2 runner compatibility, including whether a custodian-led conversion/replacement is in progress and its next checkpoint;\\n- whether fresh setup, reference-validation, access-boundary, and integrity checks can be attested against the accepted execution boundary.\\n\\nPlease do not post task payloads, hidden answers, validators, reference solutions, author logs, credentials, or private digests here. If no custodian is active, please say so at metadata level so an independent replacement can be assigned through the claims protocol.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T16:19:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6345644084\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeqG1lA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only compatibility follow-up (no private store, task payload, validator, answer, or author log accessed).\\n\\nThe current public evaluator contract does not define a generic, semantics-preserving adapter from legacy `hidden.command`/`hidden.dir` tasks to `blackbox-v1`. Its documented migration path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, repeat custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity.\\n\\nPlease answer only as safe status metadata:\\n\\n1. Can the sealed task validators be represented losslessly by `blackbox-v1` without changing covered behavior?\\n2. If yes, is the independent custodian authoring and revalidating a new immutable manifest, and what is the status/ETA?\\n3. If no, should the release record mark this corpus incompatible and awaiting custodian-authored replacement?\\n\\nNo task identifiers, objectives, source URLs, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials are needed. Qualification remains closed until custodian acceptance and compatibility evidence are recorded.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:08:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6352385428\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeuZ18g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody follow-up, current source `main@1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145` (no private corpus material accessed).\\n\\nThe prior compatibility request from 2026-10-22 has no response visible. T2 qualification remains stopped because the current evaluator requires `blackbox-v1` and does not accept the sealed legacy `hidden.command` format. Please provide a safe status update covering:\\n\\n- Whether the designated independent author/custodian is actively progressing the corpus and who currently owns the custody lane.\\n- Whether a custodian-verified, semantics-preserving conversion is possible, or whether a new immutable corpus version is required; include an ETA for the next public metadata checkpoint.\\n- Whether the custodian can provide a separate acceptance attestation for completeness/coverage, setup and reference validation, payload/validator digest derivation, access controls and author-session independence, without disclosing payloads or answers to implementers.\\n- If the current owner is unavailable, whether an explicit safe-boundary handoff to another authorized custodian can be arranged.\\n\\nNo qualification run will use the corpus until the custodian accepts its custody and integrity. Please keep private task content, validators, answers and author logs out of this public thread.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T03:46:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6356891122\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABez_Pjw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.\\n\\nRC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.\\n\\nPlease provide only safe status metadata:\\n- current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference;\\n- whether lossless conversion is being done by the custodian or a new immutable manifest is needed, with next checkpoint/ETA;\\n- whether completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, integrity, access controls, and author-session independence have been independently accepted;\\n- if no custodian is active, confirm that so an authorized replacement can be assigned.\\n\\nPlease do not include task content, objectives, validators, answers, patches, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and runner compatibility are documented.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6362746767\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfB-4VA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved immutable resolution; and (4) whether access separation, digests, independence, and custody have been accepted. If the current custodian is unavailable, please state that explicitly and identify the authorized handoff needed. Do not post task payloads, answers, validators, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until independent custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6377420884\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfDJ2ew\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent custodian verifies completeness, coverage, integrity, and execution-boundary separation.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6378649211\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfRAGFQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release convergence update (public metadata only): post-merge CI and CodeQL now pass on current main `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca` (CI run `40156576300`, CodeQL run `40156576296`). RC4 remains the newest prerelease; no stable release or final-candidate qualification has been established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15, T4 has not run, and the reproducibility workflow has not run on an RC. The metadata-only custody request from 2026-10-24 02:16 UTC remains unanswered.\\n\\nPlease reply to that request with the current custodian/owner, status and expected timing for independent custody acceptance, and whether a lossless compatibility path or replacement corpus is planned for the current evaluator contract. Please keep the reply to public metadata; do not post prompts, answers, validators, or protected task content. No held-out payload has been accessed by this implementation lane.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6393169429\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"number\":1,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:10Z\"}\n[{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v1.0.0-rc.4\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\",\"tagName\":\"v1.0.0-rc.4\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v1.0.0-rc.3\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\",\"tagName\":\"v1.0.0-rc.3\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v1.0.0-rc.1\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-21T18:54:41Z\",\"tagName\":\"v1.0.0-rc.1\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.2\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-14T09:10:47Z\",\"tagName\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.2\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.1\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-13T20:11:01Z\",\"tagName\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.1\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":984580925}},"started_at_ms":1792906611778,"completed_at_ms":1792906612763}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:36:53.735Z","ordinal":326150,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1718f-d3e7-7d83-b34f-c16295e47451","call_id":"call_b1a738a215724be4b89c2cd066247c8b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"diff --git a/cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts b/cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts\nindex 55975d6..b9cc4b1 100644\n--- a/cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts\n+++ b/cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts\n@@ -1,61 +1,286 @@\n import * as fs from \"node:fs\";\n import * as path from \"node:path\";\n import { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\n+import { mkdirVerified, writeExclusiveVerified } from \"../safe_fs.js\";\n+\n+function openSelfIgnore(workspace: string, file: string, flags: number): number {\n+  const noFollow = fs.constants.O_NOFOLLOW;\n+  if (typeof noFollow !== \"number\") {\n+    throw new Error(\"Cannot safely access .nexus/.gitignore without O_NOFOLLOW support\");\n+  }\n+  const fd = fs.openSync(file, flags | noFollow | (fs.constants.O_NONBLOCK ?? 0));\n+  try {\n+    const stat = fs.fstatSync(fd);\n+    if (!stat.isFile() || stat.nlink > 1) {\n+      throw new Error(\"Refusing to access a non-file or hard-linked .nexus/.gitignore\");\n+    }\n+    const expected = path.join(fs.realpathSync(workspace), path.relative(path.resolve(workspace), path.resolve(file)));\n+    let descriptorPath: string | undefined;\n+    try {\n+      descriptorPath = fs.readlinkSync(`/proc/self/fd/${fd}`);\n+    } catch {\n+      // On platforms without /proc, verify the opened identity against the path.\n+    }\n+    if (descriptorPath !== undefined) {\n+      if (descriptorPath !== expected) {\n+        throw new Error(\".nexus/.gitignore changed location while it was being opened\");\n+      }\n+    } else {\n+      const named = fs.lstatSync(file);\n+      if (named.isSymbolicLink() || named.dev !== stat.dev || named.ino !== stat.ino || fs.realpathSync(file) !== expected) {\n+        throw new Error(\".nexus/.gitignore changed while it was being opened\");\n+      }\n+    }\n+    return fd;\n+  } catch (error) {\n+    fs.closeSync(fd);\n+    throw error;\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+function readSelfIgnore(workspace: string, file: string): string {\n+  const fd = openSelfIgnore(workspace, file, fs.constants.O_RDONLY);\n+  try {\n+    return fs.readFileSync(fd, \"utf-8\");\n+  } finally {\n+    fs.closeSync(fd);\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+function appendSelfIgnore(workspace: string, file: string, content: string): void {\n+  const fd = openSelfIgnore(workspace, file, fs.constants.O_WRONLY | fs.constants.O_APPEND);\n+  try {\n+    fs.writeSync(fd, content);\n+  } finally {\n+    fs.closeSync(fd);\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+function openExclude(file: string, expected: string): number {\n+  const noFollow = fs.constants.O_NOFOLLOW;\n+  if (typeof noFollow !== \"number\") {\n+    throw new Error(\"Cannot safely access Git info/exclude without O_NOFOLLOW support\");\n+  }\n+  const fd = fs.openSync(file, fs.constants.O_RDWR | fs.constants.O_APPEND | noFollow | (fs.constants.O_NONBLOCK ?? 0));\n+  try {\n+    const stat = fs.fstatSync(fd);\n+    if (!stat.isFile() || stat.nlink > 1) {\n+      throw new Error(\"Refusing to access a non-file or hard-linked Git info/exclude\");\n+    }\n+    let descriptorPath: string | undefined;\n+    try {\n+      descriptorPath = fs.readlinkSync(`/proc/self/fd/${fd}`);\n+    } catch {\n+      // On platforms without /proc, verify the opened identity against the path.\n+    }\n+    if (descriptorPath !== undefined) {\n+      if (descriptorPath !== expected) {\n+        throw new Error(\"Git info/exclude changed location while it was being opened\");\n+      }\n+    } else {\n+      const named = fs.lstatSync(file);\n+      if (named.isSymbolicLink() || named.dev !== stat.dev || named.ino !== stat.ino || fs.realpathSync(file) !== expected) {\n+        throw new Error(\"Git info/exclude changed while it was being opened\");\n+      }\n+    }\n+    return fd;\n+  } catch (error) {\n+    fs.closeSync(fd);\n+    throw error;\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+function readExclude(file: string, expected: string): string {\n+  const fd = openExclude(file, expected);\n+  try {\n+    return fs.readFileSync(fd, \"utf-8\");\n+  } finally {\n+    fs.closeSync(fd);\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+function appendExclude(file: string, expected: string, content: string): void {\n+  const fd = openExclude(file, expected);\n+  try {\n+    fs.writeSync(fd, content);\n+  } finally {\n+    fs.closeSync(fd);\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+function hasGitMarkerInAncestors(workspace: string): boolean {\n+  let current = path.resolve(workspace);\n+  while (true) {\n+    try {\n+      fs.lstatSync(path.join(current, \".git\"));\n+      return true;\n+    } catch (error) {\n+      if (typeof error !== \"object\" || error === null || !(\"code\" in error) || error.code !== \"ENOENT\") {\n+        throw new Error(\"Cannot determine whether Nexus state is inside a Git worktree\", { cause: error });\n+      }\n+    }\n+    const parent = path.dirname(current);\n+    if (parent === current) return false;\n+    current = parent;\n+  }\n+}\n \n /**\n- * Ensures .nexus/ is ignored by Git in the workspace by adding it to .git/info/exclude (REQ-PER-105).\n- * Called on first workspace write by FlightRecorder and WorktreeManager.\n+ * Ensures .nexus/ is ignored by Git in the workspace (REQ-PER-105).\n+ * The self-contained rule protects state even when Git metadata is read-only;\n+ * info/exclude remains a best-effort convenience for older clients and status output.\n  */\n export function ensureGitExclude(workspace: string): void {\n+  let excludePath: string | null = null;\n+  try {\n+    const out = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"--git-path\", \"info/exclude\"], {\n+      cwd: workspace,\n+      encoding: \"utf-8\",\n+      stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"ignore\"],\n+    }).trim();\n+    if (out) {\n+      excludePath = path.isAbsolute(out) ? out : path.resolve(workspace, out);\n+    }\n+  } catch {\n+    // Fall back only when an info/exclude file is already available without Git.\n+    const candidate = path.join(workspace, \".git\", \"info\", \"exclude\");\n+    if (fs.existsSync(path.dirname(candidate))) {\n+      excludePath = candidate;\n+    }\n+  }\n+\n+  if (!excludePath) {\n+    if (hasGitMarkerInAncestors(workspace)) {\n+      throw new Error(\"Cannot verify Nexus state is ignored because Git metadata is unavailable\");\n+    }\n+    return;\n+  }\n+\n+  let commonDirPath: string | null = null;\n+  let expectedExcludePath: string | null = null;\n+  try {\n+    const commonDir = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"--git-common-dir\"], {\n+      cwd: workspace,\n+      encoding: \"utf-8\",\n+      stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"ignore\"],\n+    }).trim();\n+    commonDirPath = fs.realpathSync(path.resolve(workspace, commonDir));\n+    expectedExcludePath = path.join(commonDirPath, \"info\", \"exclude\");\n+    if (path.resolve(excludePath) !== expectedExcludePath) expectedExcludePath = null;\n+  } catch {\n+    // Updating the convenience file is optional; self-ignore verification below is authoritative.\n+  }\n+\n+  const nexusDir = path.join(workspace, \".nexus\");\n+  mkdirVerified(workspace, nexusDir);\n+  const nexusGitIgnore = path.join(nexusDir, \".gitignore\");\n   try {\n-    let excludePath: string | null = null;\n+    // Open the existing file without following links and bind the descriptor to\n+    // the expected repository path before reading it.\n+    readSelfIgnore(workspace, nexusGitIgnore);\n+  } catch (error) {\n+    if (typeof error === \"object\" && error !== null && \"code\" in error && error.code === \"ENOENT\") {\n+      try {\n+        writeExclusiveVerified(workspace, nexusGitIgnore, \"*\\n\");\n+      } catch (createError) {\n+        // Another safe creator may have won the exclusive-create race. Any\n+        // link or redirected parent still fails in readSelfIgnore below.\n+        if (typeof createError !== \"object\" || createError === null || !(\"code\" in createError) || createError.code !== \"EEXIST\") {\n+          throw createError;\n+        }\n+      }\n+    } else {\n+      throw error;\n+    }\n+  }\n+  const ignoreContent = readSelfIgnore(workspace, nexusGitIgnore);\n+  const lastRule = ignoreContent\n+    .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n+    .map((line) => line.trimEnd())\n+    .filter((line) => line.length > 0 && !line.startsWith(\"#\"))\n+    .at(-1);\n+  if (lastRule !== \"*\") {\n+    const prefix = ignoreContent.length === 0 || ignoreContent.endsWith(\"\\n\") ? \"\" : \"\\n\";\n+    appendSelfIgnore(workspace, nexusGitIgnore, `${prefix}*\\n`);\n+  }\n+\n+  const isIgnored = (relativePath: string): boolean => {\n     try {\n-      const out = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"--git-path\", \"info/exclude\"], {\n+      execFileSync(\"git\", [\"check-ignore\", \"--quiet\", \"--no-index\", \"--\", relativePath], {\n         cwd: workspace,\n-        encoding: \"utf-8\",\n-        stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"ignore\"],\n-      }).trim();\n-      if (out) {\n-        excludePath = path.isAbsolute(out) ? out : path.resolve(workspace, out);\n-      }\n-    } catch {\n-      // Fallback if git binary or rev-parse fails\n-      const candidate = path.join(workspace, \".git\", \"info\", \"exclude\");\n-      if (fs.existsSync(path.dirname(candidate))) {\n-        excludePath = candidate;\n+        stdio: \"ignore\",\n+      });\n+      return true;\n+    } catch (error) {\n+      if (typeof error === \"object\" && error !== null && \"status\" in error && error.status === 1) {\n+        return false;\n       }\n+      throw new Error(`Could not verify whether ${relativePath} is ignored by Git`, { cause: error });\n     }\n+  };\n+\n+  const protectedProbes = [\n+    \".nexus/__nexus_ignore_probe__\",\n+    \".nexus/.gitignore\",\n+    \".nexus/flights/__nexus_ignore_probe__.flightlog\",\n+    \".nexus/worktrees/__nexus_ignore_probe__/state.json\",\n+    \".nexus/tasks/__nexus_ignore_probe__.json\",\n+  ];\n+  const allProbesIgnored = (): boolean => protectedProbes.every(isIgnored);\n+  if (!allProbesIgnored()) {\n+    throw new Error(\"Git still does not ignore all Nexus state paths after updating .nexus/.gitignore\");\n+  }\n \n-    if (!excludePath) return;\n+  // This file is not required for safety: .nexus/.gitignore provides the\n+  // effective rule without mutating Git metadata. Keep the legacy rules when\n+  // available, but tolerate read-only or unusual Git directories.\n+  try {\n+    if (!expectedExcludePath || !commonDirPath) return;\n \n-    if (fs.existsSync(excludePath)) {\n-      const content = fs.readFileSync(excludePath, \"utf-8\");\n-      const rules = new Set(content.split(/\\r?\\n/).map((line) => line.trim()));\n-      // Match whole rules, not substrings: a comment or an unrelated pattern that merely mentions\n-      // `.nexus` must not suppress the ignore rule (then `/commit`'s `git add -A` could stage state).\n-      const hasRule = (rule: string): boolean => rules.has(rule) || rules.has(`/${rule}`);\n-      const linesToAdd: string[] = [];\n-      if (!hasRule(\".nexus/\") && !hasRule(\".nexus\")) {\n-        linesToAdd.push(\".nexus/\");\n-      }\n-      if (!hasRule(\".nexus/worktrees/\") && !hasRule(\".nexus/worktrees\")) {\n-        linesToAdd.push(\".nexus/worktrees/\");\n+    try {\n+      readExclude(excludePath, expectedExcludePath);\n+    } catch (error) {\n+      if (typeof error !== \"object\" || error === null || !(\"code\" in error) || error.code !== \"ENOENT\") {\n+        throw error;\n       }\n-      if (!hasRule(\".nexus/flights/\") && !hasRule(\".nexus/flights\")) {\n-        linesToAdd.push(\".nexus/flights/\");\n+      try {\n+        writeExclusiveVerified(commonDirPath, expectedExcludePath, \"\");\n+      } catch (createError) {\n+        // Another safe creator may have won the exclusive-create race.\n+        if (typeof createError !== \"object\" || createError === null || !(\"code\" in createError) || createError.code !== \"EEXIST\") {\n+          throw createError;\n+        }\n       }\n-      if (linesToAdd.length > 0) {\n-        const prefix = content.endsWith(\"\\n\") || content.length === 0 ? \"\" : \"\\n\";\n-        fs.appendFileSync(excludePath, prefix + linesToAdd.join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\");\n+    }\n+\n+    const protectedPaths = [\n+      { path: \".nexus/\", rule: \".nexus/\" },\n+      { path: \".nexus/worktrees/__nexus_ignore_probe__\", rule: \".nexus/worktrees/\" },\n+      { path: \".nexus/flights/__nexus_ignore_probe__\", rule: \".nexus/flights/\" },\n+    ];\n+\n+    for (const { path: relativePath, rule } of protectedPaths) {\n\n--- release evidence paths ---\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s4a.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s4a.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s4b.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s4b.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s5.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s5.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s5_ctrlc.py\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s6.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s6.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s6_steer_cancel.py\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s6n.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s6n.py\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s6n.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s7_resume.py\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s7a.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s7a.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s7b.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s7b.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s8.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s8.screens.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s8_cancel_tool.py\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s9.notes.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s9_quit_tool.py\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/a2probe/parser_probe.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/a2probe/stager_probe.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/a2probe/tester_probe.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/a2probe/tokens_probe.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/README.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/logs/t2-bugfix-csv-1/agent.stdout.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/manifest.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/results.jsonl\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/standalone-llamacpp.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_chatgpt_pinned_2026-10-16.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/probes/e_run.sh\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/probes/p1.mjs\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/probes/p2.mjs\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/prv/err.mts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/prv/probe.mts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/prv/tls.mts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/release_snapshot_2026-10-16.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6537)\nTotal output lines: 2\n\n{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABc0NUhA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6228759684\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTjsA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\n\\n**Done**\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\n\\n**Still open before this can close**\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record.\\n2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: {dir, into, command}` form. Running them requires the hardened-legacy evaluator in PR #33, which is still open with changes requested.\\n\\nREQ-QUAL-101 is still `open`, correctly.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6252979120\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLY8Aw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\n\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):\\n     - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks\\n     - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task\\n     - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task\\n   - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstream code in the public Nexus repository (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` records only task IDs and SHA-256 digests).\\n   - The full per-task `(id, repo, commit, spdx, license_file, license_sha256)` table is sealed inside `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2/LICENSE-AUDIT-2026-10-18.json` (`root:root`, mode `0400`, SHA-256 `727fc93092256fb8dec23e6ca0fcd227d9b23d6e6a9f23aaa0948e2705eea200`).\\n2. **T3 Sealed `heldout-t3` Corpus (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json` SHA-256 `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`):**\\n   - All 8 T3 tasks are first-party clean-room fixtures authored specifically for Nexus v1.0.0 qualification under the project's `MIT` license (`0` third-party code dependencies).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6253067267\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdNi7_Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contract can be registered before any scored execution; preserve all existing thresholds/corpus. Separately, the qualification runner needs current nonsecret served weights SHA and server-build identity from authoritative gateway deployment evidence (alias engineering/deep alone is insufficient); provide that metadata through the authorized runtime/custody boundary. No new private-store access is requested for implementation sessions. Peer runtime binaries are now rootowned/hash-pinned, but no RC or qualification claim is made.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeh…3537 tokens truncated…d.\\n\\nNo qualification run will use the corpus until the custodian accepts its custody and integrity. Please keep private task content, validators, answers and author logs out of this public thread.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T03:46:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6356891122\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABez_Pjw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.\\n\\nRC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.\\n\\nPlease provide only safe status metadata:\\n- current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference;\\n- whether lossless conversion is being done by the custodian or a new immutable manifest is needed, with next checkpoint/ETA;\\n- whether completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, integrity, access controls, and author-session independence have been independently accepted;\\n- if no custodian is active, confirm that so an authorized replacement can be assigned.\\n\\nPlease do not include task content, objectives, validators, answers, patches, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and runner compatibility are documented.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6362746767\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfB-4VA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved immutable resolution; and (4) whether access separation, digests, independence, and custody have been accepted. If the current custodian is unavailable, please state that explicitly and identify the authorized handoff needed. Do not post task payloads, answers, validators, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until independent custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6377420884\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfDJ2ew\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent custodian verifies completeness, coverage, integrity, and execution-boundary separation.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6378649211\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfRAGFQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release convergence update (public metadata only): post-merge CI and CodeQL now pass on current main `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca` (CI run `40156576300`, CodeQL run `40156576296`). RC4 remains the newest prerelease; no stable release or final-candidate qualification has been established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15, T4 has not run, and the reproducibility workflow has not run on an RC. The metadata-only custody request from 2026-10-24 02:16 UTC remains unanswered.\\n\\nPlease reply to that request with the current custodian/owner, status and expected timing for independent custody acceptance, and whether a lossless compatibility path or replacement corpus is planned for the current evaluator contract. Please keep the reply to public metadata; do not post prompts, answers, validators, or protected task content. No held-out payload has been accessed by this implementation lane.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6393169429\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"number\":1,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:10Z\"}\n[{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v1.0.0-rc.4\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\",\"tagName\":\"v1.0.0-rc.4\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v1.0.0-rc.3\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\",\"tagName\":\"v1.0.0-rc.3\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v1.0.0-rc.1\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-21T18:54:41Z\",\"tagName\":\"v1.0.0-rc.1\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.2\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-14T09:10:47Z\",\"tagName\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.2\"},{\"isDraft\":false,\"isPrerelease\":true,\"name\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.1\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-13T20:11:01Z\",\"tagName\":\"v0.1.0-alpha.1\"}]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","create_time":1792906613.7350848}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
