orkspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\", () => {\norigin/main:cli/test/helpers/tui_surface_driver.py:4:paste, an approval in review mode (with buffered keys), cancellation, compaction, a verification failure, incomplete\norigin/main:cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:190:    assert.equal(result.approvalPrompt, mode !== \"auto\", \"approval mode is independent of folder trust\");\norigin/main:cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:256:    assert.equal(result.approvalPrompt, mode === \"review\");\norigin/main:cli/test/sidecar.test.ts:35:  const app = new ApplicationCore({ endpoint: gw.url, model: \"m\", maxSteps: 6, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", approvalMode: mode, fullAccess: mode === \"auto\" } as any);\norigin/main:cli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:67:    assert.match(rendered, /Trust and continue/);\norigin/main:cli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:72:    assert.match(rendered, /Tool approvals use permission settings/);\norigin/main:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:46:  test(\"folder trust alone keeps an unset permission mode in review\", () => {\norigin/main:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:51:    const { ws } = setupRepo(\"default-review-trusted\");\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:40:**Rationale.** Folder trust protects project instructions and workspace integrations from being loaded before the operator approves those sources. Tool authority is governed by the operator's permission settings and must not change when a folder is trusted. A configured `auto` mode remains the operator's choice; when no permission mode is configured, Nexus defaults to `review`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:42:**Amendment (2026-10-24, operator direction).** This supersedes the original trust-derived mode and approval behavior. Trust affects project instruction and integration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\n\n--- PR207 candidate state ---\n## v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed-current-main-016bbc3...origin/main [ahead 12]\n\n--- live suite child ---\n1072398 1070021    07:51:02 Sl+  kimi-code\n2726168 1072398    02:31:26 Ss   /bin/bash -c cd '/home/mike/nexus-code' && set -uo pipefail overall=0 while ps -p 2610156 >/dev/null 2>&1; do sleep 30; done run_suite() {   label=\"$1\"   dir=\"$2\"   printf '\\n===== BEGIN %s (%s) =====\\n' \"$label\" \"$dir\"   (     cd \"$dir\"     export HOME=$(mktemp -d)     export XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"     export CARGO_HOME=/home/mike/.cargo     export RUSTUP_HOME=/home/mike/.rustup     make build && make test   )   status=$?   printf '===== END %s status=%s =====\\n' \"$label\" \"$status\"   if [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then overall=1; fi } run_suite DOCTOR_SCHEMA2_JOURNAL /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-doctor-schema2-journal-snapshot run_suite NON_GIT_RESTORE /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-non-git-restore-snapshot run_suite SESSION_DURABLE_FIELDS /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-session-durable-fields-final-snapshot run_suite EVAL_RESOURCE_ASSERTION /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-eval-resource-assertion-snapshot run_suite READONLY_ADMISSION /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-readonly-mode-admission-snapshot exit \"$overall\"\n3337285 2726168       42:55 S    /bin/bash -c cd '/home/mike/nexus-code' && set -uo pipefail overall=0 while ps -p 2610156 >/dev/null 2>&1; do sleep 30; done run_suite() {   label=\"$1\"   dir=\"$2\"   printf '\\n===== BEGIN %s (