:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n\n--- terminal requirement details ---\n237-| REQ-QUAL-104 | DEC-05 | Separately reported metrics, including false VERIFIED = 0. | honesty | `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-005; test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts, test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-005 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n238-| REQ-QUAL-105 | TOP_TIER Q6; DEC-05 | T4 fault injection: 9 classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment 2026-10-17: union of the nine distinct scenarios retained), 100% truthful outcomes. | failure / recovery | `eval/model_proxy.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-001; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"the model proxy injects each scheduled fault\", test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T4 (ACCEPTANCE §6.2) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n239-| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n240-| REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n242-| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n243-| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n244-\n245-## 4. Contest requirements (separate product; not client gates)\n246-\n247-These are REQ-CON-101 to REQ-CON-107, specified in [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md). The submission was **completed** (2026-10-14), judging has concluded, and no contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment). Every row remains post-contest hardening with status `open`; no evidence status is promoted by this clarification. The evidence is `evidence/G_contest_eval.md` (CON-001 to CON-014).\n248-\n249-## 5. Post-v1 backlog (recorded, not dropped)\n250-\n251-- REQ-AGT-111: single step loop.\n252-- CTX-001 full provenance graph.\n253-- CTX-002: knowledge freshness.\n254-- DISC-005: encryption sinks.\n255-- ACT-002: configurable delegation depth.\n256-- EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE I3, I4, stale-lock race, corrupt lock.\n257-- `/tdd` phase enforcement (VER-08).\n258-- `nexus eval` scoring fix (VER-07b–e).\n259-- Per-role allowlists beyond reviewer and researcher.\n--\n272-Counts are from the tables above.\n273-\n274-| Group | Rows | Breakdown |\n275-|---|---|---|\n276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n277-| Carried rows (§2.1) | 29 | 14 tested and unchanged (Keep). 1 visually-accepted (REQ-TUI-001). The rest are partial, or have open items mapped to §3. |\n278-| Contest rows (§4) | 7 | Separate product. |\n279-\n280-**No requirement is `product-qualified`.**\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","create_time":1792906688.5314481}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
