{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:43:06.719Z","ordinal":326428,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b4c60101-af1a-4145-8713-dbb0fac73a59","process_id":"96592","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","set -e\nworktree=/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3\noldfile=$(mktemp /tmp/nexus-terminal-worksheet.XXXXXX)\ngit -C \"$worktree\" show v1/terminal-matrix-rc3:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md > \"$oldfile\"\nif [ -n \"$(git -C \"$worktree\" status --porcelain)\" ]; then echo 'terminal worksheet worktree is not clean'; exit 2; fi\nif pgrep -af '/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3' | rg -v 'pgrep|rg ' >/dev/null; then echo 'terminal worksheet has an active process'; exit 3; fi\ngit -C \"$worktree\" switch -c v1/terminal-matrix-rc4-worksheet origin/main\ncp \"$oldfile\" \"$worktree/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\"\npython3 - \"$worktree/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\" <<'PY'\nimport pathlib,sys\np=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]); s=p.read_text()\nrepl={\n'published RC3 candidate':'published RC4 candidate',\n'`v1.0.0-rc.3`':'`v1.0.0-rc.4`',\n'`1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`':'`57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`',\n'`nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`':'`nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.4.tar.gz`',\n'`efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`':'`07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`',\n'https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.3/':'https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.4/',\n'`9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`':'`30f7a6eab8138423c547147989020d547bdf17ada595e362914b95c45f6067af`',\n'expected `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`':'expected `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`',\n'export NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.3':'export NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.4',\n'`1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`':'`1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`',\n}\nfor a,b in repl.items(): s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace('Use the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. Do not run this while another Nexus process is using the target installation.','Use the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. If `gh attestation verify` reports that the desktop is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Do not run the installer while another Nexus process is using the target installation.')\ns=s.replace('export NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\\ncurl -fsSL','export NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\\nexport NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.4/prefix\"\\ncurl -fsSL')\ns=s.replace('nexus --version\\n```','nexus --version\\n```')\ns=s.replace('The identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after checking the target machine.','The identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. The Ubuntu E3 desktop package archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence, but the attested installer has not completed there because its GitHub CLI is unauthenticated. Matrix status remains 0/15. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after the installed RC identity has been checked on the target machine.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngit -C \"$worktree\" diff --check && git -C \"$worktree\" diff --stat && git -C \"$worktree\" diff -- docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | sed -n '1,180p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"set -e\nworktree=/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3\noldfile=$(mktemp /tmp/nexus-terminal-worksheet.XXXXXX)\ngit -C \"$worktree\" show v1/terminal-matrix-rc3:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md > \"$oldfile\"\nif [ -n \"$(git -C \"$worktree\" status --porcelain)\" ]; then echo 'terminal worksheet worktree is not clean'; exit 2; fi\nif pgrep -af '/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3' | rg -v 'pgrep|rg ' >/dev/null; then echo 'terminal worksheet has an active process'; exit 3; fi\ngit -C \"$worktree\" switch -c v1/terminal-matrix-rc4-worksheet origin/main\ncp \"$oldfile\" \"$worktree/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\"\npython3 - \"$worktree/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\" <<'PY'\nimport pathlib,sys\np=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]); s=p.read_text()\nrepl={\n'published RC3 candidate':'published RC4 candidate',\n'`v1.0.0-rc.3`':'`v1.0.0-rc.4`',\n'`1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`':'`57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`',\n'`nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`':'`nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.4.tar.gz`',\n'`efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`':'`07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`',\n'https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.3/':'https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.4/',\n'`9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`':'`30f7a6eab8138423c547147989020d547bdf17ada595e362914b95c45f6067af`',\n'expected `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`':'expected `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`',\n'export NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.3':'export NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.4',\n'`1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`':'`1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`',\n}\nfor a,b in repl.items(): s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace('Use the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. Do not run this while another Nexus process is using the target installation.','Use the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. If `gh attestation verify` reports that the desktop is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Do not run the installer while another Nexus process is using the target installation.')\ns=s.replace('export NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\\ncurl -fsSL','export NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\\nexport NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.4/prefix\"\\ncurl -fsSL')\ns=s.replace('nexus --version\\n```','nexus --version\\n```')\ns=s.replace('The identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after checking the target machine.','The identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. The Ubuntu E3 desktop package archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence, but the attested installer has not completed there because its GitHub CLI is unauthenticated. Matrix status remains 0/15. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after the installed RC identity has been checked on the target machine.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngit -C \"$worktree\" diff --check && git -C \"$worktree\" diff --stat && git -C \"$worktree\" diff -- docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | sed -n '1,180p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Switched to a new branch 'v1/terminal-matrix-rc4-worksheet'\nbranch 'v1/terminal-matrix-rc4-worksheet' set up to track 'origin/main'.\n docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--------\n 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nindex 25cde4e..d6f6d10 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n@@ -1,21 +1,40 @@\n # Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n \n-For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an unfilled recording template; it contains no test results and does not qualify an RC.\n+For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an operator recording template for the published RC4 candidate. It contains no terminal results and does not qualify an RC.\n \n ## Installed candidate identity\n \n Fill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n \n-- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n-- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n-- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n-- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n-- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n-- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n+- RC tag: `v1.0.0-rc.4`\n+- Full RC source commit: `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`\n+- Candidate archive: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.4.tar.gz`\n+- Published archive SHA256: `07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`\n+- Release asset: <https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.4/nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz>\n+- Published checksum index SHA256: `30f7a6eab8138423c547147989020d547bdf17ada595e362914b95c45f6067af`\n+- Installation procedure/run reference: record the operator's install run below; use the pinned RC3 release asset and verify `nexus --version`\n+- Installed package digest and path: record from the actual installation; expected archive SHA256 is above\n+- `nexus --version` output reference: record the actual output; expected `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`\n - Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n - Host OS and version: __________________________________\n - Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\n \n+### Install and identity check\n+\n+Use the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. If `gh attestation verify` reports that the desktop is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Do not run the installer while another Nexus process is using the target installation.\n+\n+```sh\n+export NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.4\n+export NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\n+export NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.4/prefix\"\n+curl -fsSL https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.4/install.sh | sh\n+nexus --version\n+```\n+\n+Before the first matrix cell, confirm the printed version is `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`, verify the installed version directory's `MANIFEST.sha256`, and record the matching `.provenance.json` archive digest. If any identity differs from the candidate fields above, stop and record the observed identity; do not combine results across artifacts. The checksum and provenance attestations are published with the RC3 release.\n+\n+The identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. The Ubuntu E3 desktop package archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence, but the attested installer has not completed there because its GitHub CLI is unauthenticated. Matrix status remains 0/15. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after the installed RC identity has been checked on the target machine.\n+\n Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n \n | Environment | Version / protocol details |\n@@ -38,7 +57,7 @@ Run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by\n 6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n 7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n \n-For each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n+For each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Use one continuous capture per cell when practical; redact unrelated personal paths or notifications without cropping away the terminal state. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n \n ## Terminal × size results\n \n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":291323229}},"started_at_ms":1792906986426,"completed_at_ms":1792906986719}}
