 (57b9285c6cea)`\n24:Use the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. If `gh attestation verify` reports that the desktop is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Do not run the installer while another Nexus process is using the target installation.\n29:export NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.4/prefix\"\n31:export PATH=\"$NEXUS_PREFIX/bin:$PATH\"\n35:Before the first matrix cell, confirm the printed version is `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`, verify the installed version directory's `MANIFEST.sha256`, and record the matching `.provenance.json` archive digest. If any identity differs from the candidate fields above, stop and record the observed identity; do not combine results across artifacts. The checksum and provenance attestations are published with the RC4 release.\n37:The identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. The Ubuntu E3 desktop package archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence, but the attested installer has not completed there because its GitHub CLI is unauthenticated. Matrix status remains 0/15. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after the installed RC identity has been checked on the target machine.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":761991938}},"started_at_ms":1792907033763,"completed_at_ms":1792907034526}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:43:55.661Z","ordinal":326468,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17196-440d-7e71-9bbd-7e3bf3360aea","call_id":"call_55489821d1ae4cedac1b39fb596a2655","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## v1/terminal-matrix-rc4-worksheet...origin/main [ahead 1]\n8edb725bcfa3443fa599a7fda228875b4424f7dc\n docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------\n 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)\n3:For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an operator recording template for the published RC4 candidate. It contains no terminal results and does not qualify an RC.\n10:- Full RC source commit: `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`\n12:- Published archive SHA256: `07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`\n14:- Published checksum index SHA256: `30f7a6eab8138423c547147989020d547bdf17ada595e362914b95c45f6067af`\n15:- Installation procedure/run reference: record the operator's install run below; use the pinned RC4 release asset and verify `nexus --version`\n17:- `nexus --version` output reference: record the actual output; expected `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`\n24:Use the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. If `gh attestation verify` reports that the desktop is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Do not run the installer while another Nexus process is using the target installation.\n29:export NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.4/prefix\"\n31:export PATH=\"$NEXUS_PREFIX/bin:$PATH\"\n35:Before the first matrix cell, confirm the printed version is `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`, verify the installed version directory's `MANIFEST.sha256`, and record the matching `.provenance.json` archive digest. If any identity differs from the candidate fields above, stop and record the observed identity; do not combine results across artifacts. The checksum and provenance attestations are published with the RC4 release.\n37:The identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. The Ubuntu E3 desktop package archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence, but the attested installer has not completed there because its GitHub CLI is unauthenticated. Matrix status remains 0/15. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after the installed RC identity has been checked on the target machine.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","create_time":1792907035.661146}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
