{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:44:46.691Z","ordinal":326519,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5331aca8-0b31-4b72-9d51-e2cc9144cb6b","process_id":"10199","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,90p' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,90p' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md","name":"TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n\nFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an operator recording template for the published RC4 candidate. It contains no terminal results and does not qualify an RC.\n\n## Installed candidate identity\n\nFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n\n- RC tag: `v1.0.0-rc.4`\n- Full RC source commit: `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`\n- Candidate archive: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.4.tar.gz`\n- Published archive SHA256: `07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`\n- Release asset: <https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.4/nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.4.tar.gz>\n- Published checksum index SHA256: `30f7a6eab8138423c547147989020d547bdf17ada595e362914b95c45f6067af`\n- Installation procedure/run reference: record the operator's install run below; use the pinned RC4 release asset and verify `nexus --version`\n- Installed package digest and path: record from the actual installation; expected archive SHA256 is above\n- `nexus --version` output reference: record the actual output; expected `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n- Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\n\n### Install and identity check\n\nUse the published, version-pinned installer, then record the command transcript (with secrets omitted), installation prefix, and UTC time. If `gh attestation verify` reports that the desktop is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Do not run the installer while another Nexus process is using the target installation.\n\n```sh\nexport NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.4\nexport NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\nexport NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.4/prefix\"\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.4/install.sh | sh\nexport PATH=\"$NEXUS_PREFIX/bin:$PATH\"\nnexus --version\n```\n\nBefore the first matrix cell, confirm the printed version is `1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)`, verify the installed version directory's `MANIFEST.sha256`, and record the matching `.provenance.json` archive digest. If any identity differs from the candidate fields above, stop and record the observed identity; do not combine results across artifacts. The checksum and provenance attestations are published with the RC4 release.\n\nThe identity above is the published candidate identity, not a claim that every operator machine has installed it. The Ubuntu E3 desktop package archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence, but the attested installer has not completed there because its GitHub CLI is unauthenticated. Matrix status remains 0/15. Complete the operator, host, path, timestamp, and actual-command fields only after the installed RC identity has been checked on the target machine.\n\nRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n\n| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n|---|---|\n| xterm | |\n| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n| GNOME Terminal | |\n\n## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n\nRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n\n1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nFor each cell, archive a screenshot of the approval panel and a screenshot of the post-exit terminal state. Record a separate evidence/result reference where useful. Use one continuous capture per cell when practical; redact unrelated personal paths or notifications without cropping away the terminal state. Automated PTY runs and screenshots do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n\n## Terminal × size results\n\nSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Add the approval-panel and post-exit screenshot references for every cell. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n\n| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Evidence / result reference | Approval-panel screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Failure disposition / notes |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n\n## Acceptance gate\n\n- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":732926835}},"started_at_ms":1792907085958,"completed_at_ms":1792907086691}}
