{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:45:05.356Z","ordinal":326538,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2d993a9a-0c4c-4e1f-b548-b347667a1a41","process_id":"95731","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md')\ns=p.read_text()\nstart=s.index('## Installed candidate identity')\nend=s.index('Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used.')\nreplacement='''## Installed candidate identity\n\nLeave this section blank until the next release candidate is published and installed on the E3 desktop. Bind every cell to that exact candidate; do not use a checkout build or an older RC.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Candidate archive and published SHA256: _________________\n- Published checksum-index SHA256: _______________________\n- Release asset URL: _____________________________________\n- Installation prefix and provenance run reference: ________\n- Installed package `MANIFEST.sha256` result: ______________\n- `.provenance.json` archive digest: ______________________\n- Exact `nexus --version` output: _________________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: Ubuntu 26.04 (verified 2026-10-25)\n- Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\n\n### Candidate gate and install instructions\n\n**Do not run the acceptance matrix against RC4.** The published RC4 source selects `auto` for trusted folders. The user-directed DEC-01 amendment on current integration makes approval mode independent of folder trust and defaults to `review`. RC4 therefore does not qualify the current behavior. Wait for the next RC to be published from a source revision containing that amendment; then fill in the exact identity above before testing.\n\nOn the E3 desktop, if `gh attestation verify` reports that GitHub CLI is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Use the version-pinned installer only after the next RC is available:\n\n```sh\nexport NEXUS_VERSION='<exact-published-next-RC-tag>'\nexport NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\nexport NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/$NEXUS_VERSION/prefix\"\ncurl -fsSL \"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/$NEXUS_VERSION/install.sh\" | sh\nexport PATH=\"$NEXUS_PREFIX/bin:$PATH\"\nnexus --version\n```\n\nBefore the first matrix cell, confirm the printed version matches the candidate fields, verify the installed version directory's `MANIFEST.sha256`, and record the matching `.provenance.json` archive digest. If any identity differs, stop and record the observed identity; do not combine results across artifacts. The desktop's RC4 archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence only; RC4 was not installed through the attested installer and no acceptance cell was run. Current manual matrix status is 0/15.\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+replacement+s[end:]\ns=s.replace('| xterm | |','| xterm | XTerm(407) |')\ns=s.replace('| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |','| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | kitty 0.45.0; protocol must be enabled and verified at run time |')\ns=s.replace('| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |','| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux 3.6; GNOME Terminal 3.58.0 |')\ns=s.replace('| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |','| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code 1.143.1; record integrated terminal profile at run time |')\ns=s.replace('| GNOME Terminal | |','| GNOME Terminal | 3.58.0 |')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngit diff --check && rg -n 'RC4|rc\\.4|1\\.0\\.0-rc\\.N|0/15|XTerm|kitty 0|tmux 3|VS Code' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md && git diff --stat"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md')\ns=p.read_text()\nstart=s.index('## Installed candidate identity')\nend=s.index('Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used.')\nreplacement='''## Installed candidate identity\n\nLeave this section blank until the next release candidate is published and installed on the E3 desktop. Bind every cell to that exact candidate; do not use a checkout build or an older RC.\n\n- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n- Candidate archive and published SHA256: _________________\n- Published checksum-index SHA256: _______________________\n- Release asset URL: _____________________________________\n- Installation prefix and provenance run reference: ________\n- Installed package `MANIFEST.sha256` result: ______________\n- `.provenance.json` archive digest: ______________________\n- Exact `nexus --version` output: _________________________\n- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n- Host OS and version: Ubuntu 26.04 (verified 2026-10-25)\n- Screen capture evidence directory: _____________________\n\n### Candidate gate and install instructions\n\n**Do not run the acceptance matrix against RC4.** The published RC4 source selects `auto` for trusted folders. The user-directed DEC-01 amendment on current integration makes approval mode independent of folder trust and defaults to `review`. RC4 therefore does not qualify the current behavior. Wait for the next RC to be published from a source revision containing that amendment; then fill in the exact identity above before testing.\n\nOn the E3 desktop, if `gh attestation verify` reports that GitHub CLI is unauthenticated, run `gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web` in a user-controlled desktop terminal and complete the browser sign-in there. Do not pass a token through SSH, shell arguments, or evidence. Use the version-pinned installer only after the next RC is available:\n\n```sh\nexport NEXUS_VERSION='<exact-published-next-RC-tag>'\nexport NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1\nexport NEXUS_PREFIX=\"$HOME/nexus-qualification/$NEXUS_VERSION/prefix\"\ncurl -fsSL \"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/download/$NEXUS_VERSION/install.sh\" | sh\nexport PATH=\"$NEXUS_PREFIX/bin:$PATH\"\nnexus --version\n```\n\nBefore the first matrix cell, confirm the printed version matches the candidate fields, verify the installed version directory's `MANIFEST.sha256`, and record the matching `.provenance.json` archive digest. If any identity differs, stop and record the observed identity; do not combine results across artifacts. The desktop's RC4 archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence only; RC4 was not installed through the attested installer and no acceptance cell was run. Current manual matrix status is 0/15.\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+replacement+s[end:]\ns=s.replace('| xterm | |','| xterm | XTerm(407) |')\ns=s.replace('| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |','| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | kitty 0.45.0; protocol must be enabled and verified at run time |')\ns=s.replace('| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |','| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux 3.6; GNOME Terminal 3.58.0 |')\ns=s.replace('| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |','| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code 1.143.1; record integrated terminal profile at run time |')\ns=s.replace('| GNOME Terminal | |','| GNOME Terminal | 3.58.0 |')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngit diff --check && rg -n 'RC4|rc\\.4|1\\.0\\.0-rc\\.N|0/15|XTerm|kitty 0|tmux 3|VS Code' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md && git diff --stat"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"3:For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an operator recording template for the published RC4 candidate. It contains no terminal results and does not qualify an RC.\n24:**Do not run the acceptance matrix against RC4.** The published RC4 source selects `auto` for trusted folders. The user-directed DEC-01 amendment on current integration makes approval mode independent of folder trust and defaults to `review`. RC4 therefore does not qualify the current behavior. Wait for the next RC to be published from a source revision containing that amendment; then fill in the exact identity above before testing.\n37:Before the first matrix cell, confirm the printed version matches the candidate fields, verify the installed version directory's `MANIFEST.sha256`, and record the matching `.provenance.json` archive digest. If any identity differs, stop and record the observed identity; do not combine results across artifacts. The desktop's RC4 archive and internal manifest were verified as setup evidence only; RC4 was not installed through the attested installer and no acceptance cell was run. Current manual matrix status is 0/15.\n39:Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n43:| xterm | XTerm(407) |\n44:| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | kitty 0.45.0; protocol must be enabled and verified at run time |\n45:| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux 3.6; GNOME Terminal 3.58.0 |\n46:| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code 1.143.1; record integrated terminal profile at run time |\n75:| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\n76:| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] F