{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:30:16.998Z","ordinal":327376,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda1f648f481a08a8044e6a33464fc","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign status: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`**  \n**Acceptance: `IN_PROGRESS`**\n\n- Exact `origin/main` is `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f`. CI run `40165934790` and CodeQL `40165934792` passed on that revision, including Node 22/24 and Linux packaging/reproducibility.\n- Your “default to review” choice matches current main’s DEC-01 behavior. **RC4 does not qualify** because its trusted-folder default is `auto`.\n- The terminal worksheet candidate at `2b55c031` received independent ACCEPT. Its 15-cell human matrix remains **0/15**; see [terminal matrix worksheet](/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md).\n- RC5 notes at `8b7c09c` received independent ACCEPT; no RC5 tag, publication, or acceptance is claimed. See [RC5 release notes](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md).\n- PR #207 remains stale on base `19b30a4` with cancelled Node checks. Its exact-main replacement candidate `7a5d4dcc` has independent ACCEPT and a clean diff, but still needs tests and a new branch/PR.\n- The exclusive local suite is active on the read-only-admission snapshot, currently in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. I did not start overlapping tests. Held-out custody remains unanswered; no held-out qualification has run.\n\nNext, I’ll validate the Git-isolation candidate after the suite releases, then advance its PR and the RC sequence. No operator action is needed now."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792909814329,"completed_at_ms":1792909816998}}
