6c","turn_id":"01a171c1-0652-7382-b539-55af51f4c56c","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add9d524b1c81a0b25ab37889d13223","order":16449,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a171ae-8bc7-7162-8c6c-cfb30961ec4d","text":"Current-main CI is now fully green on exact `016bbc3`: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility all passed; CodeQL also passed. This is source-branch evidence only. The accepted Git-isolation replacement still needs its own focused/full validation and PR checks, which must wait for the active serialized local suite.","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda10b5f0c81a09f00341e54d3ebb1","order":16466,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a171bd-16b5-77a1-a7f2-7cf293506490","text":"The RC5 notes now have an independent ACCEPT against exact `8b7c09c`: merged PR scopes are accurate, PR #207 remains excluded, and the notes make no claim that RC5 is tagged or accepted. The final serialized local suite is still the remaining validation dependency before I can run the Git-isolation candidate checks.","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda1f648f481a08a8044e6a33464fc","order":16471,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a171c0-b4ae-7cd1-b6e8-91a6fe5070d1","text":"**Campaign status: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`**  \n**Acceptance: `IN_PROGRESS`**\n\n- Exact `origin/main` is `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f`. CI run `40165934790` and CodeQL `40165934792` passed on that revision, including Node 22/24 and Linux packaging/reproducibility.\n- Your “default to review” choice matches current main’s DEC-01 behavior. **RC4 does not qualify** because its trusted-folder default is `auto`.\n- The terminal worksheet candidate at `2b55c031` received independent ACCEPT. Its 15-cell human matrix remains **0/15**; see [terminal matrix worksheet](/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md).\n- RC5 notes at `8b7c09c` received independent ACCEPT; no RC5 tag, publication, or acceptance is claimed. See [RC5 release notes](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md).\n- PR #207 remains stale on base `19b30a4` with cancelled Node checks. Its exact-main replacement candidate `7a5d4dcc` has independent ACCEPT and a clean diff, but still needs tests and a new branch/PR.\n- The exclusive local suite is active on the read-only-admission snapshot, currently in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. I did not start overlapping tests. Held-out custody remains unanswered; no held-out qualification has run.\n\nNext, I’ll validate the Git-isolation candidate after the suite releases, then advance its PR and the RC sequence. No operator action is needed now.","turn_id":"01a17189-d092-7ab1-ba2e-16c982c7dc3c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda210af3c81a09743adc9c898da0e","order":16472,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a171c1-11d4-70a2-ab30-94469ec27a1c","text":"I’m checking the live suite and exact-main status first, then I’ll take the next action that the released claims and validation state allow.","turn_id":"01a171c1-0652-7382-b539-55af51f4c56c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda239e75481a0afef6c0b001e0bf8","order":16473,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a171c1-b4cb-7fb3-a1fa-be193a620394","text":"The Git-isolation lane advanced while I was monitoring the suite: its owner pushed a normal fast-forward update to PR #207 and started fresh checks. I’m reconciling that exact remote head and workflow state now; I won’t duplicate the push or test run.","turn_id":"01a171c1-0652-7382-b539-55af51f4c56c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda27d226c81a0ae734a573a071be3","order":16474,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a171c2-bb63-7131-abb3-e950c5410a52","text":"PR #207’s new Node 22/24 checks are running, and CodeQL passed. I found a separate mergeability issue: GitHub still reports the PR base as `19b30a4` and shows 18 changed files, even though current main is `016bbc3` and the reviewed candidate diff is six files. I recorded this in the coordination log; it must be refreshed and rechecked before merge.","turn_id":"01a171c1-0652-7382-b539-55af51f4c56c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda2ebed1081a084a53641badd9615","order":16481,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a171c4-6cb3-78a0-9c30-f17b9378693b","text":"Independent re-review accepted PR #207’s exact head `fb36b03`: versus current main it is still the same six-file patch, with no unreviewed changes. The apparent extra 12 files are already on main; I’ve recorded the reviewer’s recommendation to refresh the PR’s displayed base before merge. Node checks and the local suite are still running.","turn_id":"01a171c1-0652-7382-b539-55af51f4c56c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda531e23481a0839b47d79edd9ac0","order":16490,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a171cd-4d01-7c50-8022-b43822626596","text":"The exact-head PR #207 jobs and the serialized local suite remain active, with test processes still advancing. The independent review is complete, and the stale-base finding is recorded. No failures have appeared; I’m keeping the remaining validation queued behind these live runs.","turn_id":"01a171c1-0652-7382-b539-55af51f4c56c"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":16495,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at deliv