{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:49:24.537Z","ordinal":327787,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171c1-0652-7382-b539-55af51f4c56c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6cbfecb5-f058-4fde-82cb-884ac69e40d7","process_id":"87485","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find /home/mike/nexus-wt -maxdepth 2 -type d -iname '*trust*' -o -iname '*startup*' | head -50; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code branch -a --list '*trust*' '*startup*'; rg -n \"folder trust|Trust this folder|default approval|approval mode\" /home/mike/nexus-code/cli /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-* 2>/dev/null | head -100; rg -n \"startup.*trust|folder trust\" /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -20"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"find /home/mike/nexus-wt -maxdepth 2 -type d -iname '*trust*' -o -iname '*startup*' | head -50; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code branch -a --list '*trust*' '*startup*'; rg -n \"folder trust|Trust this folder|default approval|approval mode\" /home/mike/nexus-code/cli /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-* 2>/dev/null | head -100; rg -n \"startup.*trust|folder trust\" /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -20"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-suite\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-folder-trust-copy\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-workspace-trust\n+ codex/startup-folder-trust-copy\n+ v1/startup-workspace-trust\n  v1/startup-workspace-trust-rebased\n  remotes/origin/codex/startup-folder-trust-copy\n  remotes/origin/codex/startup-folder-trust-copy-20261024\n  remotes/origin/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/cf-1.0.0-beta.18\n  remotes/origin/v1/startup-workspace-trust\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:9:| [DEC-01](#dec-01-default-execution-posture) | Default execution posture | Review by default; permission mode is independent of folder trust | No (resolved) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:42:**Amendment (2026-10-24, operator direction).** This supersedes the original trust-derived mode and approval behavior. Trust affects project instruction and integration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:5:| Status | Updated by [DEC-01](../DECISIONS.md#dec-01-default-execution-posture): permission mode is independent of folder trust; unset mode defaults to review. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:14:The observations in this section describe the original audit baseline and are not assertions about the amended DEC-01 behavior. In particular, the reported trust-derived `auto` default was the defect identified by SEC-01; DEC-01 was amended on 2026-10-24 to make permission mode independent of folder trust and default to `review`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:65:   - An explicitly configured auto posture runs without asking regardless of workspace trust; folder trust controls project instructions and integrations only.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:98:| `exec` | run_command, run_tests, LSP server spawn, plugin and MCP tool calls | refused, except the confined read-only allowlist | ask | allowed under explicit auto mode regardless of folder trust |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:101:| `context_inject` | activate_skill, manage_knowledge write | refused (write) | ask when the source is untrusted (see SPEC-03) | ask only when the source is untrusted; folder trust does not decide |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:142:- Persisted sessions do **not** persist an approval mode. Resume uses the current launch posture. This avoids resurrecting authority, per PERS-004.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:146:- Unset approval mode defaults to review regardless of folder trust. Release notes and startup messaging must distinguish permission mode from folder trust. Use `--mode auto` for automatic writes and commands with per-origin egress approval; use `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` or `--yes` for full access.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:183:- **DEC-01** is resolved as amended: review by default; explicit permission mode controls approvals independently of folder trust. Nothing in this s