ion oracle) are classified as `exec` capabilities subject to the configured approval mode. In review mode, the first verifier execution prompts for approval, displaying the exact test command and resolved script body from `package.json`, `Makefile`, or `Cargo.toml`; folder trust alone does not authorize it.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-folder-trust-copy/cli/src/startup_trust.ts:132:        \"Trust this folder?\",\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:60:3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress. Folder trust only controls project instructions and workspace integrations. Input safety is strictly enforced across surfaces (REQ-SEC-103): lone Enter defaults to No, a 400ms grace period discards typed-ahead input, and approve-all requires explicit confirmation (`all` in REPL, confirmation Enter in TUI). *Limit:* in explicit `auto` posture, commands and file writes execute autonomously regardless of folder trust.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-suite/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:140:- Persisted sessions do **not** persist an approval mode. Resume uses the current launch posture. This avoids resurrecting authority, per PERS-004.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/cli/src/types.ts:61:  approvalMode?: \"auto\" | \"review\" | \"read-only\"; // Permission posture: auto, review, or read-only (DEC-01, independent of folder trust)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/cli/src/index.ts:288:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/cli/src/index.ts:353:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode