ration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:5:| Status | Updated by [DEC-01](../DECISIONS.md#dec-01-default-execution-posture): permission mode is independent of folder trust; unset mode defaults to review. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:14:The observations in this section describe the original audit baseline and are not assertions about the amended DEC-01 behavior. In particular, the reported trust-derived `auto` default was the defect identified by SEC-01; DEC-01 was amended on 2026-10-24 to make permission mode independent of folder trust and default to `review`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:65:   - An explicitly configured auto posture runs without asking regardless of workspace trust; folder trust controls project instructions and integrations only.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:98:| `exec` | run_command, run_tests, LSP server spawn, plugin and MCP tool calls | refused, except the confined read-only allowlist | ask | allowed under explicit auto mode regardless of folder trust |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:101:| `context_inject` | activate_skill, manage_knowledge write | refused (write) | ask when the source is untrusted (see SPEC-03) | ask only when the source is untrusted; folder trust does not decide |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:142:- Persisted sessions do **not** persist an approval mode. Resume uses the current launch posture. This avoids resurrecting authority, per PERS-004.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:146:- Unset approval mode defaults to review regardless of folder trust. Release notes and startup messaging must distinguish permission mode from folder trust. Use `--mode auto` for automatic writes and commands with per-origin egress approval; use `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` or `--yes` for full access.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:183:- **DEC-01** is resolved as amended: review by default; explicit permission mode controls approvals independently of folder trust. Nothing in this spec is blocked by the decision.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-01 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:46:  test(\"folder trust alone keeps an unset permission mode in review\", () => {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-workspace-trust/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:140:- Persisted sessions do **not** persist an approval mode. Resume uses the current launch posture. This avoids resurrecting authority, per PERS-004.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-workspace-trust/cli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:65:    assert.match(rendered, /Trust this folder\\?/);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-workspace-trust/cli/test/startup_unreachable_e2e.test.ts:65:prompted = read_until(\"Trust this folder?\", 10.0)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/cli/test/config.test.ts:10:  test(\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\", () => {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/cli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:65:    assert.match(rendered, /Trust this folder\\?/);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/cli/test/startup_unreachable_e2e.test.ts:65:prompted = read_until(\"Trust this folder?\", 10.0)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:41:| 2 | Add `ApprovalPolicy`: `requiresDecision(effect, {mode, trusted, sandbox, egressOrigins})`. Test the full matrix and verify that folder trust does not change decisions for a fixed mode. | new `cli/src/core/approval_policy.ts` | 1 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:43:| 4 | Replace the `autoApprove` booleans with `HarnessConfig.approvalMode`. Explicit flags and permission settings select the mode; if none is configured, default to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` retains per-origin egress approval; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access. | `config.ts:107`, `types.ts`, `index.ts:93,115`, `repl.ts:69,281,644-648`, `sidecar.ts:53,66,478,638,935` | 3 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:44:| 5 | Route verifier executions throug