{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:54:25.791Z","ordinal":327992,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171d2-d7fe-7473-a950-3592dcbf3eab","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda79f30c081a0a5c5641b9d22bca0","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.** I made two concrete updates this turn:\n\n- Verified on exact `main` `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f` that an unset approval mode defaults to **review**, independently of folder trust. No code change was needed.\n- Posted a metadata-only follow-up to the held-out custodian on [Issue #1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6394571756), asking who currently owns custody, whether the sealed corpus fits the current evaluator contract, and when acceptance/run metadata can be provided. No protected content was requested or accessed.\n\n**Release path:** Main’s CI `40165934790` and CodeQL `40165934792` passed on `016bbc3`. PR #207 (`fb36b03`) still has Node 22/24 checks running; CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed. PR #212 (`8b7c09c`) has Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JS/TS checks passing; Linux packaging is still running. The serialized local suite is also confirmed live, so I did not start overlapping tests.\n\nThe latest public release remains RC4. Held-out custody acceptance, exact-RC qualification, the human terminal matrix, and independent final acceptance remain outstanding. **No accepted RC or stable release is claimed.**\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":45,"lineEnd":47,"note":"Nexus project context"}],"rolloutIds":["01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1792911263213,"completed_at_ms":1792911265791}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:54:25.798Z","ordinal":327993,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda79f30c081a0a5c5641b9d22bca0","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.** I made two concrete updates this turn:\n\n- Verified on exact `main` `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f` that an unset approval mode defaults to **review**, independently of folder trust. No code change was needed.\n- Posted a metadata-only follow-up to the held-out custodian on [Issue #1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6394571756), asking who currently owns custody, whether the sealed corpus fits the current evaluator contract, and when acceptance/run metadata can be provided. No protected content was requested or accessed.\n\n**Release path:** Main’s CI `40165934790` and CodeQL `40165934792` passed on `016bbc3`. PR #207 (`fb36b03`) still has Node 22/24 checks running; CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed. PR #212 (`8b7c09c`) has Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JS/TS checks passing; Linux packaging is still running. The serialized local suite is also confirmed live, so I did not start overlapping tests.\n\nThe latest public release remains RC4. Held-out custody acceptance, exact-RC qualification, the human terminal matrix, and independent final acceptance remain outstanding. **No accepted RC or stable release is claimed.**\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:45-47|note=[Nexus project context]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a171d2-d7fe-7473-a950-3592dcbf3eab","create_time":1792911263.1927438,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adda79f30c081a0a5c5641b9d22b