{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:17:27.340Z","ordinal":328715,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171e6-e7a2-7bb2-92f7-17944d46f4b1","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c0013d9a-0cdb-4a09-8983-2153809b39a5","process_id":"37904","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","for f in cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts cli/test/doctor.test.ts; do printf '\\n--- %s ---\\n' \"$f\"; printf 'PR200 '; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code show 81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20:\"$f\" | rg '^\\s*(test|it)\\(' | sed -E 's/.*\\((\"[^\"]*\"|`[^`]*`).*/\\1/' | sort; printf 'PR213 '; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr213-git-exclude show HEAD:\"$f\" | rg '^\\s*(test|it)\\(' | sed -E 's/.*\\((\"[^\"]*\"|`[^`]*`).*/\\1/' | sort; done"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"for f in cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts cli/test/doctor.test.ts; do printf '\\n--- %s ---\\n' \"$f\"; printf 'PR200 '; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code show 81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20:\"$f\" | rg '^\\s*(test|it)\\(' | sed -E 's/.*\\((\"[^\"]*\"|`[^`]*`).*/\\1/' | sort; printf 'PR213 '; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr213-git-exclude show HEAD:\"$f\" | rg '^\\s*(test|it)\\(' | sed -E 's/.*\\((\"[^\"]*\"|`[^`]*`).*/\\1/' | sort; done"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\n--- cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts ---\nPR200 \"a comment mentioning .nexus does not suppress the ignore rule\"\n\"a hard-linked self-ignore file is rejected before changing its external link\"\n\"a later negation is overridden by a verified positive rule\"\n\"a missing exclude file is created with the rules\"\n\"a nested ignore negation cannot expose flight logs or worktree state\"\n\"a nested self-ignore protects Nexus state from higher-priority repository negations\"\n\"a root-anchored rule is accepted without adding a duplicate\"\n\"a symlink swap cannot write self-ignore content or alter external ignore rules\"\n\"a symlinked Nexus state directory is rejected before any outside write\"\n\"an unrelated pattern containing .nexus does not suppress the rule\"\n\"existing exact rules are not duplicated\"\n\"leading whitespace is not treated as an existing ignore rule\"\nPR213 \"a comment mentioning .nexus does not suppress the ignore rule\"\n\"a hard-linked info/exclude is not modified\"\n\"a hard-linked self-ignore file is rejected before changing its external link\"\n\"a later negation is overridden by a verified positive rule\"\n\"a missing exclude file is created with the rules\"\n\"a nested ignore negation cannot expose flight logs or worktree state\"\n\"a nested self-ignore protects Nexus state from higher-priority repository negations\"\n\"a root-anchored rule is accepted without adding a duplicate\"\n\"a symlink swap cannot write self-ignore content or alter external ignore rules\"\n\"a symlinked Nexus state directory is rejected before any outside write\"\n\"a symlinked info directory does not redirect missing exclude creation\"\n\"a symlinked info/exclude is not followed or modified\"\n\"an unrelated pattern containing .nexus does not suppress the rule\"\n\"existing exact rules are not duplicated\"\n\"leading whitespace is not treated as an existing ignore rule\"\n\n--- cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts ---\nPR200 \"ACC-PER-05: Fresh git repo with FlightRecorder writes telemetry but git status --porcelain shows nothing under .nexus/\"\n\"WorktreeManager defers .nexus exclusion until it creates workspace state\"\n\"a subdirectory workspace protects root worktree state when Git metadata is unavailable\"\n\"an ineffective read-only self-ignore rule blocks flight state writes\"\n\"ensureGitExclude is idempotent and does not duplicate entries\"\n\"unavailable exclude metadata does not prevent startup or expose flight state\"\nPR213 \"ACC-PER-05: Fresh git repo with FlightRecorder writes telemetry but git status --porcelain shows nothing under .nexus/\"\n\"Git unavailable in a linked worktree fails closed before creating flight state\"\n\"Git unavailable in nested repository workspaces fails closed before creating flight state\"\n\"WorktreeManager defers .nexus exclusion until it creates workspace state\"\n\"a subdirectory workspace protects root worktree state when Git metadata is unavailable\"\n\"an ineffective read-only self-ignore rule blocks flight state writes\"\n\"ensureGitExclude is idempotent and does not duplicate entries\"\n\"unavailable exclude metadata does not prevent startup or expose flight state\"\n\n--- cli/test/doctor.test.ts ---\nPR200 \"--deep can verify a configured model omitted from /models\"\n\"--deep engine probe passes in a large workspace (a listing bigger than the output cap is not a failure)\"\n\"--deep sends exactly one inference request and says it costs model work\"\n\"ACC-PKG-06 (REQ-DX-101): doctor stderr is empty on a healthy run (no MaxListenersExceededWarning)\"\n\"ACC-PKG-07 (REQ-DX-101): packaged doctor remedies contain no make or harness.sh\"\n\"ACC-PKG-08 (REQ-DX-102): config.env at 0644 gives a warning and repair; --fix --yes sets 0600\"\n\"ACC-PKG-09 (REQ-DX-103): workspace path with a UUID segment appears unredacted in doctor output\"\n\"MCP servers and plugins are inspected without being started or loaded\"\n\"REQ-DX-104: tui.launch verifies launchability via nexus-tui --live --check\"\n\"`nexus doctor --json` through the packaged launcher: isolated home, mock endpoint, exit code\"\n\"a cloud provider is diagnosed with that provider's protocol and credential\"\n\"a concurrent change or a held lock leaves the target alone\"\n\"a directory replaced by a link between diagnosis and repair is left alone\"\n\"a hanging endpoint is bounded by the timeout\"\n\"a linked credentials parent (~/.config -> elsewhere) gets no repair\"\n\"a linked parent (~/.nexus -> elsewhere) gets no repair, and --fix changes nothing outside\"\n\"a planted lock link is never followed or written through\"\n\"a rejected credential fails authentication\"\n\"a shell that is not on PATH fails shell.executable\"\n\"an engine binary that does not run fails engine.binary\"\n\"an explicit timeout still bounds the state integrity check\"\n\"an invalid option is a doctor execution error (exit 3) with machine-readable JSON\"\n\"an unreachable endpoint fails reachability and skips what depends on it\"\n\"config.project_env_ignored reports operator-only settings a workspace .env tries to set (REQ-SEC-110)\"\n\"confirmed repairs apply, back up previous modes, verify, and are idempotent\"\n\"default state integrity has a bounded extended deadline for slow long-lived stores\"\n\"exit codes: 0 healthy, 1 warnings, 2 failures\"\n\"failed directory creation never removes a pathname that may have been replaced\"\n\"failed exclusive creation never unlinks a pathname that may have been replaced\"\n\"help documents flags, exit codes and the repair scope\"\n\"malformed configuration fails config.valid while independent checks still run\"\n\"nothing changes without confirmation or under read-only policy\"\n\"permissions are never changed through a symbolic link\"\n\"secrets never appear in any output field or exception path\"\n\"state directories: missing warns with a repair; unwritable fails; checks home's real paths\"\n\"state integrity accepts empty and cursor-backed schema-2 histories, but reports malformed records\"\n\"state integrity directory traversal is asynchronous and leaves other event-loop work responsive\"\n\"state integrity only warns about writer-shaped temporary files and never labels arbitrary or active temp files interrupted\"\n\"state integrity stats large task directories in bounded concurrent batches\"\n\"state integrity warns when a state directory cannot be read\"\n\"state integrity warns when a state path is not a directory\"\n\"the change is bound to the verified object: a final or parent swap after diagnosis is detected\"\n\"the model list keeps the endpoint's /v1 path and the configured model is checked\"\n\"the session context diagnoses the session's own configuration\"\n\"unreadable session records are reported, never deleted\"\n\"versioned JSON: every finding carries id, status, explanation, evidence and repair availability\"\n\"~/.nexus swapped for a link after the diagnosis: repairs, lock and backups stand down\"\nPR213 \"--deep can verify a configured model omitted from /models\"\n\"--deep engine probe passes in a large workspace (a listing bigger than the output cap is not a failure)\"\n\"--deep sends exactly one inference request and says it costs model work\"\n\"ACC-PKG-06 (REQ-DX-101): doctor stderr is empty on a healthy run (no MaxListenersExceededWarning)\"\n\"ACC-PKG-07 (REQ-DX-101): packaged doctor remedies contain no make or harness.sh\"\n\"ACC-PKG-08 (REQ-DX-102): config.env at 0644 gives a warning and repair; --fix --yes sets 0600\"\n\"ACC-PKG-09 (REQ-DX-103): workspace path with a UUID segment appears unredacted in doctor output\"\n\"MCP servers and plugins are inspected without being started or loaded\"\n\"REQ-DX-104: tui.launch verifies launchability via nexus-tui --live --check\"\n\"`nexus doctor --json` through the packaged launcher: isolated home, mock endpoint, exit code\"\n\"a cloud provider is diagnosed with that provider's protocol and credential\"\n\"a concurrent change or a held lock leaves the target alone\"\n\"a directory replaced by a link between diagnosis and repair is left alone\"\n\"a hanging endpoint is bounded by the timeout\"\n\"a linked credentials parent (~/.config -> elsewhere) gets no repair\"\n\"a linked parent (~/.nexus -> elsewhere) gets no repair, and --fix changes nothing outside\"\n\"a planted lock link is never followed or written through\"\n\"a rejected credential fails authentication\"\n\"a shell that is not on PATH fails shell.executable\"\n\"an engine binary that does not run fails engine.binary\"\n\"an explicit tim