{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:30:00.826Z","ordinal":329125,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171f7-072f-7b22-b313-9d5241d78ccb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3d8fb63d-744e-416e-a91c-c43ef79666b1","process_id":"46895","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i -E 'refused connection|overloaded|stream cut|output.limit truncation|hanging.command|full.disk|SIGTERM|context overflow|rate limit' origin/main -- eval docs/v1.0.0 | head -100; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '230,320p'; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main eval | rg 't[234]|fixture|fault|long' | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n -i -E 'refused connection|overloaded|stream cut|output.limit truncation|hanging.command|full.disk|SIGTERM|context overflow|rate limit' origin/main -- eval docs/v1.0.0 | head -100; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '230,320p'; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main eval | rg 't[234]|fixture|fault|long' | head -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:237:1. refused connection mid-turn\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:238:2. 5xx / overloaded\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:239:3. stream cut mid-tool-call\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:240:4. output-limit truncation\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:243:7. context overflow at 32k\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:245:9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:90:**Amendment 2026-10-17 (governance).** The T4 protocol enumerates **nine** distinct fault scenarios (SPEC-10 §2.5, ACCEPTANCE §6.2): refused connection, 5xx/overloaded, stream cut mid-tool-call, output-limit truncation, hanging test command, disk full, context overflow at 32k, malformed tool-call JSON, and SIGTERM-then-resume. The summary count previously read \"8\" while listing all nine; the union of the distinct scenarios is retained as **nine** classes × 5 runs. No scenario is dropped or merged. Corrected here, in SPEC-10 §2.5 and in the REQUIREMENTS ledger (REQ-QUAL-105).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:193:  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:272:| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:128:| REQ-SEC-106 | SUBP-004/005 (carried) | No task-owned process survives client exit, crash, SIGTERM or SIGHUP. Services are registered. | safety | `main.rs`, `runner.rs` | TEST (ACC-PROC-02, ACC-PROC-03; `cli/test/process_lifecycle.test.ts`, `core/tests/rpc_shutdown.rs`, `core::runner::tests::background_processes_left_by_a_command_are_ended`) | tested | ACC-PROC-02, ACC-PROC-03 | **B** | SEC-07, TUI-01 | SPEC-02 / PLAN-02 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:153:| REQ-AGT-118 | Audit | Conservative token estimation; `/tokenize` used when available. | failure (context overflow) | `tokens.ts`, `client.ts`, `agent.ts` | TEST (VER-09; test:cli/test/tokens.test.ts; fixture measured on llama.cpp worker b0-live-llama-worker1, limits_version a3c2fcbc2f2b977c). 12/14 corpora within the 1.5x band (max non-floor over-estimate 1.428x, base64); 4 corpora under-estimate within the 0.8x conservative guard (worst 601/748 = 1.245x, whitespace-indented code); the 2 floor-bound exceptions are recorded per DEC-17. **Amended (DEC-17, 2026-10-17):** the ≥1 token/char floor (admission safety) takes precedence over ACC-VER-07's accuracy band for merging scripts (CJK word composition, Hangul syllables); the floor-driven over-estimate (CJK 2.00x, Hangul 1.67x) is preserved as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. Executed: `tokens.test.ts` 3/3 on snapshot `8cf3e82` and post-merge on `f771a3c` (GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS test-evidence record); independent coordinator rerun 3/3 at exact `2c70d39` with independent reviewer **ACCEPT** (docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/independent-review.md, branch v1/review-plan-11-pr-11d-ag118 @ bc9fd2c). Floor-bound accuracy exceptions preserved as recorded evidence; reconciled 2026-10-18. | tested | ACC-VER-07 | RR | VER-09 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:243:| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:44:- M3 is on the path because resume (AGT-01), work-unit durability (AGT-02a) and standalone sizing (PRV-06) are blockers, and the T4 class 9 test (SIGTERM, then resume) needs them.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:116:- Output-limit truncation refuses to run partial tool calls and tells the model how to recover (client.ts:1177-1183, 1461; agent.ts:4670-4685).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:79:- Positive completion evidence required before any tool call runs: Chat Completions needs finish_reason or [DONE] (client.ts:1436-1443); Anthropic needs message_stop and all blocks closed (anthropic.ts:218); Responses needs response.completed and completed function_call items (openai_responses.ts:101,152). RUNTIME R1 (no-finish -> stream_incomplete) + TEST (cloud_providers \"stream cut inside a tool call\").\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:106:| PRV-R5 | Standalone LM Studio, llama.cpp and vLLM complete a scripted tool-using task with no homelab config; context limit discovered or a context overflow yields compaction-and-retry or an actionable `--context-limit` message. | workflow/compat | BLOCKER (evidence) | G1 procedure, archived transcripts per server. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:150:            os.kill(self.pid, signal.SIGTERM)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:123:- Terminal restore on panic/exit including bracketed paste and kitty flags (live.rs:270-284); SIGTERM/SIGHUP watchdog.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:66:| REL-08 | S3 | installer, latest path | install.sh:21-24 | RUNTIME. Without NEXUS_VERSION: `curl: (22) ... 404` / `nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.` (only prereleases exist). The same message appears for API rate-limit (60/h unauthenticated) or network failure. There is no hint to set NEXUS_VERSION and no list of available prereleases. | The first-time \"omit version\" path fails opaquely until v1.0.0 exists, and later under rate limiting. | Tell the 404 apart from other errors. On 404 say \"no stable release yet; use NEXUS_VERSION=vX (latest prerelease: …)\". Fall back to the `releases/latest/download` redirect, which avoids the API. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:180:| EVL-R5 | **T4 fault injection**, at least 8 cases × 5 runs (proposal): gateway refuses connections mid-turn; gateway 5xx/overloaded; stream cut mid-tool-call; reply truncated at the output limit; tool timeout (a hanging test command); disk full in the workspace; context-window overflow (32k limit on a large repo); malformed tool-call JSON from the model; SIGTERM mid-turn followed by resume. | failure / recovery | BLOCKER | Per case: either recovery (task completes, scored as recovery rate) or a truthful bounded outcome. **Threshold proposal: 100% truthful, 0 false VERIFIED, 0 hangs past budget+5 min.** |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:23:| 3 | Shutdown sweep on stdin EOF, SIGTERM and SIGHUP (`tokio::signal`). `prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, SIGTERM)` at startup (Linux, `nix` or `libc` crate). | `main.rs` | 1 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:28:| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:41:| 3 | Release resolver: fetch latest stable release or pinned release tag from GitHub Releases API; parse asset metadata; exclude drafts/prereleases from default selection; handle rate limits, network errors, and missing tags. | `cli/src/upgrade.ts` | 1 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:38:1. **REQ-AGT-109.** Cancel (Esc, Ctrl-C, `prompt.cancel`, SIGINT to `nexus run`) terminates the process group of every in-flight tool within 5 s: SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after a 2 s grace.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:39:2. **REQ-SEC-106.** On a normal exit, crash of the client, SIGTERM or SIGHUP, harness-core leaves no surviving task-owned processes. This includes background processes the model started with `&`, unless they were explicitly registered as long-lived services (see §5.4).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:55:- **New RPC `cancel { request_id }`.** `killpg(pgid, SIGTERM)`, then SIGKILL after 2 s, then reply `cancelled`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:56:- **Shutdown.** On stdin EOF, SIGTERM or SIGHUP (`core/src/main.rs:194-203` RPC loop), killpg every registered group with the same TERM → KILL sequence, then exit. Install the handlers with `tokio::signal`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:57:- **Parent death.** On Linux, call `prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, SIGTERM)` in harness-core. If the node sidecar dies without closing stdin, harness-core gets a signal and runs the shutdown path. The command children are in their own groups, so the registry sweep is what cleans them up.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:69:In `cli/src/agent.ts`, pass the turn's abort signal into every `executeTool` call. The spine already has the signal (`agent.ts:4359-4372`). The existing cancellation-record semantics (synthetic tool results for undispatched calls) are kept. A tool that was killed reports `status: CANCELLED`, `exit_code: null` and `signal: SIGTERM|SIGKILL`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:66:   2. 5xx/overloaded;\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:67:   3. stream cut mid-tool-call;\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:68:   4. output-limit truncation;\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:71:   7. context overflow at 32k;\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:73:   9. SIGTERM mid-turn, then resume.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:107:- SPEC-02 (cancel and SIGTERM semantics).\norigin/main:eval/README.md:91:| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\norigin/main:eval/README.md:106:The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\norigin/main:eval/README.md:267:  has joined the leaf is not lost. It also sends the supervisor `SIGTERM` so that it can still report. If the supervisor\norigin/main:eval/agent_sandbox.mjs:46:process.on(\"SIGTERM\", () => stop(\"SIGTERM\"));\norigin/main:eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:57:for (const signal of [\"SIGTERM\", \"SIGINT\", \"SIGHUP\"]) process.on(signal, stop);\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:383:    const timer = setTimeout(() => { timedOut = true; killGroup(\"SIGTERM\"); setTimeout(() => killGroup(\"SIGKILL\"), 250).unref(); }, spec.timeoutMs);\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:586:      killTree(\"SIGTERM\");\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:16: * - overloaded: 503 with Retry-After: 1 (the endpoint is busy);\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:21: * The other T4 classes (a hanging test command, a full disk, SIGTERM then resume) come from task fixtures and the runner.\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:23:export const FAULT_KINDS = [\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"];\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:211:    if (fault?.kind === \"overloaded\") {\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:214:      return void res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: { message: \"overloaded (injected)\", type: \"overloaded\" } }));\norigin/main:eval/resources.mjs:131:    // supervisor exits. The supervisor also stops on SIGTERM. One that does not exit loses its report, so the run fails\norigin/main:eval/resources.mjs:134:    try { process.kill(child.pid, \"SIGTERM\"); } catch {}\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:610:      killGroup(\"SIGTERM\");\norigin/main:eval/validate.mjs:61:    const kinds = [\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"];\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\neval/T3.md\neval/heldout-t3-manifest.json\neval/t3.mjs\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/hidden/csv.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/repo/csv.js\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/repo/package.json\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/repo/test/csv.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-csv/task.json\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/hidden/test_duration_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/repo/durations.py\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/repo/tests/test_durations.py\neval/tasks/t2-bugfix-duration/task.json\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/hidden/report.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/repo/package.json\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/repo/src/job.js\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/repo/src/report.js\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/repo/test/report.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-debug-logs/task.json\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/hidden/test_inventory_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/repo/inventory.py\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/repo/tests/test_inventory.py\neval/tasks/t2-feature-inventory/task.json\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/hidden/slugify.hidden.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/repo/package.json\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/repo/slugify.js\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/repo/test/slugify.test.js\neval/tasks/t2-feature-slugify/task.json\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/hidden/test_tax_hidden.py\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/repo/cart.py\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/repo/invoice.py\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/repo/tests/test_totals.py\neval/tasks/t2-refactor-tax/task.json\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":46607}},"started_at_ms":1792913400824,"completed_at_ms":1792913400826}}
