uest: 1 }]);\norigin/main:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:118:  assert.deepEqual(score.faults.map((f: any) => [f.kind, f.n, f.truthful, f.recovered]), [[\"overloaded\", 1, 1, 1]]);\norigin/main:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:122:  const { records, score } = await evaluate(\"exports.add = (a, b) => a + b;\\n\", { faults: [{ kind: \"truncate\", atRequest: 1 }] });\norigin/main:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:124:  assert.equal(r.model.faultsInjected[0].kind, \"truncate\");\norigin/main:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:127:  assert.equal(score.faults[0].truthful, 1);\norigin/main:eval/README.md:57:| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\norigin/main:eval/README.md:77:- **Contamination.** Contaminated runs (the task directory changed, or its path appeared in the agent's output) are\norigin/main:eval/README.md:85:A task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\norigin/main:eval/README.md:97:What was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\norigin/main:eval/README.md:101:- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\norigin/main:eval/README.md:106:The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\norigin/main:eval/README.md:107:runner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\norigin/main:eval/README.md:175:2. The agent's changes are found by walking both trees and comparing bytes and executable bits\norigin/main:eval/README.md:178:     `pyproject.toml`, `Cargo.toml`, `go.mod` and `go.sum` may be added, changed or deleted. Every other file type,\norigin/main:eval/README.md:196:   - **Manifests** may change only plain dependency or metadata entries. Any other change refuses both checks, and so\norigin/main:eval/README.md:211:   `hardened: { baseline, applied, discarded, configChanges }`.\norigin/main:eval/README.md:221:  agent's changes there are dropped. The `npm:` alias form of a dependency spec is not refused; setup is not re-run\norigin/main:eval/README.md:322:one `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:28:   judged against the snapshot, so nothing the agent does during the probe turn can change the result. The agent may\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:41:  \"objective\": \"operator text for a long multi-part change\",\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:45:    { \"id\": \"keep-api\", \"afterToolCalls\": 15, \"text\": \"Do not change src/api.ts; adapt callers instead.\",\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:46:      \"constraint\": { \"kind\": \"file-unchanged\", \"path\": \"src/api.ts\" } },\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:64:  - `file-unchanged` — `path` exists before the run and has the same bytes at the end;\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:68:  Steering should change what the agent does after it arrives, and must not be satisfiable by doing nothing. When\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:69:  the steer is sent, a `file-absent` or `file-unchanged` path must exist. A `command` constraint must fail on the staged\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:70:  workspace before the agent starts; it is checked on a throwaway copy, and a hang there is a harness error. Otherwise the\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:3:// task is staged again (same pin or fixture, same setup) and only the agent's source changes are copied in.\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:6:// .git/config or .gitattributes could otherwise run commands as the harness user. Changes are found by walking both\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:35:/** Only files with these extensions may be added, changed or deleted (T2 languages: JS/TS, Python, Rust, Go)... */\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:37:/** ...plus these manifests, whose changes testConfigChange checks section by section (deleting one refuses the checks). */\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:80:/** The first changed TOML section whose exact header is not allowed, or null. */\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:81:function changedTomlSection(before, after, allowed) {\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:90: * Dependency manifests: a change is kept only where it is a plain dependency or package-metadata change; anything\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:93:export function testConfigChange(relative, before, after) {\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:112:      if (!allowed.has(key) && JSON.stringify(a[key]) !== JSON.stringify(b[key])) return `package.json \"${key}\" changed`;\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:120:    const key = changedTomlSection(before, after, (k) => k === \"[project]\" || k === \"[project.optional-dependencies]\");\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:121:    return key ? `pyproject.toml ${key} changed` : null;\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:124:    // [package] and [features] can switch test discovery off (autotests, build, a changed default feature set); [[test]],\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:125:    // [lib], [profile.*] and [patch] can drop or redirect targets. Only dependency tables may change.\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:126:    const key = changedTomlSection(before, after, (k) => k === \"[dependencies]\" || /^\\[dependencies\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\]$/.test(k));\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:127:    if (key) return `Cargo.toml ${key} changed`;\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:136:    return rest(before) === rest(after) ? null : \"go.mod changed outside its require directives\";\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:177: * Copies the agent's source changes from `agentWs` into `freshWs`, a fresh staging of the same baseline (setup\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:178: * included). Only source files and the checked manifests may be added, changed or deleted; blocked paths, other file\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:180: * path through a symlink are discarded. A manifest change outside dependencies, or a deleted manifest, refuses checks.\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:182:export function applyAgentChanges(agentWs, freshWs) {\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:188:  const configChanges = [];\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:194:    if (!target && MANIFESTS.has(path.basename(relative))) { configChanges.push(`${relative} added`); continue; } // a new manifest moves module or root boundaries\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:202:    const reason = testConfigChange(relative, target ? fs.readFileSync(target, \"utf8\") : null, fs.readFileSync(source, \"utf8\"));\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:203:    if (reason) configChanges.push(reason);\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:212:    if (MANIFESTS.has(path.basename(relative)) && !isTestInfraPath(relative)) { configChanges.push(`${relative} deleted`); continue; }\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:217:  return { applied, discarded: discarded.sort(), configChanges };\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:9:services. The changes are limited to the following:\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:11:| Change | File or object | Why |\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:20:- `provision.sh` applies these changes and is idempotent. It never remounts an active tmpfs.\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:31:fresh and repeated runs, rollback, refusal of a foreign account, sudoers file or symlinked root (with no changes),\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:54:| `memoryBytes` | 16 GiB | `memory.max`, with `memory.swap.max = 0` and `memory.oom.group = 1`. The charge counts the phase's anonymous memory, the page cache it faults in (reclaimable before OOM), **and the tmpfs pages it writes**. A phase that writes 6 GiB of build output therefore has about 10 GiB left for its processes. Exceeding the limit OOM-kills the whole phase, and this is recorded. |\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:63:  Then load from those tenants cannot change a run's available CPU. The X5650 is slow, so the throttle is set\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:80:   change is recorded, and calibration is repeated. No candidate result is involved.\norigin/main:eval/host/README.md:83:3. **After freeze.** Values never change in response to qualification outcomes. A change for any reason after the\norigin/main:eval/host/container-test/run.sh:2:# Exercises provision.sh and rollback.sh as root in a disposable privileged container (no host changes):\norigin/main:eval/host/container-test/run.sh:27:[[ ! -e /etc/sudoers.d/99-nexus-eval && -z \"$(ls /etc/systemd/system/*.mount 2>/dev/null)\" ]] && ok \"3b no changes on refusal\" || { bad \"3b\"; state; }\norigin/main:eval/host/container-test/run.sh:44:$R >/tmp/o 2>&1; id nexus-eval >/dev/null 2>&1 && ok \"7 rollback left a re-created account (uid changed)\" || bad \"7 rollback deleted a re-created account\"\norigin/main:eval/host/container-test/run.sh:60:$R >/tmp/o 2>&1; [[ -f /etc/sudoers.d/99-nexus-eval ]] && ok \"10 rollback left a sudoers file whose content changed\" || bad \"10 rollback deleted an edited sudoers file\"\norigin/main:eval/host/provision.sh:7:# did not create stops the run unchanged. Every creation is first recorded as `pending <kind> <value>` in a root-only\norigin/main:eval/host/provision.sh:77:# Collision checks first: nothing is changed unless every resource is absent or verifiably ours.\norigin/main:eval/host/provision.sh:93:if ((${#problems[@]})); then printf 'refusing to provision (no changes made):\\n' >&2; printf '  - %s\\n' \"${problems[@]}\" >&2; exit 1; fi\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:186:  // Workspace subpaths the command may read but not change (hardened hidden tests: the oracle's own files).\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:404:    defaults: directory ? [\"-m\", `d:u:${user}:rwx,d:u:${operatorUid}:rwx,d:m::rwx`, resolved] : null,\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:413:  if (!fs.existsSync(setfacl)) throw new Error(\"setfacl is unavailable; refusing unsafe workspace permission changes\");\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:416:    const { access, defaults } = runAsAclArgs(user, opUid, resolved, fs.statSync(resolved).isDirectory());\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:419:    if (defaults) {\norigin/main:eval/isolate.mjs:420:      const defaultResult = spawnSync(setfacl, defaults, { encoding: \"utf8\", timeout: 5000, env: { PATH: \"/usr/bin:/bin\" } });\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:4:// Bodies are streamed through unchanged unless a fault is scheduled for a request (T4, REQ-QUAL-105); nothing is\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:21: * The other T4 classes (a hanging test command, a full disk, SIGTERM then resume) come from task fixtures and the runner.\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:23:export const FAULT_KINDS = [\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"];\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:73: * Starts a forwarder on 127.0.0.1 for `upstream` (e.g. https://gateway:8443/v1). `faults`: [{ kind, atRequest }] where\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:76:export async function startModelProxy({ upstream, caFile, faults = [], profile, authToken, clientToken, socketPath, maxRequests = 1_000, maxConcurrentRequests = 1, maxRequestBytes = 1_000_000, maxCompletionTokens, maxTotalCompletionTokens }) {\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:81:  for (const f of faults) {\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:82:    if (!FAULT_KINDS.includes(f.kind) || !Number.isInteger(f.atRequest) || f.atRequest < 1) throw new Error(`invalid fault ${JSON.stringify(f)}`);\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:94:  const stats = { requests: 0, chatRequests: 0, activeInferenceRequests: 0, cancelledRequests: 0, profileContextLookups: 0, requestedCompletionTokens: 0, answered: 0, upstreamFailures: 0, faultsInjected: [], firstRequestAt: null, firstAnswerAt: null };\norigin/main:eval/model_proxy.mjs:204:    const fault = chatIndex ? faults.find((f) => f.atRequest === chatIndex) : undefined;\norigin/main:eval/model_prox