un's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\norigin/main:eval/README.md:97:What was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\norigin/main:eval/README.md:101:- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\norigin/main:eval/README.md:106:The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\norigin/main:eval/README.md:107:runner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\norigin/main:eval/README.md:175:2. The agent's changes are found by walking both trees and comparing bytes and executable bits\norigin/main:eval/README.md:178:     `pyproject.toml`, `Cargo.toml`, `go.mod` and `go.sum` may be added, changed or deleted. Every other file type,\norigin/main:eval/README.md:196:   - **Manifests** may change only plain dependency or metadata entries. Any other change refuses both checks, and so\norigin/main:eval/README.md:211:   `hardened: { baseline, applied, discarded, configChanges }`.\norigin/main:eval/README.md:221:  agent's changes there are dropped. The `npm:` alias form of a dependency spec is not refused; setup is not re-run\norigin/main:eval/README.md:322:one `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:28:   judged against the snapshot, so nothing the agent does during the probe turn can change the result. The agent may\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:41:  \"objective\": \"operator text for a long multi-part change\",\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:45:    { \"id\": \"keep-api\", \"afterToolCalls\": 15, \"text\": \"Do not change src/api.ts; adapt callers instead.\",\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:46:      \"constraint\": { \"kind\": \"file-unchanged\", \"path\": \"src/api.ts\" } },\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:64:  - `file-unchanged` — `path` exists before the run and has the same bytes at the end;\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:68:  Steering should change what the agent does after it arrives, and must not be satisfiable by doing nothing. When\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:69:  the steer is sent, a `file-absent` or `file-unchanged` path must exist. A `command` constraint must fail on the staged\norigin/main:eval/T3.md:70:  workspace before the agent starts; it is checked on a throwaway copy, and a hang there is a harness error. Otherwise the\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:3:// task is staged again (same pin or fixture, same setup) and only the agent's source changes are copied in.\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:6:// .git/config or .gitattributes could otherwise run commands as the harness user. Changes are found by walking both\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:35:/** Only files with these extensions may be added, changed or deleted (T2 languages: JS/TS, Python, Rust, Go)... */\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:37:/** ...plus these manifests, whose changes testConfigChange checks section by section (deleting one refuses the checks). */\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:80:/** The first changed TOML section whose exact header is not allowed, or null. */\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:81:function changedTomlSection(before, after, allowed) {\norigin/main:eval/hardened_check.mjs:90: * Dependency manifests: a change is kept only where it is a plain dependency or package-metadata change; anything\norigin/m…2133 tokens truncated…alse is set)\");\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:220:      faults,\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:250:    // changes (eval/hardened_check.mjs). Black-box oracles already keep expectations outside the candidate.\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:262:      hardening = { baseline: baselineTree, ...applyAgentChanges(ws, hiddenWs) };\norigin/main:eval/run.mjs:265:    const refused = (check) => ({ pass: false, status: null, timedOut: false, overflow: false, output: `hardened check refused: ${