{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:30:33.350Z","ordinal":329160,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171f7-072f-7b22-b313-9d5241d78ccb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-238c3723-9a39-402e-afc8-c811498807b3","process_id":"8450","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 2 --json title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{title,state,updatedAt,comments:(.comments[-4:]|map({createdAt,author:.author.login,body}))}'; git show origin/main:eval/heldout-manifest.json | head -100; git show origin/main:eval/README.md | sed -n '80,115p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 2 --json title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{title,state,updatedAt,comments:(.comments[-4:]|map({createdAt,author:.author.login,body}))}'; git show origin/main:eval/heldout-manifest.json | head -100; git show origin/main:eval/README.md | sed -n '80,115p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Acceptance reconciliation required before T4 execution: ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2 says “8 fault classes × 5 runs” but enumerates nine fault classes (items 1–9). PLAN-10 task 11 also says T4 (8×5), while PLAN-10 task 5 and eval/README.md describe class 9 (SIGTERM then resume). No class has been removed and no threshold has been selected here. The release owner/spec owner must resolve the denominator and run matrix without post-result relaxation; until then T4 execution is blocked.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:25:37Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code).\\n\\n- **T4 denominator (prior comment):** resolved in ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2. The DEC-05 amendment (PRs #11/#13) keeps **9 fault classes × 5 runs**, including SIGTERM + resume. **Remaining inconsistency:** `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` line 34 (task 11) still says \\\"T4 (8×5)\\\". A boundary request to the plan owner is in the claim log; ACCEPTANCE §6.2 is authoritative.\\n- **Prerequisites not yet met:** no RC exists (package `0.1.0-alpha.2`). PR #33 (evaluator confidentiality and hardened-legacy checks) is open with CHANGES-REQUIRED, and held-out runs are prohibited until it is accepted. The qualification host is provisioned and validated on PR #33's branch, but that has not been accepted on integration.\\n- Requirements `--enforce` still fails at `6a16cb6`: 11 rows below threshold, including all of this issue's QUAL rows plus REQ-AGT-002 and REQ-PRV-111.\\n\\nNo M5 run has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:27Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"T4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an execution denominator.\\n\\nThis resolves the planning-text discrepancy only. T4 qualification has not run and remains gated on an accepted installed RC, frozen workload, provider/standalone prerequisites, and the other stated qualification dependencies. No threshold or denominator was changed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 11: complete preregistered M5 qualification runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}\n{\n  \"sealed_at\": \"2026-10-18T03:05:52.513Z\",\n  \"store\": \"/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2\",\n  \"tier\": \"T2\",\n  \"task_count\": 40,\n  \"external_repo_tasks\": 40,\n  \"by_class\": {\n    \"bugfix\": 10,\n    \"debug\": 10,\n    \"feature\": 10,\n    \"refactor\": 10\n  },\n  \"by_language\": {\n    \"go\": 10,\n    \"javascript\": 10,\n    \"python\": 10,\n    \"rust\": 10\n  },\n  \"hash_scheme\": {\n    \"task_sha256\": \"sha256 of raw tasks/<id>/task.json bytes\",\n    \"hidden_sha256\": \"sha256 of sorted '<path>  <sha256(file)>\\\\n' lines over tasks/<id>/<hidden.dir> (bin/hidden_digest.mjs)\"\n  },\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ho2-go-bugfix-02\",\n      \"class\": \"bugfix\",\n      \"language\": \"go\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"easy\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/hashicorp/go-version.git\",\n        \"commit\": \"1f6705b50d3f7137a753c1f61b2e292bef70c0c2\"\n      },\n      \"task_sha256\": \"5972189a560c809cc2d87060563842ce0fa591e4f07320d294d831a59638c233\",\n      \"hidden_sha256\": \"8b88607e573deb1810a52b92c4529f27fa752eb80698dadb265dbe138309cf2b\",\n      \"batch\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ho2-go-bugfix-03\",\n      \"class\": \"bugfix\",\n      \"language\": \"go\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"medium\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/iancoleman/strcase.git\",\n        \"commit\": \"a61ebb85b34d7b831590cd8fa7faafadc161a652\"\n      },\n      \"task_sha256\": \"61d1e5b86ae76e300901f0fe90757d83d19fc496c9d6a256e2d2c4373eea5dd0\",\n      \"hidden_sha256\": \"c06d38cfc5e8967de3b85a6509714500968ee1bb4413419f1dc62327875956cb\",\n      \"batch\": 6\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ho2-go-debug-02\",\n      \"class\": \"debug\",\n      \"language\": \"go\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"medium\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/blang/semver.git\",\n        \"commit\": \"d3feafb656afb1654476e8e0ddb1c1655c14cf5b\"\n      },\n      \"task_sha256\": \"7c520d568dbe143b5ced6c54ad870fc32f9f4c8c600bc57ed0f2b9fd2449ca33\",\n      \"hidden_sha256\": \"dee6bcbeb1832cf35608f0705b374b4cd97e26a5eb36c196438e8f9b7679e49d\",\n      \"batch\": 4\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ho2-go-debug-03\",\n      \"class\": \"debug\",\n      \"language\": \"go\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"easy\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/joho/godotenv.git\",\n        \"commit\": \"a2be92d182fc04da33b365bf47c17fe0f4808aea\"\n      },\n      \"task_sha256\": \"0a83edafe191799f782a0ceddc05a4dce8d3f692f92d47c48ed3542295efc8dd\",\n      \"hidden_sha256\": \"0802bf65cf8f97d6c50aa8fe45645ed8ed8b889839be748b0f55c1e7ab5e84bd\",\n      \"batch\": 7\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ho2-go-feature-01\",\n      \"class\": \"feature\",\n      \"language\": \"go\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"easy\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/dustin/go-humanize.git\",\n        \"commit\": \"0a173b2bf17e0d69adb87075a5d4be6ed1778569\"\n      },\n      \"task_sha256\": \"e82fb7bf6e1efddf45effe69c722cff70ecae71d09ede20d74eb90bba578b55f\",\n      \"hidden_sha256\": \"4a8e85367f36e04450e4cafd1624cec84a65016e21bfc7edcd88185872627839\",\n      \"batch\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ho2-go-feature-02\",\n      \"class\": \"feature\",\n      \"language\": \"go\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"easy\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/huandu/xstrings.git\",\n        \"commit\": \"55ae428c2ac4f74d7430952ef528631e656ac92c\"\n      },\n      \"task_sha256\": \"c43bdb7fbd1582ee5069bbd92985b2802c3a247e177abc113f9034ef77c1db05\",\n      \"hidden_sha256\": \"839dd988b99a62373c1d6a38f4e09b257f1e58ab492e88a45460647f89dbf9d7\",\n      \"batch\": 5\n- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n\nWhat was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\n\n- runs;\n- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\n  hidden tests failed);\n- **recovered** (the hidden tests pass);\n- hung past budget.\n\nThe remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\nrunner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":411213275}},"started_at_ms":1792913432938,"completed_at_ms":1792913433350}}
