{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:36:06.249Z","ordinal":329298,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171f9-069c-7cc1-ba0f-4b0b55bf095d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addb1652e3881a08bab7e0bb3a3420d","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.**\n\nOn exact main `05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099`, the pre-RC requirements gate passes. Main CI’s Linux job is still running the CLI suite. PR #213’s Node 22/24 suites are also still running, so I have not refreshed or merged it; the preview against current main is conflict-free and preserves the RC5 notes.\n\nKimi’s SUITE claim remains protected. Its focused tests are active in the owner’s worktree, although the recorded claim branch does not match that worktree. I logged the discrepancy and requested reconciliation; I have not started overlapping tests.\n\nI also confirmed the accepted T4 plan requires nine fault classes across five runs. The proxy supports six injectable classes, while the CI smoke test covers only two; full T4 qualification remains pending an eligible RC.\n\nNo RC5 tag or held-out custody acceptance exists yet. I’ll proceed with PR #213 when its current checks finish; the unanswered custodian status remains an external qualification dependency."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792913765216,"completed_at_ms":1792913766249}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:36:06.330Z","ordinal":329299,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addb1652e3881a08bab7e0bb3a3420d","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.**\n\nOn exact main `05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099`, the pre-RC requirements gate passes. Main CI’s Linux job is still running the CLI suite. PR #213’s Node 22/24 suites are also still running, so I have not refreshed or merged it; the preview against current main is conflict-free and preserves the RC5 notes.\n\nKimi’s SUITE claim remains protected. Its focused tests are active in the owner’s worktree, although the recorded claim branch does not match that worktree. I logged the discrepancy and requested reconciliation; I have not started overlapping tests.\n\nI also confirmed the accepted T4 plan requires nine fault classes across five runs. The proxy supports six injectable classes, while the CI smoke test covers only two; full T4 qualification remains pending an eligible RC.\n\nNo RC5 tag or held-out custody acceptance exists yet. I’ll proceed with PR #213 when its current checks finish; the unanswered custodian status remains an external qualification dependency.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a171f9-069c-7cc1-ba0f-4b0b55bf095d","create_time":1792913765.1820295,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addb1652e3881a08bab7e0bb3a3420d","turn_id":"01a171f9-069c-7cc1-ba0f-4b0b55bf095d","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a171fc-f7ba-7912-b0fa-1fc5d6485076","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16561}}
