{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:37:10.796Z","ordinal":329348,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171fd-3278-7ca3-ad25-d2f716cb2b15","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addb1a60c9881a0a800190cd460c997","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I found a concrete T4 gap beyond the pending CI: the release plan includes hanging-test, full-disk, and SIGTERM/resume scenarios, but the scorer only creates per-class rows from proxy-injected faults. Those three scenarios cannot currently contribute to the required nine-class score. I’m checking the claim protocol and will address this in an isolated source slice, without starting tests while Kimi owns SUITE."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792913830083,"completed_at_ms":1792913830796}}
