{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:38:52.642Z","ordinal":329432,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171fd-3278-7ca3-ad25-d2f716cb2b15","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-eed22efe-65b5-4fa1-9d54-56ea207daf12","process_id":"70146","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md | rg -n -C 5 'T4|fault'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '65,105p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '220,255p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md | rg -n -C 5 'T4|fault'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '65,105p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '220,255p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | head -80"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1-# SPEC-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n2-\n3-| | |\n4-|---|---|\n5-| Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\n6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\n7-| Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\n8-| Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\n9-| Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\n10-| Acceptance | ACCEPTANCE.md §4–§7 |\n11-\n--\n20-\n21-Both results are on tuned tasks. The following are missing entirely:\n22-\n23-- a held-out task set;\n24-- T3 long tasks;\n25:- T4 fault injection;\n26-- a run on the release commit (db1ca55 was never evaluated).\n27-\n28-Scoring integrity issues:\n29-\n30-- **EVL-002.** Any Nexus run without a parsed turn (for example a crash) is rerun as \"infrastructure\". Peers are rerun only on a connection-error signature. This biases results in Nexus's favour and hides the crash rate.\n--\n59-   - regressions (repo suite, plus a pre/post diff of previously passing tests);\n60-   - crash rate and timeout rate;\n61-   - bounded-failure truthfulness;\n62-   - operator interventions (= 0 in `run` mode);\n63-   - tokens and wall time per correct task.\n64:5. **REQ-QUAL-105. T4 fault injection.** 9 fault classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n65-   1. gateway refuses connections mid-turn;\n66-   2. 5xx/overloaded;\n67-   3. stream cut mid-tool-call;\n68-   4. output-limit truncation;\n69-   5. hanging test command;\n--\n77-   - Infrastructure reruns are symmetric and evidence-based: the endpoint was unreachable before the first model call.\n78-   - Contaminated runs are excluded from pooled rates.\n79-   - Hidden tests are not readable by the agent uid.\n80-   - The scorer logs every replacement.\n81-   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n82:7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n83-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\n84-9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n85:10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n86-\n87-## 3. Design\n88-\n89-- **Harness fixes** in `eval/infra.mjs:31` and `eval/score.mjs:16-21,48-84`:\n90-  - classify a run as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** an endpoint-unreachable signature is present, for every agent;\n91-  - add `replaced_by` logging;\n92-  - exclude `contaminated: true` runs from pooled rates;\n93-  - add the new metric columns.\n94-- **Hidden-test isolation.** Private validators and expected answers must remain outside every task process's readable namespace. A task workspace may contain only its permitted baseline and task inputs; evaluation of private expectations must be performed outside that task boundary. Corpus custody and evaluator execution isolation are separate acceptance gates: the custodian's sealed-store disposition does not establish that the runner prevents task processes from reading validators. On the current integration candidate, evaluator-boundary acceptance remains open; PR #33 is not qualified for held-out use until the actual workspace-construction and execution path demonstrates this boundary and passes independent review. Do not use filesystem ownership of the custodian store as a substitute for validating the task-process boundary.\n95-- **Fingerprint.** `eval/fingerprint.mjs` queries `/v1/models` and the server-specific endpoints (SPEC-05 `ServerKind`) and records the weights hash supplied in the config. A run is refused without it.\n96:- **Fault injector.** `eval/faults/proxy.mjs` is an HTTP proxy in front of the model server that injects faults 1–4 and 7–8 by schedule. Faults 5, 6 and 9 are injected by the task fixture or the runner.\n97-- **Task authoring.** Use a `task.json` schema with `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`. Calibrate so that no task is solved 5/5 by every agent (EVL G6).\n98-\n99-## 4. Procedure and evidence\n100-\n101-- See [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) §4–§7 for the qualification runbook, environments and pass/fail table.\n\n(C) Remove the commands.\n\n**Rationale.** Evidence for multi-unit convergence is thin. EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE lists I3, I4 and a stale-lock race as open, and post-remediation dogfooding was INTEGRATION_BLOCKED. Removing the commands throws away working code. Silent data loss is not acceptable even in experimental features.\n\n**Affected requirements:** REQ-AGT-102, 103, 107; SPEC-04.\n\n## DEC-04: Issue #12 open normative blockers\n\n| Item | Resolution | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| EXT-004 (middleware before/after audit) | **Implement** (SPEC-03 §3.5) | Small change. Plugins can rewrite tool I/O silently today. |\n| CTX-001 (per-item provenance for injected context) | **Partially implement**: skills, knowledge and other injected context carry source path and trust state (SPEC-03 §3.4). The full provenance graph is post-v1. | The risky injected sources are covered. A full implementation is a large redesign with low marginal safety benefit once trust gating exists. |\n| CTX-002 (freshness and version applicability of knowledge) | **Descoped to post-v1**, with this written rationale: auto-extraction is off by default (DEC-15) and knowledge is trust-gated, so stale knowledge can only come from the operator's own explicit saves. | Accepted risk, recorded. |\n| UI-006/007, DEDUP-003, \"no Git remote\", SUBP-004/005 deferrals | **Recorded as superseded** in REQUIREMENTS §2 (Ratatui adopted; on-demand tool groups; public GitHub). SUBP-004 and SUBP-005 are replaced by SPEC-02. | Governance hygiene (HIST-11). |\n\n## DEC-05: v1 evaluation protocol and thresholds\n\n**Chosen protocol (SPEC-10):**\n- 40 held-out T2 tasks, at least 20 from external repositories at pinned commits, across JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go, with at least 6 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug).\n- 5 runs per task and configuration.\n- Peers: Goose and OpenCode, on the same model and budgets.\n- 9 T4 fault classes × 5 runs.\n- 8 T3 long tasks × 5 runs.\n\n**Amendment 2026-10-17 (governance).** The T4 protocol enumerates **nine** distinct fault scenarios (SPEC-10 §2.5, ACCEPTANCE §6.2): refused connection, 5xx/overloaded, stream cut mid-tool-call, output-limit truncation, hanging test command, disk full, context overflow at 32k, malformed tool-call JSON, and SIGTERM-then-resume. The summary count previously read \"8\" while listing all nine; the union of the distinct scenarios is retained as **nine** classes × 5 runs. No scenario is dropped or merged. Corrected here, in SPEC-10 §2.5 and in the REQUIREMENTS ledger (REQ-QUAL-105).\n\n**Amendment 2026-10-18 (owner decision, T3 false-presence gate).** For the T3 closing fact-sheet probe (REQ-QUAL-109, ACCEPTANCE §6.3), **false-presence = 0** (claiming a missing file is present) is gated in addition to **false-absence = 0** (claiming an existing file is absent), so an agent cannot trivially satisfy false-absence = 0 by answering `present` for every fact. Every T3 task fact sheet is required to contain both `expected: \"present\"` and `expected: \"absent\"` facts.\n\n**Thresholds, all must hold:**\n\n| Metric | Threshold |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED | **0** (hard) |\n| Held-out T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | **≥ 60% absolute** and **≥ (best matched peer − 10 points)** |\n| Correctness per task class | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 outcome truthfulness | 100% |\n| T4 hangs beyond budget + 5 min | 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | 0 |\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":826638073}},"started_at_ms":1792913931815,"completed_at_ms":1792913932642}}
