 // Deterministic .flightlog session recording (default: false)\ncli/src/types.ts:102:  /** The operation's deadline expired before an answer was received (bridge-level; the runner reports its own via `timed_out`). */\ncli/src/types.ts:107: * How an automatically continued turn ends. Progressing work has no step or time ceiling by default: it ends on\ncli/src/types.ts:112:  /** Operator-set total steps for one turn (STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED); Infinity (the default) when none was set. */\ncli/src/types.ts:114:  /** Operator-set wall-clock minutes for one turn (TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED); Infinity (the default) when none was set. */\ncli/src/theme.ts:20:  default: {\ncli/src/theme.ts:86:  private activeThemeName: string = \"default\";\ncli/src/theme.ts:87:  private currentScheme: ColorScheme = PRESET_THEMES.default;\ncli/src/ui.ts:40:      // ora's default stdin discarding puts stdin in raw mode and leaves readline paused afterwards,\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:48:| L3 | Throwaway git repo with a broken `add` and a `node:test` test. `NEXUS_PROVIDER=chatgpt NEXUS_MODEL=gpt-6-luna nexus run \"...fix it so the existing test passes. Do not modify the test.\"` | `TASK COMPLETED - VERIFIED (npm test)`. The fix is correct and the test is unmodified, so the label is truthful. It took 7 requests, 83,331 input and 376 output tokens, 18 s. The run also showed: `npm test` executed without approval (SEC-01/VER-01 confirmed live); `.nexus/` left untracked in the workspace (PER-06); `context_limit=65536 (client_default)` (PRV-06b). | see log | `evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \"Blocked\" is established, from reproduced defects. \"Qualified\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\ncli/src/providers.ts:7: * - Provider definition (PROVIDERS): identity, wire protocol, default base URL, credential variable, auth style.\neval/README.md:20:| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\neval/README.md:24:| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\neval/README.md:44:- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\neval/README.md:57:| T4 fault injector | not started |\neval/README.md:69:only (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:9:| [DEC-01](#dec-01-default-execution-posture) | Default execution posture | Review by default; auto only in trusted workspaces | No (resolved) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:19:| [DEC-11](#dec-11-retention-defaults) | Retention defaults | 90 days / 2 GB; audit log 10 MB × 5; first GC needs acknowledgement | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:23:| [DEC-15](#dec-15-knowledge-auto-extraction) | Knowledge auto-extraction | Off by default, opt-in | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:28:## DEC-01: Default execution posture\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:30:**Question.** What protects the user by default from model-initiated command execution and network egress? See SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05 and TUI-07.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:34:| A | Review by default: write, exec and egress ask | Safest. More prompts. Changes existing users' habits. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:35:| B | Auto with an enforced sandbox by default | Few prompts. bwrap is unavailable on some hosts (WSL, rootless containers), and the Docker fallback is unpinned and networked. Egress is unsolved. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:43:- The eval and demo runners pass `--yes` explicitly.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:49:**Options.** (A) Remove the REPL. **(B, chosen)** The REPL is a supported secondary surface: used for non-TTY input, scripting and fallback, with its approvals fixed to the TUI's standard. (C) The REPL stays the default.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:51:**Rationale.** The REPL is the only interactive surface when stdin or stdout is not a terminal, and when the Rust TUI is missing. Removing it loses a fallback. Keeping it as the default contradicts UI-004.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:75:| CTX-002 (freshness and version applicability of knowledge) | **Descoped to post-v1**, with this written rationale: auto-extraction is off by default (DEC-15) and knowledge is trust-gated, so stale knowledge can only come from the operator's own explicit saves. | Accepted risk, recorded. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:84:- 8 T4 fault classes × 5 runs.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:96:| T4 outcome truthfulness | 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:97:| T4 hangs beyond budget + 5 min | 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:142:## DEC-11: Retention defaults\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:161:- One exception is allowed during the freeze: if the contest rules permit errata, a single erratum may state that the documented deploy builds the legacy Experiment-1 Worker and that reproduction is operator-host only. The owner checks the rules first; the default is no change.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:162:- Client work that touches `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` (PLAN-01 task 8, `--yes`) is deferred until after judging. Until then, the client keeps backward-compatible behaviour for `nexus run` invoked by the demo. In practice the demo passes the auto posture explicitly via `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` in its own environment once the client changes, and no demo file needs editing, because the env var is read by the client.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:172:**Chosen:** off by default; opt-in with `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, with a visible notice each time a rule is saved. Workspace knowledge is loaded only when the workspace is trusted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:192:- The standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 tasks) and the T4 subset run in both profiles.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:217:| X6 | After judging: provide a clean Cloudflare account and VM for CON-106. During judging: check whether contest rules permit an erratum (default: no change) | DEC-13 | Post-contest 