endpoint <url>\", \"Endpoint to diagnose (default: as a session would resolve it)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:324:    .option(\"--timeout <ms>\", \"Per-check time limit in milliseconds (default 4000)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:666:  .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:667:  .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model name identifier (default: active model in LM Studio/vLLM)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:668:  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory (default: current directory)\")\ncli/src/config.ts:20:  // 1. Installation directory defaults\ncli/src/config.ts:35:  //    shipped default already applied in step 1 and must not outrank the user's global config)\ncli/src/config.ts:65:/** Base URL of a provider connection: the operator's override (flag or NEXUS_<ID>_BASE_URL), else the provider default. */\ncli/src/config.ts:185: * defaults. There is no default step or time ceiling: progressing work continues until it completes, is cancelled,\ncli/src/fewshots.ts:113:    // Default to precise edit exemplar\ncli/src/tools.ts:8:import { CapabilityRegistry, HARNESS_TOOLS, defaultRegistry } from \"./core/capabilities.js\";\ncli/src/tools.ts:10:export { HARNESS_TOOLS, defaultRegistry };\ncli/src/tools.ts:113:/** Default `run_command` deadline in the Rust runner (seconds); mirrored here so the bridge can outlast it. */\ncli/src/tools.ts:115:/** Extra time the bridge waits beyond the runner's own deadline (kill grace + reply), so the runner's structured result wins. */\ncli/src/tools.ts:120: * Deadline ownership for one RPC. For `run_command` the runner owns the command deadline (`runnerSecs`) and the bridge's\ncli/src/tools.ts:123:export function rpcDeadlines(toolName: string, args: Record<string, any>): { runnerSecs?: number; bridgeMs: number } {\ncli/src/tools.ts:125:    const runnerSecs = typeof args.timeout_secs === \"number\" && args.timeout_secs > 0 ? args.timeout_secs : RUN_COMMAND_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SECS;\ncli/src/tools.ts:126:    return { runnerSecs, bridgeMs: (runnerSecs + RPC_GRACE_SECS) * 1000 };\ncli/src/tools.ts:134:  private defaultShell: string;\ncli/src/tools.ts:152:    defaultShell: string = \"bash\",\ncli/src/tools.ts:160:    this.defaultShell = defaultShell;\ncli/src/tools.ts:253:        this.rpcProcess.kill(\"SIGTERM\");\ncli/src/tools.ts:328:    // The runner's deadline is stated explicitly (never left to the Rust default) so the two timers cannot disagree.\ncli/src/tools.ts:329:    const params = deadlines.runnerSecs === undefined ? args : { ...args, timeout_secs: deadlines.runnerSecs };\ncli/src/tools.ts:344:            error: `RPC request for '${toolName}' timed out after ${timeoutMs / 1000}s without an answer from the command runner (result unknown)`,\ncli/src/tools.ts:603:          // The end of the run's output (where runners report counts): bounded, and what coverage is judged from.\ncli/src/tools.ts:750:    // Default the shell and wrap with sandbox if enabled\ncli/src/tools.ts:753:        args.shell = this.defaultShell;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:55:   - covers vLLM (`max_model_len`), llama.cpp (`GET /props` → `default_generation_settings.n_ctx`), LM Studio (`GET /api/v0/models` → `loaded_context_length`), and Ollama (`POST /api/show` → `model_info.*.context_length`, or `num_ctx`);\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:57:   - only then uses the 65536 default, labelled `client_default` in `/status`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:60:4. **REQ-PRV-104.** Every network call has a timeout and honours operator cancel. Inference has separate first-byte (default 120 s), idle inter-chunk (default 120 s) and optional total timeouts. Replays of timed-out generations are bounded (max 1) and visible.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:69:   - **(a) Live:** Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration, through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`. The proxy strips every gateway extension and, in a second profile, emulates the llama.cpp, vLLM and Ollama `/models` and overflow shapes. In both profiles, Nexus passes the standalone T2 subset and the T4 subset at the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 threshold, and turns are recorded with receipts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:78:10. **REQ-TUI-105.** At session start (TUI and REPL) the endpoint is probed with a 3 s `GET /models`. An unreachable or misconfigured endpoint is reported with the URL, the cause, and the fix (`nexus doctor`, `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, `/connect`). A never-reachable endpoint ends the turn with guidance after a bounded wait (default 2 minutes for \"never succeeded this session\", versus the existing 20-minute recovery deadline for \"was working\").\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:83:- **Timeouts.** In `client.ts:744-747,1627-1630`, replace the single `AbortSignal.timeout(total)` with a watchdog that is reset on each chunk. The env keys `LOCAL_LLM_FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT_MS`, `LOCAL_LLM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS` and `LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS` (total, default 0 = off for local, 900 s for cloud) are operator-only (SPEC-03).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:86:- **Never-reachable bound.** In `provider_recovery.ts`, add a `everSucceeded` flag per endpoint per session. When it is false, the deadline is `NEXUS_FIRST_CONTACT_DEADLINE_MS` (default 120000).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:91:- Changing the default total timeout for local endpoints to \"off\" (idle and first-byte only) is a behaviour change. It is beneficial for slow local generation, and the release notes must mention it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:106:| ACC-INF-10 | ACCEPTANCE §4.2 passes: the live stripped-proxy profiles (plain, plus emulated llama.cpp/vLLM/Ollama shapes) on the standalone T2 and T4 subsets, and server-kind conformance fixtures in CI. Receipts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:112:- SPEC-10 provides the standalone task set and runner.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:23:| Runtime services | The local inference gateway is configured in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`: endpoint `https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`, model `engineering/b0`, key redacted, `LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL=bash`. The repo-tracked `cli/.env` holds LM Studio defaults (`localhost:1234`, key \"local\"). **The audit sent no requests to the gateway.** With owner authorization (2026-10-14, small spend), it made live cloud calls through the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections: two `providers verify` runs and one `nexus run` bug-fix task. See EVIDENCE §3. | RT (values redacted) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:24:| External dependencies | Node ≥ 20 (runtime), GitHub Releases (installer), optional bubblewrap/Docker (sandbox), optional cloud providers (OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, ChatGPT/Copilot OAuth, compatible), optional MCP servers, DuckDuckGo (default `search_web`). | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:45:- **No default step ceiling.** Turns end on completion, cancel, stagnation or failure.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:59:1. **Safe by default on untrusted input.** Content from a repository, a web page, a skill or a tool output cannot cause unapproved host execution, egress, or configuration changes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:65:7. **Qualified.** Held-out matched evaluation, plus fault injection, meeting the pre-registered thresholds in DEC-05.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:103:| Model → host shell | Approval or sandbox | Default auto with no sandbox (SEC-01); verifier runs bypass even review mode (VER-01); prose and reasoning JSON executed (VER-02/03) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:134:| Agent loop and core (`cli/src/agent.ts`, `core/{turn,app,execution_tracking,objective,provider_recovery,operation_runner}.ts`, `team.ts`) | 9 | Full read | A_core_agent | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:139:| Rust harness-core: `core/src/{main, file_ops, runner, search, git_ops, cst, trigram}.rs`, `core/tests` | 9 | main/runner full read; file_ops mostly full (delimiter validator 400-575 skipped); others grep + runtime | C | file_ops.rs:400-575 not reviewed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:169:| SEC-01 | S1 | B | Every interactive run | `repl.ts:69`, `sidecar.ts:935`, `index.ts:93,115`, `runner.rs:116-157` | SRC | Prompt-injected host commands run without a prompt or sandbox | REQ-SEC-101 (SPEC-01) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:176:| TUI-07 | S2 | B | Default posture | `sidecar.ts:935`; `quickstart.md:55` | SRC + DOC | Docs imply review; the default is auto | REQ-SEC-101 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:177:| SEC-02 | S2 | RR | run_command | `security.ts:12-23,78-89`; `runner.rs:64-107` | RT | Denylist bypassed; false positives | REQ-SEC-108 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:182:| SEC-07 | S2 | B | Cancel and exit | `tools.ts:247-347`; `runner.rs:164-223` | RT | Orphaned processes | REQ-SEC-106, REQ-AGT-109 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:183:| SEC-08 | S3 | RR | Output and reads | `runner.rs:177-193`; `file_ops.rs:205-277` | MEAS (785 MB / 590 MB RSS) | OOM risk | REQ-SEC-107 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:187:| TUI-01 | S1 | B | Cancel or quit during a tool | `tools.ts`; `runner.rs:167`; `live_state.rs:1566` | RT (PTY s8/s9) | Stop does not stop; orphans after quit | REQ-AGT-109, REQ-SEC-106 (SPEC-02) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:208:| PRV-15 | S3 | RR | search_web | `search_web.ts:49,94,143-152` | SRC | Fabricated \"result\"; DuckDuckGo default | REQ-PRV-108 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:209:| PRV-06 | S2 | B | Standalone LM Studio and llama.cpp | `provider_capabilities.ts:29,72` | SRC + INF | 65536 default; overflow ends the turn | REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-102 (SPEC-05) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:252:| AGT-11 | S3 | RR | Team outcome | `operation_runner.ts:651-663` | SRC | COMPLETE without a change | REQ-AGT-107 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:253:| AGT-12 | S4 | RR | Operation bound | `operation_runner.ts:95-137` | SRC | Dead-end decision | REQ-AGT-107 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:297:| PRV-06b | S3 | B (via REQ-PRV-101) | Cloud context sizing | `provider_capabilities.ts` | RT (live): ChatGPT run reported `context_limit=65536 (client_default)` | Large-window cloud models are under-used, and small-window ones overflow | Covered by REQ-PRV-101, extended to provider catalog limits |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:337:| **Implementation self-assessment** (what the code does) | **Blocked.** 31 blocker requirements (REQUIREMENTS §3), plus the partially met carried commitment REQ-AGT-002. Five themes: (1) unsafe defaults and injection-to-action paths; (2) process ownership; (3) shipped-product parity; (4) continuity gaps in resume and work units; (5) standalone context sizing. | Source + reproductions above |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:358:  - Same-runner byte-reproducible packages.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:372:- No cross-runner reproducibility check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER**: packaged TUI default, documented commands work, single version identity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: launcher routing, doctor fixes, installer messaging. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:18:**The packaged TUI is unreachable.** No command reaches the TUI. `nexus --live` returns \"unknown option\". The packaged `lib/core/nexus-tui --live` fails with \"sidecar not found\" because it assumes the checkout layout (`core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live.rs:126-131`). Doctor nevertheless reports `PASS tui.build` (REL-01, TUI-04, DX-05; RUNTIME). The ISSUE12 requirement UI-004 (\"the TUI is the default interactive surface\") is therefore false for the shipped product.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:65:- **Commander default action** (`cli/src/index.ts:745-757`). With no args, if `process.stdin.isTTY && process.stdout.isTTY` and `nexus-tui` resolves (`NEXUS_HOME/lib/core/nexus-tui`, or `<repo>/core/target/release/nexus-tui`), `execFileSync`/`spawn` it with `--live --sidecar <resolved> --node process.execPath -- <args>` and `stdio: inherit`, and exit with its code. Otherwise fall back to the REPL with a one-line notice.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:66:- **Top-level `--repl`, `--live`, `-r/--resume [id]`, `--approve`.** Declared as global options that map onto the default action, so the USER_MANUAL commands work (DEC-02).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:99:- Removing the free-text default from `harness.sh` changes the developer workflow: `nexus fix the bug` becomes `nexus run \"fix the bug\"`. Alternatively, keep free text but only when the first word is not a valid identifier-like command name. Recommended: explicit `run`. Release notes must say so.\ncli/src/doctor.ts:28:import { defaultSessionsDir } from \"./session.js\";\ncli/src/doctor.ts:29:import { defaultTaskStateDir } from \"./core/state.js\";\ncli/src/doctor.ts:92:  /** Home directory for state checks; defaults to the operator's home. */\ncli/src/doctor.ts:273: * installation `.env`, then the built-in default.\ncli/src/doctor.ts:291:    let source = \"default\";\ncli/src/doctor.ts:298:    else if (value === \"(not set)\" || (fallback && value === fallback)) source = \"default\";\ncli/src/doctor.ts:552:    { id: \"state.sessions\", dir: ctx.home === os.homedir() ? defaultSessionsDir() : path.join(ctx.home, \".nexus\", \"sessions\"), what: \"saved sessions\" },\ncli/src/doctor.ts:553:    { id: \"state.tasks\", dir: ctx.home === os.homedir() ? defaultTaskStateDir() : path.join(ctx.home, \".nexus\", \"tasks\"), what: \"durable task state\" },\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:1:# SPEC-01: Safe execution defaults and approval integrity\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:5:| Status | Ready. Default posture resolved by [DEC-01](../DECISIONS.md#dec-01-default-execution-posture) (option C: review in untrusted workspaces, auto in trusted ones). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:9:| Plan | [PLAN-01](../plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:14:Nexus's default interactive mode is `auto` on both surfaces (`cli/src/sidecar.ts:935`, `cli/src/index.ts:93,115`, `cli/src/repl.ts:69`). In `auto`:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:16:- `run_command` executes `bash -c <string>` on the host as the user (`core/src/runner.rs:116-157`). The only confinement is the working directory. No sandbox is applied unless `--sandbox` is passed (`cli/src/config.ts:107`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:17:- The only guard is a substring denylist, implemented twice (`cli/src/security.ts:12-23,78-89`; `core/src/runner.rs:64-107`). It is bypassed by `rm -r -f /`, `rm -rf \"$HOME\"` and `find / -delete`, and it blocks legitimate `rm -rf ./build` (SEC-02, reproduced).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:26:The REPL approval prompt is `[Y/n/d/a]` with Yes as the default (`cli/src/repl.ts:353,385`):\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:31:The packaged `nexus` opens the REPL by default (see SPEC-06), so this weaker surface is what release users get.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:43:| SEC-01 default auto, no sandbox | SOURCE | evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md §3 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:54:1. **REQ-SEC-101.** Without operator opt-in, no command execution and no network egress initiated by the model happens without either an operator decision or an enforced sandbox. Which one is the default is decided in DEC-01.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:64:   - All of them go through the Rust runner (sandbox, cancel and output bounds apply), never host `execSync`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:72:- Default posture wiring for the CLI, REPL and sidecar.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:101:Each capability declaration must state its class. A unit test enumerates the registry and fails on any capability without a class. MCP and plugin tools registered at runtime default to `exec`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:144:- Changing the default for untrusted workspaces from `auto` to review (DEC-01 option C) is a user-visible change. Release notes and the startup banner must state it. Provide `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` and `nexus trust .` + `--yes` for scripted users.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:146:- The test suites that assume auto default (`cli/test/harness.test.ts`, `sidecar*.test.ts`) must be updated to set the mode explicitly. This is a large but mechanical change.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:159:| Keep auto default and only document it | Contradicts REQ-SEC-101. Quickstart already says \"review requested actions\" (TUI-07). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:160:| Make the sandbox mandatory | bwrap is not available on all hosts (WSL, containers without userns), and Docker fallback is unpinned and networked (SEC-10). DEC-01 rejected it as the default (option B). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:177:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:184:- SPEC-06 makes the TUI the packaged default, which reduces exposure to the REPL but does not remove it.\ncli/src/client.ts:156: * the operator configured none, `operatorEndpoint`: the command-line endpoint or the built-in default). A key that a\ncli/src/client.ts:503:  /** \"cloud\" when `url` (default: the active endpoint) receives content outside the operator's machines/network. */\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Runs evaluation tasks against an agent configuration and appends one JSON line per run (see eval/README.md).\n// Each run gets a fresh workspace (the task's repository at its pinned commit, or its fixture), the agent runs with the\n// task's budgets and a wall-clock timeout, then the task's hidden tests (never present while the agent runs) and its\n// regression command are run in that workspace. Nothing is scored here: eval/score.mjs reads the JSON lines.\nimport { spawnSync, spawn } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\nconst args = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\nif (args.out) args.out = path.resolve(args.out); // agents run elsewhere: paths handed to them must be absolute\nif (!args.config || !args.out) {\n  console.error(\"usage: eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/<name>.json --out <dir> [--tasks eval/tasks] [--only id,id] [--runs N]\");\n  process.exit(2);\n}\nconst config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(args.config, \"utf8\"));\nconst tasksDir = path.resolve(args.tasks ?? path.join(ROOT, \"eval/tasks\"));\nconst runs = Number(args.runs ?? config.runs ?? 1);\nconst only = args.only ? new Set(String(args.only).split(\",\")) : null;\n// --pairs \"task run,task run\": rerun exactly these (runs that failed on infrastructure; see eval/infra.mjs).\nconst pairs = args.pairs ? String(args.pairs).split(\",\").filter(Boolean).map((p) => p.trim().split(/\\s+/)) : null;\nfs.mkdirSync(args.out, { recursive: true });\nconst resultsFile = path.join(args.out, \"results.jsonl\");\n\nconst identity = harnessIdentity();\nconst tasks = fs.readdirSync(tasksDir).filter((d) => fs.existsSync(path.join(tasksDir, d, \"task.json\")) && (!only || only.has(d))).sort();\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(args.out, \"manifest.json\"), JSON.stringify({ createdAt: new Date().toISOString(), harness: identity, config: redactConfig(config), runs, tasks, host: os.hostname(), node: process.version }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n\n// Run-major order (every task once, then again): a pass cut short still has the same number of runs per task.\nconst apiKey = readApiKey(config.apiKey);\nconst caFile = config.caFile ? expandHome(config.caFile) : null;\nconst caBundle = caFile ? writeCaBundle(caFile) : null;\nfor (let run = 1; run <= runs; run++) {\n  for (const id of tasks) {\n    if (pairs && !pairs.some(([t, r]) => t === id && Number(r) === run)) continue;\n    const task = { ...JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(tasksDir, id, \"task.json\"), \"utf8\")), dir: path.join(tasksDir, id) };\n    const record = await runOnce(task, run);\n    fs.appendFileSync(resultsFile, JSON.stringify(record) + \"\\n\");\n    console.log(`${new Date().toISOString()} ${config.name} ${id} run ${run}: ${record.turn?.outcome ?? record.error ?? `exit ${record.exitCode}`} hidden=${record.hiddenPass} regression=${record.regressionPass} ${Math.round(record.wallMs / 1000)}s`);\n  }\n}\n\nasync function runOnce(task, run) {\n  const ws = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), `nexus-eval-${task.id}-`));\n  const home = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-home-\"));\n  const base = { task: task.id, tier: task.tier, config: config.name, agent: config.agent ?? \"nexus\", run, harness: identity.string, model: config.model, startedAt: new Date().toISOString() };\n  try {\n    prepareWorkspace(task, ws);\n    const sourceBefore = treeDigest(task.dir);\n    const started = Date.now();\n    const agent = await runAgent(task, ws, home);\n    const wallMs = Date.now() - started;\n    // Agents run as the operator's user, so the task sources (hidden tests included) are readable; a run that changed\n    // them or names their path is marked contaminated rather than silently scored.\n    const contaminated = treeDigest(task.dir) !== sourceBefore || `${agent.stdout}${agent.stderr}`.includes(tasksDir);\n    const hidden = runCheck(task, ws, task.hidden, true);\n    const regression = task.regression ? runCheck(task, ws, task.regression, false) : null;\n    const turn = agent.json?.turn ?? null;\n    // Nexus reports a structured outcome; for the other agents a clean exit within the budget is their completion claim.\n    const claimedComplete = turn\n      ? turn.execution === \"COMPLETED\" && [\"VERIFIED\", \"REGRESSION_FREE\", \"UNVERIFIED\", \"NOT_REQUIRED\"].includes(turn.outcome)\n      : agent.code === 0 && !agent.timedOut;\n    return {\n      ...base,\n      wallMs,\n      exitCode: agent.code,\n      timedOut: agent.timedOut,\n      turn: turn && { execution: turn.execution, outcome: turn.outcome, reason: turn.reason ?? null, steps: turn.steps ?? null, contextNotRetained: turn.contextNotRetained ?? 0 },\n      claimedComplete,\n      claimedVerified: turn?.outcome === \"VERIFIED\",\n      hiddenPass: hidden.pass,\n      regressionPass: regression ? regression.pass : null,\n      falseVerified: turn?.outcome === \"VERIFIED\" && !hidden.pass,\n      contaminated,\n      tokens: agent.json?.tokenStats ?? null,\n      logs: saveLogs(task, run, agent, hidden, regression),\n    };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { ...base, wallMs: 0, error: String(err?.message ?? err), hiddenPass: false, regressionPass: null, falseVerified: false, claimedComplete: false, claimedVerified: false };\n  } finally {\n    if (!args.keep) {\n      fs.rmSync(ws, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction prepareWorkspace(task, ws) {\n  if (task.fixture) {\n    fs.cpSync(path.join(task.dir, task.fixture), ws, { recursive: true });\n    sh(\"git init -q && git add -A && git -c user.name=eval -c user.email=eval@example.invalid commit -qm fixture\", ws);\n  } else if (task.repo) {\n    const cache = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/.cache\", createHash(\"sha256\").update(task.repo.url).digest(\"hex\").slice(0, 16));\n    if (!fs.existsSync(cache)) sh(`git clone -q --no-checkout ${shellQuote(task.repo.url)} ${shellQuote(cache)}`, ROOT);\n    sh(`git -C ${shellQuote(cache)} cat-file -e ${task.repo.commit}^{commit} || git -C ${shellQuote(cache)} fetch -q origin ${task.repo.commit}`, ROOT);\n    sh(`git clone -q --shared ${shellQuote(cache)} ${shellQuote(ws)} && git -C ${shellQuote(ws)} checkout -q ${task.repo.commit}`, ROOT);\n  } else throw new Error(`task ${task.id} has neither fixture nor repo`);\n  for (const cmd of task.setup ?? []) sh(cmd, ws);\n}\n\n/**\n * The command line and environment for one agent run. Each agent gets a fresh HOME holding only its gateway settings\n * (no operator plugins, extensions or memory), the same endpoint and model, and the key through its environment.\n */\nfunction agentCommand(task, ws, home, budget) {\n  const ep = config.endpoint;\n  const keyEnv = apiKey ? { LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY: apiKey, OPENAI_API_KEY: apiKey, GW_KEY: apiKey } : {};\n  const caEnv = caBundle ? { NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS: caFile, SSL_CERT_FILE: caBundle, REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE: caBundle } : {};\n  // PWD too: some agents take the project from $PWD rather than the process's working directory.\n  const env = { ...process.env, ...(config.env ?? {}), ...keyEnv, ...caEnv, HOME: home, PWD: ws, XDG_CONFIG_HOME: path.join(home, \".config\"), XDG_DATA_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/share\"), XDG_STATE_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/state\") };\n  const agent = config.agent ?? \"nexus\";\n  if (agent === \"nexus\") {\n    env.LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT = ep;\n    return { cmd: process.execPath, argv: [path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist/index.js\"), \"run\", \"--json\", \"-w\", ws, \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", config.model, \"-s\", \"30\", \"--max-total-steps\", String(budget.steps), \"--max-turn-minutes\", String(budget.minutes), ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"aider\") {\n    return { cmd: \"aider\", argv: [\"--model\", `openai/${config.model}`, \"--openai-api-base\", ep, \"--yes-always\", \"--no-auto-commits\", \"--no-dirty-commits\", \"--no-gitignore\", \"--no-show-model-warnings\", \"--no-check-update\", \"--analytics-disable\", \"--no-pretty\", \"--no-fancy-input\", ...(config.args ?? []), \"--message\", task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"opencode\") {\n    const dir = path.join(home, \".config/opencode\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n    const limits = config.limits ?? { context: 65536, output: 8192 };\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"opencode.json\"), JSON.stringify({\n      $schema: \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n      autoupdate: false,\n      share: \"disabled\",\n      permission: { edit: \"allow\", bash: \"allow\", webfetch: \"deny\" },\n      provider: { gw: { npm: \"@ai-sdk/openai-compatible\", name: \"gateway\", options: { baseURL: ep, apiKey: \"{env:GW_KEY}\" }, models: { [config.model]: { name: config.model, limit: limits } } } },\n      model: `gw/${config.model}`,\n    }, null, 2));\n    // Provider packages are cached across runs (not per run): the cache holds code, not state.\n    env.XDG_CACHE_HOME = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/.cache/xdg-cache\");\n    return { cmd: \"opencode\", argv: [\"run\", \"--model\", `gw/${config.model}`, ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"goose\") {\n    const u = new URL(ep);\n    Object.assign(env, { GOOSE_PROVIDER: \"openai\", GOOSE_MODEL: config.model, OPENAI_HOST: u.origin, OPENAI_BASE_PATH: `${u.pathname.replace(/^\\/|\\/$/g, \"\")}/chat/completions`, GOOSE_MODE: \"auto\", GOOSE_DISABLE_KEYRING: \"1\", GOOSE_CONTEXT_LIMIT: String(config.limits?.context ?? 65536) });\n    return { cmd: \"goose\", argv: [\"run\", \"--no-session\", \"--with-builtin\", \"developer\", ...(config.args ?? []), \"-t\", task.objective], env };\n  }\n  throw new Error(`agent ${agent} has no adapter`);\n}\n\nfunction runAgent(task, ws, home) {\n  const budget = { steps: task.steps ?? config.steps ?? 300, minutes: task.minutes ?? config.minutes ?? 120 };\n  const { cmd, argv, env } = agentCommand(task, ws, home, budget);\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    const child = spawn(cmd, argv, { cwd: ws, env, stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"], detached: true });\n    let stdout = \"\";\n    let stderr = \"\";\n    child.stdout.on(\"data\", (c) => (stdout += c));\n    child.stderr.on(\"data\", (c) => (stderr += c));\n    let timedOut = false;\n    // The whole process group: agents start helpers (servers, shells) that must not outlive the run.\n    const killGroup = (sig) => {\n      try {\n        process.kill(-child.pid, sig);\n      } catch {}\n    };\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n      timedOut = true;\n      killGroup(\"SIGTERM\");\n      setTimeout(() => killGroup(\"SIGKILL\"), 10_000).unref();\n    }, (budget.minutes + 5) * 60_000);\n    child.on(\"error\", (err) => (stderr += `spawn error: ${err.message}\\n`));\n    child.on(\"close\", (code) => {\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      killGroup(\"SIGKILL\");\n      resolve({ code, timedOut, stdout, stderr, json: lastJson(stdout) });\n    });\n  });\n}\n\nfunction runCheck(task, ws, check, hidden) {\n  if (hidden && check.dir) fs.cpSync(path.join(task.dir, check.dir), path.join(ws, check.into ?? check.dir), { recursive: true });\n  const r = spawnSync(\"bash\", [\"-c\", check.command], { cwd: ws, encoding: \"utf8\", timeout: (check.timeoutSec ?? 300) * 1000, env: { ...process.env, CI: \"1\" } });\n  return { pass: r.status === 0, status: r.status, output: `${r.stdout ?? \"\"}${r.stderr ?? \"\"}`.slice(-20_000) };\n}\n\nfunction saveLogs(task, run, agent, hidden, regression) {\n  const dir = path.join(args.out, \"logs\", `${task.id}-${run}`);\n  fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"agent.stdout.json\"), agent.stdout);\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"agent.stderr.log\"), agent.stderr.slice(-200_000));\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"hidden.log\"), hidden.output);\n  if (regression) fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"regression.log\"), regression.output);\n  return path.relative(args.out, dir);\n}\n\nfunction treeDigest(dir) {\n  const hash = createHash(\"sha256\");\n  const walk = (d) => {\n    for (const e of fs.readdirSync(d, { withFileTypes: true }).sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))) {\n      const p = path.join(d, e.name);\n      hash.update(path.relative(dir, p));\n      if (e.isDirectory()) walk(p);\n      else hash.update(fs.readFileSync(p));\n    }\n  };\n  walk(dir);\n  return hash.digest(\"hex\");\n}\n\nfunction lastJson(text) {\n  const start = text.indexOf(\"{\");\n  for (let i = start; i >= 0 && i < text.length; i = text.indexOf(\"{\", i + 1)) {\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(text.slice(i));\n    } catch {}\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction harnessIdentity() {\n  const git = (...a) => spawnSync(\"git\", a, { cwd: ROOT, encoding: \"utf8\" }).stdout.trim();\n  const commit = git(\"rev-parse\", \"--short=12\", \"HEAD\");\n  const dirty = Boolean(git(\"status\", \"--porcelain\", \"--untracked-files=no\", \"--\", \".\", \":(exclude)cli/dist\"));\n  return { commit, dirty, string: `${commit}${dirty ? \"-dirty\" : \"\"}` };\n}\n\n/** `{ file, var }`: the key is read from a KEY=value file (e.g. ~/.config/nexus/config.env); never logged. */\nfunction readApiKey(spec) {\n  if (!spec) return null;\n  const file = expandHome(spec.file);\n  const line = fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").find((l) => l.startsWith(`${spec.var}=`));\n  if (!line) throw new Error(`${spec.var} not found in ${spec.file}`);\n  return line.slice(spec.var.length + 1).trim();\n}\n\n/** System CAs plus the gateway's CA, for agents that read SSL_CERT_FILE / REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE (Python, Rust). */\nfunction writeCaBundle(caFile) {\n  const system = [\"/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt\", \"/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt\"].find((f) => fs.existsSync(f));\n  const bundle = path.join(args.out, \"ca-bundle.pem\");\n  fs.writeFileSync(bundle, (system ? fs.readFileSync(system, \"utf8\") : \"\") + \"\\n\" + fs.readFileSync(caFile, \"utf8\"));\n  return bundle;\n}\n\nfunction redactConfig(c) {\n  const env = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(c.env ?? {}).map(([k, v]) => [k, /KEY|TOKEN|SECRET|PASSWORD/i.test(k) ? \"***\" : v]));\n  return { ...c, env };\n}\n\nfunction expandHome(f) {\n  return f.replace(/^~(?=\\/)/, os.homedir());\n}\n\nfunction sh(cmd, cwd) {\n  const r = spawnSync(\"bash\", [\"-c\", cmd], { cwd, encoding: \"utf8\" });\n  if (r.status !== 0) throw new Error(`${cmd}: ${r.stderr || r.stdout}`);\n  return r.stdout;\n}\n\nfunction shellQuote(s) {\n  return `'${String(s).replace(/'/g, `'\\\\''`)}'`;\n}\n\nfunction parseArgs(list) {\n  const out = {};\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n    const key = list[i].replace(/^--/, \"\");\n    const next = list[i + 1];\n    if (next === undefined || next.startsWith(\"--\")) out[key] = true;\n    else {\n      out[key] = next;\n      i++;\n    }\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\n\n`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\nseparately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\n\n```bash\nnode eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\nnode eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\n```\n\nEach run: a fresh workspace (the task's `fixture`, or its `repo.url` at `repo.commit`, cached in `eval/.cache`), a fresh\n`HOME`, the agent with the task's budgets and a wall-clock timeout, then the task's **hidden** tests (copied in only\nafter the agent has stopped) and its `regression` command. `manifest.json` records the harness build (commit, dirty),\nthe configuration (secrets in `env` masked), host and Node version; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`.\n\n## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Pre-registered thresholds (from the assessment, fixed before any live run)\n\n- false VERIFIED = 0 across all runs;\n- T2 hidden-test pass rate (pooled over all T2 runs of a configuration, point estimate, 95 % intervals reported) ≥ the\n  best matched peer on the same local model **minus 10 percentage points**; and no task where that peer passes ≥ 4/5\n  runs while Nexus passes ≤ 1/5. (Fixed 2026-10-13, before the first scored run. Rationale: at ~50 runs per\n  configuration the 95 % interval half-width near 50 % is ~13 points, so a tighter margin is not distinguishable from\n  noise and a looser one would accept a clear loss; the per-task guard stops a pooled rate hiding a task class Nexus\n  cannot do.) The 6-task pilot is directional only; qualification needs the full task set;\n- T3: false-absence claims = 0 and steering constraints honoured in ≥ 95 % of runs;\n- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\n- ≥ 5 runs per task-configuration, per-task results with 95 % intervals.\n\n## Status\n\n| Part | State |\n|---|---|\n| Runner, scorer, manifest, per-run logs | done |\n| T1 self-test (`selftest-add`, scripted model, in `make test` via `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`) | done |\n| Nexus adapter | done |\n| Peer adapters (OpenCode, Goose, Aider, Codex) | not started |\n| T2/T3 task set (pilot 12, external repos, hidden tests) | not started |\n| T3 fact-sheet scorer (absence claims) and steering checks | not started |\n| T4 fault injector | not started |\n| Live runs | blocked on inference hours, cloud budget and peer installs (operator decision) |\n\n## Pilot 2026-10-13 (4 h appliance window)\n\nConfigurations `configs/pilot-*.json`: Nexus, Aider 0.86.2, OpenCode 1.18.35, Goose 1.27.2, all on\n`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\nfixture tasks (`t2-*`; each hidden test checked to fail on the fixture and pass on a reference fix kept outside the\nrepo). Budgets 60 steps / 20 min per task (Nexus steps; others by wall clock). The four agents run concurrently on the\nsame worker, so wall times include queueing.\n\nDeviations from §9, recorded before the run: fixture tasks rather than external repositories at pinned commits; T2\nonly (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\none `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\nruns per task as many as the window allows, run-major, target 5.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26439}},"started_at_ms":1792914191158,"completed_at_ms":1792914191158}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:43:12.085Z","ordinal":329698,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17203-76d5-7210-b91b-93934d167c81","call_id":"call_c5512472a4534f12900a964d6a55ea9b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10027)\nTotal output lines: 480\n\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 12329)\nTotal output lines: 524\n\n{\"agent\":\"KimiCode-defect-scan\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-objective-continuation-timeout\",\"since\":\"2026-10-25T08:08:00Z\",\"scope\":\"Short local-mock provider-client blocker reproduction; no live inference.\"}\ncli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:18:/** Async: the scripted gateway answers from this process, so the runner must not block its event loop. */\ncli/src/approval_review.ts:73:    default: {\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:57:  /** Prompt history file; defaults to ~/.nexus_history. */\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:316:   * per kind (default, --llm) waits; cancellation and shutdown end waiting requests with that outcome.\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:908:    .option(\"--max-total-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\")\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:909:    .option(\"--strict-token-count\", \"Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\")\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:910:    .option(\"--max-turn-minutes <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\")\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:911:    .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:24:| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\ncli/src/types.ts:48:  apiKey?: string;           // Optional for local servers (defaults to \"local\")\ncli/src/types.ts:49:  maxSteps: number;          // Steps per segment (default 30). With `continuation` (the default), a segment boundary is a durable checkpoint, never the end of the task.\ncli/src/types.ts:55:  temperature: number;       // Default 0.2 for precise coding\ncli/src/types.ts:57:  shell: string;             // Linux shell: \"bash\", \"zsh\", \"sh\" (default: \"bash\")\ncli/src/types.ts:66:  credentialOrigin?: string;     // Origin apiKey belongs to (default: endpoint's origin); never sent elsewhere\ncli/src/types.ts:67:  contextLimit?: number;     // Maximum model context window token limit (default: 65536)\ncli/src/types.ts:68:  completionReserveTokens?: number; // Context reserved for each model completion (default: 8192)\ncli/src/types.ts:69:  toolResponseReserveTokens?: number; // Tool-output headroom policy for the following tool results (default: min(4096, context/8))\ncli/src/types.ts:72:   * Off by default: without it an unmeasured request proceeds on the labelled client estimate (provider_capabilities.ts).\ncli/src/types.ts:75:  sandbox?: boolean | string; // Linux namespace / bwrap / container isolation (default: false)\ncli/src/types.ts:76:  worktree?: boolean;        // Isolated ephemeral git worktree execution (default: false)\ncli/src/types.ts:78:  verifierTimeoutSecs?: number; // Deadline for the completion verifier (default 300); env NEXUS_VERIFIER_TIMEOUT_SECS\ncli/src/types.ts:79:  recordFlight?: boolean;    // Deterministic .flightlog session recording (default: false)\ncli/src/types.ts:102:  /** The operation's deadline expired before an answer was received (bridge-level; the runner reports its own via `timed_out`). */\ncli/src/types.ts:107: * How an automatically continued turn ends. Progressing work has no step or time ceiling by default: it ends on\ncli/src/types.ts:112:  /** Operator-set total steps for one turn (STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED); Infinity (the default) when none was set. */\ncli/src/types.ts:114:  /** Operator-set wall-clock minutes for one turn (TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED); Infinity (the default) when none was set. */\ncli/src/theme.ts:20:  default: {\ncli/src/theme.ts:86:  private activeThemeName: string = \"default\";\ncli/src/theme.ts:87:  private currentScheme: ColorScheme = PRESET_THEMES.default;\ncli/src/ui.ts:40:      // ora's default stdin discarding puts stdin in raw mode and leaves readline paused afterwards,\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:48:| L3 | Throwaway git repo with a broken `add` and a `node:test` test. `NEXUS_PROVIDER=chatgpt NEXUS_MODEL=gpt-6-luna nexus run \"...fix it so the existing test passes. Do not modify the test.\"` | `TASK COMPLETED - VERIFIED (npm test)`. The fix is correct and the test is unmodified, so the label is truthful. It took 7 requests, 83,331 input and 376 output tokens, 18 s. The run also showed: `npm test` executed without approval (SEC-01/VER-01 confirmed live); `.nexus/` left untracked in the workspace (PER-06); `context_limit=65536 (client_default)` (PRV-06b). | see log | `evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \"Blocked\" is established, from reproduced defects. \"Qualified\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\ncli/src/providers.ts:7: * - Provider definition (PROVIDERS): identity, wire protocol, default base URL, credential variable, auth style.\neval/README.md:20:| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\neval/README.md:24:| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\neval/README.md:44:- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\neval/README.md:57:| T4 fault injector | not started |\neval/README.md:69:only (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:9:| [DEC-01](#dec-01-default-execution-posture) | Default execution posture | Review by default; auto only in trusted workspaces | No (resolved) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:19:| [DEC-11](#dec-11-retention-defaults) | Retention defaults | 90 days / 2 GB; audit log 10 MB × 5; first GC needs acknowledgement | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:23:| [DEC-15](#dec-15-knowledge-auto-extraction) | Knowledge auto-extraction | Off by default, opt-in | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:28:## DEC-01: Default execution posture\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:30:**Question.** What protects the user by default from model-initiated command execution and network egress? See SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05 and TUI-07.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:34:| A | Review by default: write, exec and egress ask | Safest. More prompts. Changes existing users' habits. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:35:| B | Auto with an enforced sandbox by default | Few prompts. bwrap is unavailable on some hosts (WSL, rootless containers), and the Docker fallback is unpinned and networked. Egress is unsolved. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:43:- The eval and demo runners pass `--yes` explicitly.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:49:**Options.** (A) Remove the REPL. **(B, chosen)** The REPL is a supported secondary surface: used for non-TTY input, scripting and fallback, with its approvals fixed to the TUI's standard. (C) The REPL stays the default.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:51:**Rationale.** The REPL is the only interactive surface when stdin or stdout is not a terminal, and when the Rust TUI is missing. Removing it loses a fallback. Keeping it as the default contradicts UI-004.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:75:| CTX-002 (freshness and version applicability of knowledge) | **Descoped to post-v1**, with this written rationale: auto-extraction is off by default (DEC-15) and knowledge is trust-gated, so stale knowledge can only come from the operator's own explicit saves. | Accepted risk, recorded. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:84:- 8 T4 fault classes × 5 runs.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:96:| T4 outcome truthfulness | 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:97:| T4 hangs beyond budget + 5 min | 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:142:## DEC-11: Retention defaults\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:161:- One exception is allowed during the freeze: if the contest rules permit errata, a single erratum may state that the documented deploy builds the legacy Experiment-1 Worker and that reproduction is operator-host only. The owner checks the rules first; the default is no change.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:162:- Client work that touches `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` (PLAN-01 task 8, `--yes`) is deferred until after judging. Until then, the client keeps backward-compatible behaviour for `nexus run` invoked by the demo. In practice the demo passes the auto posture explicitly via `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` in its own environment once the client changes, and no demo file needs editing, because the env var is read by the client.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:172:**Chosen:** off by default; opt-in with `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, with a visible notice each time a rule is saved. Workspace knowledge is loaded only when the workspace is trusted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:192:- The standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 tasks) and the T4 subset run in both profiles.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:217:| X6 | After judging: provide a clean Cloudflare account and VM for CON-106. During judging: check whether contest rules permit an erratum (default: no change) | DEC-13 | Post-contest |\ncli/src/index.ts:70:  .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:71:  .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:72:  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory (default: current directory)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:73:  .option(\"-s, --max-steps <number>\", \"Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:74:  .option(\"--max-total-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:75:  .option(\"--strict-token-count\", \"Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:76:  .option(\"--max-turn-minutes <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:77:  .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:79:  .option(\"-t, --temperature <number>\", \"Model temperature (default: 0.2)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:80:  .option(\"--shell <type>\", \"Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash)\", \"bash\")\ncli/src/index.ts:82:  .option(\"--context-limit <tokens>\", \"Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:85:  .option(\"--sandbox [mode]\", \"Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:94:  .option(\"--provider <id>\", \"Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:98:  .option(\"-r, --resume [id]\", \"Resume previous session (defaults to latest if id omitted)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:123:  .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Local LLM endpoint (default: http://localhost:1234/v1 or $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:124:  .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model name identifier (default: active model in LM Studio/vLLM)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:125:  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory to inspect and modify (default: current directory)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:127:  .option(\"--max-total-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:128:  .option(\"--strict-token-count\", \"Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:129:  .option(\"--max-turn-minutes <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:130:  .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:133:  .option(\"--shell <type>\", \"Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash or $LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL)\", \"bash\")\ncli/src/index.ts:135:  .option(\"--context-limit <tokens>\", \"Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:138:  .option(\"--sandbox [mode]\", \"Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:147:  .option(\"--provider <id>\", \"Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:170:        // Fallback to default\ncli/src/index.ts:234:  .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:235:  .option(\"-k, --api-key <key>\", \"API key / token (default: $LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:312:    .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Endpoint to diagnose (default: as a session would resolve it)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:324:    .option(\"--timeout <ms>\", \"Per-check time limit in milliseconds (default 4000)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:666:  .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:667:  .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model name identifier (default: active model in LM Studio/vLLM)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:668:  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory (default: current directory)\")\ncli/src/config.ts:20:  // 1. Installation directory defaults\ncli/src/config.ts:35:  //    shipped default already applied in step 1 and must not outrank the user's global config)\ncli/src/config.ts:65:/** Base URL of a provider connection: the operator's override (flag or NEXUS_<ID>_BASE_URL), else the provider default. */\ncli/src/config.ts:185: * defaults. There is no default step or time ceiling: progressing work continues until it completes, is cancelled,\ncli/src/fewshots.ts:113:    // Default to precise edit exemplar\ncli/src/tools.ts:8:import { CapabilityRegistry, HARNESS_TOOLS, defaultRegistry } from \"./core/capabilities.js\";\ncli/src/tools.ts:10:export { HARNESS_TOOLS, defaultRegistry };\ncli/src/tools.ts:113:/** Default `run_command` deadline in the Rust runner (seconds); mirrored here so the bridge can outlast it. */\ncli/src/tools.ts:115:/** Extra time the bridge waits beyond the runner's own deadline (kill grace + reply), so the runner's structured result wins. */\ncli/src/tools.ts:120: * Deadline ownership for one RPC. For `run_command` the runner owns the command deadline (`runnerSecs`) and the bridge's\ncli/src/tools.ts:123:export function rpcDeadlines(toolName: string, args: Record<string, any>): { runnerSecs?: number; bridgeMs: number } {\ncli/src/tools.ts:125:    const runnerSecs = typeof args.timeout_secs === \"number\" && args.timeout_secs > 0 ? args.timeout_secs : RUN_COMMAND_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SECS;\ncli/src/tools.ts:126:    return { runnerSecs, bridgeMs: (runnerSecs + RPC_GRACE_SECS) * 1000 };\ncli/src/tools.ts:134:  private defaultShell: string;\ncli/src/tools.ts:152:    defaultShell: string = \"bash\",\ncli/src/tools.ts:160:    this.defaultShell = defaultShell;\ncli/src/tools.ts:253:        this.rpcProcess.kill(\"SIGTERM\");\ncli/src/tools.ts:328:    // The runner's deadline is stated explicitly (never left to the Rust default) so the two timers cannot disagree.\ncli/src/tools.ts:329:    const params = deadlines.runnerSecs === undefined ? args : { ...args, timeout_secs: deadlines.runnerSecs };\ncli/src/tools.ts:344:            error: `RPC request for '${toolName}' timed out after ${timeoutMs / 1000}s without an answer from the command runner (result unknown)`,\ncli/src/tools.ts:603:          // The end of the run's output (where runners report counts): bounded, and what coverage is judged from.\ncli/src/tools.ts:750:    // Default the shell and wrap with sandbox if enabled\ncli/src/tools.ts:753:        args.shell = this.defaultShell;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:55:   - covers vLLM (`max_model_len`), llama.cpp (`GET /props` → `default_generation_settings.n_ctx`), LM Studio (`GET /api/v0/models` → `loaded_context_length`), and Ollama (`POST /api/show` → `model_info.*.context_length`, or `num_ctx`);\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:57:   - only then uses the 65536 default, labelled `client_default` in `/status`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:60:4. **REQ-PRV-104.** Every network call has a timeout and honours operator cancel. Inference has separate first-byte (default 120 s), idle inter-chunk (default 120 s) and optional total timeouts. Replays of timed-out generations are bounded (max 1) and visible.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:69:   - **(a) Live:** Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration, through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`. The proxy strips every gateway extension and, in a second profile, emulates the llama.cpp, vLLM and Ollama `/models` and overflow shapes. In both profiles, Nexus passes the standalone T2 subset and the T4 subset at the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 threshold, and turns are recorded with receipts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:78:10. **REQ-TUI-105.** At session start (TUI and REPL) the endpoint is probed with a 3 s `GET /models`. An unreachable or misconfigured endpoint is reported with the URL, the cause, and the fix (`nexus doctor`, `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, `/connect`). A never-reachable endpoint ends the turn with guidance after a bounded wait (default 2 minutes for \"never succeeded this session\", versus the existing 20-minute recovery deadline for \"was working\").\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:83:- **Timeouts.** In `client.ts:744-747,1627-1630`, replace the single `AbortSignal.timeout(total)` with a watchdog that is reset on each chunk. The env keys `LOCAL_LLM_FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT_MS`, `LOCAL_LLM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS` and `LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS` (total, default 0 = off for local, 900 s for cloud) are operator-only (SPEC-03).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:86:- **Never-reachable bound.** In `provider_recovery.ts`, add a `everSucceeded` flag per endpoint per session. When it is false, the deadline is `NEXUS_FIRST_CONTACT_DEADLINE_MS` (default 120000).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:91:- Changing the default total timeout for local endpoints to \"off\" (idle and first-byte only) is a behaviour change. It is beneficial for slow local generation, and the release notes must mention it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:106:| ACC-INF-10 | ACCEPTANCE §4.2 passes: the live stripped-proxy profiles (plain, plus emulated llama.cpp/vLLM/Ollama shapes) on the standalone T2 and T4 subsets, and server-kind conformance fixtures in CI. Receipts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:112:- SPEC-10 provides the standalone task set and runner.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:23:| Runtime services | The local inference gateway is configured in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`: endpoint `https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`, model `engineering/b0`, key redacted, `LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL=bash`. The repo-tracked `cli/.env` holds LM Studio defaults (`localhost:1234`, key \"local\"). **The audit sent no requests to the gateway.** With owner authorization (2026-10-14, small spend), it made live cloud calls through the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections: two `providers verify` runs and one `nexus run` bug-fix task. See EVIDENCE §3. | RT (values redacted) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:24:| External dependencies | Node ≥ 20 (runtime), GitHub Releases (installer), optional bubblewrap/Docker (sandbox), optional cloud providers (OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, ChatGPT/Copilot OAuth, compatible), optional MCP servers, DuckDuckGo (default `search_web`). | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:45:- **No default step ceiling.** Turns end on completion, cancel, stagnation or failure.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:59:1. **Safe by default on untrusted input.*…27 tokens truncated…o default and only document it | Contradicts REQ-SEC-101. Quickstart already says \"review requested actions\" (TUI-07). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:160:| Make the sandbox mandatory | bwrap is not available on all hosts (WSL, containers without userns), and Docker fallback is unpinned and networked (SEC-10). DEC-01 rejected it as the default (option B). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:177:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:184:- SPEC-06 makes the TUI the packaged default, which reduces exposure to the REPL but does not remove it.\ncli/src/client.ts:156: * the operator configured none, `operatorEndpoint`: the command-line endpoint or the built-in default). A key that a\ncli/src/client.ts:503:  /** \"cloud\" when `url` (default: the active endpoint) receives content outside the operator's machines/network. */\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Runs evaluation tasks against an agent configuration and appends one JSON line per run (see eval/README.md).\n// Each run gets a fresh workspace (the task's repository at its pinned commit, or its fixture), the agent runs with the\n// task's budgets and a wall-clock timeout, then the task's hidden tests (never present while the agent runs) and its\n// regression command are run in that workspace. Nothing is scored here: eval/score.mjs reads the JSON lines.\nimport { spawnSync, spawn } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\nconst args = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\nif (args.out) args.out = path.resolve(args.out); // agents run elsewhere: paths handed to them must be absolute\nif (!args.config || !args.out) {\n  console.error(\"usage: eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/<name>.json --out <dir> [--tasks eval/tasks] [--only id,id] [--runs N]\");\n  process.exit(2);\n}\nconst config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(args.config, \"utf8\"));\nconst tasksDir = path.resolve(args.tasks ?? path.join(ROOT, \"eval/tasks\"));\nconst runs = Number(args.runs ?? config.runs ?? 1);\nconst only = args.only ? new Set(String(args.only).split(\",\")) : null;\n// --pairs \"task run,task run\": rerun exactly these (runs that failed on infrastructure; see eval/infra.mjs).\nconst pairs = args.pairs ? String(args.pairs).split(\",\").filter(Boolean).map((p) => p.trim().split(/\\s+/)) : null;\nfs.mkdirSync(args.out, { recursive: true });\nconst resultsFile = path.join(args.out, \"results.jsonl\");\n\nconst identity = harnessIdentity();\nconst tasks = fs.readdirSync(tasksDir).filter((d) => fs.existsSync(path.join(tasksDir, d, \"task.json\")) && (!only || only.has(d))).sort();\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(args.out, \"manifest.json\"), JSON.stringify({ createdAt: new Date().toISOString(), harness: identity, config: redactConfig(config), runs, tasks, host: os.hostname(), node: process.version }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n\n// Run-major order (every task once, then again): a pass cut short still has the same number of runs per task.\nconst apiKey = readApiKey(config.apiKey);\nconst caFile = config.caFile ? expandHome(config.caFile) : null;\nconst caBundle = caFile ? writeCaBundle(caFile) : null;\nfor (let run = 1; run <= runs; run++) {\n  for (const id of tasks) {\n    if (pairs && !pairs.some(([t, r]) => t === id && Number(r) === run)) continue;\n    const task = { ...JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(tasksDir, id, \"task.json\"), \"utf8\")), dir: path.join(tasksDir, id) };\n    const record = await runOnce(task, run);\n    fs.appendFileSync(resultsFile, JSON.stringify(record) + \"\\n\");\n    console.log(`${new Date().toISOString()} ${config.name} ${id} run ${run}: ${record.turn?.outcome ?? record.error ?? `exit ${record.exitCode}`} hidden=${record.hiddenPass} regression=${record.regressionPass} ${Math.round(record.wallMs / 1000)}s`);\n  }\n}\n\nasync function runOnce(task, run) {\n  const ws = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), `nexus-eval-${task.id}-`));\n  const home = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-home-\"));\n  const base = { task: task.id, tier: task.tier, config: config.name, agent: config.agent ?? \"nexus\", run, harness: identity.string, model: config.model, startedAt: new Date().toISOString() };\n  try {\n    prepareWorkspace(task, ws);\n    const sourceBefore = treeDigest(task.dir);\n    const started = Date.now();\n    const agent = await runAgent(task, ws, home);\n    const wallMs = Date.now() - started;\n    // Agents run as the operator's user, so the task sources (hidden tests included) are readable; a run that changed\n    // them or names their path is marked contaminated rather than silently scored.\n    const contaminated = treeDigest(task.dir) !== sourceBefore || `${agent.stdout}${agent.stderr}`.includes(tasksDir);\n    const hidden = runCheck(task, ws, task.hidden, true);\n    const regression = task.regression ? runCheck(task, ws, task.regression, false) : null;\n    const turn = agent.json?.turn ?? null;\n    // Nexus reports a structured outcome; for the other agents a clean exit within the budget is their completion claim.\n    const claimedComplete = turn\n      ? turn.execution === \"COMPLETED\" && [\"VERIFIED\", \"REGRESSION_FREE\", \"UNVERIFIED\", \"NOT_REQUIRED\"].includes(turn.outcome)\n      : agent.code === 0 && !agent.timedOut;\n    return {\n      ...base,\n      wallMs,\n      exitCode: agent.code,\n      timedOut: agent.timedOut,\n      turn: turn && { execution: turn.execution, outcome: turn.outcome, reason: turn.reason ?? null, steps: turn.steps ?? null, contextNotRetained: turn.contextNotRetained ?? 0 },\n      claimedComplete,\n      claimedVerified: turn?.outcome === \"VERIFIED\",\n      hiddenPass: hidden.pass,\n      regressionPass: regression ? regression.pass : null,\n      falseVerified: turn?.outcome === \"VERIFIED\" && !hidden.pass,\n      contaminated,\n      tokens: agent.json?.tokenStats ?? null,\n      logs: saveLogs(task, run, agent, hidden, regression),\n    };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { ...base, wallMs: 0, error: String(err?.message ?? err), hiddenPass: false, regressionPass: null, falseVerified: false, claimedComplete: false, claimedVerified: false };\n  } finally {\n    if (!args.keep) {\n      fs.rmSync(ws, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction prepareWorkspace(task, ws) {\n  if (task.fixture) {\n    fs.cpSync(path.join(task.dir, task.fixture), ws, { recursive: true });\n    sh(\"git init -q && git add -A && git -c user.name=eval -c user.email=eval@example.invalid commit -qm fixture\", ws);\n  } else if (task.repo) {\n    const cache = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/.cache\", createHash(\"sha256\").update(task.repo.url).digest(\"hex\").slice(0, 16));\n    if (!fs.existsSync(cache)) sh(`git clone -q --no-checkout ${shellQuote(task.repo.url)} ${shellQuote(cache)}`, ROOT);\n    sh(`git -C ${shellQuote(cache)} cat-file -e ${task.repo.commit}^{commit} || git -C ${shellQuote(cache)} fetch -q origin ${task.repo.commit}`, ROOT);\n    sh(`git clone -q --shared ${shellQuote(cache)} ${shellQuote(ws)} && git -C ${shellQuote(ws)} checkout -q ${task.repo.commit}`, ROOT);\n  } else throw new Error(`task ${task.id} has neither fixture nor repo`);\n  for (const cmd of task.setup ?? []) sh(cmd, ws);\n}\n\n/**\n * The command line and environment for one agent run. Each agent gets a fresh HOME holding only its gateway settings\n * (no operator plugins, extensions or memory), the same endpoint and model, and the key through its environment.\n */\nfunction agentCommand(task, ws, home, budget) {\n  const ep = config.endpoint;\n  const keyEnv = apiKey ? { LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY: apiKey, OPENAI_API_KEY: apiKey, GW_KEY: apiKey } : {};\n  const caEnv = caBundle ? { NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS: caFile, SSL_CERT_FILE: caBundle, REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE: caBundle } : {};\n  // PWD too: some agents take the project from $PWD rather than the process's working directory.\n  const env = { ...process.env, ...(config.env ?? {}), ...keyEnv, ...caEnv, HOME: home, PWD: ws, XDG_CONFIG_HOME: path.join(home, \".config\"), XDG_DATA_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/share\"), XDG_STATE_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/state\") };\n  const agent = config.agent ?? \"nexus\";\n  if (agent === \"nexus\") {\n    env.LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT = ep;\n    return { cmd: process.execPath, argv: [path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist/index.js\"), \"run\", \"--json\", \"-w\", ws, \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", config.model, \"-s\", \"30\", \"--max-total-steps\", String(budget.steps), \"--max-turn-minutes\", String(budget.minutes), ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"aider\") {\n    return { cmd: \"aider\", argv: [\"--model\", `openai/${config.model}`, \"--openai-api-base\", ep, \"--yes-always\", \"--no-auto-commits\", \"--no-dirty-commits\", \"--no-gitignore\", \"--no-show-model-warnings\", \"--no-check-update\", \"--analytics-disable\", \"--no-pretty\", \"--no-fancy-input\", ...(config.args ?? []), \"--message\", task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"opencode\") {\n    const dir = path.join(home, \".config/opencode\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n    const limits = config.limits ?? { context: 65536, output: 8192 };\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"opencode.json\"), JSON.stringify({\n      $schema: \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n      autoupdate: false,\n      share: \"disabled\",\n      permission: { edit: \"allow\", bash: \"allow\", webfetch: \"deny\" },\n      provider: { gw: { npm: \"@ai-sdk/openai-compatible\", name: \"gateway\", options: { baseURL: ep, apiKey: \"{env:GW_KEY}\" }, models: { [config.model]: { name: config.model, limit: limits } } } },\n      model: `gw/${config.model}`,\n    }, null, 2));\n    // Provider packages are cached across runs (not per run): the cache holds code, not state.\n    env.XDG_CACHE_HOME = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/.cache/xdg-cache\");\n    return { cmd: \"opencode\", argv: [\"run\", \"--model\", `gw/${config.model}`, ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"goose\") {\n    const u = new URL(ep);\n    Object.assign(env, { GOOSE_PROVIDER: \"openai\", GOOSE_MODEL: config.model, OPENAI_HOST: u.origin, OPENAI_BASE_PATH: `${u.pathname.replace(/^\\/|\\/$/g, \"\")}/chat/completions`, GOOSE_MODE: \"auto\", GOOSE_DISABLE_KEYRING: \"1\", GOOSE_CONTEXT_LIMIT: String(config.limits?.context ?? 65536) });\n    return { cmd: \"goose\", argv: [\"run\", \"--no-session\", \"--with-builtin\", \"developer\", ...(config.args ?? []), \"-t\", task.objective], env };\n  }\n  throw new Error(`agent ${agent} has no adapter`);\n}\n\nfunction runAgent(task, ws, home) {\n  const budget = { steps: task.steps ?? config.steps ?? 300, minutes: task.minutes ?? config.minutes ?? 120 };\n  const { cmd, argv, env } = agentCommand(task, ws, home, budget);\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    const child = spawn(cmd, argv, { cwd: ws, env, stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"], detached: true });\n    let stdout = \"\";\n    let stderr = \"\";\n    child.stdout.on(\"data\", (c) => (stdout += c));\n    child.stderr.on(\"data\", (c) => (stderr += c));\n    let timedOut = false;\n    // The whole process group: agents start helpers (servers, shells) that must not outlive the run.\n    const killGroup = (sig) => {\n      try {\n        process.kill(-child.pid, sig);\n      } catch {}\n    };\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n      timedOut = true;\n      killGroup(\"SIGTERM\");\n      setTimeout(() => killGroup(\"SIGKILL\"), 10_000).unref();\n    }, (budget.minutes + 5) * 60_000);\n    child.on(\"error\", (err) => (stderr += `spawn error: ${err.message}\\n`));\n    child.on(\"close\", (code) => {\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      killGroup(\"SIGKILL\");\n      resolve({ code, timedOut, stdout, stderr, json: lastJson(stdout) });\n    });\n  });\n}\n\nfunction runCheck(task, ws, check, hidden) {\n  if (hidden && check.dir) fs.cpSync(path.join(task.dir, check.dir), path.join(ws, check.into ?? check.dir), { recursive: true });\n  const r = spawnSync(\"bash\", [\"-c\", check.command], { cwd: ws, encoding: \"utf8\", timeout: (check.timeoutSec ?? 300) * 1000, env: { ...process.env, CI: \"1\" } });\n  return { pass: r.status === 0, status: r.status, output: `${r.stdout ?? \"\"}${r.stderr ?? \"\"}`.slice(-20_000) };\n}\n\nfunction saveLogs(task, run, agent, hidden, regression) {\n  const dir = path.join(args.out, \"logs\", `${task.id}-${run}`);\n  fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"agent.stdout.json\"), agent.stdout);\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"agent.stderr.log\"), agent.stderr.slice(-200_000));\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"hidden.log\"), hidden.output);\n  if (regression) fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"regression.log\"), regression.output);\n  return path.relative(args.out, dir);\n}\n\nfunction treeDigest(dir) {\n  const hash = createHash(\"sha256\");\n  const walk = (d) => {\n    for (const e of fs.readdirSync(d, { withFileTypes: true }).sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))) {\n      const p = path.join(d, e.name);\n      hash.update(path.relative(dir, p));\n      if (e.isDirectory()) walk(p);\n      else hash.update(fs.readFileSync(p));\n    }\n  };\n  walk(dir);\n  return hash.digest(\"hex\");\n}\n\nfunction lastJson(text) {\n  const start = text.indexOf(\"{\");\n  for (let i = start; i >= 0 && i < text.length; i = text.indexOf(\"{\", i + 1)) {\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(text.slice(i));\n    } catch {}\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction harnessIdentity() {\n  const git = (...a) => spawnSync(\"git\", a, { cwd: ROOT, encoding: \"utf8\" }).stdout.trim();\n  const commit = git(\"rev-parse\", \"--short=12\", \"HEAD\");\n  const dirty = Boolean(git(\"status\", \"--porcelain\", \"--untracked-files=no\", \"--\", \".\", \":(exclude)cli/dist\"));\n  return { commit, dirty, string: `${commit}${dirty ? \"-dirty\" : \"\"}` };\n}\n\n/** `{ file, var }`: the key is read from a KEY=value file (e.g. ~/.config/nexus/config.env); never logged. */\nfunction readApiKey(spec) {\n  if (!spec) return null;\n  const file = expandHome(spec.file);\n  const line = fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").find((l) => l.startsWith(`${spec.var}=`));\n  if (!line) throw new Error(`${spec.var} not found in ${spec.file}`);\n  return line.slice(spec.var.length + 1).trim();\n}\n\n/** System CAs plus the gateway's CA, for agents that read SSL_CERT_FILE / REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE (Python, Rust). */\nfunction writeCaBundle(caFile) {\n  const system = [\"/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt\", \"/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt\"].find((f) => fs.existsSync(f));\n  const bundle = path.join(args.out, \"ca-bundle.pem\");\n  fs.writeFileSync(bundle, (system ? fs.readFileSync(system, \"utf8\") : \"\") + \"\\n\" + fs.readFileSync(caFile, \"utf8\"));\n  return bundle;\n}\n\nfunction redactConfig(c) {\n  const env = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(c.env ?? {}).map(([k, v]) => [k, /KEY|TOKEN|SECRET|PASSWORD/i.test(k) ? \"***\" : v]));\n  return { ...c, env };\n}\n\nfunction expandHome(f) {\n  return f.replace(/^~(?=\\/)/, os.homedir());\n}\n\nfunction sh(cmd, cwd) {\n  const r = spawnSync(\"bash\", [\"-c\", cmd], { cwd, encoding: \"utf8\" });\n  if (r.status !== 0) throw new Error(`${cmd}: ${r.stderr || r.stdout}`);\n  return r.stdout;\n}\n\nfunction shellQuote(s) {\n  return `'${String(s).replace(/'/g, `'\\\\''`)}'`;\n}\n\nfunction parseArgs(list) {\n  const out = {};\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n    const key = list[i].replace(/^--/, \"\");\n    const next = list[i + 1];\n    if (next === undefined || next.startsWith(\"--\")) out[key] = true;\n    else {\n      out[key] = next;\n      i++;\n    }\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\n\n`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\nseparately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\n\n```bash\nnode eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\nnode eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\n```\n\nEach run: a fresh workspace (the task's `fixture`, or its `repo.url` at `repo.commit`, cached in `eval/.cache`), a fresh\n`HOME`, the agent with the task's budgets and a wall-clock timeout, then the task's **hidden** tests (copied in only\nafter the agent has stopped) and its `regression` command. `manifest.json` records the harness build (commit, dirty),\nthe configuration (secrets in `env` masked), host and Node version; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`.\n\n## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Pre-registered thresholds (from the assessment, fixed before any live run)\n\n- false VERIFIED = 0 across all runs;\n- T2 hidden-test pass rate (pooled over all T2 runs of a configuration, point estimate, 95 % intervals reported) ≥ the\n  best matched peer on the same local model **minus 10 percentage points**; and no task where that peer passes ≥ 4/5\n  runs while Nexus passes ≤ 1/5. (Fixed 2026-10-13, before the first scored run. Rationale: at ~50 runs per\n  configuration the 95 % interval half-width near 50 % is ~13 points, so a tighter margin is not distinguishable from\n  noise and a looser one would accept a clear loss; the per-task guard stops a pooled rate hiding a task class Nexus\n  cannot do.) The 6-task pilot is directional only; qualification needs the full task set;\n- T3: false-absence claims = 0 and steering constraints honoured in ≥ 95 % of runs;\n- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\n- ≥ 5 runs per task-configuration, per-task results with 95 % intervals.\n\n## Status\n\n| Part | State |\n|---|---|\n| Runner, scorer, manifest, per-run logs | done |\n| T1 self-test (`selftest-add`, scripted model, in `make test` via `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`) | done |\n| Nexus adapter | done |\n| Peer adapters (OpenCode, Goose, Aider, Codex) | not started |\n| T2/T3 task set (pilot 12, external repos, hidden tests) | not started |\n| T3 fact-sheet scorer (absence claims) and steering checks | not started |\n| T4 fault injector | not started |\n| Live runs | blocked on inference hours, cloud budget and peer installs (operator decision) |\n\n## Pilot 2026-10-13 (4 h appliance window)\n\nConfigurations `configs/pilot-*.json`: Nexus, Aider 0.86.2, OpenCode 1.18.35, Goose 1.27.2, all on\n`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\nfixture tasks (`t2-*`; each hidden test checked to fail on the fixture and pass on a reference fix kept outside the\nrepo). Budgets 60 steps / 20 min per task (Nexus steps; others by wall clock). The four agents run concurrently on the\nsame worker, so wall times include queueing.\n\nDeviations from §9, recorded before the run: fixture tasks rather than external repositories at pinned commits; T2\nonly (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\none `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\nruns per task as many as the window allows, run-major, target 5.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a171fd-3278-7ca3-ad25-d2f716cb2b15","create_time":1792914192.0851421}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
