{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:43:28.338Z","ordinal":329718,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171fd-3278-7ca3-ad25-d2f716cb2b15","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4117a611-9422-4338-b569-71335cbf6687","process_id":"99204","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '75,125p' eval/README.md; rg -n 'T4|faultRows|faults' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md eval/run.mjs eval/model_proxy.mjs; sed -n '185,250p' eval/run.mjs; sed -n '1,120p' eval/model_proxy.mjs"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '75,125p' eval/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"eval/README.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'T4|faultRows|faults' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md eval/run.mjs eval/model_proxy.mjs","query":"T4|faultRows|faults","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '185,250p' eval/run.mjs","name":"run.mjs","path":"eval/run.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,120p' eval/model_proxy.mjs","name":"model_proxy.mjs","path":"eval/model_proxy.mjs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"  before the proxy fall back to each agent's own connection-failure message, and the script says how many it judged\n  that way.\n- **Contamination.** Contaminated runs (the task directory changed, or its path appeared in the agent's output) are\n  left out of pooled pass rates and counted separately.\n- **Reruns are listed.** `score.mjs` lists every replaced run with what it showed and what the rerun showed.\n- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n\nWhat was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\n\n- runs;\n- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\n  hidden tests failed);\n- **recovered** (the hidden tests pass);\n- hung past budget.\n\nThe remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\nrunner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n  everything except class and difficulty.\n- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n  inside the Bubblewrap mount namespace and does not bind the task store or validator sources; its `HOME`, `/tmp`,\n  `/run`, and network namespace are isolated. Runtime files are explicit read-only binds. The harness grants the\n  evaluator UID ACL access only to the disposable workspace, home and per-run proxy directory. Before qualification,\n  verify the account and these existing operating-system permissions through the approved local setup procedure:\n  1. `sudo useradd --system --create-home nexus-eval`\neval/model_proxy.mjs:4:// Bodies are streamed through unchanged unless a fault is scheduled for a request (T4, REQ-QUAL-105); nothing is\neval/model_proxy.mjs:14: * Faults the proxy can inject into the Nth chat request of a run (SPEC-10 T4 classes it can produce itself):\neval/model_proxy.mjs:21: * The other T4 classes (a hanging test command, a full disk, SIGTERM then resume) come from task fixtures and the runner.\neval/model_proxy.mjs:73: * Starts a forwarder on 127.0.0.1 for `upstream` (e.g. https://gateway:8443/v1). `faults`: [{ kind, atRequest }] where\neval/model_proxy.mjs:76:export async function startModelProxy({ upstream, caFile, faults = [], profile, authToken, clientToken, socketPath, maxRequests = 1_000, maxConcurrentRequests = 1, maxRequestBytes = 1_000_000, maxCompletionTokens, maxTotalCompletionTokens }) {\neval/model_proxy.mjs:81:  for (const f of faults) {\neval/model_proxy.mjs:94:  const stats = { requests: 0, chatRequests: 0, activeInferenceRequests: 0, cancelledRequests: 0, profileContextLookups: 0, requestedCompletionTokens: 0, answered: 0, upstreamFailures: 0, faultsInjected: [], firstRequestAt: null, firstAnswerAt: null };\neval/model_proxy.mjs:204:    const fault = chatIndex ? faults.find((f) => f.atRequest === chatIndex) : undefined;\neval/model_proxy.mjs:205:    if (fault) stats.faultsInjected.push({ kind: fault.kind, atRequest: chatIndex });\neval/model_proxy.mjs:325:    stats: () => ({ ...stats, faultsInjected: [...stats.faultsInjected] }),\neval/model_proxy.mjs:344:  if (!m || (m.faultsInjected?.length ?? 0) > 0) return false;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:25:- T4 fault injection;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:64:5. **REQ-QUAL-105. T4 fault injection.** 9 fault classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:82:7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:85:10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:96:- **Fault injector.** `eval/faults/proxy.mjs` is an HTTP proxy in front of the model server that injects faults 1–4 and 7–8 by schedule. Faults 5, 6 and 9 are injected by the task fixture or the runner.\neval/run.mjs:208:    // T4: a task (or the config) may schedule faults for the proxy to inject; they are recorded with the run.\neval/run.mjs:209:    const faults = task.faults ?? config.faults ?? [];\neval/run.mjs:210:    if (faults.length && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"fault injection needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\neval/run.mjs:220:      faults,\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:308:   - 2 T4 classes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:13:- new `eval/faults/`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:18:- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:28:| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:29:| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:34:| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:54:  - T4 smoke.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:64:The original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\n    await prepareWorkspace(task, ws);\n    // Taken now, while .git is the harness's own: after the agent runs, nothing executes git against its workspace.\n    const baselineTree = gitRev(ws, \"HEAD^{tree}\");\n    const t3Baseline = task.tier === \"T3\" ? steeringBaseline(task, ws) : null;\n    // On the per-run task copy, so the steering hook in runAgent can read it. The commands run on a throwaway copy of\n    // the staged workspace, so the agent starts on exactly the staged tree.\n    const t3BaselineResources = [];\n    if (task.tier === \"T3\") {\n      const probe = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, `nexus-eval-t3-baseline-${task.id}-`));\n      try {\n        fs.cpSync(ws, probe, { recursive: true, verbatimSymlinks: true });\n        task.t3CommandBaseline = await commandBaseline(task, (command) => runIsolated(command, { cwd: probe, home: true, timeoutSec: 300, resources: config.resources ?? null, protectedCorpusPaths: protectedCorpusPathsForRun() }).then((r) => {\n          if (r.resources) t3BaselineResources.push(r.resources);\n          const error = r.containmentProblem ?? (r.timedOut ? \"timed out\" : r.overflow ? \"output limit\" : r.status === null ? \"did not exit\" : null);\n          return { pass: r.status === 0 && !error, error };\n        }));\n      } finally {\n        fs.rmSync(probe, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      }\n    }\n    const sourceBefore = treeDigest(task.dir);\n    // Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder, so whether the model was reachable is observed by the\n    // harness, the same way for every agent (eval/infra.mjs). `config.proxy: false` connects agents directly.\n    // T4: a task (or the config) may schedule faults for the proxy to inject; they are recorded with the run.\n    const faults = task.faults ?? config.faults ?? [];\n    if (faults.length && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"fault injection needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    // A standalone profile (DEC-16) shows agents a plain server; the proxy then holds the real key, agents get none.\n    if (config.serverProfile && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"serverProfile needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    const proxyDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-proxy-\"));\n    fs.chmodSync(proxyDir, 0o700);\n    const socketPath = path.join(proxyDir, \"proxy.sock\");\n    const localToken = REDACTED;\n    const proxy = await startModelProxy({\n      upstream: config.endpoint,\n      caFile,\n      faults,\n      profile: config.serverProfile,\n      authToken: apiKey ?? undefined,\n      clientToken: localToken,\n      socketPath,\n      maxRequests: config.limits?.requests ?? 1_000,\n      maxCompletionTokens: config.limits?.output,\n      maxTotalCompletionTokens: config.limits?.totalOutput,\n    });\n    const started = Date.now();\n    let agent;\n    let agentEndedAt;\n    try {\n      agent = await runAgent(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDir, localToken);\n      agentEndedAt = Date.now();\n      if (config.runAs) {\n        for (const dir of [ws, home]) await normalizeRunAsPermissions(config.runAs, dir, asUserSpec);\n      }\n    } finally {\n      await proxy?.close();\n      fs.rmSync(proxyDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n    const wallMs = agentEndedAt - started;\n    if (agent.containmentProblem) throw new Error(`candidate containment failed: ${agent.containmentProblem}`);\n    const model = proxy ? proxy.stats() : null;\n    const contaminated = treeDigest(task.dir) !== sourceBefore || `${agent.stdout}${agent.stderr}`.includes(tasksDir);\n    // T3 judges the workspace as it was when the objective's work ended (snapshot taken before the probe turn).\n    const t3 = agent.t3Driver ? scoreT3Run({ task, baseline: t3Baseline, driver: agent.t3Driver, preconditions: agent.t3Preconditions, compactions: countCompactions(home) }) : null;\n    // Legacy hidden tests share a process with candidate code. In qualification (or with hardenedChecks) they never\n    // run in the agent's workspace: each check gets a fresh staging of the baseline with only the agent's source\n    // changes (eval/hardened_check.mjs). Black-box oracles already keep expectations outside the candidate.\n// A per-run forwarder between an agent and the model endpoint. Every agent reaches the model through it the same way,\n// so the harness itself observes whether the model was reachable during a run (REQ-QUAL-106): how many requests were\n// made, how many got an answer, and how many failed upstream (connection errors and 502/503/504 from the endpoint).\n// Bodies are streamed through unchanged unless a fault is scheduled for a request (T4, REQ-QUAL-105); nothing is\n// logged.\nimport http from \"node:http\";\nimport https from \"node:https\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport { timingSafeEqual } from \"node:crypto\";\n\nconst UPSTREAM_DOWN = new Set([502, 503, 504]);\n\n/**\n * Faults the proxy can inject into the Nth chat request of a run (SPEC-10 T4 classes it can produce itself):\n * - refuse: the connection is dropped without an answer (the endpoint went away mid-turn);\n * - overloaded: 503 with Retry-After: 1 (the endpoint is busy);\n * - stream_cut: the stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment (a transport drop inside a tool call);\n * - truncate: the reply is marked cut at the output limit (finish_reason \"length\");\n * - context_overflow: llama.cpp's context-overflow error (HTTP 400, exceed_context_size_error);\n * - malformed_tool_json: the first tool call's arguments are made invalid JSON.\n * The other T4 classes (a hanging test command, a full disk, SIGTERM then resume) come from task fixtures and the runner.\n */\nexport const FAULT_KINDS = [\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"];\n\n/**\n * Standalone profiles (DEC-16, REQ-PRV-106): the agent sees a plain OpenAI-compatible server instead of the gateway.\n * Every gateway extension is removed (limits and capabilities in /models, /tokenize, X-AIHost-* headers). An emulated\n * profile also answers as that server would about its context (llama.cpp /props, Ollama /api/show, vLLM max_model_len)\n * and reshapes context-overflow errors into its format; the numbers are the gateway's real ones.\n */\nexport const PROFILES = [\"plain\", \"llamacpp\", \"vllm\", \"ollama\"];\nconst OWNER = { plain: \"organization\", llamacpp: \"llamacpp\", vllm: \"vllm\", ollama: \"library\" };\n\nfunction profileModel(profile, entry) {\n  const ctx = entry.context_length ?? entry.max_model_len ?? null;\n  const base = { id: entry.id, object: \"model\", owned_by: OWNER[profile] };\n  if (profile === \"llamacpp\" && ctx) return { ...base, meta: { n_ctx_train: ctx } };\n  if (profile === \"vllm\" && ctx) return { ...base, max_model_len: ctx };\n  return base;\n}\n\nfunction overflowBody(profile, ctx) {\n  if (profile === \"llamacpp\") return { error: { code: 400, message: \"the request exceeds the available context size, try increasing it\", type: \"exceed_context_size_error\", n_ctx: ctx } };\n  if (profile === \"vllm\") return { object: \"error\", message: `This model's maximum context length is ${ctx ?? \"unknown\"} tokens. However, you requested more tokens.`, type: \"BadRequestError\", code: 400 };\n  return { error: { message: \"This request exceeds the model's maximum context length.\", type: \"invalid_request_error\", code: \"context_length_exceeded\" } };\n}\n\n/** Rewrites an SSE body as it passes, chunk by chunk; `edit` returns the text to forward (or null to cut the stream). */\nfunction rewriteStream(upstreamRes, res, edit) {\n  let pending = \"\";\n  upstreamRes.setEncoding(\"utf8\");\n  upstreamRes.on(\"data\", (chunk) => {\n    pending += chunk;\n    const events = pending.split(\"\\n\\n\");\n    pending = events.pop() ?? \"\";\n    for (const event of events) {\n      const out = edit(event);\n      if (out === null) {\n        res.socket?.destroy();\n        upstreamRes.destroy();\n        return;\n      }\n      res.write(`${out}\\n\\n`);\n    }\n  });\n  upstreamRes.on(\"end\", () => {\n    if (pending) res.write(edit(pending) ?? \"\");\n    res.end();\n  });\n}\n\n/**\n * Starts a forwarder on 127.0.0.1 for `upstream` (e.g. https://gateway:8443/v1). `faults`: [{ kind, atRequest }] where\n * atRequest counts chat requests from 1. Returns its base URL (same path as the upstream), live counters, and close().\n */\nexport async function startModelProxy({ upstream, caFile, faults = [], profile, authToken, clientToken, socketPath, maxRequests = 1_000, maxConcurrentRequests = 1, maxRequestBytes = 1_000_000, maxCompletionTokens, maxTotalCompletionTokens }) {\n  if (profile !== undefined && !PROFILES.includes(profile)) throw new Error(`unknown profile ${profile}; one of ${PROFILES.join(\", \")}`);\n  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(maxRequests) || maxRequests < 1 || !Number.isSafeInteger(maxConcurrentRequests) || maxConcurrentRequests < 1 || !Number.isSafeInteger(maxRequestBytes) || maxRequestBytes < 1) throw new Error(\"invalid evaluation proxy request limits\");\n  if (maxCompletionTokens !== undefined && (!Number.isSafeInteger(maxCompletionTokens) || maxCompletionTokens < 1)) throw new Error(\"invalid per-request completion-token limit\");\n  if (maxTotalCompletionTokens !== undefined && (!Number.isSafeInteger(maxTotalCompletionTokens) || maxTotalCompletionTokens < 1)) throw new Error(\"invalid aggregate completion-token limit\");\n  for (const f of faults) {\n    if (!FAULT_KINDS.includes(f.kind) || !Number.isInteger(f.atRequest) || f.atRequest < 1) throw new Error(`invalid fault ${JSON.stringify(f)}`);\n  }\n  const target = new URL(upstream);\n  const basePath = target.pathname.replace(/\\/$/, \"\");\n  const allowedRoutes = new Map([\n    [\"GET /models\", \"catalog\"],\n    [\"POST /chat/completions\", \"inference\"],\n    [\"POST /responses\", \"inference\"],\n    [\"POST /messages\", \"inference\"],\n  ]);\n  const client = target.protocol === \"https:\" ? https : http;\n  const ca = caFile ? fs.readFileSync(caFile) : undefined;\n  const stats = { requests: 0, chatRequests: 0, activeInferenceRequests: 0, cancelledRequests: 0, profileContextLookups: 0, requestedCompletionTokens: 0, answered: 0, upstreamFailures: 0, faultsInjected: [], firstRequestAt: null, firstAnswerAt: null };\n\n  /** The upstream /models entries (for an emulated profile's context answers). */\n  const upstreamModels = () => new Promise((resolve) => {\n    const r = client.request({ protocol: target.protocol, hostname: target.hostname, port: target.port || (target.protocol === \"https:\" ? 443 : 80), method: \"GET\", path: `${target.pathname.replace(/\\/$/, \"\")}/models`, headers: { host: target.host, ...(authToken ? { authorization: `Bearer ${authToken}` } : {}) }, ca }, (res) => {\n      let body = \"\";\n      res.setEncoding(\"utf8\");\n      res.on(\"data\", (c) => (body += c));\n      res.on(\"end\", () => { try { resolve(JSON.parse(body).data ?? []); } catch { resolve([]); } });\n    });\n    r.on(\"error\", () => resolve([]));\n    r.end();\n  });\n  const firstContext = async () => { const m = (await upstreamModels())[0]; return m?.context_length ?? m?.max_model_len ?? null; };\n  const sendJson = (res, status, body) => { res.writeHead(status, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" }); res.end(JSON.stringify(body)); };\n\n  const server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\n    stats.requests++;\n    if (clientToken) {\n      const supplied = /^Bearer (.+)$/.exec(String(req.headers.authorization ?? \"\"))?.[1] ?? \"\";\n      const expected = Buffer.from(clientToken);\n      const actual = Buffer.from(supplied);\n      if (actual.length !== expected.length || !timingSafeEqual(actual, expected)) {\n        req.resume();\n        return void sendJson(res, 401, { error: { type: \"authentication_error\", message: \"evaluation proxy authentication failed\" } });\n      }\n    }\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":719664624}},"started_at_ms":1792914207615,"completed_at_ms":1792914208335}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:43:29.402Z","ordinal":329719,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17203-ba7a-7370-99a3-25e792a9aa3c","call_id":"call_ae09c6d3add94850bb14b792be063c64","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"  before the proxy fall back to each agent's own connection-failure message, and the script says how many it judged\n  that way.\n- **Contamination.** Contaminated runs (the task directory changed, or its path appeared in the agent's output) are\n  left out of pooled pass rates and counted separately.\n- **Reruns are listed.** `score.mjs` lists every replaced run with what it showed and what the rerun showed.\n- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n\nWhat was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\n\n- runs;\n- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\n  hidden tests failed);\n- **recovered** (the hidden tests pass);\n- hung past budget.\n\nThe remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\nrunner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n  everything except class and difficulty.\n- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n  inside the Bubblewrap mount namespace and does not bind the task store or validator sources; its `HOME`, `/tmp`,\n  `/run`, and network namespace are isolated. Runtime files are explicit read-only binds. The harness grants the\n  evaluator UID ACL access only to the disposable workspace, home and per-run proxy directory. Before qualification,\n  verify the account and these existing operating-system permissions through the approved local setup procedure:\n  1. `sudo useradd --system --create-home nexus-eval`\neval/model_proxy.mjs:4:// Bodies are streamed through unchanged unless a fault is scheduled for a request (T4, REQ-QUAL-105); nothing is\neval/model_proxy.mjs:14: * Faults the proxy can inject into the Nth chat request of a run (SPEC-10 T4 classes it can produce itself):\neval/model_proxy.mjs:21: * The other T4 classes (a hanging test command, a full disk, SIGTERM then resume) come from task fixtures and the runner.\neval/model_proxy.mjs:73: * Starts a forwarder on 127.0.0.1 for `upstream` (e.g. https://gateway:8443/v1). `faults`: [{ kind, atRequest }] where\neval/model_proxy.mjs:76:export async function startModelProxy({ upstream, caFile, faults = [], profile, authToken, clientToken, socketPath, maxRequests = 1_000, maxConcurrentRequests = 1, maxRequestBytes = 1_000_000, maxCompletionTokens, maxTotalCompletionTokens }) {\neval/model_proxy.mjs:81:  for (const f of faults) {\neval/model_proxy.mjs:94:  const stats = { requests: 0, chatRequests: 0, activeInferenceRequests: 0, cancelledRequests: 0, profileContextLookups: 0, requestedCompletionTokens: 0, answered: 0, upstreamFailures: 0, faultsInjected: [], firstRequestAt: null, firstAnswerAt: null };\neval/model_proxy.mjs:204:    const fault = chatIndex ? faults.find((f) => f.atRequest === chatIndex) : undefined;\neval/model_proxy.mjs:205:    if (fault) stats.faultsInjected.push({ kind: fault.kind, atRequest: chatIndex });\neval/model_proxy.mjs:325:    stats: () => ({ ...stats, faultsInjected: [...stats.faultsInjected] }),\neval/model_proxy.mjs:344:  if (!m || (m.faultsInjected?.length ?? 0) > 0) return false;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:25:- T4 fault injection;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:64:5. **REQ-QUAL-105. T4 fault injection.** 9 fault classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:82:7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:85:10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:96:- **Fault injector.** `eval/faults/proxy.mjs` is an HTTP proxy in front of the model server that injects faults 1–4 and 7–8 by schedule. Faults 5, 6 and 9 are injected by the task fixture or the runner.\neval/run.mjs:208:    // T4: a task (or the config) may schedule faults for the proxy to inject; they are recorded with the run.\neval/run.mjs:209:    const faults = task.faults ?? config.faults ?? [];\neval/run.mjs:210:    if (faults.length && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"fault injection needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\neval/run.mjs:220:      faults,\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:308:   - 2 T4 classes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:13:- new `eval/faults/`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:18:- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:28:| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:29:| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:34:| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:54:  - T4 smoke.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:64:The original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\n    await prepareWorkspace(task, ws);\n    // Taken now, while .git is the harness's own: after the agent runs, nothing executes git against its workspace.\n    const baselineTree = gitRev(ws, \"HEAD^{tree}\");\n    const t3Baseline = task.tier === \"T3\" ? steeringBaseline(task, ws) : null;\n    // On the per-run task copy, so the steering hook in runAgent can read it. The commands run on a throwaway copy of\n    // the staged workspace, so the agent starts on exactly the staged tree.\n    const t3BaselineResources = [];\n    if (task.tier === \"T3\") {\n      const probe = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, `nexus-eval-t3-baseline-${task.id}-`));\n      try {\n        fs.cpSync(ws, probe, { recursive: true, verbatimSymlinks: true });\n        task.t3CommandBaseline = await commandBaseline(task, (command) => runIsolated(command, { cwd: probe, home: true, timeoutSec: 300, resources: config.resources ?? null, protectedCorpusPaths: protectedCorpusPathsForRun() }).then((r) => {\n          if (r.resources) t3BaselineResources.push(r.resources);\n          const error = r.containmentProblem ?? (r.timedOut ? \"timed out\" : r.overflow ? \"output limit\" : r.status === null ? \"did not exit\" : null);\n          return { pass: r.status === 0 && !error, error };\n        }));\n      } finally {\n        fs.rmSync(probe, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      }\n    }\n    const sourceBefore = treeDigest(task.dir);\n    // Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder, so whether the model was reachable is observed by the\n    // harness, the same way for every agent (eval/infra.mjs). `config.proxy: false` connects agents directly.\n    // T4: a task (or the config) may schedule faults for the proxy to inject; they are recorded with the run.\n    const faults = task.faults ?? config.faults ?? [];\n    if (faults.length && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"fault injection needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    // A standalone profile (DEC-16) shows agents a plain server; the proxy then holds the real key, agents get none.\n    if (config.serverProfile && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"serverProfile needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    const proxyDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-proxy-\"));\n    fs.chmodSync(proxyDir, 0o700);\n    const socketPath = path.join(proxyDir, \"proxy.sock\");\n    const localToken = REDACTED;\n    const proxy = await startModelProxy({\n      upstream: config.endpoint,\n      caFile,\n      faults,\n      profile: config.serverProfile,\n      authToken: apiKey ?? undefined,\n      clientToken: localToken,\n      socketPath,\n      maxRequests: config.limits?.requests ?? 1_000,\n      maxCompletionTokens: config.limits?.output,\n      maxTotalCompletionTokens: config.limits?.totalOutput,\n    });\n    const started = Date.now();\n    let agent;\n    let agentEndedAt;\n    try {\n      agent = await runAgent(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDir, localToken);\n      agentEndedAt = Date.now();\n      if (config.runAs) {\n        for (const dir of [ws, home]) await normalizeRunAsPermissions(config.runAs, dir, asUserSpec);\n      }\n    } finally {\n      await proxy?.close();\n      fs.rmSync(proxyDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n    const wallMs = agentEndedAt - started;\n    if (agent.containmentProblem) throw new Error(`candidate containment failed: ${agent.containmentProblem}`);\n    const model = proxy ? proxy.stats() : null;\n    const contaminated = treeDigest(task.dir) !== sourceBefore || `${agent.stdout}${agent.stderr}`.includes(tasksDir);\n    // T3 judges the workspace as it was when the objective's work ended (snapshot taken before the probe turn).\n    const t3 = agent.t3Driver ? scoreT3Run({ task, baseline: t3Baseline, driver: agent.t3Driver, preconditions: agent.t3Preconditions, compactions: countCompactions(home) }) : null;\n    // Legacy hidden tests share a process with candidate code. In qualification (or with hardenedChecks) they never\n    // run in the agent's workspace: each check gets a fresh staging of the baseline with only the agent's source\n    // changes (eval/hardened_check.mjs). Black-box oracles already keep expectations outside the candidate.\n// A per-run forwarder between an agent and the model endpoint. Every agent reaches the model through it the same way,\n// so the harness itself observes whether the model was reachable during a run (REQ-QUAL-106): how many requests were\n// made, how many got an answer, and how many failed upstream (connection errors and 502/503/504 from the endpoint).\n// Bodies are streamed through unchanged unless a fault is scheduled for a request (T4, REQ-QUAL-105); nothing is\n// logged.\nimport http from \"node:http\";\nimport https from \"node:https\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport { timingSafeEqual } from \"node:crypto\";\n\nconst UPSTREAM_DOWN = new Set([502, 503, 504]);\n\n/**\n * Faults the proxy can inject into the Nth chat request of a run (SPEC-10 T4 classes it can produce itself):\n * - refuse: the connection is dropped without an answer (the endpoint went away mid-turn);\n * - overloaded: 503 with Retry-After: 1 (the endpoint is busy);\n * - stream_cut: the stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment (a transport drop inside a tool call);\n * - truncate: the reply is marked cut at the output limit (finish_reason \"length\");\n * - context_overflow: llama.cpp's context-overflow error (HTTP 400, exceed_context_size_error);\n * - malformed_tool_json: the first tool call's arguments are made invalid JSON.\n * The other T4 classes (a hanging test command, a full disk, SIGTERM then resume) come from task fixtures and the runner.\n */\nexport const FAULT_KINDS = [\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"];\n\n/**\n * Standalone profiles (DEC-16, REQ-PRV-106): the agent sees a plain OpenAI-compatible server instead of the gateway.\n * Every gateway extension is removed (limits and capabilities in /models, /tokenize, X-AIHost-* headers). An emulated\n * profile also answers as that server would about its context (llama.cpp /props, Ollama /api/show, vLLM max_model_len)\n * and reshapes context-overflow errors into its format; the numbers are the gateway's real ones.\n */\nexport const PROFILES = [\"plain\", \"llamacpp\", \"vllm\", \"ollama\"];\nconst OWNER = { plain: \"organization\", llamacpp: \"llamacpp\", vllm: \"vllm\", ollama: \"library\" };\n\nfunction profileModel(profile, entry) {\n  const ctx = entry.context_length ?? entry.max_model_len ?? null;\n  const base = { id: entry.id, object: \"model\", owned_by: OWNER[profile] };\n  if (profile === \"llamacpp\" && ctx) return { ...base, meta: { n_ctx_train: ctx } };\n  if (profile === \"vllm\" && ctx) return { ...base, max_model_len: ctx };\n  return base;\n}\n\nfunction overflowBody(profile, ctx) {\n  if (profile === \"llamacpp\") return { error: { code: 400, message: \"the request exceeds the available context size, try increasing it\", type: \"exceed_context_size_error\", n_ctx: ctx } };\n  if (profile === \"vllm\") return { object: \"error\", message: `This model's maximum context length is ${ctx ?? \"unknown\"} tokens. However, you requested more tokens.`, type: \"BadRequestError\", code: 400 };\n  return { error: { message: \"This request exceeds the model's maximum context length.\", type: \"invalid_request_error\", code: \"context_length_exceeded\" } };\n}\n\n/** Rewrites an SSE body as it passes, chunk by chunk; `edit` returns the text to forward (or null to cut the stream). */\nfunction rewriteStream(upstreamRes, res, edit) {\n  let pending = \"\";\n  upstreamRes.setEncoding(\"utf8\");\n  upstreamRes.on(\"data\", (chunk) => {\n    pending += chunk;\n    const events = pending.split(\"\\n\\n\");\n    pending = events.pop() ?? \"\";\n    for (const event of events) {\n      const out = edit(event);\n      if (out === null) {\n        res.socket?.destroy();\n        upstreamRes.destroy();\n        return;\n      }\n      res.write(`${out}\\n\\n`);\n    }\n  });\n  upstreamRes.on(\"end\", () => {\n    if (pending) res.write(edit(pending) ?? \"\");\n    res.end();\n  });\n}\n\n/**\n * Starts a forwarder on 127.0.0.1 for `upstream` (e.g. https://gateway:8443/v1). `faults`: [{ kind, atRequest }] where\n * atRequest counts chat requests from 1. Returns its base URL (same path as the upstream), live counters, and close().\n */\nexport async function startModelProxy({ upstream, caFile, faults = [], profile, authToken, clientToken, socketPath, maxRequests = 1_000, maxConcurrentRequests = 1, maxRequestBytes = 1_000_000, maxCompletionTokens, maxTotalCompletionTokens }) {\n  if (profile !== undefined && !PROFILES.includes(profile)) throw new Error(`unknown profile ${profile}; one of ${PROFILES.join(\", \")}`);\n  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(maxRequests) || maxRequests < 1 || !Number.isSafeInteger(maxConcurrentRequests) || maxConcurrentRequests < 1 || !Number.isSafeInteger(maxRequestBytes) || maxRequestBytes < 1) throw new Error(\"invalid evaluation proxy request limits\");\n  if (maxCompletionTokens !== undefined && (!Number.isSafeInteger(maxCompletionTokens) || maxCompletionTokens < 1)) throw new Error(\"invalid per-request completion-token limit\");\n  if (maxTotalCompletionTokens !== undefined && (!Number.isSafeInteger(maxTotalCompletionTokens) || maxTotalCompletionTokens < 1)) throw new Error(\"invalid aggregate completion-token limit\");\n  for (const f of faults) {\n    if (!FAULT_KINDS.includes(f.kind) || !Number.isInteger(f.atRequest) || f.atRequest < 1) throw new Error(`invalid fault ${JSON.stringify(f)}`);\n  }\n  const target = new URL(upstream);\n  const basePath = target.pathname.replace(/\\/$/, \"\");\n  const allowedRoutes = new Map([\n    [\"GET /models\", \"catalog\"],\n    [\"POST /chat/completions\", \"inference\"],\n    [\"POST /responses\", \"inference\"],\n    [\"POST /messages\", \"inference\"],\n  ]);\n  const client = target.protocol === \"https:\" ? https : http;\n  const ca = caFile ? fs.readFileSync(caFile) : undefined;\n  const stats = { requests: 0, chatRequests: 0, activeInferenceRequests: 0, cancelledRequests: 0, profileContextLookups: 0, requestedCompletionTokens: 0, answered: 0, upstreamFailures: 0, faultsInjected: [], firstRequestAt: null, firstAnswerAt: null };\n\n  /** The upstream /models entries (for an emulated profile's context answers). */\n  const upstreamModels = () => new Promise((resolve) => {\n    const r = client.request({ protocol: target.protocol, hostname: target.hostname, port: target.port || (target.protocol === \"https:\" ? 443 : 80), method: \"GET\", path: `${target.pathname.replace(/\\/$/, \"\")}/models`, headers: { host: target.host, ...(authToken ? { authorization: `Bearer ${authToken}` } : {}) }, ca }, (res) => {\n      let body = \"\";\n      res.setEncoding(\"utf8\");\n      res.on(\"data\", (c) => (body += c));\n      res.on(\"end\", () => { try { resolve(JSON.parse(body).data ?? []); } catch { resolve([]); } });\n    });\n    r.on(\"error\", () => resolve([]));\n    r.end();\n  });\n  const firstContext = async () => { const m = (await upstreamModels())[0]; return m?.context_length ?? m?.max_model_len ?? null; };\n  const sendJson = (res, status, body) => { res.writeHead(status, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" }); res.end(JSON.stringify(body)); };\n\n  const server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\n    stats.requests++;\n    if (clientToken) {\n      const supplied = /^Bearer (.+)$/.exec(String(req.headers.authorization ?? \"\"))?.[1] ?? \"\";\n      const expected = Buffer.from(clientToken);\n      const actual = Buffer.from(supplied);\n      if (actual.length !== expected.length || !timingSafeEqual(actual, expected)) {\n        req.resume();\n        return void sendJson(res, 401, { error: { type: \"authentication_error\", message: \"evaluation proxy authentication failed\" } });\n      }\n    }\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a171fd-3278-7ca3-ad25-d2f716cb2b15","create_time":1792914209.4024887}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
