{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:46:21.384Z","ordinal":329897,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a171fd-3278-7ca3-ad25-d2f716cb2b15","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addb3cbb98481a0a36cce2b993f3c22","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign status: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; no accepted RC or completed release is claimed.**\n\nI continued the evaluator work in the isolated worktree based on `05994a4`. The scorer now lists all nine T4 fault classes, distinguishes T4 qualification runs from T1 smoke runs, and checks that recorded fault sources match their class. I added synthetic regression cases and updated the smoke assertion.\n\n`node --check eval/score.mjs` and `git diff --check` pass. I have **not** run behavior tests: Kimi still holds the exclusive `SUITE` claim. I logged a safe-boundary request for its exact run result and explicit claim release or transfer. The hanging-command, full-disk, and SIGTERM/resume runner mechanisms remain unfinished.\n\nAt the latest CI check, main’s Node 22 and 24 jobs passed, Linux packaging was still running, and CodeQL passed. PR #213’s exact-head Node 22 and 24 jobs were still running. The shared dirty checkout remains untouched."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792914379754,"completed_at_ms":1792914381384}}
