{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T07:50:45.660Z","ordinal":330119,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17206-a967-7e82-86a7-fbef02280228","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addb4d3106481a0ae4351a44464b9e6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.**\n\nI strengthened the T4 scorer in the isolated worktree at base `05994a4`. It now lists all nine fault classes, checks that each class has the expected injection source, and counts only T4 records toward the five-runs-per-class gate. I also added regression cases and updated the smoke assertions in [score.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs).\n\nI ran a synthetic scorer check on the separate Ubuntu desktop using the exact edited scorer file. All assertions passed: nine classes × five runs passed; a six-class set failed; forged source metadata failed; and T2 fault records did not count as T4 qualification. This validates scorer behavior only—it is not a repository test-suite result or T4 qualification.\n\nMain CI is now fully green on `05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099`, including Node 22, Node 24, Linux packaging, and CodeQL. PR #213 has been updated to that base at head `5b521985`; its exact-head tests and CodeQL are still running.\n\nKimi’s `SUITE` claim remains protected, although no test process was visible at the latest check. I have not run local tests. The real hanging-command, full-disk, and SIGTERM/resume fault mechanisms remain unfinished, as do held-out/provider, exact-RC, cross-runner, and human terminal qualification."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792914643091,"completed_at_ms":1792914645660}}
