auto mode runs without asking regardless of workspace trust.\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:46:  test(\"folder trust alone keeps an unset permission mode in review\", () => {\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:226:      assert.equal(promptLog.length, 0, \"explicit auto mode should not depend on workspace trust\");\ncli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py:58:            session.wait_text(\"Trust this folder?\", timeout=20)\ncli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:190:    assert.equal(result.approvalPrompt, mode !== \"auto\", \"approval mode is independent of folder trust\");\ncli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:201:ptyTest(\"ACC-SAFE-01: launcher permission mode is independent of folder trust\", { timeout: 900_000 }, async () => {\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:211:   * Gated by workspace trust: returns empty string if workspace is untrusted (REQ-SEC-113).\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:238:   * Gated by workspace trust and read-only mode.\ncli/src/startup_trust.ts:106:      `Run 'nexus trust .' to load them. Tool approvals follow your permission settings.\\n`,\ncli/src/startup_trust.ts:132:        \"Trust this folder?\",\ncli/src/startup_trust.ts:141:        \"Tool approvals use permission settings.\",\ncli/src/startup_trust.ts:142:        \"Folder trust doesn't change approvals.\",\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:33: * In --read-only mode, workspace trust never authorizes executing project plugins/MCP.\ncli/src/index.ts:288:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:353:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ncli/src/index.ts:385:  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\ncli/src/types.ts:61:  approvalMode?: \"auto\" | \"review\" | \"read-only\"; // Permission posture: auto, review, or read-only (DEC-01, independent of folder trust)\ncli/src/skills.ts:64:    // Project workspace locations (gated by workspace trust)\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:60:3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress. Folder trust only controls project instructions and workspace integrations. Input safety is strictly enforced across surfaces (REQ-SEC-103): lone Enter defaults to No, a 400ms grace period discards typed-ahead input, and approve-all requires explicit confirmation (`all` in REPL, confirmation Enter in TUI). *Limit:* in explicit `auto` posture, commands and file writes execute autonomously regardless of folder trust.\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:61:4. **Workspace trust.** Trust is managed via `nexus trust` and stored in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json`; interactive startup asks for trust before loading project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`). In untrusted workspaces, project instructions, workspace MCP configs, plugins, skills, and `.nexus/knowledge.json` are not loaded (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114). The operator may continue without trust under the existing permission mode or exit. *Limit:* configuration in the operator's home directory (`~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/`) is always trusted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:9:| [DEC-01](#dec-01-default-execution-posture) | Default execution posture | Review by default; permission mode is independent of folder trust | No (resolved) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:40:**Rationale.** Folder trust protects project instructions and workspace integrations from being loaded before the operator approves those sources. Tool authority is governed by the operator's permission settings and must not change when a folder is trusted. A configured `auto` mode remains the operator's…2424 tokens truncated….md:118:- **Workspace trust before executing project configuration** (Claude Code and Codex document trust prompts for\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:259:| B2 | **Workspace trust**: never import workspace plugins or start workspace MCP servers until the operator trusts that workspace (per-path trust record); `--read-only` disables both; MCP children get an environment allowlist | T-03 | clone a repo containing `plugins/x.mjs` and `.mcp.json` that touch a sentinel → no sentinel without explicit trust, in every mode |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:296:| 1 | B1 execution authority + B2 workspace trust (+ R4 listing confinement, T13 dry-run) | 0 | capability × mode × context matrix complete and enforced; adversarial suite blocked; no regression in existing suites |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY `test:cli/test/repl_approval