 for 'compatible')\")\n  .option(\"--planner-provider <id>\", \"Cloud provider for the planner model (requires --planner-model)\")\n  .option(\"--coder-provider <id>\", \"Cloud provider for the coder model (requires --coder-model)\")\n  .option(\"-j, --json\", \"Output machine-readable JSON structured result (UI-002, UI-003)\")\n  .option(\"-r, --resume [id]\", \"Resume previous session or task state\")\n  .action(async (promptParts: string[], _options: any, cmd: Command) => {\n    // Preserve inherited CLI values when the command-level duplicate only has\n    // its default; explicitly supplied command options still take precedence.\n    const options = cmd.optsWithGlobals();\n    for (const option of cmd.options) {\n      const name = option.attributeName();\n      if (cmd.getOptionValueSource(name) !== \"default\") options[name] = _options[name];\n    }\n    let prompt = promptParts.join(\" \").trim();\n    const config = buildConfig(options);\n    config.surface = \"headless\";\n    const isJson = Boolean(options.json);\n\n    // Auto-detect loaded model if model is 'local-model'\n    if (config.model === \"local-model\") {\n      try {\n        const client = new LocalLlmClient(config);\n        const models = await client.listModels();\n        if (models.length > 0) {\n          config.model = models[0];\n          if (!isJson) {\n            console.log(pc.dim(`🔍 Auto-detected active model: ${pc.bold(config.model)}`));\n          }\n        }\n      } catch {\n        // Fallback to default\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (!isJson && (config.provider || config.plannerProvider || config.coderProvider)) console.error(pc.dim(describeTarget(config)));\n    const app = new ApplicationCore(config);\n\n    let resumeTaskId: string | undefined;\n    if (options.resume !== undefined && options.resume !== false) {\n      if (typeof options.resume === \"string\" && options.resume !== \"latest\") {\n        resumeTaskId = options.resume;\n      } else {\n        const targetWorkspace = config.workspace || process.cwd();\n        const tasks = app\n          .getStateManager()\n          .listTasks({ workspace: targetWorkspace })\n          .filter((t) => t.taskId !== app.getTaskId());\n        if (tasks.length === 0) {\n          console.error(`no task to resume in ${targetWorkspace}; see 'nexus status'`);\n          app.shutdown();\n          exitAfterFlush(2);\n          return;\n        }\n        resumeTaskId = tasks[0].taskId;\n      }\n      if (!prompt) {\n        prompt = \"continue\";\n      }\n    } else if (!prompt) {\n      console.error(\"error: missing required argument 'prompt'\");\n      app.shutdown();\n      exitAfterFlush(1);\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Operator stop authority: first SIGINT cancels the active turn; a second one terminates immediately.\n    const abort = new AbortController();\n    let sigints = 0;\n    const onSigint = () => {\n      sigints++;\n      if (sigints === 1) {\n        abort.abort(new Error(\"SIGINT\"));\n        if (!isJson) console.error(pc.yellow(\"\\nInterrupt received: no further work will be started (Ctrl-C again to terminate immediately).\"));\n      } else {\n        process.exit(130);\n      }\n    };\n    process.on(\"SIGINT\", onSigint);\n\n    try {\n      const result = await app.runTask(prompt, {\n        json: isJson,\n        resumeTaskId,\n        signal: abort.signal,\n      });\n\n      const cloud = UsageLedger.global().cloudTotals();\n      if (isJson) {\n        console.log(JSON.stringify(cloud.requests ? { ...result, cloudUsage: cloud } : result, null, 2));\n      } else if (cloud.requests) {\n        console.error(pc.dim(UsageLedger.global().summary()!));\n      }\n\n      app.shutdown();\n      exitAfterFlush(result.exitCode);\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      if (isJson) {\n        console.log(JSON.stringify({\n          taskId: app.getTaskId(),\n          success: false,\n          status: \"failed\",\n          prompt,\n          output: \"\",\n          plan: [],\n   - crash rate and timeout rate;\n   - bounded-failure truthfulness;\n   - operator interventions (= 0 in `run` mode);\n   - tokens and wall time per correct task.\n5. **REQ-QUAL-105. T4 fault injection.** 9 fault classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n   1. gateway refuses connections mid-turn;\n   2. 5xx/overloaded;\n   3. stream cut mid-tool-call;\n   4. output-limit truncation;\n   5. hanging test command;\n   6. workspace disk full;\n   7. context overflow at 32k;\n   8. malformed tool-call JSON;\n   9. SIGTERM mid-turn, then resume.\n\n   Gate (proposal): 100% truthful outcome, 0 false VERIFIED, 0 hangs beyond budget + 5 minutes.\n6. **REQ-QUAL-106. Scoring integrity.**\n   - Infrastructure reruns are symmetric and evidence-based: the endpoint was unreachable before the first model call.\n   - Contaminated runs are excluded from pooled rates.\n   - Hidden tests are not readable by the agent uid.\n   - The scorer logs every replacement.\n   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n10:  \"scripts\": {\n11:    \"build\": \"tsc && node scripts/write_build_info.mjs\",\n12:    \"test\": \"node scripts/run_tests.mjs && bash ../scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\",\n13-    \"start\": \"node dist/index.js\",\n14-    \"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"\n15-  },\n16-  \"keywords\": [\n17-    \"ai\",\n18-    \"coding-agent\",\n19-    \"codex\",\n20-    \"claude-code\",\n21-    \"vllm\",\n22-    \"lm-studio\",\n23-    \"rust\"\n24-  ],\n25-  \"author\": \"\",\n26-  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n27-  \"engines\": {\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":781997753}},"started_at_ms":1792915180667,"completed_at_ms":1792915181449}}
