{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:01:38.193Z","ordinal":330656,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17211-7ad4-71c1-9c02-690a797dca89","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17211-7ad4-71c1-9c02-690a797dca89","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016addb752e00881a0a247481dcf20b8df","usage":{"input_tokens":161914,"cached_input_tokens":157056,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1853,"reasoning_output_tokens":1757,"total_tokens":163767},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2014684,"cached_input_tokens":1940480,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":13121,"reasoning_output_tokens":11292,"total_tokens":2027805},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6029517552,"cached_input_tokens":5964904320,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17124795,"reasoning_output_tokens":9870280,"total_tokens":6046642347}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:01:40.426Z","ordinal":330657,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17211-7ad4-71c1-9c02-690a797dca89","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c3178e5d-34cb-4034-afb7-01f7014ce143","process_id":"33330","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,125p' eval/score.mjs; sed -n '225,280p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,125p' eval/score.mjs","name":"score.mjs","path":"eval/score.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '225,280p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Scores eval results (results.jsonl from eval/run.mjs). Scores are reported separately and never combined\n// (qualification assessment §9): completion claimed, artifact correct (hidden tests), false VERIFIED, regressions,\n// bounded failure, wall time, steps, tokens — per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals for rates.\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\n\nconst T4_FAULT_CLASSES = [\n  \"refuse\",\n  \"overloaded\",\n  \"stream_cut\",\n  \"truncate\",\n  \"hanging_test_command\",\n  \"full_disk\",\n  \"context_overflow\",\n  \"malformed_tool_json\",\n  \"sigterm_resume\",\n];\nconst T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS = 5;\nconst T4_PROXY_CLASSES = new Set([\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"]);\nconst T4_RUNNER_CLASSES = new Set([\"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"sigterm_resume\"]);\n\n// Several files may be given: a later record for the same configuration, task and run replaces an earlier one (a rerun\n// of a run that failed on infrastructure, see eval/infra.mjs). The replaced records stay in their files.\nconst files = process.argv.slice(2).filter((a) => !a.startsWith(\"--\"));\nconst pairMode = process.argv.includes(\"--pairs\");\nif (!files.length) {\n  console.error(\"usage: eval/score.mjs <results.jsonl>... [--pairs] [--json]\");\n  process.exit(2);\n}\nconst peerComparison = pairMode ? validateMatchedPeers(files) : null;\nconst byRun = new Map();\n/** Every replacement is listed (REQ-QUAL-106): which run, what it showed, and what the rerun showed. */\nconst replacements = [];\nconst outcomeOf = (r) => r.error ? `error: ${r.error}` : r.turn?.outcome ?? (r.timedOut ? \"timed out\" : `exit ${r.exitCode}`);\nfor (const file of files) {\n  for (const r of fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean).map((l) => JSON.parse(l))) {\n    const key = `${r.config}\\t${r.task}\\t${r.run}`;\n    const prior = byRun.get(key);\n    if (prior) replacements.push({ config: r.config, task: r.task, run: r.run, was: outcomeOf(prior), now: outcomeOf(r) });\n    byRun.set(key, r);\n  }\n}\nconst replaced = replacements.length;\nconst records = [...byRun.values()];\n/** A run that ended without a result of its own: Nexus without a turn report, or any agent killed by a signal. */\nconst crashed = (r) => !r.error && !r.timedOut && (r.exitCode === null || ((r.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\" && !r.turn));\n\n/** 95 % Wilson score interval for k successes out of n. */\nexport function wilson(k, n) {\n  if (!n) return [0, 0];\n  const z = 1.96;\n  const p = k / n;\n  const denom = 1 + (z * z) / n;\n  const centre = (p + (z * z) / (2 * n)) / denom;\n  const half = (z * Math.sqrt((p * (1 - p)) / n + (z * z) / (4 * n * n))) / denom;\n  return [Math.max(0, centre - half), Math.min(1, centre + half)];\n}\n\nconst median = (xs) => {\n  const s = xs.filter((x) => typeof x === \"number\").sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  return s.length ? (s.length % 2 ? s[(s.length - 1) / 2] : (s[s.length / 2 - 1] + s[s.length / 2]) / 2) : null;\n};\n\nconst groups = new Map();\nfor (const r of records) {\n  const key = `${r.config}\\t${r.task}`;\n  if (!groups.has(key)) groups.set(key, []);\n  groups.get(key).push(r);\n}\n\nconst rows = [...groups.entries()].map(([key, rs]) => {\n  const [config, task] = key.split(\"\\t\");\n  const n = rs.length;\n  const count = (f) => rs.filter(f).length;\n  const correct = count((r) => r.hiddenPass);\n  return {\n    config,\n    task,\n    tier: rs[0].tier,\n    n,\n    claimed: count((r) => r.claimedComplete),\n    correct,\n    correctCI: wilson(correct, n),\n    falseVerified: count((r) => r.falseVerified),\n    regressions: count((r) => r.regressionPass === false),\n    errors: count((r) => r.error),\n    contaminated: count((r) => r.contaminated),\n    timedOut: count((r) => r.timedOut),\n    medianWallS: median(rs.map((r) => r.wallMs / 1000)),\n    medianSteps: median(rs.map((r) => r.turn?.steps?.used)),\n    medianTokens: median(rs.map((r) => r.tokens?.total)),\n  };\n});\n\nconst totals = {\n  runs: records.length,\n  falseVerified: records.filter((r) => r.falseVerified).length,\n  errors: records.filter((r) => r.error).length,\n  crashed: records.filter(crashed).length,\n  contaminated: records.filter((r) => r.contaminated).length,\n  replacedByRerun: replaced,\n};\n\n// Pooled rates leave contaminated runs out (the agent could have seen the hidden tests); they are counted separately.\nconst pooled = [...new Set(records.map((r) => r.config))].map((config) => {\n  const all = records.filter((r) => r.config === config);\n  const rs = all.filter((r) => !r.contaminated);\n  const k = rs.filter((r) => r.hiddenPass).length;\n  const sum = (xs) => xs.reduce((a, b) => a + (b ?? 0), 0);\n  return {\n    config,\n    n: rs.length,\n    excludedContaminated: all.length - rs.length,\n    correct: k,\n    rate: rs.length ? k / rs.length : 0,\n    ci: wilson(k, rs.length),\n    falseVerified: all.filter((r) => r.falseVerified).length,\n    crashRate: all.length ? all.filter(crashed).length / all.length : 0,\n    regressions: rs.filter((r) => r.regressionPass === false).length,\n    // Cost of the whole configuration's runs per correct result (failed runs cost too).\n    tokensPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.tokens?.total)) / k : null,\n    wallSecondsPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.wallMs)) / 1000 / k : null,\n  };\n});\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":145882868}},"started_at_ms":1792915299279,"completed_at_ms":1792915300425}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:01:41.693Z","ordinal":330658,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17214-653d-7a11-ad89-4fca0ae1bd85","call_id":"call_284574a3fa094864bb60f5fcf78b6826","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Scores eval results (results.jsonl from eval/run.mjs). Scores are reported separately and never combined\n// (qualification assessment §9): completion claimed, artifact correct (hidden tests), false VERIFIED, regressions,\n// bounded failure, wall time, steps, tokens — per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals for rates.\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\n\nconst T4_FAULT_CLASSES = [\n  \"refuse\",\n  \"overloaded\",\n  \"stream_cut\",\n  \"truncate\",\n  \"hanging_test_command\",\n  \"full_disk\",\n  \"context_overflow\",\n  \"malformed_tool_json\",\n  \"sigterm_resume\",\n];\nconst T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS = 5;\nconst T4_PROXY_CLASSES = new Set([\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"]);\nconst T4_RUNNER_CLASSES = new Set([\"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"sigterm_resume\"]);\n\n// Several files may be given: a later record for the same configuration, task and run replaces an earlier one (a rerun\n// of a run that failed on infrastructure, see eval/infra.mjs). The replaced records stay in their files.\nconst files = process.argv.slice(2).filter((a) => !a.startsWith(\"--\"));\nconst pairMode = process.argv.includes(\"--pairs\");\nif (!files.length) {\n  console.error(\"usage: eval/score.mjs <results.jsonl>... [--pairs] [--json]\");\n  process.exit(2);\n}\nconst peerComparison = pairMode ? validateMatchedPeers(files) : null;\nconst byRun = new Map();\n/** Every replacement is listed (REQ-QUAL-106): which run, what it showed, and what the rerun showed. */\nconst replacements = [];\nconst outcomeOf = (r) => r.error ? `error: ${r.error}` : r.turn?.outcome ?? (r.timedOut ? \"timed out\" : `exit ${r.exitCode}`);\nfor (const file of files) {\n  for (const r of fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean).map((l) => JSON.parse(l))) {\n    const key = `${r.config}\\t${r.task}\\t${r.run}`;\n    const prior = byRun.get(key);\n    if (prior) replacements.push({ config: r.config, task: r.task, run: r.run, was: outcomeOf(prior), now: outcomeOf(r) });\n    byRun.set(key, r);\n  }\n}\nconst replaced = replacements.length;\nconst records = [...byRun.values()];\n/** A run that ended without a result of its own: Nexus without a turn report, or any agent killed by a signal. */\nconst crashed = (r) => !r.error && !r.timedOut && (r.exitCode === null || ((r.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\" && !r.turn));\n\n/** 95 % Wilson score interval for k successes out of n. */\nexport function wilson(k, n) {\n  if (!n) return [0, 0];\n  const z = 1.96;\n  const p = k / n;\n  const denom = 1 + (z * z) / n;\n  const centre = (p + (z * z) / (2 * n)) / denom;\n  const half = (z * Math.sqrt((p * (1 - p)) / n + (z * z) / (4 * n * n))) / denom;\n  return [Math.max(0, centre - half), Math.min(1, centre + half)];\n}\n\nconst median = (xs) => {\n  const s = xs.filter((x) => typeof x === \"number\").sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  return s.length ? (s.length % 2 ? s[(s.length - 1) / 2] : (s[s.length / 2 - 1] + s[s.length / 2]) / 2) : null;\n};\n\nconst groups = new Map();\nfor (const r of records) {\n  const key = `${r.config}\\t${r.task}`;\n  if (!groups.has(key)) groups.set(key, []);\n  groups.get(key).push(r);\n}\n\nconst rows = [...groups.entries()].map(([key, rs]) => {\n  const [config, task] = key.split(\"\\t\");\n  const n = rs.length;\n  const count = (f) => rs.filter(f).length;\n  const correct = count((r) => r.hiddenPass);\n  return {\n    config,\n    task,\n    tier: rs[0].tier,\n    n,\n    claimed: count((r) => r.claimedComplete),\n    correct,\n    correctCI: wilson(correct, n),\n    falseVerified: count((r) => r.falseVerified),\n    regressions: count((r) => r.regressionPass === false),\n    errors: count((r) => r.error),\n    contaminated: count((r) => r.contaminated),\n    timedOut: count((r) => r.timedOut),\n    medianWallS: median(rs.map((r) => r.wallMs / 1000)),\n    medianSteps: median(rs.map((r) => r.turn?.steps?.used)),\n    medianTokens: median(rs.map((r) => r.tokens?.total)),\n  };\n});\n\nconst totals = {\n  runs: records.length,\n  falseVerified: records.filter((r) => r.falseVerified).length,\n  errors: records.filter((r) => r.error).length,\n  crashed: records.filter(crashed).length,\n  contaminated: records.filter((r) => r.contaminated).length,\n  replacedByRerun: replaced,\n};\n\n// Pooled rates leave contaminated runs out (the agent could have seen the hidden tests); they are counted separately.\nconst pooled = [...new Set(records.map((r) => r.config))].map((config) => {\n  const all = records.filter((r) => r.config === config);\n  const rs = all.filter((r) => !r.contaminated);\n  const k = rs.filter((r) => r.hiddenPass).length;\n  const sum = (xs) => xs.reduce((a, b) => a + (b ?? 0), 0);\n  return {\n    config,\n    n: rs.length,\n    excludedContaminated: all.length - rs.length,\n    correct: k,\n    rate: rs.length ? k / rs.length : 0,\n    ci: wilson(k, rs.length),\n    falseVerified: all.filter((r) => r.falseVerified).length,\n    crashRate: all.length ? all.filter(crashed).length / all.length : 0,\n    regressions: rs.filter((r) => r.regressionPass === false).length,\n    // Cost of the whole configuration's runs per correct result (failed runs cost too).\n    tokensPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.tokens?.total)) / k : null,\n    wallSecondsPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.wallMs)) / 1000 / k : null,\n  };\n});\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17211-7ad4-71c1-9c02-690a797dca89","create_time":1792915301.6934223}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
