{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:11:01.776Z","ordinal":331150,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17211-7ad4-71c1-9c02-690a797dca89","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-22e2e48a-07a3-41dd-be31-ef85c4cba2c1","process_id":"58198","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find eval/host -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%p\\n' | sort; rg -n 'resource-profile|workspaceRoot|tmpfs' eval/host scripts docs/v1.0.0 -g '*.sh' -g '*.md' -g '*.json' | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"list_files","cmd":"find eval/host -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf \"%p\\\\n\"","path":"host"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'resource-profile|workspaceRoot|tmpfs' eval/host scripts docs/v1.0.0 -g '*.sh' -g '*.md' -g '*.json'","query":"resource-profile|workspaceRoot|tmpfs","path":"host"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"eval/host/README.md\neval/host/bubblewrap.mjs\neval/host/container-test/run.sh\neval/host/container-test/systemctl-shim\neval/host/operator_home.mjs\neval/host/provision.sh\neval/host/resource-profile.json\neval/host/rollback.sh\neval/host/validate.mjs\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:174:- **PR #26 evaluator boundary:** PR #26 head `c019575` contains the independently reviewed dedicated-tmpfs preflight and adversarial staged-Git/external-store canary; it is rebased on `886766b`, while integration has since advanced to `5193984`. Exact-head CI run [39119705161](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119705161) is still running its Node 20/22/24 CLI suites at this checkpoint. It must be rebased and requalified on `5193984` before merge. A local synthetic permission probe passed (0711 accepted; 0755 and 0721 rejected); the targeted TypeScript test could not run on this host because no dedicated tmpfs was mounted, and the shared `/dev/shm` correctly failed preflight. That failed local attempt is not counted as a pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:191:  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:273:| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:291:1. **Close remaining source & host prerequisites on `v1/integration`:** Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (Continuity M1/M3/L5), `PLAN-10 PR-10j` (dedicated-tmpfs storage preflight & canary), and `PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` (qualification-host provisioning bundle and frozen resource profile); update the stale `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 sentence now that PR #21 (`a7126aa`) implements draft-then-publish for stable tags.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:52:| SEC-04 | S2 | read-only mode | authority.ts:44-136; tools.ts:485-495, 755-779 | RUNTIME (Repro R2). `isSafeReadOnlyCommand` allows `cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa`, `cat /etc/passwd`, `tail -f /dev/null`. The allowlist does not confine paths. The sandbox runs `--ro-bind / /` with the network unshared, so host secrets are readable and returned to the (possibly cloud) model. | `--read-only` reads like \"safe to point at an untrusted repo\", but it still discloses home-directory secrets. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: in read-only/sandbox mode, mask `$HOME` (tmpfs over home, then ro-bind the workspace only), or path-confine the allowlisted commands. |\neval/host/container-test/run.sh:4:# Every line must read PASS. systemctl is a shim that mounts and unmounts the unit's tmpfs.\neval/host/container-test/run.sh:65:umount /srv/nexus-qual/ws; touch /srv/nexus-qual/ws/leftover; mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /srv/nexus-qual/ws -o size=1m 2>/dev/null; umount /srv/nexus-qual/ws\neval/host/README.md:16:| Size-capped tmpfs | `srv-nexus\\x2dqual-ws.mount` at `/srv/nexus-qual/ws`, `size=storageBytes,mode=0711,uid=<operator>,nosuid,nodev` | The resource contract's `workspaceRoot`: the hard cap on what a run keeps, across all phases. |\neval/host/README.md:20:- `provision.sh` applies these changes and is idempotent. It never remounts an active tmpfs.\neval/host/README.md:45:`resource-profile.json` holds the values. The three frozen T2 configs and every T3/T4 config embed them as their\neval/host/README.md:54:| `memoryBytes` | 16 GiB | `memory.max`, with `memory.swap.max = 0` and `memory.oom.group = 1`. The charge counts the phase's anonymous memory, the page cache it faults in (reclaimable before OOM), **and the tmpfs pages it writes**. A phase that writes 6 GiB of build output therefore has about 10 GiB left for its processes. Exceeding the limit OOM-kills the whole phase, and this is recorded. |\neval/host/README.md:56:| `storageBytes` | 20 GiB | The size of the dedicated tmpfs. It caps everything a run holds in its workspace and home **across phases**, because when a phase's cgroup is removed, its tmpfs charges move to the unlimited parent. Writes beyond the cap fail with `ENOSPC`. Runs are serial, and each run's directories are removed afterwards. |\neval/host/README.md:66:  plus a multi-GiB target directory on tmpfs both count. The measurement below records this repository's own\neval/host/README.md:68:- **Storage.** The worst-case RAM is a full tmpfs plus a phase at its memory limit: 20 + 16 = 36 GiB. Together with\neval/host/resource-profile.json:8:  \"workspaceRoot\": \"/srv/nexus-qual/ws\"\neval/host/rollback.sh:25:workspace_root=$(jq -er .workspaceRoot \"$HERE/resource-profile.json\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:48:| 9 | Read-only HOME masking: bwrap `--tmpfs $HOME --ro-bind <ws> <ws>`. Without bwrap, path-confine the allowlisted commands (reject `~`, `$`, absolute paths, and `..` that escapes). | `sandbox.ts:131-181`; `core/authority.ts:44-136` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:122:In `cli/src/sandbox.ts`, when the read-only domain is active, mount a tmpfs over `$HOME` and ro-bind only the workspace. When bwrap is not available, read-only mode must refuse `run_command` unless the command matches the read-only allowlist **and** every path argument resolves inside the workspace. Use the Rust jail through a `resolve_paths` RPC, or reject any argument containing `~`, `$` or an absolute path.\neval/host/provision.sh:5:# systemd mount unit for the tmpfs workspace root (and the root's parent directory if absent), and /opt/nexus-qual.\neval/host/provision.sh:14:readonly PROFILE=\"$HERE/resource-profile.json\"\neval/host/provision.sh:31:workspace_root=$(jq -er .workspaceRoot \"$PROFILE\")\neval/host/provision.sh:134:# 4. The size-capped tmpfs workspace root, owned by the operator. Mode 0711 lets the evaluator traverse to the per-run\neval/host/provision.sh:136:#    remounts, unlike an ACL on the tmpfs root.\neval/host/provision.sh:145:Description=Nexus qualification workspace root (size-capped tmpfs)\neval/host/provision.sh:148:What=tmpfs\neval/host/provision.sh:150:Type=tmpfs\neval/host/provision.sh:159:# start, never restart: remounting a tmpfs would discard any run in progress.\neval/host/provision.sh:162:[[ \"$live\" == \"tmpfs $storage_bytes $op_uid 711\" ]] || { echo \"mounted $workspace_root is '$live', not 'tmpfs $storage_bytes $op_uid 711'; run rollback.sh, then provision again\" >&2; exit 1; }\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":836632626}},"started_at_ms":1792915860939,"completed_at_ms":1792915861776}}
