{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:13:05.847Z","ordinal":331255,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1721e-d5b7-7c62-9ce9-39a6d4e0b871","author":"/root/t4_runner_independent_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/t4_runner_independent_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — read-only review of the uncommitted diff against `05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099`. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run suites, use the gateway, or access held-out content.\n\n- **SIGTERM/resume evidence can pass without a successful resume.** [`eval/score.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs:137) accepts `resumed: true` without checking `resumeExitCode` or `resumeTurn`. [`eval/run.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs:545) sets `resumed: true` unconditionally after the attempt returns. Thus records with no successful resume result can satisfy the runner-evidence check. Require evidence of a successful resumed invocation and its resulting turn, and add a regression test proving missing/failed resume evidence fails T4.\n\n- **The advertised SIGTERM grace period is bypassed for remaining children.** [`eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:93) calls `finish` when the main child exits; `finish` immediately invokes `killPayload()` at line 114, even when a SIGTERM grace timer is pending. A child still flushing state can therefore be killed before the requested grace expires. The new test uses only one process, so it cannot detect this. Preserve the grace interval for surviving payload processes and test with a child that flushes after its parent exits.\n\n- **The trigger does not establish that SIGTERM occurred mid-turn.** [`eval/run.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs:647) sends SIGTERM as soon as the proxy reports one answer. That proves a response was returned, but not that the turn was still active or had reached resumable progress. Record and require evidence that the turn was active when signaled and that the subsequent run resumed that interrupted work.\n\nThe corrected memory fixture now writes data to `/tmp`, which the isolated runner mounts as tmpfs; that addresses the prior pipe-output-vs-memory-allocation issue. The new supervisor fixture verifies signal delivery and cleanup for a single process, but needs the descendant/grace case above."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17211-7ad4-71c1-9c02-690a797dca89","create_time":1792915985.8471117}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16586}}
