{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:19:41.265Z","ordinal":331674,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b6d407e5-09a0-4c52-afd8-f8aca04c91fe","process_id":"65385","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i \"nexus v1|t4|held.?out|release\" /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -35"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -i 'nexus v1|t4|held.?out|release' /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","query":"nexus v1|t4|held.?out|release","path":"MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:# Task Group: Nexus Code client release and Cloudflare contest publication\n3:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code; reuse_rule=recheck the exact release revision, downloadable artifact, endpoint configuration, contest rules, Cloudflare account, broker installation, and credentials; this records a 2026-10-23 partial result, not portable release or contest readiness.\n9:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/rollout-2026-10-13T16-47-30-01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-23T04:47:40+00:00, thread_id=01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15, contest CI/video/submission material verified; clean-account reproducibility blocked)\n19:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/rollout-2026-10-13T16-47-30-01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-23T04:47:40+00:00, thread_id=01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15, prerelease/installer evidence exists; representative inference remains unverified)\n30:- the user required exact downloadable-artifact and clean-environment verification before declaring readiness -> packaging structure, a release workflow, or a fresh-home install alone is insufficient. [Task 2]\n37:- The stated support envelope is Linux x86-64/glibc with Node.js 20+; do not claim portability beyond it. The rollout records prerelease `v0.1.0-alpha.1`, release workflow `38459471967`, checksum `39548ab8b6ba4043e930f8a30d99ce6f9f787f68c8c46b1b10a9a2f1ea7e5ec8`, and fresh-home installer verification. [Task 2]\n42:- Symptom: a package looks releasable from structure or installer success. Cause: no endpoint was listening at the default local endpoint, so representative inference was not exercised. Fix: require a configured installed-client inference operation before setting `CLIENT_RELEASE_READY`. [Task 2]\n88:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost; reuse_rule=revalidate model/release/inventory/live gateway state and preserve the shared worktree before reuse; the selections and validation results are release-specific, and 22 generic validator checks plus listed vLLM/cancellation limits remain unproven.\n120:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost; reuse_rule=revalidate current vllm-top/gateway health contract, polling cadence, release, and host before reuse; this records a successful `v0.10.2` deployment, not a general guarantee for unrelated inventory sources.\n140:- Regression coverage sends stopped then healthy snapshots to the same `App` instance in `app::gateway_lifecycle_tests::gateway_worker_stop_and_recovery_are_reconciled_without_restarting_app`. `cargo test --manifest-path vllm-top/Cargo.toml` passed `141` tests; release build and console-only Ansible deployment passed, with live `vllm-top 0.10.2`. [Task 1]\n182:- Build isolated debug/release artifacts before classifying suite results. Archive suites can be distorted by missing Git metadata and host npm `EALLOWSCRIPTS`; compare baseline and candidate, then report environmental failures separately rather than calling either a clean verification. [Task 1][Task 2]\n187:- Symptom: initial isolated suites fail before a candidate is fully built. Cause: required debug/release artifacts were absent. Fix: build scratch-copy artifacts first, then classify tests. [Task 1]\n222:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (rollout metadata recorded cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost); reuse_rule=inspect the current HEAD and preserve any dirty working tree before reviewing; re-run TypeScript, Rust, and PTY coverage before treating this code-review result as release qualification.\n241:- Live launch path: `harness.sh` -> `core/target/release/nexus-tui --live` -> TypeScript `cli/dist/sidecar.js` over NDJSON. The evidence protocol has sidecar-generated evidence IDs, `tool.detail`, and receipt requests; `cli/src/evidence.ts` maintains a bounded redacted ledger. [Task 1]\n331:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/rollout-2026-10-13T16-47-30-01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-23T04:47:40+00:00, thread_id=01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15, contest CI/video/submission material verified; clean-account reproducibility blocked)\n335:- CONTEST_SUBMISSION_READY, CLIENT_RELEASE_READY, Cloudflare Artifacts, Workers, cf deploy --secrets-file, EXPERIMENT_AUTH, protected broker, /opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker, clean-clone, judge-owned account, ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9, 38471712649, e05006b6-5dce-47d1-b2ff-15995e41a886\n343:- the user required separate `CLIENT_RELEASE_READY/BLOCKED` and `CONTEST_SUBMISSION_READY/BLOCKED` dispositions with exact revisions, hashes, commands, CI results, and concrete blockers. [Task 5]\n526:- security/t5820-credential-remediation-sync, 26b6f7393c317a3578d36da7888c8fb03addb136, 198 passed, 49 failed, 959 passed, Gitleaks, make quality, t5820-release-integrity, t5820-v128-terminal-qualification, git status, explicit worktree paths\n590:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost; reuse_rule=revalidate service/release/config state and treat all credentials, sessions, fixture paths, and checkout state as time-specific; never use these notes to bypass authentication, expose secrets, directly reach workers, or mutate protected production services.\n677:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost; reuse_rule=recheck authoritative contracts, acceptance records, release identities, and workload/horizon coverage before any readiness declaration; do not infer readiness from deployment health or adjacent phases.\n691:- No canonical `AUTONOMOUS_ENGINEERING_READY` contract or composite acceptance route was found. The verified B+ release, healthy gateway/workers, rollback release, and 65/65 Phase 14 artifacts do not establish AES readiness. [Task 1]\n699:scope: `/home/mike/Projects/aihost` host onboarding, Ubuntu Noble/Resolute platform-baseline work, and the approved commissioning sequence for Dell Precision 5820 `ai-5820-01`; baseline implementation is partial and sandbox review remains a release-blocking boundary.\n712:## Task 2: Implement release-aware Noble/Resolute baseline with pre-mutation gates, partial\n733:- The raw bootstrap gate must run before `apt-get update` and accept exactly `ubuntu:24.04:noble` or `ubuntu:26.04:resolute`. Since `ansible.cfg` sets `inject_facts_as_vars = false`, guarded playbooks must use `ansible_facts.distribution`, `ansible_facts.distribution_version`, and `ansible_facts.distribution_release`. [Task 2]\n734:- Release-aware tests must actually render and inspect APT sources. The Noble and Resolute harnesses were digest-pinned, source-rendering-aware, release-pin-aware, and reported `changed=0` on initial and transition idempotency reruns before the final safety finding. [Task 2]\n752:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, read-only baseline; decision portfolio and five reports unfinished)\n777:# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\n778:scope: Integrate reviewed CI prerequisites and accurately track Nexus v1 release gates, claims, and held-out boundaries; use for `v1/integration` readiness work, not as a substitute for exact-RC qualification.\n779:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (worktree used: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10g-rebased); reuse_rule=recheck integration HEAD, claim ownership/staleness, exact CI, acceptance documents, and release state; recorded alpha.2 status and blockers are time-specific.\n781:## Task 1: Monitor exact-head CI/reviews and merge PR #10 without calling it a release, success for integration; partial for qualification\n785:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, PR #10 integrated; qualification blocked)\n789:- Nexus v1, PR #10, bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0, CI 39085388798, v1/integration, 2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2, check_requirements.mjs --enforce, REQ-QUAL-101, ACCEPTANCE.md, CONCURRENCY.md\n795:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, held-out payload preserved; readiness files untouched)\n799:- FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md, PLAN-10_READINESS_T2, nexus-claims, stale claim, 24-hour threshold, PR #9, held-out, fresh branch CI\n803:- reviewers and the release workflow distinguish source/CI acceptance from RC/product qualification -> never call a gree