nt RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:87:- 9 T4 fault classes × 5 runs.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:90:**Amendment 2026-10-17 (governance).** The T4 protocol enumerates **nine** distinct fault scenarios (SPEC-10 §2.5, ACCEPTANCE §6.2): refused connection, 5xx/overloaded, stream cut mid-tool-call, output-limit truncation, hanging test command, disk full, context overflow at 32k, malformed tool-call JSON, and SIGTERM-then-resume. The summary count previously read \"8\" while listing all nine; the union of the distinct scenarios is retained as **nine** classes × 5 runs. No scenario is dropped or merged. Corrected here, in SPEC-10 §2.5 and in the REQUIREMENTS ledger (REQ-QUAL-105).\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:103:| T4 outcome truthfulness | 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:104:| T4 hangs beyond budget + 5 min | 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:204:- The standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 tasks) and the T4 subset run in both profiles.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:245:9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:308:   - 2 T4 classes.\neval/README.md:53:| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\neval/README.md:83:## Fault injection (T4)\neval/README.md:106:The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\neval/README.md:107:runner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\neval/README.md:267:  has joined the leaf is not lost. It also sends the supervisor `SIGTERM` so that it can still report. If the supervisor\neval/README.md:296:- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\neval/README.md:309:| T4 fault injector | in progress |\neval/README.md:310:| Qualification runs | blocked on independent corpus custody, enforced aggregate sandbox resource limits, completed T3/T4 workloads, exact-RC/provider evidence, and the required operational approvals; the earlier pilot's inference-hour, cloud-budget, and peer-install decisions also remain separate prerequisites |\neval/README.md:321:only (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\neval/agent_sandbox.mjs:46:process.on(\"SIGTERM\", () => stop(\"SIGTERM\"));\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:11:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:25:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:55:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:79:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:119:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:140:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:155:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:166:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:179:- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:191:  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:193:  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:249:- The source suite includes the T1 evaluator smoke and two-fault T4 smoke. These do not establish the full T2, T3, T4 qualification thresholds.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:255:| `REQ-AGT-002` | partial | Zero false `VERIFIED` across the frozen qualification workloads; source regression tests pass (`1,152/1,152` at `a7126aa`) but no held-out evaluation exists. | T2/T3/T4 RC runs | Qualification operator | Run the preregistered acceptance set on an installed RC and retain per-run evidence; fix and repeat any false `VERIFIED`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:271:| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:272:| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:286:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:295:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:6:- **Eval:** the harness is sound for matched T2 fixture runs. The only results come from a 6-task pilot that is self-declared as tuned. No held-out set, no T3/T4, no fault injection. It cannot qualify v1 task quality as it stands.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:92:| EVL-001 | S1 (v1 task-quality claim) | Qualification evidence | eval/README.md:42,47-58; docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:62-63 | DOC-CLAIM + SOURCE. The only scored evidence is 6 in-repo T2 fixture tasks. RESULT.md itself says \"These six tasks were used to find and fix the issues … it does not qualify Nexus. Qualification needs a fresh task set.\" Missing: held-out tasks, the T3 long-task set, the T4 fault injector, the T3 fact-sheet scorer, and runs on the release candidate. The measured builds are 76f4081, ed17e99 and 4fcbe68-dirty; their rebased equivalents (fe576f1, d116e99, 0090f9c) are on main, but db1ca55 itself was never evaluated. | No basis for a v1 claim about task quality. The pilot verdict was \"NOT QUALIFIED (false VERIFIED=2)\". The rerun had 0 false VERIFIED, but on tuned tasks. | A v1 protocol is in §7. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:180:| EVL-R5 | **T4 fault injection**, at least 8 cases × 5 runs (proposal): gateway refuses connections mid-turn; gateway 5xx/overloaded; stream cut mid-tool-call; reply truncated at the output limit; tool timeout (a hanging test command); disk full in the workspace; context-window overflow (32k limit on a large repo); malformed tool-call JSON from the model; SIGTERM mid-turn followed by resume. | failure / recovery | BLOCKER | Per case: either recovery (task completes, scored as recovery rate) or a truthful bounded outcome. **Threshold proposal: 100% truthful, 0 false VERIFIED, 0 hangs past budget+5 min.** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:183:| EVL-R8 | **Pass thresholds (proposal, owner input needed):** false VERIFIED = 0 (hard). Held-out T2 pooled correctness ≥ best matched peer − 10 points, and ≥60% absolute (proposal). No task class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) below 40%. Crash rate ≤2%. T4 truthful = 100%. Regression rate ≤5%. | release gate | BLOCKER | Scorer verdict table, signed off before the RC run. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:184:| EVL-R9 | The T1 self-test stays in CI, and a T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) is added to CI | regression | RELEASE-REQUIRED | `make test` includes both |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:55:| REQ-CON-01..04 | TEST-001..004 | Every security invariant has local automated test; negative fixtures (no effect on deny); synthetic secret egress fixtures; candidate mutation fixtures | P2 §27 | DEMONSTRATED | P | Top-tier §6.10: suites missed A1, T1–T4, T-01..T-06 — TEST-001 \"every invariant\" not true at 10-12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:63:| REQ-AGT-50 | Q1/E1 | Completes representative objectives at pre-registered threshold (≥5 runs/task, T1–T4 tiers) | TOP_TIER §3,§9; eval/README | T2 pilot only (6 fixture tasks): first run NOT QUALIFIED (2 false VERIFIED); rerun ed17e99 87% (26/30), 0 false VERIFIED vs Goose 80% (evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/SCORES_rerun_ed17e99.md). T3/T4 never run; \"qualification needs the full task set\" (RESULT.md) | N (self-run, pre-registered) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:135:| HIST-10 | S3 | Governance | tasks/todo.md; GitHub repo | INFERENCE: zero GitHub issues; open items (I3, I4, stale-lock race, CTX/EXT blockers, TUI P3s, B1 egress gating, eval T3/T4) live only in markdown across ~40 docs | Open work invisible to contributors; easy to drop | Migrate open items to issues with v1 milestone |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:181:| Eval T3/T4 tiers | Run eval/ T3 (long-task, steering) and T4 (fault injected) per TOP_TIER §9 thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:197:| REQ-AGT-V1-03 | Eval T2 full set + T3 + T4 meet TOP_TIER §9 thresholds (false VERIFIED = 0) | Q1/Q3/Q6 unproven | RELEASE-REQUIRED | eval run artefacts |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:228:| Eval T3/T4 tiers; full 24-task set | TOP_TIER §9 | Not run | Open |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:23:| 3 | Shutdown sweep on stdin EOF, SIGTERM and SIGHUP (`tokio::signal`). `prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, SIGTERM)` at startup (Linux, `nix` or `libc` crate). | `main.rs` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:69:   - **(a) Live:** Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration, through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`. The proxy strips every gateway extension and, in a second profile, emulates the llama.cpp, vLLM and Ollama `/models` and overflow shapes. In both profiles, Nexus passes the standalone T2 subset and the T4 subset at the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 threshold, and turns are recorded with receipts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:106:| ACC-INF-10 | ACCEPTANCE §4.2 passes: the live stripped-proxy profiles (plain, plus emulated llama.cpp/vLLM/Ollama shapes) on the standalone T2 and T4 subsets, and server-kind conformance fixtures in CI. Receipts are archived. |\neval/model_proxy.mjs:4:// Bodies are streamed through unchanged unless a fault is scheduled for a request (T4, REQ-QUAL-105); nothing is\neval/model_proxy.mjs:14: * Faults the proxy can inject into the Nth chat request of a run (SPEC-10 T4 classes it can produce itself):\neval/model_proxy.mjs:21: * The other T4 classes (a hanging test command, a full disk, SIGTERM then resume) come from task fixtures and the runner.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:123:- Terminal restore on panic/exit including bracketed paste and kitty flags (live.rs:270-284); SIGTERM/SIGHUP watchdog.\neval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:59:  if (name !== \"SIGTERM\" || !Number.isSafeInteger(graceMs) || graceMs < 0 || graceMs > 30_000) return;\neval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:94:for (const signal of [\"SIGTERM\", \"SIGINT\", \"SIGHUP\"]) process.on(signal, stop);\neval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:101:  // The main command may exit before a descendant finishes handling SIGTERM. Let the\neval/resources.mjs:131:    if (name !== \"SIGTERM\" || !Number.isSafeInteger(graceMs) || graceMs < 0 || graceMs > 30_000) {\neval/resources.mjs:132:      throw new Error(\"contained payload supports SIGTERM with a grace period from 0 to 30000 ms\");\neval/resources.mjs:143:    // supervisor exits. The supervisor also stops on SIGTERM. One that does not exit loses its report, so the run fails\neval/resources.mjs:146:    try { process.kill(child.pid, \"SIGTERM\"); } catch {}\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:38:1. **REQ-AGT-109.** Cancel (Esc, Ctrl-C, `prompt.cancel`, SIGINT to `nexus run`) terminates the process group of every in-flight tool within 5 s: SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after a 2 s grace.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:39:2. **REQ-SEC-106.** On a normal exit, crash of the client, SIGTERM or SIGHUP, harness-core leaves no surviving task-owned processes. This includes background processes the model started with `&`, unless they were explicitly registered as long-lived services (see §5.4).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:55:- **New RPC `cancel { request_id }`.** `killpg(pgid, SIGTERM)`, then SIGKILL after 2 s, then reply `cancelled`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:56:- **Shutdown.** On stdin EOF, SIGTERM or SIGHUP (`core/src/main.rs:194-203` RPC loop), killpg every registered group with the same TERM → KILL sequence, then exit. Install the handlers with `tokio::signal`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:57:- **Parent death.** On Linux, call `prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, SIGTERM)` in harness-core. If the node sidecar dies without closing stdin, harness-core gets a signal and runs the shutdown path. The command children are in their own groups, so the registry sweep is what cleans them up.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:69:In `cli/src/agent.ts`, pass the turn's abort signal into every `executeTool` call. The spine already has the signal (`agent.ts:4359-4372`). The existing cancellation-record semantics (synthetic tool results for undispatched calls) are kept. A tool that was killed reports `status: CANCELLED`, `exit_code: null` and `signal: SIGTERM|SIGKILL`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:18:- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:28:| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:29:| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:34:| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:54:  - T4 smoke.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:64:The original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\neval/score.mjs:8:const T4_FAULT_CLASSES = [\neval/score.mjs:13:  \"hanging_test_command\",\neval/score.mjs:14:  \"full_disk\",\neval/score.mjs:19:const T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS = 5;\neval/score.mjs:20:const T4_PROXY_CLASSES = new Set([\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\"]);\neval/score.mjs:21:const T4_RUNNER_CLASSES = new Set([\"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"sigterm_resume\"]);\neval/score.mjs:127:// T4: emit all nine preregistered classes, including empty rows. Proxy, task-fixture, and\neval/score.mjs:133:const expectedSource = (kind) => T4_PROXY_CLASSES.has(kind) ? \"model_proxy\" : T4_RUNNER_CLASSES.has(kind) ? \"task_fixture_or_runner\" : null;\neval/score.mjs:138:    return evidence.signal === \"SIGTERM\"\neval/score.mjs:143:      && evidence.payloadExitSignal === \"SIGTERM\"\neval/score.mjs:148:  if (event.kind === \"hanging_test_command\") return evidence.observedHung === true && evidence.timedOut === true && evidence.containmentCleaned === true;\neval/score.mjs:149:  if (event.kind === \"full_disk\") return evidence.writeFailedWithEnospc === true && Number.isSafeInteger(evidence.storageLimitBytes) && evidence.storageLimitBytes > 0;\neval/score.mjs:152:const t4Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T4\");\neval/score.mjs:153:const invalidT4Events = t4Runs.flatMap((r) => t4Events(r)\neval/score.mjs:154:  .filter((f) => !expectedSource(f.kind) || f.source !== expectedSource(f.kind) || (T4_RUNNER_CLASSES.has(f.kind) && !runnerEvidenceValid(f)))\neval/score.mjs:156:const faultRows = T4_FAULT_CLASSES.map((kind) => {\neval/score.mjs:172:    gate: rs.length >= T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS && qualificationTruthful === rs.length && rs.every((r) => !r.timedOut) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\",\neval/score.mjs:176:  requiredClasses: T4_FAULT_CLASSES.length,\neval/score.mjs:177:  requiredRunsPerClass: T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS,\neval/score.mjs:180:  invalidEvents: invalidT4Events.length,\neval/score.mjs:181:  gate: invalidT4Events.length === 0 && faultRows.every((r) => r.gate === \"PASS\") ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\",\neval/score.mjs:222:    console.log(\"\\n| T4 fault | injected runs | qualification runs | truthful | recovered | hung past budget | gate |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\");\neval/score.mjs:225:  console.log(`\\nT4 gate: ${t4.gate} (${t4.observedClasses}/${t4.requiredClasses} classes; ${t4.requiredRunsPerClass} runs required per class; ${t4.invalidEvents} invalid injection records)`);\neval/run.mjs:208:    // T4: a task (or the config) may schedule faults for the proxy to inject; they are recorded with the run.\neval/run.mjs:531:  if (task.tier !== \"T4\" || (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") !== \"nexus\" || config.qualification !== true || !config.resources) {\neval/run.mjs:539:    signal: \"SIGTERM\",\neval/run.mjs:553:    stdout: `${interrupted.stdout}\\n--- T4 SIGTERM in