{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:20:06.391Z","ordinal":331689,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-57e9f154-3739-43e2-867d-ccc1e43ef2c9","process_id":"56043","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '80,115p' eval/README.md; sed -n '230,265p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '1,180p' docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md; rg -n 't4RunnerFault|tier.*T4|T4 fault' eval --glob '!results/**' --glob '!evidence/**'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '80,115p' eval/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"eval/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '230,265p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","name":"PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 't4RunnerFault|tier.*T4|T4 fault' eval --glob '!results/**' --glob '!evidence/**'","query":"t4RunnerFault|tier.*T4|T4 fault","path":"eval"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n\nWhat was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\n\n- runs;\n- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\n  hidden tests failed);\n- **recovered** (the hidden tests pass);\n- hung past budget.\n\nThe remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\nrunner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n# PLAN-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\nImplements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harness fixes are milestone **M3**. Task authoring runs in parallel from M1. Runs are **M5**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-110.\n- Decisions: DEC-05, DEC-06, DEC-07.\n- Owner actions: X2, X3, X4, X5.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\n- new `eval/fingerprint.mjs`\n- new `eval/faults/`\n- `eval/tasks/`\n- `eval/configs/`\n- `eval/README.md`\n- `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`\n- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Location | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Symmetric infrastructure classification. A run counts as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** there is an unreachable signature. Same rule for every agent. Crash and timeout rates are reported. | `infra.mjs:31`; `run.mjs` (record `first_model_request_at` from the proxy log) | — |\n| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\n| 3 | Hidden-test isolation. Hidden tests are stored under a separate uid (`nexus-eval`, created by the operator, owner action under X3) with mode 0700, and copied in after the agent exits. The agent runs with an allow-listed env. | `run.mjs:57-59,114,178` | — |\n| 4 | Fingerprint. Record server kind, build, weights sha256 (from config), and sampling settings. Refuse the run if the fingerprint is missing. Temperature 0 or a fixed seed for every agent where the agent supports it. | new `fingerprint.mjs`; `configs/*.json` | PLAN-05 task 1 |\n| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\n| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\n| 7 | Task schema `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`, with a validator. | `eval/tasks/schema.json`; `run.mjs` | — |\n| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n- **PR-10b:** tasks 3, 4, 7.\n- **PR-10c:** tasks 5, 6.\n- **PR-10d:** tasks 9, 10.\n- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\n\nTask 8 is data work. Tasks 11 and 12 are operations work.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `eval_harness.test.ts`:\n  - infra symmetry: a Nexus crash is counted as a failure, not rerun;\n  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\n  - fingerprint refusal;\n  - T4 smoke.\n\n## Effort and uncertainty\n\n| Work | Estimate | Main uncertainty |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harness fixes | 4–6 engineer-days | — |\n| Task authoring | 40 T2 tasks at 1–2 hours each, plus 8 T3 tasks at 3–4 hours each: roughly 10–14 days of author time | Author availability (X2) |\n| Run wall time (historical estimate; see below) | (40×5 + 8×5 + 40) runs per agent × 3 agents ≈ 840 runs. At a median 6 min/run serial on one inference host, about 84 hours, roughly 4 days of continuous inference. T3 runs are longer. | Inference-host availability and thermal behaviour (see the `experiments/thermal-soak` history). This is the critical-path risk for M5. |\n\nThe original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\n- The DEC-05 thresholds were evaluated with the scorer verdict table, signed off before the run and reported after it.\n- REQ-QUAL-109/110 are met.\neval/README.md:53:| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\neval/README.md:309:| T4 fault injector | in progress |\neval/score.mjs:152:const t4Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T4\");\neval/score.mjs:222:    console.log(\"\\n| T4 fault | injected runs | qualification runs | truthful | recovered | hung past budget | gate |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\");\neval/run.mjs:528:  if (task.t4RunnerFault !== \"sigterm_resume\") {\neval/run.mjs:531:  if (task.tier !== \"T4\" || (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") !== \"nexus\" || config.qualification !== true || !config.resources) {\neval/validate.mjs:64:  if (task.t4RunnerFault !== undefined) {\neval/validate.mjs:65:    need(task.tier === \"T4\" && task.t4RunnerFault === \"sigterm_resume\", \"t4RunnerFault is supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task\");\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":226757287}},"started_at_ms":1792916405164,"completed_at_ms":1792916406391}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:20:07.542Z","ordinal":331690,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17225-44f6-79a1-ba8b-faaac6cbd3bb","call_id":"call_46989c087fe44337bf371c7e89ebb12c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n\nWhat was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\n\n- runs;\n- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\n  hidden tests failed);\n- **recovered** (the hidden tests pass);\n- hung past budget.\n\nThe remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\nrunner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n# PLAN-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\nImplements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harness fixes are milestone **M3**. Task authoring runs in parallel from M1. Runs are **M5**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-110.\n- Decisions: DEC-05, DEC-06, DEC-07.\n- Owner actions: X2, X3, X4, X5.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\n- new `eval/fingerprint.mjs`\n- new `eval/faults/`\n- `eval/tasks/`\n- `eval/configs/`\n- `eval/README.md`\n- `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`\n- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Location | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Symmetric infrastructure classification. A run counts as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** there is an unreachable signature. Same rule for every agent. Crash and timeout rates are reported. | `infra.mjs:31`; `run.mjs` (record `first_model_request_at` from the proxy log) | — |\n| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\n| 3 | Hidden-test isolation. Hidden tests are stored under a separate uid (`nexus-eval`, created by the operator, owner action under X3) with mode 0700, and copied in after the agent exits. The agent runs with an allow-listed env. | `run.mjs:57-59,114,178` | — |\n| 4 | Fingerprint. Record server kind, build, weights sha256 (from config), and sampling settings. Refuse the run if the fingerprint is missing. Temperature 0 or a fixed seed for every agent where the agent supports it. | new `fingerprint.mjs`; `configs/*.json` | PLAN-05 task 1 |\n| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\n| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\n| 7 | Task schema `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`, with a validator. | `eval/tasks/schema.json`; `run.mjs` | — |\n| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n- **PR-10b:** tasks 3, 4, 7.\n- **PR-10c:** tasks 5, 6.\n- **PR-10d:** tasks 9, 10.\n- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\n\nTask 8 is data work. Tasks 11 and 12 are operations work.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `eval_harness.test.ts`:\n  - infra symmetry: a Nexus crash is counted as a failure, not rerun;\n  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\n  - fingerprint refusal;\n  - T4 smoke.\n\n## Effort and uncertainty\n\n| Work | Estimate | Main uncertainty |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harness fixes | 4–6 engineer-days | — |\n| Task authoring | 40 T2 tasks at 1–2 hours each, plus 8 T3 tasks at 3–4 hours each: roughly 10–14 days of author time | Author availability (X2) |\n| Run wall time (historical estimate; see below) | (40×5 + 8×5 + 40) runs per agent × 3 agents ≈ 840 runs. At a median 6 min/run serial on one inference host, about 84 hours, roughly 4 days of continuous inference. T3 runs are longer. | Inference-host availability and thermal behaviour (see the `experiments/thermal-soak` history). This is the critical-path risk for M5. |\n\nThe original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\n- The DEC-05 thresholds were evaluated with the scorer verdict table, signed off before the run and reported after it.\n- REQ-QUAL-109/110 are met.\neval/README.md:53:| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\neval/README.md:309:| T4 fault injector | in progress |\neval/score.mjs:152:const t4Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T4\");\neval/score.mjs:222:    console.log(\"\\n| T4 fault | injected runs | qualification runs | truthful | recovered | hung past budget | gate |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\");\neval/run.mjs:528:  if (task.t4RunnerFault !== \"sigterm_resume\") {\neval/run.mjs:531:  if (task.tier !== \"T4\" || (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") !== \"nexus\" || config.qualification !== true || !config.resources) {\neval/validate.mjs:64:  if (task.t4RunnerFault !== undefined) {\neval/validate.mjs:65:    need(task.tier === \"T4\" && task.t4RunnerFault === \"sigterm_resume\", \"t4RunnerFault is supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task\");\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792916407.54221}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
