{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:20:32.378Z","ordinal":331709,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-84c3d70c-fbc0-4214-8a6b-28dbc42eac8c","process_id":"97478","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"2\\.5|hanging test|full.?disk|disk full|SIGTERM\" docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '100,170p' docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md; sed -n '90,115p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; sed -n '220,245p' eval/score.mjs"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"2\\\\.5|hanging test|full.?disk|disk full|SIGTERM\" docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"2\\.5|hanging test|full.?disk|disk full|SIGTERM","path":"SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '100,170p' docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","name":"SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '90,115p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md","name":"DECISIONS.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '220,245p' eval/score.mjs","name":"score.mjs","path":"eval/score.mjs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:182:| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:241:5. hanging test command\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:242:6. disk full\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:245:9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:69:   5. hanging test command;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:70:   6. workspace disk full;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:73:   9. SIGTERM mid-turn, then resume.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:107:- SPEC-02 (cancel and SIGTERM semantics).\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:90:**Amendment 2026-10-17 (governance).** The T4 protocol enumerates **nine** distinct fault scenarios (SPEC-10 §2.5, ACCEPTANCE §6.2): refused connection, 5xx/overloaded, stream cut mid-tool-call, output-limit truncation, hanging test command, disk full, context overflow at 32k, malformed tool-call JSON, and SIGTERM-then-resume. The summary count previously read \"8\" while listing all nine; the union of the distinct scenarios is retained as **nine** classes × 5 runs. No scenario is dropped or merged. Corrected here, in SPEC-10 §2.5 and in the REQUIREMENTS ledger (REQ-QUAL-105).\n\n- See [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) §4–§7 for the qualification runbook, environments and pass/fail table.\n- All runs are archived under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`, with the manifest, raw JSONL, the scorer output and SHA256SUMS.\n\n## 5. Dependencies\n\n- SPEC-01 (`run` mode needs an explicit `--yes`).\n- SPEC-02 (cancel and SIGTERM semantics).\n- SPEC-04 (resume).\n- SPEC-05 (server kind, receipts).\n- DEC-05, DEC-06 and DEC-07 (all resolved). Owner actions X2, X3 and X4 are needed.\n- Hardware: the homelab inference host, reached through its gateway only, is the sole inference path (DEC-16). Every agent's runs are serial on it.\n**Amendment 2026-10-17 (governance).** The T4 protocol enumerates **nine** distinct fault scenarios (SPEC-10 §2.5, ACCEPTANCE §6.2): refused connection, 5xx/overloaded, stream cut mid-tool-call, output-limit truncation, hanging test command, disk full, context overflow at 32k, malformed tool-call JSON, and SIGTERM-then-resume. The summary count previously read \"8\" while listing all nine; the union of the distinct scenarios is retained as **nine** classes × 5 runs. No scenario is dropped or merged. Corrected here, in SPEC-10 §2.5 and in the REQUIREMENTS ledger (REQ-QUAL-105).\n\n**Amendment 2026-10-18 (owner decision, T3 false-presence gate).** For the T3 closing fact-sheet probe (REQ-QUAL-109, ACCEPTANCE §6.3), **false-presence = 0** (claiming a missing file is present) is gated in addition to **false-absence = 0** (claiming an existing file is absent), so an agent cannot trivially satisfy false-absence = 0 by answering `present` for every fact. Every T3 task fact sheet is required to contain both `expected: \"present\"` and `expected: \"absent\"` facts.\n\n**Thresholds, all must hold:**\n\n| Metric | Threshold |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED | **0** (hard) |\n| Held-out T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | **≥ 60% absolute** and **≥ (best matched peer − 10 points)** |\n| Correctness per task class | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 outcome truthfulness | 100% |\n| T4 hangs beyond budget + 5 min | 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| `run`-mode operator interventions | 0 |\n\n**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\n\n**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\n\n**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\n\n  for (const p of pooled) console.log(`| ${p.config} | ${p.n} | ${p.correct} | ${pct(p.rate)} (${pct(p.ci[0])}–${pct(p.ci[1])}) | ${p.falseVerified} | ${pct(p.crashRate)} | ${p.regressions} | ${p.tokensPerCorrect?.toFixed(0) ?? \"–\"} | ${p.wallSecondsPerCorrect?.toFixed(0) ?? \"–\"} |`);\n  if (faultRows.length) {\n    console.log(\"\\n| T4 fault | injected runs | qualification runs | truthful | recovered | hung past budget | gate |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\");\n    for (const f of faultRows) console.log(`| ${f.kind} | ${f.n} | ${f.qualificationRuns} | ${f.truthful} (${f.truthfulRate === null ? \"–\" : pct(f.truthfulRate)}) | ${f.recovered} | ${f.hungPastBudget} | ${f.gate} |`);\n  }\n  console.log(`\\nT4 gate: ${t4.gate} (${t4.observedClasses}/${t4.requiredClasses} classes; ${t4.requiredRunsPerClass} runs required per class; ${t4.invalidEvents} invalid injection records)`);\n  if (t3) {\n    console.log(`\\nT3 · ${t3.tasks} task(s), ${t3.runs} run(s)${t3.shapeMet ? \"\" : ` (needs ${T3_TASKS} tasks × ${T3_RUNS_PER_TASK} runs)`} · ineligible (steps < 60 or compactions < 2, or no result) ${t3.ineligible} · false absences ${t3.falseAbsences} · false presences ${t3.falsePresences} · contaminated ${t3.contaminated} · probe unanswered ${t3.probeUnanswered} · steering honoured ${t3.steeringHonoured}/${t3.steeringItems} (${pct(t3.steeringRate)}) · gate ${t3.gate}`);\n  }\n  if (replacements.length) {\n    console.log(\"\\nReplaced by rerun:\");\n    for (const r of replacements) console.log(`- ${r.config} ${formatTaskId(r.task)} run ${r.run}: ${r.was} → ${r.now}`);\n  }\n  if (peerComparison) {\n    console.log(`\\nMatched peer comparison · ${peerComparison.matchedRuns} runs · model ${peerComparison.model.alias}`);\n    for (const [agent, version] of Object.entries(peerComparison.versions)) console.log(`- ${agent}: ${version}`);\n    console.log(\"| task | runs | Nexus correct | Goose correct | OpenCode correct |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\");\n    for (const task of peerComparison.tasks) console.log(`| ${formatTaskId(task.task)} | ${task.runs} | ${task.correct.nexus} | ${task.correct.goose} | ${task.correct.opencode} |`);\n  }\n  console.log(\"\");\n  console.log(\"| config | task | tier | n | claimed | correct (95% CI) | false VERIFIED | regressions | timed out | contaminated | median wall s | median steps | median tokens |\");\n  console.log(\"|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\");\n  for (const r of rows) {\n    console.log(`| ${r.config} | ${formatTaskId(r.task)} | ${r.tier} | ${r.n} | ${r.claimed} | ${r.correct} (${pct(r.correctCI[0])}–${pct(r.correctCI[1])}) | ${r.falseVerified} | ${r.regressions} | ${r.timedOut} | ${r.contaminated} | ${r.medianWallS?.toFixed(0) ?? \"–\"} | ${r.medianSteps ?? \"–\"} | ${r.medianTokens ?? \"–\"} |`);\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":859076207}},"started_at_ms":1792916431518,"completed_at_ms":1792916432378}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:20:33.606Z","ordinal":331710,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17225-aac6-7e72-9c39-283c640c3c7e","call_id":"call_509378c3a4be42569cf70604ca4257cb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:182:| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:241:5. hanging test command\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:242:6. disk full\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:245:9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:69:   5. hanging test command;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:70:   6. workspace disk full;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:73:   9. SIGTERM mid-turn, then resume.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:107:- SPEC-02 (cancel and SIGTERM semantics).\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:90:**Amendment 2026-10-17 (governance).** The T4 protocol enumerates **nine** distinct fault scenarios (SPEC-10 §2.5, ACCEPTANCE §6.2): refused connection, 5xx/overloaded, stream cut mid-tool-call, output-limit truncation, hanging test command, disk full, context overflow at 32k, malformed tool-call JSON, and SIGTERM-then-resume. The summary count previously read \"8\" while listing all nine; the union of the distinct scenarios is retained as **nine** classes × 5 runs. No scenario is dropped or merged. Corrected here, in SPEC-10 §2.5 and in the REQUIREMENTS ledger (REQ-QUAL-105).\n\n- See [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) §4–§7 for the qualification runbook, environments and pass/fail table.\n- All runs are archived under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`, with the manifest, raw JSONL, the scorer output and SHA256SUMS.\n\n## 5. Dependencies\n\n- SPEC-01 (`run` mode needs an explicit `--yes`).\n- SPEC-02 (cancel and SIGTERM semantics).\n- SPEC-04 (resume).\n- SPEC-05 (server kind, receipts).\n- DEC-05, DEC-06 and DEC-07 (all resolved). Owner actions X2, X3 and X4 are needed.\n- Hardware: the homelab inference host, reached through its gateway only, is the sole inference path (DEC-16). Every agent's runs are serial on it.\n**Amendment 2026-10-17 (governance).** The T4 protocol enumerates **nine** distinct fault scenarios (SPEC-10 §2.5, ACCEPTANCE §6.2): refused connection, 5xx/overloaded, stream cut mid-tool-call, output-limit truncation, hanging test command, disk full, context overflow at 32k, malformed tool-call JSON, and SIGTERM-then-resume. The summary count previously read \"8\" while listing all nine; the union of the distinct scenarios is retained as **nine** classes × 5 runs. No scenario is dropped or merged. Corrected here, in SPEC-10 §2.5 and in the REQUIREMENTS ledger (REQ-QUAL-105).\n\n**Amendment 2026-10-18 (owner decision, T3 false-presence gate).** For the T3 closing fact-sheet probe (REQ-QUAL-109, ACCEPTANCE §6.3), **false-presence = 0** (claiming a missing file is present) is gated in addition to **false-absence = 0** (claiming an existing file is absent), so an agent cannot trivially satisfy false-absence = 0 by answering `present` for every fact. Every T3 task fact sheet is required to contain both `expected: \"present\"` and `expected: \"absent\"` facts.\n\n**Thresholds, all must hold:**\n\n| Metric | Threshold |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED | **0** (hard) |\n| Held-out T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | **≥ 60% absolute** and **≥ (best matched peer − 10 points)** |\n| Correctness per task class | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 outcome truthfulness | 100% |\n| T4 hangs beyond budget + 5 min | 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| `run`-mode operator interventions | 0 |\n\n**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\n\n**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\n\n**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\n\n  for (const p of pooled) console.log(`| ${p.config} | ${p.n} | ${p.correct} | ${pct(p.rate)} (${pct(p.ci[0])}–${pct(p.ci[1])}) | ${p.falseVerified} | ${pct(p.crashRate)} | ${p.regressions} | ${p.tokensPerCorrect?.toFixed(0) ?? \"–\"} | ${p.wallSecondsPerCorrect?.toFixed(0) ?? \"–\"} |`);\n  if (faultRows.length) {\n    console.log(\"\\n| T4 fault | injected runs | qualification runs | truthful | recovered | hung past budget | gate |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\");\n    for (const f of faultRows) console.log(`| ${f.kind} | ${f.n} | ${f.qualificationRuns} | ${f.truthful} (${f.truthfulRate === null ? \"–\" : pct(f.truthfulRate)}) | ${f.recovered} | ${f.hungPastBudget} | ${f.gate} |`);\n  }\n  console.log(`\\nT4 gate: ${t4.gate} (${t4.observedClasses}/${t4.requiredClasses} classes; ${t4.requiredRunsPerClass} runs required per class; ${t4.invalidEvents} invalid injection records)`);\n  if (t3) {\n    console.log(`\\nT3 · ${t3.tasks} task(s), ${t3.runs} run(s)${t3.shapeMet ? \"\" : ` (needs ${T3_TASKS} tasks × ${T3_RUNS_PER_TASK} runs)`} · ineligible (steps < 60 or compactions < 2, or no result) ${t3.ineligible} · false absences ${t3.falseAbsences} · false presences ${t3.falsePresences} · contaminated ${t3.contaminated} · probe unanswered ${t3.probeUnanswered} · steering honoured ${t3.steeringHonoured}/${t3.steeringItems} (${pct(t3.steeringRate)}) · gate ${t3.gate}`);\n  }\n  if (replacements.length) {\n    console.log(\"\\nReplaced by rerun:\");\n    for (const r of replacements) console.log(`- ${r.config} ${formatTaskId(r.task)} run ${r.run}: ${r.was} → ${r.now}`);\n  }\n  if (peerComparison) {\n    console.log(`\\nMatched peer comparison · ${peerComparison.matchedRuns} runs · model ${peerComparison.model.alias}`);\n    for (const [agent, version] of Object.entries(peerComparison.versions)) console.log(`- ${agent}: ${version}`);\n    console.log(\"| task | runs | Nexus correct | Goose correct | OpenCode correct |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\");\n    for (const task of peerComparison.tasks) console.log(`| ${formatTaskId(task.task)} | ${task.runs} | ${task.correct.nexus} | ${task.correct.goose} | ${task.correct.opencode} |`);\n  }\n  console.log(\"\");\n  console.log(\"| config | task | tier | n | claimed | correct (95% CI) | false VERIFIED | regressions | timed out | contaminated | median wall s | median steps | median tokens |\");\n  console.log(\"|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\");\n  for (const r of rows) {\n    console.log(`| ${r.config} | ${formatTaskId(r.task)} | ${r.tier} | ${r.n} | ${r.claimed} | ${r.correct} (${pct(r.correctCI[0])}–${pct(r.correctCI[1])}) | ${r.falseVerified} | ${r.regressions} | ${r.timedOut} | ${r.contaminated} | ${r.medianWallS?.toFixed(0) ?? \"–\"} | ${r.medianSteps ?? \"–\"} | ${r.medianTokens ?? \"–\"} |`);\n  }\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792916433.6063678}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
