two T4 smoke cases passed 2/2 on ubuntu-desktop using a snapshot of exact base 05994a4 plus only this claimed slice diff. Source test runner used a fresh isolated HOME/XDG and the exact-main CI package harness-core; no inference or held-out data. An initial attempt under /tmp was correctly refused by the harness protected-runtime-root policy and is recorded as an environment-path setup failure; relocating the disposable snapshot under /home/mike allowed the tests to run. Local Kimi SUITE remains active; no local tests were started.\n3965:2026-10-25T08:02:01Z codex-root CLAIM FILE_eval_resources.mjs FILE_eval_cgroup_supervisor.mjs for PLAN-10 T4 SIGTERM/resume orchestration\n3966:2026-10-25T08:11:59Z codex-root PLAN-10_PR-10c progress: added cgroup-supervisor FD control channel for graceful SIGTERM delivery to every payload pid with bounded forced cleanup; added host fixture proving handler writes its state marker before supervisor cleanup; run-agent signals only after first model response and restarts Nexus with --resume; scorer rejects runner-fault labels lacking runner evidence; task validation accepts sigterm_resume only on T4; corrected memory enforcement fixture to allocate tmpfs-backed pages (instead of output-limited tail). Separate ubuntu-desktop targeted checks: T4 scoring + task validation + graceful signal 3/3 PASS; T4 proxy smoke 2/2 PASS. Broader resource-contract check confirmed memory OOM and process-count enforcement, then failed at workspace-storage assertion because this host uses shared /dev/shm rather than required dedicated size-capped tmpfs; recorded as environment prerequisite, not pass. No held-out tasks/inference. Exact source base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099; independent review pending.\n3967:2026-10-25T09:12:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_FOLLOWUP_FIXES: Addressed independent T4 review findings in claimed worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4, branch v1/plan-10-pr10c-t4-qualification, exact base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099. Scorer now requires delivered SIGTERM during an active inference turn, first process exit by SIGTERM, resume exit 0, and resulting turn COMPLETED; runner records these observations rather than unconditional resumed=true. Supervisor defers cgroup cleanup/escalation until SIGTERM grace elapses even when main child exits, allowing descendants to flush. Added regressions for missing resume evidence/inactive signal and descendant flush. On ubuntu-desktop isolated snapshot with fresh HOME/XDG: T4 scorer+supervisor focused patterns 2/2 PASS; T4 smoke patterns 2/2 PASS; diff-check PASS. No inference, held-out task, or full suite. Independent read-only re-review requested; no commit/PR until disposition.\n3968:2026-10-25T09:18:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_WRAPPER_SIGNAL_FIX: Follow-up independent review identified that child.close observes the systemd-run wrapper, while the contained supervisor reports the actual payload signal. Replaced scorer input with payloadExitSignal sourced from containment.final.signal; recorded supervisorWrapperExitSignal separately for diagnosis. Added regression rejecting wrapper-only SIGTERM. Exact branch base remains 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099; diff-check clean. Ubuntu desktop isolated HOME/XDG targeted T4 scorer and descendant-grace cases PASS 2/2 after correction. Fresh independent read-only re-review requested; no commit/PR, qualification, inference, or held-out access.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs:13:  \"hanging_test_command\",\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs:14:  \"full_disk\",\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs:21:const T4_RUNNER_CLASSES = new Set([\"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"sigterm_resume\"]);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs:148:  if (event.kind === \"hanging_test_command\") return evidence.observedHung === true && evidence.timedOut === true && evidence.containmentCleaned === true;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs:149:  if (event.kind === \"full_disk\") return evidence.writeFailedWithEnospc === true && Number.isSafeInteger(evidence.storageLimitBytes) && evidence.storageLimitBytes > 0;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:234:  const kinds = [\"refuse\", \"overloaded\", \"stream_cut\", \"truncate\", \"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"context_overflow\", \"malformed_tool_json\", \"sigterm_resume\"];\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:236:    const runnerClass = [\"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"sigterm_resume\"].includes(kind);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:239:      : kind === \"hanging_test_command\"\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:240:        ? { observedHung: true, timedOut: true, containmentCleaned: true }\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:241:        : kind === \"full_disk\"\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:242:          ? { writeFailedWithEnospc: true, storageLimitBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 }\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:254:      model: [\"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"sigterm_resume\"].includes(kind) ? { faultsInjected: [] } : { faultsInjected: [event] },\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:255:      t4FaultsInjected: [\"hanging_test_command\", \"full_disk\", \"sigterm_resume\"].includes(kind) ? [event] : [],\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:365:  assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, t4RunnerFault: \"sigterm_resume\" }, dir).join(), /supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task/);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:366:  assert.deepEqual(validateTask({ ...good, tier: \"T4\", t4RunnerFault: \"sigterm_resume\" }, dir), []);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:367:  assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, tier: \"T4\", t4RunnerFault: \"full_disk\" }, dir).join(), /supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task/);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs:528:  if (task.t4RunnerFault !== \"sigterm_resume\") {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/validate.mjs:64:  if (task.t4RunnerFault !== undefined) {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/validate.mjs:65:    need(task.tier === \"T4\" && task.t4RunnerFault === \"sigterm_resume\", \"t4RunnerFault is supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task\");\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792916738.159419}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
