{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:25:49.004Z","ordinal":331949,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-db140d5d-4359-41c6-bf3e-8dec405548cb","process_id":"53682","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,120p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/README.md && sed -n '180,315p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs && sed -n '490,585p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs && sed -n '120,190p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs && sed -n '1,60p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,120p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '180,315p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs","name":"run.mjs","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '490,585p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs","name":"run.mjs","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/run.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '120,190p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs","name":"score.mjs","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,60p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","name":"PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\n\n`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\nseparately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\n\n`docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` is a historical checkpoint at source revision `6151a23`; use this file and the current\nrunner source for evaluator behavior added after that revision. Neither document represents completed M5 qualification.\n\n```bash\nnode eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\nnode eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\nnode eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$NEXUS_RESULTS\" \"$GOOSE_RESULTS\" \"$OPENCODE_RESULTS\"\n```\n\nEach run uses a frozen copy of the task tree, a fresh workspace and `HOME`, and a unique output directory. The agent\nreceives only its workspace, isolated home, selected read-only runtime files, and a run-scoped token for a local proxy;\nthe real gateway credential stays in the harness process. The candidate runs in Bubblewrap user, PID and network\nnamespaces, with nested user namespaces disabled. Legacy development tasks may still use `hidden: { dir, into, command }`;\nthose commands execute against the candidate workspace after the agent exits and are **not safe for qualification**, because\nvalidator code can inspect or modify files in that workspace. Qualification requires `hidden: { protocol: \"blackbox-v1\",\ncasesFile, runtime, argv, timeoutMs, totalTimeoutMs, maxOutputBytes }`. Its private JSON cases contain only `input` and\n`expected`; the host evaluator keeps expected values in its process and launches the candidate runtime separately for each\ninput using a fresh top-level Bubblewrap boundary. The candidate receives one input on stdin and returns one JSON value on\nstdout. Its workspace is read-only; private oracle files are not mounted. Candidate output and diagnostics are discarded,\nand result logs contain only case counts and failed indexes. Supported runtimes are explicitly allowlisted (`node`,\n`python3`); the only argument is a validated relative candidate entrypoint (no runtime flags, eval expressions, or extra\narguments), and per-case/aggregate time and output bounds are enforced. Oracle files must be outside the copied fixture.\nAbsolute paths, traversal, symlinks and unsupported fixture entries are rejected. `manifest.json` records the harness source-file hashes, model fingerprint, corpus/task\nhashes when qualification is configured, executable version, budgets, host and Node version. Each result records the\nexecutable version and effective step/minute budget; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`. The runner refuses an\nexisting output directory so a retry cannot append to or replace prior evidence.\n\nQualification runs require `nexusExecutable` to name the absolute path of the installed RC,\n`expectedAgentVersion` to pin its version, and `nexusPackageSha256` to record the expected release-asset digest from checksum verification. The runner checks `nexus --version` and refuses the checkout\n`cli/dist/index.js` or a version mismatch before starting an agent. Peer versions are read using each adapter's\n`--version` command inside the same Bubblewrap filesystem/network boundary, with a cleared environment and bounded\noutput/time; executable paths and SHA-256 hashes are archived alongside the RC package\ndigest. `score.mjs --pairs` takes exactly the Nexus,\nGoose and OpenCode result files and refuses mismatched model fingerprints, sampling declarations, context/output\nlimits, explicit per-task request and aggregate requested-output ceilings, run pairs, executable identities, or\neffective step/minute budgets. The proxy permits only model-catalog and inference routes, strips client-supplied\nauthorization and control-plane headers, and enforces configured request/body/output ceilings. These are requested\ncompletion-token ceilings, not exact usage accounting. It reports peer hidden-test results\nseparately; scores are never combined. The Nexus adapter passes the recorded temperature and step/minute limits;\nOpenCode receives a primary evaluation agent with the recorded step limit, temperature and seed; Goose receives the\nmatching `--max-turns`, context/output limits and temperature settings. Qualification mode currently requires\n`sampling.temperature` to be `0` across all three adapters; seed metadata remains recorded when configured.\n\n## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Scoring integrity\n\n- **Model proxy.** Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder (`eval/model_proxy.mjs`) that `run.mjs`\n  starts. Each record carries `model: { requests, answered, upstreamFailures, firstRequestAt, firstAnswerAt }`. Set\n  `\"proxy\": false` in a config to connect agents directly; such runs are then scored only by the legacy rule below.\n- **Infrastructure reruns** (`eval/infra.mjs`). A run is rerun only when the model never answered *and* the endpoint\n  was observed failing, or when the harness itself errored. The rule is the same for every agent. A run in which the\n  model answered is always scored: a crash is a failure (and counts towards the crash rate), not a rerun. Records from\n  before the proxy fall back to each agent's own connection-failure message, and the script says how many it judged\n  that way.\n- **Contamination.** Contaminated runs (the task directory changed, or its path appeared in the agent's output) are\n  left out of pooled pass rates and counted separately.\n- **Reruns are listed.** `score.mjs` lists every replaced run with what it showed and what the rerun showed.\n- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n\nWhat was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\n\n- runs;\n- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\n  hidden tests failed);\n- **recovered** (the hidden tests pass);\n- hung past budget.\n\nThe remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\nrunner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n  everything except class and difficulty.\n- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n  const checkDirs = [];\n  const home = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, \"nexus-eval-home-\"));\n  const budget = effectiveBudget(task, config);\n  const base = { task: task.id, tier: task.tier, ...(task.tier === \"T3\" ? { t3SteeringItems: task.steering.length } : {}), config: config.name, agent: config.agent ?? \"nexus\", agentVersion: agentIdentity.record, budget, run, harness: identity.string, model: config.model, startedAt: new Date().toISOString() };\n  try {\n    await prepareWorkspace(task, ws);\n    // Taken now, while .git is the harness's own: after the agent runs, nothing executes git against its workspace.\n    const baselineTree = gitRev(ws, \"HEAD^{tree}\");\n    const t3Baseline = task.tier === \"T3\" ? steeringBaseline(task, ws) : null;\n    // On the per-run task copy, so the steering hook in runAgent can read it. The commands run on a throwaway copy of\n    // the staged workspace, so the agent starts on exactly the staged tree.\n    const t3BaselineResources = [];\n    if (task.tier === \"T3\") {\n      const probe = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, `nexus-eval-t3-baseline-${task.id}-`));\n      try {\n        fs.cpSync(ws, probe, { recursive: true, verbatimSymlinks: true });\n        task.t3CommandBaseline = await commandBaseline(task, (command) => runIsolated(command, { cwd: probe, home: true, timeoutSec: 300, resources: config.resources ?? null, protectedCorpusPaths: protectedCorpusPathsForRun() }).then((r) => {\n          if (r.resources) t3BaselineResources.push(r.resources);\n          const error = r.containmentProblem ?? (r.timedOut ? \"timed out\" : r.overflow ? \"output limit\" : r.status === null ? \"did not exit\" : null);\n          return { pass: r.status === 0 && !error, error };\n        }));\n      } finally {\n        fs.rmSync(probe, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      }\n    }\n    const sourceBefore = treeDigest(task.dir);\n    // Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder, so whether the model was reachable is observed by the\n    // harness, the same way for every agent (eval/infra.mjs). `config.proxy: false` connects agents directly.\n    // T4: a task (or the config) may schedule faults for the proxy to inject; they are recorded with the run.\n    const faults = task.faults ?? config.faults ?? [];\n    if (faults.length && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"fault injection needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    // A standalone profile (DEC-16) shows agents a plain server; the proxy then holds the real key, agents get none.\n    if (config.serverProfile && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"serverProfile needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    const proxyDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-proxy-\"));\n    fs.chmodSync(proxyDir, 0o700);\n    const socketPath = path.join(proxyDir, \"proxy.sock\");\n    const localToken = REDACTED;\n    const proxy = await startModelProxy({\n      upstream: config.endpoint,\n      caFile,\n      faults,\n      profile: config.serverProfile,\n      authToken: apiKey ?? undefined,\n      clientToken: localToken,\n      socketPath,\n      maxRequests: config.limits?.requests ?? 1_000,\n      maxCompletionTokens: config.limits?.output,\n      maxTotalCompletionTokens: config.limits?.totalOutput,\n    });\n    const started = Date.now();\n    let agent;\n    let agentEndedAt;\n    try {\n      agent = await runAgent(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDir, localToken, proxy);\n      agentEndedAt = Date.now();\n      if (config.runAs) {\n        for (const dir of [ws, home]) await normalizeRunAsPermissions(config.runAs, dir, asUserSpec);\n      }\n    } finally {\n      await proxy?.close();\n      fs.rmSync(proxyDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n    const wallMs = agentEndedAt - started;\n    if (agent.containmentProblem) throw new Error(`candidate containment failed: ${agent.containmentProblem}`);\n    const model = proxy ? proxy.stats() : null;\n    const contaminated = treeDigest(task.dir) !== sourceBefore || `${agent.stdout}${agent.stderr}`.includes(tasksDir);\n    // T3 judges the workspace as it was when the objective's work ended (snapshot taken before the probe turn).\n    const t3 = agent.t3Driver ? scoreT3Run({ task, baseline: t3Baseline, driver: agent.t3Driver, preconditions: agent.t3Preconditions, compactions: countCompactions(home) }) : null;\n    // Legacy hidden tests share a process with candidate code. In qualification (or with hardenedChecks) they never\n    // run in the agent's workspace: each check gets a fresh staging of the baseline with only the agent's source\n    // changes (eval/hardened_check.mjs). Black-box oracles already keep expectations outside the candidate.\n    const hardened = (config.qualification === true || config.hardenedChecks === true) && task.hidden?.protocol !== \"blackbox-v1\";\n    let hardening = null;\n    let hiddenWs = ws;\n    let regressionWs = ws;\n    if (hardened) {\n      hiddenWs = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, `nexus-eval-check-${task.id}-`));\n      regressionWs = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, `nexus-eval-regression-${task.id}-`));\n      checkDirs.push(hiddenWs, regressionWs);\n      await prepareWorkspace(task, hiddenWs);\n      // Fixture tasks commit at staging time, so compare content (the tree), not the commit id.\n      if (gitRev(hiddenWs, \"HEAD^{tree}\") !== baselineTree) throw new Error(\"hardened check workspace staged a different baseline\");\n      hardening = { baseline: baselineTree, ...applyAgentChanges(ws, hiddenWs) };\n      cloneWorkspace(hiddenWs, regressionWs);\n    }\n    const refused = (check) => ({ pass: false, status: null, timedOut: false, overflow: false, output: `hardened check refused: ${hardening.configChanges.join(\"; \")}`, refused: true, resources: null, containmentProblem: null, check });\n    const hidden = hardening?.configChanges.length ? refused(\"hidden\") : await runCheck(task, hiddenWs, task.hidden, true, { readOnlyHidden: hardened });\n    const regression = task.regression ? (hardening?.configChanges.length ? refused(\"regression\") : await runCheck(task, regressionWs, task.regression, false)) : null;\n    for (const [phase, check] of [[\"hidden\", hidden], [\"regression\", regression]]) {\n      if (check?.containmentProblem) throw new Error(`${phase} check containment failed: ${check.containmentProblem}`);\n    }\n    const turn = agent.json?.turn ?? null;\n    // Nexus reports a structured outcome; for the other agents a clean exit within the budget is their completion claim.\n    const claimedComplete = turn\n      ? turn.execution === \"COMPLETED\" && [\"VERIFIED\", \"REGRESSION_FREE\", \"UNVERIFIED\", \"NOT_REQUIRED\"].includes(turn.outcome)\n      : agent.code === 0 && !agent.timedOut && !agent.outputExceeded;\n    return {\n      ...base,\n      wallMs,\n      exitCode: agent.code,\n      timedOut: agent.timedOut,\n      outputExceeded: agent.outputExceeded,\n      turn: turn && { execution: turn.execution, outcome: turn.outcome, reason: turn.reason ?? null, steps: turn.steps ?? null, contextNotRetained: turn.contextNotRetained ?? 0 },\n      claimedComplete,\n      claimedVerified: turn?.outcome === \"VERIFIED\",\n      hiddenPass: hidden.pass,\n      regressionPass: regression ? regression.pass : null,\n      falseVerified: turn?.outcome === \"VERIFIED\" && !hidden.pass,\n      contaminated,\n      tokens: agent.json?.tokenStats ?? null,\n      ...(hardening ? { hardened: { baseline: hardening.baseline, applied: hardening.applied.length, discarded: hardening.discarded, configChanges: hardening.configChanges } } : {}),\n      ...(t3 ? { t3 } : {}),\n      model,\n      ...(agent.t4FaultsInjected?.length ? { t4FaultsInjected: agent.t4FaultsInjected } : {}),\n      resources: config.resources ? { agent: agent.resources, hidden: hidden.resources ?? null, regression: regression?.resources ?? null, ...(t3BaselineResources.length ? { t3Baseline: t3BaselineResources } : {}) } : null,\n      logs: saveLogs(task, run, agent, hidden, regression),\n    };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { ...base, wallMs: 0, error: String(err?.message ?? err), hiddenPass: false, regressionPass: null, falseVerified: false, claimedComplete: false, claimedVerified: false };\n  } finally {\n    if (!args.keep) {\n      for (const dir of checkDirs) fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      fs.rmSync(ws, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nasync function prepareWorkspace(task, ws) {\n  if (task.fixture) {\n    const fixture = confinedPath(task.dir, task.fixture);\n    assertNoSymlinks(fixture);\n    fs.cpSync(fixture, ws, { recursive: true, verbatimSymlinks: true });\n    sh(\"git\", [\"init\", \"-q\"], ws);\n    sh(\"git\", [\"add\", \"-A\"], ws);\n    sh(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"user.name=eval\", \"-c\", \"user.email=eval@example.invalid\", \"commit\", \"-qm\", \"fixture\"], ws);\n        const roots = (config.sandboxRuntimeRoots ?? []).flatMap((root) => { try { return [fs.realpathSync(root)]; } catch { return []; } });\n        if (!roots.some((root) => packageDir === root || packageDir.startsWith(`${root}${path.sep}`))) throw new Error(`T3 runs the sidecar from ${packageDir}, which must be under sandboxRuntimeRoots`);\n        env.NEXUS_HOME = packageDir;\n      }\n      const sidecarArgs = [sidecar, \"--yes\", \"-w\", \"/workspace\", \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", config.model, \"-t\", String(sampling.temperature), \"-s\", \"30\", \"--max-total-steps\", String(budget.steps), \"--max-turn-minutes\", String(budget.minutes), ...contextArgs, ...(config.args ?? [])];\n      return checkout ? { cmd: process.execPath, argv: sidecarArgs, env, protocol: true } : { cmd: \"/usr/bin/env\", argv: [\"node\", ...sidecarArgs], env, protocol: true };\n    }\n    return { cmd: agentIdentity.command, argv: [...agentIdentity.argsPrefix, \"run\", \"--yes\", \"--json\", \"-w\", \"/workspace\", \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", config.model, \"-t\", String(sampling.temperature), \"-s\", \"30\", \"--max-total-steps\", String(budget.steps), \"--max-turn-minutes\", String(budget.minutes), ...contextArgs, ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"aider\") {\n    return { cmd: agentIdentity.command, argv: [\"--model\", `openai/${config.model}`, \"--openai-api-base\", ep, \"--yes-always\", \"--no-auto-commits\", \"--no-dirty-commits\", \"--no-gitignore\", \"--no-show-model-warnings\", \"--no-check-update\", \"--analytics-disable\", \"--no-pretty\", \"--no-fancy-input\", ...(config.args ?? []), \"--message\", task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"opencode\") {\n    const dir = path.join(home, \".config/opencode\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n    const modelOptions = { temperature: sampling.temperature, ...(sampling.seed !== undefined ? { seed: sampling.seed } : {}) };\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"opencode.json\"), JSON.stringify({\n      $schema: \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n      autoupdate: false,\n      share: \"disabled\",\n      permission: { edit: \"allow\", bash: \"allow\", webfetch: \"deny\" },\n      agent: { \"nexus-eval\": { mode: \"primary\", steps: budget.steps } },\n      provider: { gw: { npm: \"@ai-sdk/openai-compatible\", name: \"gateway\", options: { baseURL: ep, apiKey: \"{env:GW_KEY}\" }, models: { [config.model]: { name: config.model, limit: limits, options: modelOptions } } } },\n      model: `gw/${config.model}`,\n    }, null, 2));\n    // Provider packages are cached across runs (not per run): the cache holds code, not state.\n    env.XDG_CACHE_HOME = path.join(home, \".cache\");\n    return { cmd: agentIdentity.command, argv: [\"run\", \"--agent\", \"nexus-eval\", \"--model\", `gw/${config.model}`, ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\n  }\n  if (agent === \"goose\") {\n    const u = new URL(ep);\n    Object.assign(env, { GOOSE_PROVIDER: \"openai\", GOOSE_MODEL: config.model, OPENAI_HOST: u.origin, OPENAI_BASE_PATH: `${u.pathname.replace(/^\\/|\\/$/g, \"\")}/chat/completions`, GOOSE_MODE: \"auto\", GOOSE_DISABLE_KEYRING: \"1\", GOOSE_CONTEXT_LIMIT: String(limits.context), GOOSE_MAX_TOKENS: String(limits.output), GOOSE_MAX_TURNS: String(budget.steps), GOOSE_TEMPERATURE: String(sampling.temperature) });\n    return { cmd: agentIdentity.command, argv: [\"run\", \"--no-session\", \"--with-builtin\", \"developer\", \"--max-turns\", String(budget.steps), ...(config.args ?? []), \"-t\", task.objective], env };\n  }\n  throw new Error(`agent ${agent} has no adapter`);\n}\n\nasync function runAgent(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken, proxy) {\n  if (task.t4RunnerFault !== \"sigterm_resume\") {\n    return runAgentAttempt(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken);\n  }\n  if (task.tier !== \"T4\" || (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") !== \"nexus\" || config.qualification !== true || !config.resources) {\n    throw new Error(\"sigterm_resume requires an installed Nexus qualification run with the kernel resource contract\");\n  }\n  const interrupted = await runAgentAttempt(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken, { signalAfterAnswer: true, proxy });\n  const signal = interrupted.t4Signal;\n  if (!signal?.delivered) return { ...interrupted, t4FaultsInjected: [] };\n  const resumed = await runAgentAttempt(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken, { resume: true });\n  const evidence = {\n    signal: \"SIGTERM\",\n    delivered: signal.delivered,\n    deliveredProcesses: signal.deliveredProcesses,\n    forced: signal.forced,\n    firstExitCode: signal.firstExitCode,\n    payloadExitSignal: signal.payloadExitSignal,\n    supervisorWrapperExitSignal: signal.supervisorWrapperExitSignal,\n    signalDuringActiveTurn: signal.signalDuringActiveTurn,\n    resumed: resumed.code === 0 && resumed.json?.turn?.execution === \"COMPLETED\",\n    resumeExitCode: resumed.code,\n    resumeTurnExecution: resumed.json?.turn?.execution ?? null,\n  };\n  return {\n    ...resumed,\n    stdout: `${interrupted.stdout}\\n--- T4 SIGTERM interruption ---\\n${resumed.stdout}`,\n    stderr: `${interrupted.stderr}\\n--- T4 resume attempt ---\\n${resumed.stderr}`,\n    t4FaultsInjected: [{ kind: \"sigterm_resume\", source: \"task_fixture_or_runner\", evidence }],\n  };\n}\n\nfunction runAgentAttempt(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken, { signalAfterAnswer = false, proxy = null, resume = false } = {}) {\n  const { cmd, argv, env, protocol } = agentCommand(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, localToken);\n  if (resume) {\n    if ((config.agent ?? \"nexus\") !== \"nexus\" || protocol) throw new Error(\"T4 resume is supported only by Nexus run mode\");\n    const promptIndex = argv.lastIndexOf(task.objective);\n    if (promptIndex < 0) throw new Error(\"could not remove original prompt before Nexus resume\");\n    argv.splice(promptIndex, 1);\n    argv.push(\"--resume\");\n  }\n  if (config.qualification === true && !config.runAs) throw new Error(\"qualification candidate execution requires the dedicated evaluator account\");\n  if (config.runAs) grantRunAsAccess(config.runAs, [ws, home, proxyDirectory]);\n  const runtimePaths = [fs.realpathSync(cmd), ...agentIdentity.argsPrefix.filter((item) => path.isAbsolute(item)), ...(config.sandboxRuntimePaths ?? [])];\n  if ((config.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\" && agentIdentity.argsPrefix[0] === path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist/index.js\")) {\n    runtimePaths.push(path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist\"));\n    const modules = path.join(ROOT, \"cli/node_modules\");\n    for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(modules, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n      if (entry.isDirectory() && entry.name !== \".bin\") runtimePaths.push(path.join(modules, entry.name));\n    }\n    const coreBinary = path.join(ROOT, \"core/target/release/harness-core\");\n    if (fs.existsSync(coreBinary)) runtimePaths.push(coreBinary);\n  }\n  const sandboxRuntimePaths = [...new Set(runtimePaths)];\n  const allowedRuntimeRoots = [...new Set([...(config.sandboxRuntimeRoots ?? []), ...((config.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\" && agentIdentity.argsPrefix[0] === path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist/index.js\") ? [path.join(ROOT, \"cli\"), path.join(ROOT, \"core\")] : [])])];\n  const supervisorPath = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/agent_sandbox.mjs\");\n  const corpusPaths = custodyCorpusPathsForRun();\n  const protectedCorpusPaths = protectedCorpusPathsForRun();\n  const corpusOverlap = runtimeCorpusOverlapProblem(sandboxRuntimePaths, allowedRuntimeRoots, tasksDir, corpusPaths, {\n    regressions: rs.filter((r) => r.regressionPass === false).length,\n    // Cost of the whole configuration's runs per correct result (failed runs cost too).\n    tokensPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.tokens?.total)) / k : null,\n    wallSecondsPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.wallMs)) / 1000 / k : null,\n  };\n});\n\n// T4: emit all nine preregistered classes, including empty rows. Proxy, task-fixture, and\n// runner-injected events share one scoring path so a proxy-only result cannot look complete.\nconst t4Events = (r) => [\n  ...(r.model?.faultsInjected ?? []).map((f) => ({ ...f, source: f.source ?? \"model_proxy\" })),\n  ...(r.t4FaultsInjected ?? []),\n];\nconst expectedSource = (kind) => T4_PROXY_CLASSES.has(kind) ? \"model_proxy\" : T4_RUNNER_CLASSES.has(kind) ? \"task_fixture_or_runner\" : null;\nconst runnerEvidenceValid = (event) => {\n  const evidence = event.evidence;\n  if (!evidence || typeof evidence !== \"object\") return false;\n  if (event.kind === \"sigterm_resume\") {\n    return evidence.signal === \"SIGTERM\"\n      && evidence.delivered === true\n      && Number.isInteger(evidence.deliveredProcesses)\n      && evidence.deliveredProcesses > 0\n      && evidence.signalDuringActiveTurn === true\n      && evidence.payloadExitSignal === \"SIGTERM\"\n      && evidence.resumed === true\n      && evidence.resumeExitCode === 0\n      && evidence.resumeTurnExecution === \"COMPLETED\";\n  }\n  if (event.kind === \"hanging_test_command\") return evidence.observedHung === true && evidence.timedOut === true && evidence.containmentCleaned === true;\n  if (event.kind === \"full_disk\") return evidence.writeFailedWithEnospc === true && Number.isSafeInteger(evidence.storageLimitBytes) && evidence.storageLimitBytes > 0;\n  return false;\n};\nconst t4Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T4\");\nconst invalidT4Events = t4Runs.flatMap((r) => t4Events(r)\n  .filter((f) => !expectedSource(f.kind) || f.source !== expectedSource(f.kind) || (T4_RUNNER_CLASSES.has(f.kind) && !runnerEvidenceValid(f)))\n  .map((f) => ({ task: r.task, run: r.run, kind: f.kind ?? null, source: f.source ?? null })));\nconst faultRows = T4_FAULT_CLASSES.map((kind) => {\n  const injected = records.filter((r) => t4Events(r).some((f) => f.kind === kind && f.source === expectedSource(kind)));\n  const rs = t4Runs.filter((r) => t4Events(r).some((f) => f.kind === kind && f.source === expectedSource(kind)));\n  const truthful = injected.filter((r) => !r.error && !r.falseVerified && !crashed(r) && !r.timedOut && !r.outputExceeded).length;\n  const qualificationTruthful = rs.filter((r) => !r.error && !r.falseVerified && !crashed(r) && !r.timedOut && !r.outputExceeded).length;\n  const recovered = injected.filter((r) => r.hiddenPass).length;\n  const hungPastBudget = injected.filter((r) => r.timedOut).length;\n  return {\n    kind,\n    n: injected.length,\n    qualificationRuns: rs.length,\n    qualificationTruthful,\n    truthful,\n    truthfulRate: injected.length ? truthful / injected.length : null,\n    recovered,\n    hungPastBudget,\n    gate: rs.length >= T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS && qualificationTruthful === rs.length && rs.every((r) => !r.timedOut) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\",\n  };\n});\nconst t4 = {\n  requiredClasses: T4_FAULT_CLASSES.length,\n  requiredRunsPerClass: T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS,\n  observedClasses: faultRows.filter((r) => r.qualificationRuns > 0).length,\n  totalRuns: faultRows.reduce((n, r) => n + r.qualificationRuns, 0),\n  invalidEvents: invalidT4Events.length,\n  gate: invalidT4Events.length === 0 && faultRows.every((r) => r.gate === \"PASS\") ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\",\n};\n\n// T3 (REQ-QUAL-109): every T3 run counts. A run with no T3 result, too few steps or fewer than two compactions is\n// ineligible and fails the workload rather than leaving it; DEC-05 thresholds are false-absence 0, steering >= 95%.\nconst T3_TASKS = 8;\nconst T3_RUNS_PER_TASK = 5;\nconst t3Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T3\");\nconst t3 = t3Runs.length ? (() => {\n  const honoured = t3Runs.flatMap((r) => r.t3?.steering ?? []).filter((s) => s.honoured).length;\n# PLAN-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\nImplements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harness fixes are milestone **M3**. Task authoring runs in parallel from M1. Runs are **M5**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-110.\n- Decisions: DEC-05, DEC-06, DEC-07.\n- Owner actions: X2, X3, X4, X5.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\n- new `eval/fingerprint.mjs`\n- new `eval/faults/`\n- `eval/tasks/`\n- `eval/configs/`\n- `eval/README.md`\n- `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`\n- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Location | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Symmetric infrastructure classification. A run counts as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** there is an unreachable signature. Same rule for every agent. Crash and timeout rates are reported. | `infra.mjs:31`; `run.mjs` (record `first_model_request_at` from the proxy log) | — |\n| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\n| 3 | Hidden-test isolation. Hidden tests are stored under a separate uid (`nexus-eval`, created by the operator, owner action under X3) with mode 0700, and copied in after the agent exits. The agent runs with an allow-listed env. | `run.mjs:57-59,114,178` | — |\n| 4 | Fingerprint. Record server kind, build, weights sha256 (from config), and sampling settings. Refuse the run if the fingerprint is missing. Temperature 0 or a fixed seed for every agent where the agent supports it. | new `fingerprint.mjs`; `configs/*.json` | PLAN-05 task 1 |\n| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\n| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\n| 7 | Task schema `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`, with a validator. | `eval/tasks/schema.json`; `run.mjs` | — |\n| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n- **PR-10b:** tasks 3, 4, 7.\n- **PR-10c:** tasks 5, 6.\n- **PR-10d:** tasks 9, 10.\n- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\n\nTask 8 is data work. Tasks 11 and 12 are operations work.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `eval_harness.test.ts`:\n  - infra symmetry: a Nexus crash is counted as a failure, not rerun;\n  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\n  - fingerprint refusal;\n  - T4 smoke.\n\n## Effort and uncertainty\n\n| Work | Estimate | Main uncertainty |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harness fixes | 4–6 engineer-days | — |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27150}},"started_at_ms":1792916749003,"completed_at_ms":1792916749003}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:25:50.345Z","ordinal":331950,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1722a-8009-7662-8e89-a052f3c424fd","call_id":"call_5aef1041ff3e45daa9f5864882ba8451","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8385)\nTotal output lines: 483\n\n# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\n\n`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\nseparately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\n\n`docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` is a historical checkpoint at source revision `6151a23`; use this file and the current\nrunner source for evaluator behavior added after that revision. Neither document represents completed M5 qualification.\n\n```bash\nnode eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\nnode eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\nnode eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$NEXUS_RESULTS\" \"$GOOSE_RESULTS\" \"$OPENCODE_RESULTS\"\n```\n\nEach run uses a frozen copy of the task tree, a fresh workspace and `HOME`, and a unique output directory. The agent\nreceives only its workspace, isolated home, selected read-only runtime files, and a run-scoped token for a local proxy;\nthe real gateway credential stays in the harness process. The candidate runs in Bubblewrap user, PID and network\nnamespaces, with nested user namespaces disabled. Legacy development tasks may still use `hidden: { dir, into, command }`;\nthose commands execute against the candidate workspace after the agent exits and are **not safe for qualification**, because\nvalidator code can inspect or modify files in that workspace. Qualification requires `hidden: { protocol: \"blackbox-v1\",\ncasesFile, runtime, argv, timeoutMs, totalTimeoutMs, maxOutputBytes }`. Its private JSON cases contain only `input` and\n`expected`; the host evaluator keeps expected values in its process and launches the candidate runtime separately for each\ninput using a fresh top-level Bubblewrap boundary. The candidate receives one input on stdin and returns one JSON value on\nstdout. Its workspace is read-only; private oracle files are not mounted. Candidate output and diagnostics are discarded,\nand result logs contain only case counts and failed indexes. Supported runtimes are explicitly allowlisted (`node`,\n`python3`); the only argument is a validated relative candidate entrypoint (no runtime flags, eval expressions, or extra\narguments), and per-case/aggregate time and output bounds are enforced. Oracle files must be outside the copied fixture.\nAbsolute paths, traversal, symlinks and unsupported fixture entries are rejected. `manifest.json` records the harness source-file hashes, model fingerprint, corpus/task\nhashes when qualification is configured, executable version, budgets, host and Node version. Each result records the\nexecutable version and effective step/minute budget; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`. The runner refuses an\nexisting output directory so a retry cannot append to or replace prior evidence.\n\nQualification runs require `nexusExecutable` to name the absolute path of the installed RC,\n`expectedAgentVersion` to pin its version, and `nexusPackageSha256` to record the expected release-asset digest from checksum verification. The runner checks `nexus --version` and refuses the checkout\n`cli/dist/index.js` or a version mismatch before starting an agent. Peer versions are read using each adapter's\n`--version` command inside the same Bubblewrap filesystem/network boundary, with a cleared environment and bounded\noutput/time; executable paths and SHA-256 hashes are archived alongside the RC package\ndigest. `score.mjs --pairs` takes exactly the Nexus,\nGoose and OpenCode result files and refuses mismatched model fingerprints, sampling declarations, context/output\nlimits, explicit per-task request and aggregate requested-output ceilings, run pairs, executable identities, or\neffective step/minute budgets. The proxy permits only model-catalog and inference routes, strips client-supplied\nauthorization and control-plane headers, and enforces configured request/body/output ceilings. These are requested\ncompletion-token ceilings, not exact usage accounting. It reports peer hidden-test results\nseparately; scores are never combined. The Nexus adapter passes the recorded temperature and step/minute limits;\nOpenCode receives a primary evaluation agent with the recorded step limit, temperature and seed; Goose receives the\nmatching `--max-turns`, context/output limits and temperature settings. Qualification mode currently requires\n`sampling.temperature` to be `0` across all three adapters; seed metadata remains recorded when configured.\n\n## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Scoring integrity\n\n- **Model proxy.** Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder (`eval/model_proxy.mjs`) that `run.mjs`\n  starts. Each record carries `model: { requests, answered, upstreamFailures, firstRequestAt, firstAnswerAt }`. Set\n  `\"proxy\": false` in a config to connect agents directly; such runs are then scored only by the legacy rule below.\n- **Infrastructure reruns** (`eval/infra.mjs`). A run is rerun only when the model never answered *and* the endpoint\n  was observed failing, or when the harness itself errored. The rule is the same for every agent. A run in which the\n  model answered is always scored: a crash is a failure (and counts towards the crash rate), not a rerun. Records from\n  before the proxy fall back to each agent's own connection-failure message, and the script says how many it judged\n  that way.\n- **Contamination.** Contaminated runs (the task directory changed, or its path appeared in the agent's output) are\n  left out of pooled pass rates and counted separately.\n- **Reruns are listed.** `score.mjs` lists every replaced run with what it showed and what the rerun showed.\n- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n\nWhat was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\n\n- runs;\n- **truthful** (the run ended with its own result, did not hang past its budget, and never claimed VERIFIED while the\n  hidden tests failed);\n- **recovered** (the hidden tests pass);\n- hung past budget.\n\nThe remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\nrunner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n\n## Qualification runs\n\nA config with `\"qualification\": true` is the v1.0.0 evidence run (docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md §6). `run.mjs` refuses to start\none, before any agent runs, unless every item below holds:\n\n- **Tasks are well formed** (`eval/validate.mjs`): one source (fixture, or a repo pinned to a full commit id), an isolated\n  `blackbox-v1` hidden oracle, and `class` (bugfix · feature · refactor · debug) and `difficulty` (easy · medium · hard). Development runs check\n  everything except class and difficulty.\n- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n  const checkDirs = [];\n  const home = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, \"nexus-eval-home-\"));\n  const budget = effectiveBudget(task, config);\n  const base = { task: task.id, tier: task.tier, ...(task.tier === \"T3\" ? { t3SteeringItems: task.steering.length } : {}), config: config.name, agent: config.agent ?? \"nexus\", agentVersion: agentIdentity.record, budget, run, harness: identity.string, model: config.model, startedAt: new Date().toISOString() };\n  try {\n    await prepareWorkspace(task, ws);\n    // Taken now, while .git is the harness's own: after the agent runs, nothing executes git against its workspace.\n    const baselineTree = gitRev(ws, \"HEAD^{tree}\");\n    const t3Baseline = task.tier === \"T3\" ? steeringBaseline(task, ws) : null;\n    // On the per-run task copy, so the steering hook in runAgent can read it. The commands run on a throwaway copy of\n    // the staged workspace, so the agent starts on exactly the staged tree.\n    const t3BaselineResources = [];\n    if (task.tier === \"T3\") {\n      const probe = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(scratch, `nexus-eval-t3-baseline-${task.id}-`));\n      try {\n        fs.cpSync(ws, probe, { recursive: true, verbatimSymlinks: true });\n        task.t3CommandBaseline = await commandBaseline(task, (command) => runIsolated(command, { cwd: probe, home: true, timeoutSec: 300, resources: config.resources ?? null, protectedCorpusPaths: protectedCorpusPathsForRun() }).then((r) => {\n          if (r.resources) t3BaselineResources.push(r.resources);\n          const error = r.containmentProblem ?? (r.timedOut ? \"timed out\" : r.overflow ? \"output limit\" : r.status === null ? \"did not exit\" : null);\n          return { pass: r.status === 0 && !error, error };\n        }));\n      } finally {\n        fs.rmSync(probe, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      }\n    }\n    const sourceBefore = treeDigest(task.dir);\n    // Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder, so whether the model was reachable is observed by the\n    // harness, the same way for every agent (eval/infra.mjs). `config.proxy: false` connects agents directly.\n    // T4: a task (or the config) may schedule faults for the proxy to inject; they are recorded with the run.\n    const faults = task.faults ?? config.faults ?? [];\n    if (faults.length && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"fault injection needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    // A standalone profile (DEC-16) shows agents a plain server; the proxy then holds the real key, agents get none.\n    if (config.serverProfile && config.proxy === false) throw new Error(\"serverProfile needs the model proxy (proxy: false is set)\");\n    const proxyDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-proxy-\"));\n    fs.chmodSync(proxyDir, 0o700);\n    const socketPath = path.join(proxyDir, \"proxy.sock\");\n    const localToken = REDACTED;\n    const proxy = await startModelProxy({\n      upstream: config.endpoint,\n      caFile,\n      faults,\n      profile: config.serverProfile,\n      authToken: apiKey ?? undefined,\n      clientToken: localToken,\n      socketPath,\n      maxReques…2385 tokens truncated…ume requires an installed Nexus qualification run with the kernel resource contract\");\n  }\n  const interrupted = await runAgentAttempt(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken, { signalAfterAnswer: true, proxy });\n  const signal = interrupted.t4Signal;\n  if (!signal?.delivered) return { ...interrupted, t4FaultsInjected: [] };\n  const resumed = await runAgentAttempt(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken, { resume: true });\n  const evidence = {\n    signal: \"SIGTERM\",\n    delivered: signal.delivered,\n    deliveredProcesses: signal.deliveredProcesses,\n    forced: signal.forced,\n    firstExitCode: signal.firstExitCode,\n    payloadExitSignal: signal.payloadExitSignal,\n    supervisorWrapperExitSignal: signal.supervisorWrapperExitSignal,\n    signalDuringActiveTurn: signal.signalDuringActiveTurn,\n    resumed: resumed.code === 0 && resumed.json?.turn?.execution === \"COMPLETED\",\n    resumeExitCode: resumed.code,\n    resumeTurnExecution: resumed.json?.turn?.execution ?? null,\n  };\n  return {\n    ...resumed,\n    stdout: `${interrupted.stdout}\\n--- T4 SIGTERM interruption ---\\n${resumed.stdout}`,\n    stderr: `${interrupted.stderr}\\n--- T4 resume attempt ---\\n${resumed.stderr}`,\n    t4FaultsInjected: [{ kind: \"sigterm_resume\", source: \"task_fixture_or_runner\", evidence }],\n  };\n}\n\nfunction runAgentAttempt(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, proxyDirectory, localToken, { signalAfterAnswer = false, proxy = null, resume = false } = {}) {\n  const { cmd, argv, env, protocol } = agentCommand(task, ws, home, budget, agentIdentity, localToken);\n  if (resume) {\n    if ((config.agent ?? \"nexus\") !== \"nexus\" || protocol) throw new Error(\"T4 resume is supported only by Nexus run mode\");\n    const promptIndex = argv.lastIndexOf(task.objective);\n    if (promptIndex < 0) throw new Error(\"could not remove original prompt before Nexus resume\");\n    argv.splice(promptIndex, 1);\n    argv.push(\"--resume\");\n  }\n  if (config.qualification === true && !config.runAs) throw new Error(\"qualification candidate execution requires the dedicated evaluator account\");\n  if (config.runAs) grantRunAsAccess(config.runAs, [ws, home, proxyDirectory]);\n  const runtimePaths = [fs.realpathSync(cmd), ...agentIdentity.argsPrefix.filter((item) => path.isAbsolute(item)), ...(config.sandboxRuntimePaths ?? [])];\n  if ((config.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\" && agentIdentity.argsPrefix[0] === path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist/index.js\")) {\n    runtimePaths.push(path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist\"));\n    const modules = path.join(ROOT, \"cli/node_modules\");\n    for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(modules, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n      if (entry.isDirectory() && entry.name !== \".bin\") runtimePaths.push(path.join(modules, entry.name));\n    }\n    const coreBinary = path.join(ROOT, \"core/target/release/harness-core\");\n    if (fs.existsSync(coreBinary)) runtimePaths.push(coreBinary);\n  }\n  const sandboxRuntimePaths = [...new Set(runtimePaths)];\n  const allowedRuntimeRoots = [...new Set([...(config.sandboxRuntimeRoots ?? []), ...((config.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\" && agentIdentity.argsPrefix[0] === path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist/index.js\") ? [path.join(ROOT, \"cli\"), path.join(ROOT, \"core\")] : [])])];\n  const supervisorPath = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/agent_sandbox.mjs\");\n  const corpusPaths = custodyCorpusPathsForRun();\n  const protectedCorpusPaths = protectedCorpusPathsForRun();\n  const corpusOverlap = runtimeCorpusOverlapProblem(sandboxRuntimePaths, allowedRuntimeRoots, tasksDir, corpusPaths, {\n    regressions: rs.filter((r) => r.regressionPass === false).length,\n    // Cost of the whole configuration's runs per correct result (failed runs cost too).\n    tokensPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.tokens?.total)) / k : null,\n    wallSecondsPerCorrect: k ? sum(rs.map((r) => r.wallMs)) / 1000 / k : null,\n  };\n});\n\n// T4: emit all nine preregistered classes, including empty rows. Proxy, task-fixture, and\n// runner-injected events share one scoring path so a proxy-only result cannot look complete.\nconst t4Events = (r) => [\n  ...(r.model?.faultsInjected ?? []).map((f) => ({ ...f, source: f.source ?? \"model_proxy\" })),\n  ...(r.t4FaultsInjected ?? []),\n];\nconst expectedSource = (kind) => T4_PROXY_CLASSES.has(kind) ? \"model_proxy\" : T4_RUNNER_CLASSES.has(kind) ? \"task_fixture_or_runner\" : null;\nconst runnerEvidenceValid = (event) => {\n  const evidence = event.evidence;\n  if (!evidence || typeof evidence !== \"object\") return false;\n  if (event.kind === \"sigterm_resume\") {\n    return evidence.signal === \"SIGTERM\"\n      && evidence.delivered === true\n      && Number.isInteger(evidence.deliveredProcesses)\n      && evidence.deliveredProcesses > 0\n      && evidence.signalDuringActiveTurn === true\n      && evidence.payloadExitSignal === \"SIGTERM\"\n      && evidence.resumed === true\n      && evidence.resumeExitCode === 0\n      && evidence.resumeTurnExecution === \"COMPLETED\";\n  }\n  if (event.kind === \"hanging_test_command\") return evidence.observedHung === true && evidence.timedOut === true && evidence.containmentCleaned === true;\n  if (event.kind === \"full_disk\") return evidence.writeFailedWithEnospc === true && Number.isSafeInteger(evidence.storageLimitBytes) && evidence.storageLimitBytes > 0;\n  return false;\n};\nconst t4Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T4\");\nconst invalidT4Events = t4Runs.flatMap((r) => t4Events(r)\n  .filter((f) => !expectedSource(f.kind) || f.source !== expectedSource(f.kind) || (T4_RUNNER_CLASSES.has(f.kind) && !runnerEvidenceValid(f)))\n  .map((f) => ({ task: r.task, run: r.run, kind: f.kind ?? null, source: f.source ?? null })));\nconst faultRows = T4_FAULT_CLASSES.map((kind) => {\n  const injected = records.filter((r) => t4Events(r).some((f) => f.kind === kind && f.source === expectedSource(kind)));\n  const rs = t4Runs.filter((r) => t4Events(r).some((f) => f.kind === kind && f.source === expectedSource(kind)));\n  const truthful = injected.filter((r) => !r.error && !r.falseVerified && !crashed(r) && !r.timedOut && !r.outputExceeded).length;\n  const qualificationTruthful = rs.filter((r) => !r.error && !r.falseVerified && !crashed(r) && !r.timedOut && !r.outputExceeded).length;\n  const recovered = injected.filter((r) => r.hiddenPass).length;\n  const hungPastBudget = injected.filter((r) => r.timedOut).length;\n  return {\n    kind,\n    n: injected.length,\n    qualificationRuns: rs.length,\n    qualificationTruthful,\n    truthful,\n    truthfulRate: injected.length ? truthful / injected.length : null,\n    recovered,\n    hungPastBudget,\n    gate: rs.length >= T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS && qualificationTruthful === rs.length && rs.every((r) => !r.timedOut) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\",\n  };\n});\nconst t4 = {\n  requiredClasses: T4_FAULT_CLASSES.length,\n  requiredRunsPerClass: T4_RUNS_PER_CLASS,\n  observedClasses: faultRows.filter((r) => r.qualificationRuns > 0).length,\n  totalRuns: faultRows.reduce((n, r) => n + r.qualificationRuns, 0),\n  invalidEvents: invalidT4Events.length,\n  gate: invalidT4Events.length === 0 && faultRows.every((r) => r.gate === \"PASS\") ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\",\n};\n\n// T3 (REQ-QUAL-109): every T3 run counts. A run with no T3 result, too few steps or fewer than two compactions is\n// ineligible and fails the workload rather than leaving it; DEC-05 thresholds are false-absence 0, steering >= 95%.\nconst T3_TASKS = 8;\nconst T3_RUNS_PER_TASK = 5;\nconst t3Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T3\");\nconst t3 = t3Runs.length ? (() => {\n  const honoured = t3Runs.flatMap((r) => r.t3?.steering ?? []).filter((s) => s.honoured).length;\n# PLAN-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\nImplements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harness fixes are milestone **M3**. Task authoring runs in parallel from M1. Runs are **M5**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-110.\n- Decisions: DEC-05, DEC-06, DEC-07.\n- Owner actions: X2, X3, X4, X5.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\n- new `eval/fingerprint.mjs`\n- new `eval/faults/`\n- `eval/tasks/`\n- `eval/configs/`\n- `eval/README.md`\n- `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`\n- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Location | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Symmetric infrastructure classification. A run counts as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** there is an unreachable signature. Same rule for every agent. Crash and timeout rates are reported. | `infra.mjs:31`; `run.mjs` (record `first_model_request_at` from the proxy log) | — |\n| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\n| 3 | Hidden-test isolation. Hidden tests are stored under a separate uid (`nexus-eval`, created by the operator, owner action under X3) with mode 0700, and copied in after the agent exits. The agent runs with an allow-listed env. | `run.mjs:57-59,114,178` | — |\n| 4 | Fingerprint. Record server kind, build, weights sha256 (from config), and sampling settings. Refuse the run if the fingerprint is missing. Temperature 0 or a fixed seed for every agent where the agent supports it. | new `fingerprint.mjs`; `configs/*.json` | PLAN-05 task 1 |\n| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\n| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\n| 7 | Task schema `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`, with a validator. | `eval/tasks/schema.json`; `run.mjs` | — |\n| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n- **PR-10b:** tasks 3, 4, 7.\n- **PR-10c:** tasks 5, 6.\n- **PR-10d:** tasks 9, 10.\n- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\n\nTask 8 is data work. Tasks 11 and 12 are operations work.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `eval_harness.test.ts`:\n  - infra symmetry: a Nexus crash is counted as a failure, not rerun;\n  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\n  - fingerprint refusal;\n  - T4 smoke.\n\n## Effort and uncertainty\n\n| Work | Estimate | Main uncertainty |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harness fixes | 4–6 engineer-days | — |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792916750.345063}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
