{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:28:45.044Z","ordinal":332135,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016addbdba28a881a089166962a40991a4","status":"completed","call_id":"call_b7ca97467c6e4fb2bb2da516101c55d0","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/t4_fixtures.mjs\\n@@\\n   if (fixture.kind === \\\"full_disk\\\" && fixture.tool !== \\\"run_command\\\") {\\n     problems.push(\\\"full_disk requires tool run_command\\\");\\n   }\\n+  if (fixture.kind === \\\"full_disk\\\" && (!Number.isSafeInteger(fixture.storageLimitBytes) || fixture.storageLimitBytes < 1)) {\\n+    problems.push(\\\"full_disk requires a positive storageLimitBytes matching the qualification resource contract\\\");\\n+  }\\n@@\\n-      const observedHung = /(?:timed?s*out|timeout|deadline exceeded)/i.test(output)\\n-        && (!Number.isSafeInteger(timeout) || timeout === fixture.timeoutSecs);\\n+      const observedHung = /(?:timed\\\\s*out|timeout|deadline exceeded)/i.test(output)\\n+        && timeout === fixture.timeoutSecs;\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r=await tools.apply_patch(patch);\ntext(r);\nconst patch2 = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/README.md\\n@@\\n-The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\\n-runner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\\n+The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\\n+runner case. A fixture task declares `t4Fixture: { kind, tool: \\\"run_command\\\", command, timeoutSecs }` for a hanging\\n+test, or `t4Fixture: { kind: \\\"full_disk\\\", tool: \\\"run_command\\\", command, storageLimitBytes }` for a full disk. The\\n+runner counts a fixture only when the candidate's structured transcript contains that exact command, the tool result\\n+shows the timeout or ENOSPC condition, and the task process cgroup reports successful cleanup with no survivors. The\\n+full-disk limit must match the frozen resource contract. Task metadata identifies the expected fixture; it cannot\\n+provide evidence or a pass bit. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r2=await tools.apply_patch(patch2);\ntext(r2);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792916922.1605105}}}
