{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:30:28.596Z","ordinal":332248,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1722e-bef3-7442-a91e-3e06f0d46b18","author":"/root/t4_runner_independent_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/t4_runner_independent_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — read-only review; `git diff --check` passes. I did not run tests or access gateway/held-out data.\n\n1. **The runtime does not expose the transcript this evidence collector requires.** `observeT4Fixture` returns no evidence unless `agent.json.messages` exists ([`eval/t4_fixtures.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/t4_fixtures.mjs:36)). But Nexus’s `TaskExecutionResult` has no `messages` field; it exposes `output`, `logs`, and a turn result ([`cli/src/core/app.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/src/core/app.ts:41), [construction](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/cli/src/core/app.ts:296)). The tests supply synthetic `json.messages`, so they do not establish that actual qualification runs can produce hanging-test or full-disk evidence. As written, those classes will not be recorded from the real Nexus runner.\n\n2. **The observed output can claim a fault without causing one.** The collector treats text matching `timeout` or `ENOSPC` as proof ([`eval/t4_fixtures.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/t4_fixtures.mjs:52)). A declared command such as `printf 'timeout\\n'` with the expected timeout argument, or one that prints `ENOSPC`, satisfies those checks without hanging or exhausting workspace storage. Task validation accepts arbitrary nonempty commands ([`eval/t4_fixtures.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/t4_fixtures.mjs:14)); the scorer then accepts the resulting booleans and a positive storage limit ([`eval/score.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4/eval/score.mjs:148)). Require runner-observed timeout/ENOSPC receipts tied to the exact call and enforced workspace boundary, rather than matching output text alone.\n\nNo private data is added to the new evidence fields; they contain a command hash and bounded status metadata."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792917028.5957139}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16608}}
