ll implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:11:- DOC: documentation claim\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:62:| `evidence/F_requirements_history.md` | Requirement provenance | 19 claim spot-checks against HEAD; `gh issue list` (0 issues) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:206:| HIST-03 | S2 | RR | Docs, plugins | `USER_MANUAL.md:294` | SRC | False sandbox claim | REQ-SEC-117 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:221:| PRV-17 | S4 | RR | Docs | `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `USER_MANUAL.md:3` | DOC vs SRC | Overstated claims | REQ-DX-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:230:| VER-04 | S2 | B | VERIFIED claims | `tester.ts:356-360` | RT (probe) | False VERIFIED by basename coincidence | REQ-AGT-114 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:304:| HIST-06 | S3 | RR | Docs | USER_MANUAL, ARCHITECTURE, quickstart | SRC/DOC | Wrong commands; parity claim | REQ-DX-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:308:| EVL-001 | S1 | B | v1 quality claim | `eval/` | DOC + SRC | No qualifying evidence | REQ-QUAL-101..105 (SPEC-10) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:363:- **Self-critical history.** The project's own reviews repeatedly refused to over-claim: Issue #12 left open, the eval pilot self-graded NOT QUALIFIED. Evidence: F §5.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:39:| DOC | documentation claim |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:139:| REQ-SEC-117 | Audit | No false plugin-sandbox claim. `executeSandboxed` is removed. | honesty | `plugins.ts:254-300`; `USER_MANUAL.md:294` | TEST (SEC-09, HIST-03; test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"PluginManager executes custom plugins in-process without false sandbox (REQ-SEC-117)\") | tested | ACC-GOV-04 | RR | SEC-09, HIST-03 | SPEC-03 / PLAN-03 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:227:| REQ-DX-105 | Audit | User docs make no claim contradicted by source, contain no homelab IDs, and make no parity claims. | honesty | docs | ACC-GOV-04 (scripts/security_gates.sh) | tested | ACC-GOV-04 | RR | as listed | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:59:**Options.** (A) Fully supported. **(B, chosen)** Shipped and labelled **experimental** in help and docs. Excluded from the qualification task-quality claims. But the following are still fixed for v1:\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:120:- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:151:**Chosen:** Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 20 for v1.0.0, which is what is built and tested. The docs keep the conservative \"≥ 2.35\" claim; the binaries reference glibc symbols ≤ 2.34. macOS, arm64 and musl are post-v1 roadmap items.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:204:**Tradeoff:** live evidence for server kinds other than llama.cpp is limited to emulated shapes. This is stated plainly rather than over-claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:12:## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:15:- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:37:- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:55:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:75:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:85:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:94:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:95:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:96:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:101:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:109:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:110:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:27:| docs/PERS002_*, WP05_*, CRED003_* | grep for verdicts/claims; PHASE2S review not read (63KB). Excluded for budget. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:57:| SEC-09 | S3 | plugins | plugins.ts:254-300 | SOURCE. `executeSandboxed` (\"Execute untrusted ... plugin code inside an isolated Worker\") uses eval in a worker_thread. That is not an isolation boundary (full Node API). It is unused: grep found no callers. | A misleading security claim in code. A future caller would trust it. | POST-V1: delete it or rename it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:3:Repo HEAD db1ca55 (v0.1.0-alpha.2-2). Read-only. All \"claimed status\" values are DOC-CLAIM unless mar…1944 tokens truncated…col it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:57:   - completion claimed;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:81:   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:14:| C6 | Clean-account run (owner action X6): fresh VM and Cloudflare account. Follow the G1 procedure in `evidence/G_contest_eval.md` §6 and commit a redacted run record. | — | Required for a reproducibility claim |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:99:| Docs not fully re-verified | Only claims relevant to findings (resume, compaction commit, team 15-step cap) were checked against code; remaining claims in COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md are UNVERIFIED by this audit. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:73:8. **REQ-AGT-119.** Experimental surfaces (DEC-07: `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles) are labelled experimental in help and docs and excluded from qualification claims. `nexus eval` runs in a worktree and never touches the operator's checkout. Team reviewer and researcher roles run with a read-only tool set.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:8:| Findings | HIST-01, HIST-02, HIST-03, HIST-06, HIST-09, HIST-10, HIST-11, DOC-01, PRV-17, AGT-07, CON-012, EVL-006, VER-07 (EXEC-011 claim) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:51:   - make no claims contradicted by source at the RC;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:53:   - make no parity or marketing claims without evidence;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:72:| `USER_MANUAL.md:3` | Remove the parity claim. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:76:| `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md` | Use neutral examples. Correct the redaction and catalog claims. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/BRIEF.md:13:- Historical docs/reviews and \"VERIFIED\" claims are evidence to check, not proof.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:21:| upstream/node-v24.21.0/{pubring.kbx, SHASUMS256.txt, .sig} (vendored) | sha256 compared with README claim; `gpgv` signature check run locally against the vendored keyring. Keyring provenance (nodejs/release-keys commit) not independently re-fetched. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:88:| CON-011 | S3 | Worker auth | agent-collab-worker/src/index.ts:10-21 | SOURCE. The single static shared bearer (`EXPERIMENT_AUTH`) is used for every run, with no expiry. The compare is constant-time except for the length check. `/health` is unauthenticated and minimal (OK). The Artifacts binding covers the whole namespace; the Worker reads only the configured repo. | Acceptable for a bounded demo, not for a multi-tenant service. The contest doc already disclaims production security (CONTEST.md:15). | Per-run or HMAC tokens after the contest. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:92:| EVL-001 | S1 (v1 task-quality claim) | Qualification evidence | eval/README.md:42,47-58; docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:62-63 | DOC-CLAIM + SOURCE. The only scored evidence is 6 in-repo T2 fixture tasks. RESULT.md itself says \"These six tasks were used to find and fix the issues … it does not qualify Nexus. Qualification needs a fresh task set.\" Missing: held-out tasks, the T3 long-task set, the T4 fault injector, the T3 fact-sheet scorer, and runs on the release candidate. The measured builds are 76f4081, ed17e99 and 4fcbe68-dirty; their rebased equivalents (fe576f1, d116e99, 0090f9c) are on main, but db1ca55 itself was never evaluated. | No basis for a v1 claim about task quality. The pilot verdict was \"NOT QUALIFIED (false VERIFIED=2)\". The rerun had 0 false VERIFIED, but on tuned tasks. | A v1 protocol is in §7. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:133:- **The docs are honest about the block:** CONTEST.md:15,65,89 and VIDEO_ASSET.md:19 do not claim reproducibility. Offline modes are labelled. In real-agent mode the demo labels the control/treatment contrast as historical (nexus-demo.mjs:313-314).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:167:| CON-R4 | One independent clean-account Cloudflare-backed end-to-end run, with a committed redacted run record | failure / evidence | BLOCKER (contest claim of reproducibility). Otherwise submit with an explicit \"operator-host only\" statement. | G1 procedure |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:176:| EVL-R1 | **Held-out set:** at least 40 T2 tasks (proposal). At least 50% from external repos at pinned commits (JS/TS, Python, Rust, Go). The held-out half is authored by someone other than the Nexus developer and kept outside the repo (encrypted or private) until the freeze. The 6 pilot tasks plus the routing engx T01-T12 count as a *development* set only. | workflow | BLOCKER for any v1 quality claim | The manifest lists task sha256s committed *before* the release-candidate (RC) freeze. Tasks are revealed after scoring. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:179:| EVL-R4 | **Metrics, reported separately:** hidden-test correctness; completion claimed; false VERIFIED; regressions (repo suite plus a pre/post diff of previously passing tests); crash rate; timeout rate; bounded-failure truthfulness (outcome ∈ {BLOCKED, BUDGET_EXHAUSTED, UNVERIFIED} with a correct reason when hidden tests fail); intervention count (operator inputs required, which must be 0 in `run` mode); cost (tokens and wall time per correct task) | workflow | BLOCKER | The scorer emits each metric. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:19:| 5 | Remove the parity claim, homelab identifiers, and the `file:///` link. Correct the ARCHITECTURE controls-and-limits section. | `USER_MANUAL.md:3`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `MCP_GUIDE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md` | M0 (cheap, standalone) |\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"diff --git a/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts b/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\nindex f1e350e..cec2688 100644\n--- a/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\n+++ b/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\n@@ -237,9 +237,9 @@ test(\"T4 scoring requires all nine classes and five injected runs per class\", ()\n     const evidence = kind === \"sigterm_resume\"\n       ? { signal: \"SIGTERM\", delivered: true, deliveredProcesses: 1, signalDuringActiveTurn: true, payloadExitSignal: \"SIGTERM\", supervisorWrapperExitSignal: null, resumed: true, resumeExitCode: 0, resumeTurnExecution: \"COMPLETED\" }\n       : kind === \"hanging_test_command\"\n-        ? { observedHung: true, timedOut: true, containmentCleaned: true }\n+        ? { observedHung: true, timedOut: true, containmentCleaned: true, tool: \"run_command\", commandSha256: \"a\".repeat(64), timeoutSecs: 60 }\n         : kind === \"full_disk\"\n-          ? { writeFailedWithEnospc: true, storageLimitBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 }\n+          ? { writeFailedWithEnospc: true, containmentCleaned: true, tool: \"run_command\", commandSha256: \"a\".repeat(64), storageLimitBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 }\n           : undefined;\n     const event = { kind, source: runnerClass ? \"task_fixture_or_runner\" : \"model_proxy\", ...(evidence ? { evidence } : {}) };\n     return {\n@@ -365,6 +365,10 @@ test(\"task validation: pinned repos, one source, and black-box hidden oracle for\n   assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, t4RunnerFault: \"sigterm_resume\" }, dir).join(), /supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task/);\n   assert.deepEqual(validateTask({ ...good, tier: \"T4\", t4RunnerFault: \"sigterm_resume\" }, dir), []);\n   assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, tier: \"T4\", t4RunnerFault: \"full_disk\" }, dir).join(), /supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task/);\n+  assert.deepEqual(validateTask({ ...good, tier: \"T4\", t4Fixture: { kind: \"hanging_test_command\", tool: \"run_command\", command: \"npm test\", timeoutSecs: 60 } }, dir), []);\n+  assert.deepEqual(validateTask({ ...good, tier: \"T4\", t4Fixture: { kind: \"full_disk\", tool: \"run_command\", command: \"./test-disk-cap.sh\", storageLimitBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 } }, dir), []);\n+  assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, t4Fixture: { kind: \"full_disk\", tool: \"run_command\", command: \"./test-disk-cap.sh\", storageLimitBytes: 64 } }, dir).join(), /only as an object on a T4 task/);\n+  assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, tier: \"T4\", t4Fixture: { kind: \"full_disk\", tool: \"run_command\", command: \"./test-disk-cap.sh\" } }, dir).join(), /positive storageLimitBytes/);\n   assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, repo: { url: good.repo.url, commit: \"main\" } }, dir).join(), /pinned/);\n   assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, fixture: \"repo\" }, dir).join(), /exactly one of fixture or repo/);\n   assert.match(validateTask({ ...good, hidden: {} }, dir).join(), /hidden.command/);\n@@ -389,6 +393,24 @@ test(\"task validation: pinned repos, one source, and black-box hidden oracle for\n   assert.match(validateTask({ ...qualifiedTask, hidden: { ...oracle, argv: [\"--eval\"] } }, dir, { qualification: true }).join(), /normalized relative candidate entrypoint/);\n });\n \n+test(\"T4 fixture evidence is derived from the exact tool transcript and resource boundary\", async () => {\n+  const { observeT4Fixture } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/t4_fixtures.mjs\"));\n+  const task = { tier: \"T4\", t4Fixture: { kind: \"hanging_test_command\", tool: \"run_command\", command: \"npm test\", timeoutSecs: 30 } };\n+  const call = { id: \"call-1\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"run_command\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ command: \"npm test\", timeout_secs: 30 }) } };\n+  const agent = { json: { messages: [{ role: \"assistant\", tool_calls: [call] }, { role: \"tool\", tool_call_id: \"call-1\", content: \"Command timed out after 30 seconds.\" }] } };\n+  const containment = { cleaned: true, survivorsAfterExit: 0 };\n+  const hang = observeT4Fixture(task, agent, containment, { storageBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 });\n+  assert.equal(hang[0].evidence.observedHung, true);\n+  assert.equal(observeT4Fixture(task, { ...agent, json: { messages: [] } }, containment, {}).length, 0);\n+  assert.equal(observeT4Fixture(task, agent, { cleaned: false, survivorsAfterExit: 1 }, {}).at(0).evidence.containmentCleaned, false);\n+\n+  const diskTask = { tier: \"T4\", t4Fixture: { kind: \"full_disk\", tool: \"run_command\", command: \"./test-disk-cap.sh\", storageLimitBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 } };\n+  const diskCall = { id: \"call-2\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"run_command\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ command: \"./test-disk-cap.sh\", timeout_secs: 30 }) } };\n+  const diskAgent = { json: { messages: [{ role: \"assistant\", tool_calls: [diskCall] }, { role: \"tool\", tool_call_id: \"call-2\", content: \"write failed: ENOSPC\" }] } };\n+  assert.equal(observeT4Fixture(diskTask, diskAgent, containment, { storageBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 })[0].evidence.writeFailedWithEnospc, true);\n+  assert.equal(observeT4Fixture(diskTask, diskAgent, containment, { storageBytes: 128 * 1024 * 1024 })[0].evidence.storageLimitBytes, null);\n+});\n+\n test(\"black-box oracle keeps canary expectations outside the candidate process and returns sanitized evidence\", { timeout: 15_000 }, async () => {\n   const { runBlackBoxOracle } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/oracle.mjs\"));\n   const taskDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"eval-private-task-\"));\ndiff --git a/eval/README.md b/eval/README.md\nindex 484673f..07264b8 100644\n--- a/eval/README.md\n+++ b/eval/README.md\n@@ -104,7 +104,12 @@ What was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never tre\n - hung past budget.\n \n The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\n-runner case. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n+runner case. A fixture task declares `t4Fixture: { kind, tool: \"run_command\", command, timeoutSecs }` for a hanging\n+test, or `t4Fixture: { kind: \"full_disk\", tool: \"run_command\", command, storageLimitBytes }` for a full disk. The\n+runner counts a fixture only when the candidate's structured transcript contains that exact command, the tool result\n+shows the timeout or ENOSPC condition, and the task process cgroup reports successful cleanup with no survivors. The\n+full-disk limit must match the frozen resource contract. Task metadata identifies the expected fixture; it cannot\n+provide evidence or a pass bit. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\n \n ## Qualification runs\n \ndiff --git a/eval/run.mjs b/eval/run.mjs\nindex 50eec08..c47a4c5 100644\n--- a/eval/run.mjs\n+++ b/eval/run.mjs\n@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ import { applyAgentChanges, cloneWorkspace } from \"./hardened_check.mjs\";\n import { containmentProblem, resourceProbeProblem, spawnContained } from \"./resources.mjs\";\n import { StringDecoder } from \"node:string_decoder\";\n import { commandBaseline, countCompactions, createT3Driver, scoreT3Run, steeringBaseline, steeringPrecondition, t3Snapshot } from \"./t3.mjs\";\n+import { observeT4Fixture } from \"./t4_fixtures.mjs\";\n \n const ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\n const args = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\n@@ -242,6 +243,7 @@ async function runOnce(task, run) {\n     const wallMs = agentEndedAt - started;\n     if (agent.containmentProblem) throw new Error(`candidate containment failed: ${agent.containmentProblem}`);\n     const model = proxy ? proxy.stats() : null;\n+    const fixtureFaults = observeT4Fixture(task, agent, agent.resources, config.resources);\n     const contaminated = treeDigest(task.dir) !== sourceBefore || `${agent.stdout}${agent.stderr}`.includes(tasksDir);\n     // T3 judges the workspace as it was when the objective's work ended (snapshot taken before the probe turn).\n     const t3 = agent.t3Driver ? scoreT3Run({ task, baseline: t3Baseline, driver: agent.t3Driver, preconditions: agent.t3Preconditions, compactions: countCompactions(home) }) : null;\n@@ -290,7 +292,7 @@ async function runOnce(task, run) {\n       ...(hardening ? { hardened: { baseline: hardening.baseline, applied: hardening.applied.length, discarded: hardening.discarded, configChanges: hardening.configChanges } } : {}),\n       ...(t3 ? { t3 } : {}),\n       model,\n-      ...(agent.t4FaultsInjected?.length ? { t4FaultsInjected: agent.t4FaultsInjected } : {}),\n+      ...((agent.t4FaultsInjected?.length || fixtureFaults.length) ? { t4FaultsInjected: [...(agent.t4FaultsInjected ?? []), ...fixtureFaults] } : {}),\n       resources: config.resources ? { agent: agent.resources, hidden: hidden.resources ?? null, regression: regression?.resources ?? null, ...(t3BaselineResources.length ? { t3Baseline: t3BaselineResources } : {}) } : null,\n       logs: saveLogs(task, run, agent, hidden, regression),\n     };\n@@ -766,7 +768,7 @@ function harnessIdentity() {\n   const git = (...a) => spawnSync(\"git\", a, { cwd: ROOT, encoding: \"utf8\" }).stdout.trim();\n   const commit = git(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\");\n   const dirty = Boolean(git(\"status\", \"--porcelain\", \"--untracked-files=all\", \"--\", \".\", \":(exclude)cli/dist\"));\n-  const sourceFiles = [\"eval/run.mjs\", \"eval/validate.mjs\", \"eval/isolate.mjs\", \"eval/hide_oracle.cjs\", \"eval/hide_oracle.py\", \"eval/unlink_then_exec.sh\", \"eval/agent_sandbox.mjs\", \"eval/model_proxy.mjs\", \"eval/score.mjs\", \"eval/infra.mjs\", \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\", \"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\", \"eval/t3.mjs\", \"eval/hardened_check.mjs\"];\n+  const sourceFiles = [\"eval/run.mjs\", \"eval/validate.mjs\", \"eval/t4_fixtures.mjs\", \"eval/isolate.mjs\", \"eval/hide_oracle.cjs\", \"eval/hide_oracle.py\", \"eval/unlink_then_exec.sh\", \"eval/agent_sandbox.mjs\", \"eval/model_proxy.mjs\", \"eval/score.mjs\", \"eval/infra.mjs\", \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\", \"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\", \"eval/t3.mjs\", \"eval/hardened_check.mjs\"];\n   const sourceDigests = sourceFiles.map((file) => ({ file, sha256: createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, file))).digest(\"hex\") }));\n   const sourceSha256 = createHash(\"sha256\").update(JSON.stringify(sourceDigests)).digest(\"hex\");\n   return { commit, dirty, sourceDigests, sourceSha256, string: `${commit.slice(0, 12)}${dirty ? \"-dirty\" : \"\"}` };\ndiff --git a/eval/score.mjs b/eval/score.mjs\nindex 62a84c1..6cead81 100644\n--- a/eval/score.mjs\n+++ b/eval/score.mjs\n@@ -145,8 +145,8 @@ const runnerEvidenceValid = (event) => {\n       && evidence.resumeExitCode === 0\n       && evidence.resumeTurnExecution === \"COMPLETED\";\n   }\n-  if (event.kind === \"hanging_test_command\") return evidence.observedHung === true && evidence.timedOut === true && evidence.containmentCleaned === true;\n-  if (event.kind === \"full_disk\") return evidence.writeFailedWithEnospc === true && Number.isSafeInteger(evidence.storageLimitBytes) && evidence.storageLimitBytes > 0;\n+  if (event.kind === \"hanging_test_command\") return evidence.observedHung === true && evidence.timedOut === true && evidence.containmentCleaned === true && /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(evidence.commandSha256 ?? \"\") && evidence.tool === \"run_command\" && Number.isSafeInteger(evidence.timeoutSecs) && evidence.timeoutSecs > 0;\n+  if (event.kind === \"full_disk\") return evidence.writeFailedWithEnospc === true && evidence.containmentCleaned === true && /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(evidence.commandSha256 ?? \"\") && evidence.tool === \"run_command\" && Number.isSafeInteger(evidence.storageLimitBytes) && evidence.storageLimitBytes > 0;\n   return false;\n };\n const t4Runs = records.filter((r) => r.tier === \"T4\");\ndiff --git a/eval/validate.mjs b/eval/validate.mjs\nindex 3d48cab..30befcd 100644\n--- a/eval/validate.mjs\n+++ b/eval/validate.mjs\n@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ import { assertNoSymlinks, candidateSandboxHostMountSources, confinedPath, runti\n import { blackBoxOracleProblem } from \"./oracle.mjs\";\n import { t3TaskProblems } from \"./t3.mjs\";\n import { resourceProbeProblem } from \"./resources.mjs\";\n+import { t4FixtureProblems } from \"./t4_fixtures.mjs\";\n \n export const TIERS = [\"T1\", \"T2\", \"T3\", \"T4\"];\n export const CLASSES = [\"bugfix\", \"feature\", \"refactor\", \"debug\"];\n@@ -64,6 +65,7 @@ export function validateTask(task, dir, { qualification = false } = {}) {\n   if (task.t4RunnerFault !== undefined) {\n     need(task.tier === \"T4\" && task.t4RunnerFault === \"sigterm_resume\", \"t4RunnerFault is supported only as sigterm_resume on a T4 task\");\n   }\n+  problems.push(...t4FixtureProblems(task));\n   if (task.class !== undefined || qualification) need(CLASSES.includes(task.class), `class must be one of ${CLASSES.join(\", \")}`);\n   if (task.difficulty !== undefined || qualification) need(DIFFICULTIES.includes(task.difficulty), `difficulty must be one of ${DIFFICULTIES.join(\", \")}`);\n   return problems;\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792917365.8047645}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
