      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n          simulated: Boolean(this.config.dryRun),\n        },\n        shouldExit: false,\n      };\n    }\n\n    this.ui.printToolCall(toolName, args);\n    const dispatch = ++this.toolDispatchSeq;\n    this.observer?.onToolStart?.({ dispatch, callId: call.id, tool: toolName, args });\n    const subject = String(args.path ?? args.file_path ?? args.command ?? args.url ?? args.query ?? \"\").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").slice(0, 120);\n    this.activity(\"tool\", { tool: toolName, ...(subject ? { subject } : {}) });\n\n    const cap = this.capabilityRegistry.getByToolName(toolName);\n    const isMutating = cap ? cap.mutating : !READ_ONLY_TOOLS.has(toolName);\n\n    if (onConfirm && isMutating) {\n      this.activity(\"approval\", { tool: toolName, ...(subject ? { subject } : {}) });\n      const approved = await onConfirm(toolName, args);\n      if (approved) this.activity(\"tool\", { tool: toolName, ...(subject ? { subject } : {}) });\n      if (!approved) {\n        console.log(`⚠️ Tool execution cancelled by user.`);\n        const cancelMsg =\n          \"Error: Execution was rejected by the user. Ask the user for clarification or proceed with an alternative approach.\";\n        const receipt: ExecutionReceipt = {\n          invocationId: call.id,\n          taskId: this.activeWorktree?.taskId || this.currentTaskId,\n          actor,\n          executionDomain: actor === \"subagent\" ? \"subagent\" : \"agent_orchestration\",\n          capabilityId:\n            this.capabilityRegistry.getByToolName(toolName)?.id || \"unknown\",\n          toolName,\n          targetResources: extractTargetResources(toolName, args),\n          success: false,\n          output: \"\",\n          error: cancelMsg,\n          durationMs: 0,\n          candidateMutated: false,\n          status: \"DENIED\",\n          timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n          simulated: Boolean(this.config.dryRun),\n        };\n        if (this.flightRecorder) {\n          this.flightRecorder.recordToolResult(\n            currentStep,\n            call.id,\n            toolName,\n            false,\n            cancelMsg,\n            0,\n            \"Rejected by user\"\n          );\n        const state = this.stateManager.loadTaskState(taskId);\n        if (state.validationReceipts && state.validationReceipts.length > 0) {\n          return state.validationReceipts[state.validationReceipts.length - 1];\n        }\n      } catch {}\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Executes a task through the unified execution spine and durable state lifecycle (UI-001, UI-002, UI-003).\n   */\n  public async runTask(prompt: string, options: RunTaskOptions = {}): Promise<TaskExecutionResult> {\n    const startTime = Date.now();\n    const taskId = this.agent.getTaskId();\n\n    if (options.resumeTaskId) {\n      await this.recoverTask(options.resumeTaskId);\n    }\n\n    this.emit(\"task:start\", {\n      taskId,\n      prompt,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    });\n\n    const capturedLogs: string[] = [];\n    const shouldCapture = Boolean(options.json || options.quiet);\n\n    // Intercept stdout/console when machine-readable JSON is requested\n    const originalLog = console.log;\n    const originalWarn = console.warn;\n    const originalError = console.error;\n    const originalStdoutWrite = process.stdout.write.bind(process.stdout);\n\n    if (shouldCapture) {\n      console.log = (...args: any[]) => {\n        capturedLogs.push(args.map((a) => (typeof a === \"string\" ? a : JSON.stringify(a))).join(\" \"));\n      };\n      console.warn = (...args: any[]) => {\n        capturedLogs.push(\"[WARN] \" + args.map((a) => (typeof a === \"string\" ? a : JSON.stringify(a))).join(\" \"));\n      };\n      console.error = (...args: any[]) => {\n        capturedLogs.push(\"[ERROR] \" + args.map((a) => (typeof a === \"string\" ? a : JSON.stringify(a))).join(\" \"));\n      };\n      // Streamed model tokens are written with process.stdout.write; capture them too so --json stdout is only the JSON document.\n      (process.stdout as any).write = (chunk: any, encoding?: any, cb?: any): boolean => {\n        capturedLogs.push(typeof chunk === \"string\" ? chunk : Buffer.from(chunk).toString(\"utf-8\"));\n        const done = typeof encoding === \"function\" ? encoding : cb;\n        if (typeof done === \"function\") done();\n        return true;\n      };\n    }\n\n    let taskError: Error | undefined;\n    let turn: TurnResult | undefined;\n    try {\n      turn = await this.agent.run(prompt, options.onConfirm, { signal: options.signal });\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      taskError = err;\n    } finally {\n      if (shouldCapture) {\n        console.log = originalLog;\n        console.warn = originalWarn;\n        console.error = originalError;\n        process.stdout.write = originalStdoutWrite as typeof process.stdout.write;\n      }\n    }\n\n    const finalTurn: TurnResult = turn ?? failedTurnFromError(taskError, this.config.maxSteps);\n\n    // Capture durable task state snapshot\n    let durableState: DurableTaskState;\n    try {\n      durableState = withDurableSync(() => this.agent.checkpointDurableState(\"Task execution finished\", finalTurn));\n    } catch {\n      durableState = this.getTaskState();\n    }\n\n    // Persist session envelope synchronously\n    const messages = this.agent.getMessages();\n    withDurableSync(() => this.sessionManager.saveSession({\n      id: taskId,\n      taskId,\n      sessionId: taskId,\n      title: prompt.slice(0, 60).replace(/\\n/g, \" \"),\n      createdAt: durableState.createdAt || new Date().toISOString(),\n      updatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n      workspace: this.config.workspace,\n      model: this.config.model,\n      status: lifecycleStatusForTurn(finalTurn),\n      lastTurn: finalTurn,\n      messages,\n      unverifiedChangesPending: this.agent.hasUnverifiedChanges(),\n      tokenStats: this.agent.getTokenStats(),\n      activePlan: durableState.activePlan,\n      milestones: durableState.milestones,\n      candidateId: durableState.candidateId,\n      validationReceipts: durableState.validationReceipts,\n      worktreeBinding: durableState.worktreeBinding,\n      findings: durableState.findings,\n      objective: this.agent.getObjective() ?? null,\n      // Compactions this record commits; their originals are archived beside the task state (`<task>.history.jsonl`).\n      history: this.agent.getHistoryCompleteness(),\n    }, this.agent.getWorkspacePathIdentity()));\n\n    // Extract last assistant output\n    let outputText = \"\";\n    for (let i = messages.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n      if (messages[i].role === \"assistant\" && messages[i].content) {\n        const c = messages[i].content;\n        outputText = typeof c === \"string\" ? c : JSON.stringify(c);\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n\n    const durationMs = Date.now() - startTime;\n    const success = turnSucceeded(finalTurn);\n\n    const result: TaskExecutionResult = {\n      taskId,\n      success,\n      status: lifecycleStatusForTurn(finalTurn),\n      prompt,\n      output: outputText,\n      plan: durableState.activePlan || [],\n      milestones: durableState.milestones || [],\n      candidateId: durableState.candidateId || null,\n      candidateIdentity: durableState.candidateIdentity || null,\n      validationReceipts: durableState.validationReceipts || [],\n      worktreeBinding: durableState.worktreeBinding || null,\n      tokenStats: this.agent.getTokenStats(),\n      durationMs,\n      error: taskError ? taskError.message : undefined,\n      logs: shouldCapture ? capturedLogs : undefined,\n      turn: finalTurn,\n      exitCode: exitCodeForTurn(finalTurn),\n    };\n\n    this.emit(\"task:end\", result);\n    return result;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Executes an explicit direct shell / operator command through the ExecutionSpine (ACT-004, AUTH-001).\n   * Formally logs execution with 'operator' actor identity.\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse std::path::Path;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct RunCommandArgs {\n    pub command: String,\n    pub cwd: Option<String>,\n    #[serde(default = \"default_timeout\")]\n    pub timeout_secs: u64,\n    #[serde(default = \"default_shell\")]\n    pub shell: String,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub pty: bool,\n}\n\nfn default_timeout() -> u64 {\n    60\n}\n\nfn default_shell() -> String {\n    #[cfg(windows)]\n    return \"powershell.exe\".to_string();\n    #[cfg(not(windows))]\n    return \"bash\".to_string();\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct RunCommandResult {\n    pub command: String,\n    pub shell: String,\n    pub exit_code: Option<i32>,\n    pub stdout: String,\n    pub stderr: String,\n    pub duration_ms: u128,\n    pub timed_out: bool,\n}\n\nconst MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS: usize = 32_000;\n\nfn truncate_output(s: &str) -> String {\n    if s.len() > MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS {\n        let half = MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS / 2;\n        let mut head_idx = half;\n        while !s.is_char_boundary(head_idx) && head_idx > 0 {\n            head_idx -= 1;\n        }\n        let mut tail_idx = s.len().saturating_sub(half);\n        while !s.is_char_boundary(tail_idx) && tail_idx < s.len() {\npub fn run_command(args: RunCommandArgs, base_dir: &Path) -> Result<RunCommandResult, String> {\n    if let Some(reason) = is_dangerous_command(&args.command) {\n        return Err(format!(\"Security Violation: Dangerous command blocked by safety guard ({reason}): '{}'\", args.command));\n    }\n\n    let base_canon = base_dir.canonicalize().map_err(|e| format!(\"Invalid workspace directory: {e}\"))?;\n\n    let working_dir = match args.cwd {\n        Some(ref d) => {\n            let p = Path::new(d);\n            let target_path = if p.is_absolute() {\n                p.to_path_buf()\n            } else {\n                base_dir.join(p)\n            };\n            if !target_path.exists() {\n                return Err(format!(\"Working directory does not exist: {}\", target_path.display()));\n            }\n            let canon = target_path.canonicalize().map_err(|e| format!(\"Invalid cwd: {e}\"))?;\n            if !canon.starts_with(&base_canon) {\n                return Err(format!(\"Security Violation: cwd escapes workspace jail: {d}\"));\n            }\n            canon\n        }\n        None => base_canon.clone(),\n    };\n\n    let shell_name = if args.shell.trim().is_empty() {\n        default_shell()\n    } else {\n        args.shell.trim().to_string()\n    };\n\n    if args.pty {\n        return run_command_pty(&args.command, &working_dir, args.timeout_secs, &shell_name);\n    }\n\n    let start = Instant::now();\n\n    // Cross-platform shell process execution (Candidate #50)\n    let mut cmd = Command::new(&shell_name);\n    #[cfg(windows)]\n    if shell_name.contains(\"powershell\") {\n        cmd.args([\"-NoProfile\", \"-Command\", &args.command]);\n    } else {\n        cmd.args([\"/C\", &args.command]);\n    }\n    #[cfg(not(windows))]\n    cmd.args([\"-c\", &args.command]);\n\n    cmd.current_dir(&working_dir)\n        .stdin(Stdio::null())\n        .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n        .stderr(Stdio::piped());\n\n    // Own process group, so a timeout can end the shell AND everything it started. Killing only the shell leaves\n    // descendants alive holding the output pipes (the call then blocks until they exit, and they outlive it).\n    #[cfg(unix)]\n    std::os::unix::process::CommandExt::process_group(&mut cmd, 0);\n\n    let mut child = cmd.spawn().map_err(|e| {\n        format!(\"Failed to execute '{}' via {shell_name}: {e}\", args.command)\n    })?;\n\n    let stdout = child.stdout.take().ok_or(\"Failed to capture stdout\")?;\n    let stderr = child.stderr.take().ok_or(\"Failed to capture stderr\")?;\n\n    // Readers append to shared buffers, so output already read is kept even if a pipe stays open past the drain.\n    let reader = |pipe: Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>| {\n        let collected = std::sync::Arc::new(std::sync::Mutex::new(Vec::new()));\n        let sink = std::sync::Arc::clone(&collected);\n        let (done_tx, done_rx) = std::sync::mpsc::channel::<()>();\n        std::thread::spawn(move || {\n            let mut pipe = pipe;\n            let mut chunk = [0u8; 8192];\n            loop {\n                match pipe.read(&mut chunk) {\n                    Ok(0) | Err(_) => break,\n                    Ok(n) => sink.lock().unwrap().extend_from_slice(&chunk[..n]),\n                }\n            }\n            let _ = done_tx.send(());\n        });\n        (collected, done_rx)\n    };\n    let (stdout_buf, stdout_done) = reader(Box::new(stdout));\n    let (stderr_buf, stderr_done) = reader(Box::new(stderr));\n\n    let timeout = Duration::from_secs(args.timeout_secs);\n    let poll_interval = Duration::from_millis(50);\n    let mut timed_out = false;\n\n    let exit_status = loop {\n        match child.try_wait() {\n            Ok(Some(status)) => break Some(status),\n            Ok(None) => {\n                if start.elapsed() > timeout {\n                    terminate_process_tree(&mut child);\n                    timed_out = true;\n                    break None;\n                }\n                std::thread::sleep(poll_interval);\n            }\n            Err(e) => {\n                return Err(format!(\"Error waiting for process: {e}\"));\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\n    // How long to wait for the pipes to close after the shell ended. A process the command left running in the\n    // background (`server &`) can hold them open: what was read so far is returned and that process is left alone.\n    let drain = if timed_out { Duration::from_millis(100) } else { Duration::from_millis(500) };\n    let drain_deadline = Instant::now() + drain;\n    let _ = stdout_done.recv_timeout(drain_deadline.saturating_duration_since(Instant::now()));\n    let _ = stderr_done.recv_timeout(drain_deadline.saturating_duration_since(Instant::now()));\n    let stdout_bytes = std::mem::take(&mut *stdout_buf.lock().unwrap());\n    let stderr_bytes = std::mem::take(&mut *stderr_buf.lock().unwrap());\n    let duration_ms = start.elapsed().as_millis();\n\n    let raw_stdout = String::from_utf8_lossy(&stdout_bytes).to_string();\n    let raw_stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&stderr_bytes).to_string();\n\n    Ok(RunCommandResult {\n        command: args.command,\n        shell: shell_name,\n        exit_code: exit_status.and_then(|s| s.code()),\n        stdout: truncate_output(&raw_stdout),\n        stderr: truncate_output(&raw_stderr),\n        duration_ms,\n        timed_out,\n    })\n}\n\n/// Ends the command's whole process group: SIGTERM first so well-behaved tools can clean up, then SIGKILL for\n/// anything still alive (the group id stays valid while any member lives, so descendants are covered even after\n/// the shell has exited). Always reaps the shell.\nfn terminate_process_tree(child: &mut std::process::Child) {\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"They also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_agent-collab-worker_package.json/owner.json\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792917371.3099504}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
