{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:43:20.185Z","ordinal":332879,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1723a-84f9-7630-b648-15e061723a43","call_id":"call_9bb9300b3190494983f0fbb79d9b54cf","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The notes match the merged PRs. PR #207 remains open, and no unmerged #207 change is claimed; the `.nexus/` commit-exclusion behavior is already present on the base through merged PR #198. The notes describe RC5 artifacts as expected workflow outputs and do not claim that RC5 is tagged, published, or accepted.\\n\\nRead-only review; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — candidate `fb36b03c2ad9a22f4e94139accccee1d2f137ae3` versus current `main` at `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f`.\\n\\nThe six-file security patch is unchanged. Its diff SHA-256 is `55b0230bcdb125cecc263c83afbb83dc9bc54cab24ca557209a92f57d503de7a`.\\n\\nThe reported 18-file diff against stale base `19b30a4` includes 12 files changed on current `main` since that base; they add no candidate-only changes versus current `main`. Refreshing the PR base to `016bbc3` will make its displayed scope clear. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/t4_runner_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792917800.1854033}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
